श्वेतवासस्
श्वेतवासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A religious mendicant, wearing white garments.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतवाह|श्वेतवाहः
श्वेतवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and वाह a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतवाहन|श्वेतवाहनः
श्वेतवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 ARJUNA.<BR>3 The Makara, a marine monster.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतवाहिन्
श्वेतवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and वाह a vehicle, (a horse,) इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतशुङ्ग|श्वेतशुंग|श्वेतशुङ्गः
श्वेतशुङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and शुङ्ग awn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतसर्प|श्वेतसर्पः
श्वेतसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>1 A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>2 A white snake.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, सर्प what creeps or grows, or a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतसार|श्वेतसारः
श्वेतसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa catechu)<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, सार pith or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतसुरसा
श्वेतसुरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A white variety of the Nyctanthes arbor-tristis.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and सुरसा the Rasan, &c. to which it is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतहय|श्वेतहयः
श्वेतहय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A white horse.<BR>2 The horse of INDRA.<BR>3 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and हय a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतहस्तिन्
श्वेतहस्तिन्<BR>m. (-स्ती)<BR>1 A white elephant.<BR>2 The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and हस्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतार्क|श्वेतार्कः
श्वेतार्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>Gigantic swallow-wort, (Asclepias gigantea,) with white flowers.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and अर्क the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतोदर|श्वेतोदरः
श्वेतोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्य|श्वैत्यं
श्वैत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Whiteness.<BR>2 Vitiligo.<BR>E.<BR>श्वित or श्वेत, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्र|श्वैत्रं
श्वैत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Vitiligo.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत to be white, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वोवसीयस|श्वोवसीयसं
श्वोवसीयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेस and वस both particles implying auspiciousness, ईयसुन् affixed to the latter, and a final vowel added to the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष<BR>The thirty-first consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, and second sibilant, corresponding to Sh, pronounced in some schools Kh: this letter is usually the first element of the roots, the derivatives of which commence with स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष<BR>mfn. (षः-षा-षं)<BR>Best, excellent.<BR>m. (षः)<BR>1 A learned man, a teacher.<BR>2 A nipple.<BR>3 Loss, destruction.<BR>4 Rest, remainder.<BR>5 Loss of knowledge previously acquired.<BR>6 Eternal happiness, final emancipation.<BR>7 Heaven, paradise.<BR>8 Sleep.<BR>9 End, term.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 The embryo.<BR>2 Patience, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, &c., aff. क or ड and the consonant unchanged, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षग
षग<BR>(ए) षगे r. 1st cl. (सगति)<BR>To cover: also written सग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षघ
षघ<BR>r. 5th cl. (सघ्नोति)<BR>To hurt or kill: also सघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षच
षच<BR>r. 1st cl. (सचते)<BR>1 To wet, to moisten, to sprinkle.<BR>2 To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>(सचति)<BR>1 To be connected.<BR>2 To understand thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षञ्च
षञ्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (सञ्चति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षञ्ज
षञ्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (सजति)<BR>To embrace, to cling or adhere to, to be in contact or connexion with.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>to hand down from, to be suspended.<BR>With वि and आङ्,<BR>to struggle together.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>to be attached or devoted to.<BR>(उ) षञ्जु r. 1st cl. (सञ्जति-ते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट
षट<BR>r. 1st cl. (सटति)<BR>To be a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्क|षट्कः
षट्क<BR>mfn. (-ट्कः-ट्का-ट्कं)<BR>1 Six.<BR>2 Having six, six-fold, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and कन् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्ण|षट्कर्णः
षट्कर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A sort of lute.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and कर्ण an ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्म्मन्|षट्कर्मन्
षट्कर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 An adept, (in the Tantras, &c.)<BR>n. (-र्म्म or pl. र्म्माणि)<BR>1 The six acts proper for a Brahman, (collectively,) or teaching the Vedas, holy study, offering sacrifices, conducting them for others, giving, accepting gifts.<BR>2 Six acts allowable to a Brahman for subsistence, or gleaning, accepting gifts, asking alms, agriculture, trade, and tending cattle, or according to some lending money at interest.<BR>3 The six acts taught in the Tantras, or killing, infatuating, enthralling, expelling, exciting animosity, and the stopping or privation of any faculty.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, कर्म्मन् act or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कोण|षट्कोणं
षट्कोण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A hexagon, a six-angled figure.<BR>2 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चरण|षट्चरणः
षट्चरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and चरण a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्ट
षट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (षट्टयति)<BR>1 To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>2 To give.<BR>3 To be strong.<BR>4 To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्त्रिंशत्
षट्त्रिंशत्<BR>f. (-शत्)<BR>1 Thirty-six.<BR>2 A work on law.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and त्रिंशत् thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पद|षट्पदः
षट्पद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A bee.<BR>mf. (-दः-दी)<BR>A louse.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदप्रिय|षट्पदप्रियः
षट्पदप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Nagesara, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>षट्पद a bee, and प्रिय beloved by; equally applicable therefore to the lotus, jasmine, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदातिथि|षट्पदातिथिः
षट्पदातिथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>2 The Champaka.<BR>E.<BR>षट्पद a bee, अतिथि a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्प्रज्ञ|षट्प्रज्ञः
षट्प्रज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A sage, one acquainted with the four objects of human existence, or virtue, wealth, desire, and final happiness, and with the nature of the world, and of divine truth.<BR>2 A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and प्रज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडक्षीण|षडक्षीणः
षडक्षीण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and अक्षि the eye, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्ग|षडङ्गं|षडङ्गः
षडङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Having six limbs or members.<BR>2 Having six parts, six ingredients, &c.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Six parts of the body collectively; as the two arms, two legs, and the head, and waist.<BR>2 The six supplementary parts of the Vedas, or grammar, prosody, astronomy, pronunciation, the meaning of unusual terms, and the ritual of the Hindu religion.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्गजित्
षडङ्गजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>षडङ्ग the six members, and जित् who subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्गपानीय
षडङ्गपानीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A infusion or decoction of six drugs.<BR>E.<BR>षडङ्ग, and पानीय drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्घ्रि|षडंघ्रि|षडङ्घ्रिः
षडङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and अङ्घ्रि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडभिज्ञ|षडभिज्ञः
षडभिज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञ)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, (branches of learning or piety,) and अभिज्ञ understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडानन|षडाननः
षडानन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and आनन a face; having six faces, four directed to the four cardinal points, and two to the zenith and nadir, according to some accounts, though not generally so represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडूषण|षडूषणं
षडूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Six spices collectively, or long-pepper, black-pepper, dried ginger, the root of long-pepper, the fruit of the plumbago, and of the Piper chavya.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and ऊषण a spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडृतु|षडृतुः
षडृतु<BR>m. plur. (-तवः)<BR>The six seasons; also personified as divinities.<BR>E.<BR>षष्, and ऋतु a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=869" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षङ्गव
षङ्गव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A yoke of six oxen, or six oxen collectively.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and गो an ox, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुण
षड्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Six-fold, six times.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An assemblage of six qualities or properties.<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>The six acts of a king, in his military character, or peace, war, marching, halting, sowing dissension, seeking protection.<BR>E.<BR>षष्, and गुण a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थ|षड्ग्रन्थः
षड्ग्रन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>A variety of the Cæsalpinia bonducella.<BR>f. (-न्था)<BR>Orris root, (Acorus calamus.)<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थिका|षड्ग्रंथिका
षड्ग्रन्थिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>E.<BR>षड्ग्रन्थ as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ज|षड्जः
षड्ज<BR>m. (-ड्जः)<BR>The fourth note of the Hindu gamut.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and ज born: supposed to require for its articulation the employment of the tongue, teeth, palate, nose, throat, and chest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्धा
षड्धा<BR>ind.<BR>In six ways.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भाग|षड्भागः
षड्भाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A sixth, a sixth part.<BR>E.<BR>षष्, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भागभाज्
षड्भागभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Entitled to a sixth.<BR>E.<BR>षड्भाग, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भुज|षड्भुजः
षड्भुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Six-armed, six-sided.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A hexagon.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The water-melon.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, भुज an arm or branch, &c., aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रेखा
षड्रेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A water-melon.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्वर्ग|षड्वर्गः
षड्वर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A class or aggregate of six, as of six defects, desire, wrath, covetousness, bewilderment, pride, and envy.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्वर्गवश्य
षड्वर्गवश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Subject to the six vices.<BR>E.<BR>षड्वर्ग, and वश्य to be subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विध|षड्विधं
षड्विध<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-धं)<BR>In six ways, of six kinds.<BR>E.<BR>षष्, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विन्दु
षड्विन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and विन्दु a drop or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण
षण<BR>(उ) षणु r. 8th cl. (सनोति सनुते)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To serve or honor; also written षन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ड|षंड|षंडः|षण्डः
षण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A bull at liberty.<BR>2 A eunuch.<BR>3 A multitude, a heap.<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>A quantity of lotuses.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give, ड Uṇādi aff.; also शण्ड, षण्ढ, and शण्ड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्डाली|षंडाली
षण्डाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A measure of oil, the vessel holding a Chitank.<BR>2 A wanton woman.<BR>3 A pond, a pool.<BR>E.<BR>षण्ड a bull, a eunuch, &c., and अल to be able, affs. अच् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ढ|षंढ|षंढः|षण्ढः
षण्ढ<BR>m. (-ण्ढः)<BR>A eunuch: see षण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मास|षण्मासः
षण्मास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A half year, six months.<BR>E.<BR>षष्, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मास्य|षण्मास्यः
षण्मास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Six months old, of six months standing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षण्मास, and यत् aff.; also षाण्मास्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मुख|षण्मुखः
षण्मुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षत्वणत्व
षत्वणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The substitution of the letters ष or ण for स, and न in grammatical derivatives.<BR>E.<BR>ष and ण the letters, with the abstract affix attached to each respectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षद
षद<BR>(औ ॡ) औषदॢ^1 r. 1st and 6th cls. (सीदति)<BR>1 To wither, to wane, to perish gradually.<BR>2 To be low-spirited, to despond, to be weary or distressed, to lack energy.<BR>3 To break or destroy.<BR>4 To go or move.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>आषदॢ r. 1st and 10th cls. (आसादति आसादयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To assail, to encounter.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>1 To be exhausted or languid.<BR>2 To finish.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To obtain, to attain, to reach or arrive at.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To ascend.<BR>2 To destroy.<BR>With उप,<BR>To approach.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To sit in or on.<BR>2 To stand.<BR>3 To protect.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To be propitious to, to favour or be pleased with.<BR>2 To please or propitiate.<BR>3 To purify.<BR>4 To smile.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be languid or sorrowful.<BR>With सम्,<BR>1 To attain.<BR>2 To be in company or society with.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321. note: Devanagari 'w' and 'd' difficult to distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षध
षध<BR>r. 5th cl. (षध्नोति)<BR>To wish to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षन
षन<BR>(उ) षनु r. 8th cl. (सनोति सनुते)<BR>To give; also षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षप
षप<BR>r. 1st cl. (सपति)<BR>1 To be connected.<BR>2 To understand thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षम
षम<BR>r. 1st cl. (समति)<BR>1 To be unconfused.<BR>2 To be confused.<BR>r. 10th cl. (समयति)<BR>To perplex or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षम्ब
षम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (सम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (सम्बयति)<BR>To unite, to join, to collect or assemble together; also read सम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्ज्ज|षर्ज
षर्ज्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (सर्ज्जति)<BR>To earn, to acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्ध
षर्ध<BR>r. 1st cl. (सर्द्धति)<BR>1 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्व|षर्व्व
षर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (सर्वति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To injure, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्षपी
षर्षपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A small bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षल
षल<BR>r. 1st cl. (सलति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्
षष्<BR>mfn. plu. only (षट् or षड्)<BR>Six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टि|षष्टिः
षष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्ठिः)<BR>Sixty.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, डटि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक|षष्टिकः
षष्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Bought with sixty.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A kind of rice of quick growth.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, (days,) ठन् aff. or षष्ठि sixty, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक्य|षष्टिक्यं
षष्टिक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Fit for rice of quick growth, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>षष्टिक, and यन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टितम|षष्टितमः
षष्टितम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Sixtieth.<BR>E.<BR>षष्टि sixty, and तमट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिधा
षष्टिधा<BR>ind.<BR>In sixty ways.<BR>E.<BR>षष्टि sixty, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठ|षष्ठः
षष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Sixth.<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1 DURGĀ.<BR>2 The sixth day of the lunar fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, डटि aff., and थुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठक|षष्ठकः
षष्ठक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sixth.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्न
षष्ठान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>A sixth meal, i. e. one in three days.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठ, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नकाल
षष्ठान्नकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The taking of food once in three days, as an act of penance.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठान्न, and काल time; also with कन् added, षष्ठान्नकालकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नकालता
षष्ठान्नकालता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Eating once in three days, on the evening of the third day.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठान्नकाल, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठिन्
षष्ठिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>Being or having the sixth (year, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठ, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठिमत्त
षष्ठिमत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठि sixth, (year,) and मत्त furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठिहायन
षष्ठिहायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A kind of rice.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठि sixth, हायन a year: then full grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस
षस<BR>r. 2nd cl. (सस्ति)<BR>To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस्ज
षस्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (सज्जति)<BR>To move, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस्ति
षस्ति<BR>r. 2nd cl. (सस्ति)<BR>To sleep, (this is not universally considered to be a root.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षह
षह<BR>r. 1st cl. (सहते) r. 4th cl. (सह्यति) 1st and 10th cls. (सहति साहयति.)<BR>1 To bear, to endure, to suffer or support, to forbear, to have patience.<BR>2 To be content or satisfied.<BR>3 To be able.<BR>With उत् prefixed,<BR>1 To make effort or exertion, to persevere, to energize.<BR>2 To be happy or delighted.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To be violent.<BR>With वि,<BR>To determine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=870" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्
षाट्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्कौशिक
षाट्कौशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Enveloped in six sheathes.<BR>E.<BR>षट्, and कोश a sheath, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडव|षाडवः
षाडव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Sentiment, passion.<BR>2 Singing, music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्य|षाड्गुण्यं
षाड्गुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 An aggregate of six properties or qualities.<BR>2 The six acts of royal military policy.<BR>3 Increase or multiplication, six-fold.<BR>E.<BR>षङ्गुण, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मातुर|षाण्मातुरः
षाण्मातुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and मातृ a mother, अण् aff.; having been brought up by the six Kṛttikās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मासिक
षाण्मासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or relating to six months, half yearly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षण्मास, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षात्वणत्विक|षात्वणत्विकः
षात्वणत्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relative to the substitution of ष or ण for स and न, (as a rule, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>ठक् added to षत्वणत्व as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाध
षाध<BR>(उ) साधु r. 4th cl. (साध्यति)<BR>1 To effect, to accomplish or complete.<BR>2 To succeed; also साध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षान्त्व
षान्त्व<BR>r. 10th cl. (सान्त्वयति)<BR>To console, to comfort; also सान्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाष्ठ|षाष्ठः
षाष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Sixth.<BR>E.<BR>षष्ठ the same, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षि
षि<BR>(ञ्) षिञ् r. 5th cl. (सिनोति सिनुते) r. 9th cl. (सिनातिसिनीते)<BR>To tie, to bind.<BR>With अधि and अव prefixed,<BR>To accomplish.<BR>With वि and अव,<BR>To transact as business.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be an object or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिच
षिच<BR>(औ) षिचा r. 6th cl. (सिञ्चति-ते)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>1 To anoint, to initiate.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिट
षिट<BR>r. 1st cl. (सिटति)<BR>To disregard, to contemn, to despise, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिड्ग|षिड्गः
षिड्ग<BR>m. (-ड्गः)<BR>1 A catamite.<BR>2 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>3 A gallant.<BR>E.<BR>षिट to despise, Uṇādi aff. गन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिध
षिध<BR>r. 1st cl. (सेधति)<BR>To go.<BR>(ऊ) षिधू r. 1st cl. (सेधति)<BR>1 To command, to order.<BR>2 To ordain, especially with respect to holy observances.<BR>2 To do an auspicious act. or one indicating good fortune.<BR>(उ) षिध r. 4th cl. (सिध्यति)<BR>1 To succeed, to effect fully or completely.<BR>2 To complete a series of mystical observances by which supernatural powers are attained, to be an adept, to be initiated.<BR>2 To be perfect, to be finished or accomplished.<BR>4 To be right or correct^1.<BR>With नि or प्रति prefixed,<BR>(निषेधति प्रतिषेधति)<BR>To prevent, to prohibit.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To be celebrated or notorious.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिभ
षिभ<BR>(उ) षिभु r. 1st cl. (सेभति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिम्भ
षिम्भ<BR>(उ) षिम्भु r. 1st cl. (सिम्भति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिल
षिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (सिलति)<BR>To glean: more usually सिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिव
षिव<BR>(उ) षिवु r. 4th cl. (सीव्यति)<BR>1 To sew, to stitch.<BR>3 To sow, as seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षु|षुः
षु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (सौति)<BR>1 To bear, to bring forth.<BR>2 To possess power or supremacy.<BR>(ञ) षुञ् r. 5th cl. (सुनोति सुनुते)<BR>1 To bathe, preparatory to a sacrifice.<BR>2 To distil, to extract a spirit.<BR>3 To churn, to stir or agitate.<BR>4 To pain.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To sprinkle.<BR>2 To bathe.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To bear or bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुट्ट
षुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (सुट्टयति)<BR>1 To disregard, to despise.<BR>2 To be small or shallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुभ
षुभ<BR>r. 1st cl. (सोभति) r. 6th cl. (सुभति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>3 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुम्भ
षुम्भ<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (सुम्भति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>3 To be beautiful.<BR>4 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुर
षुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (सुरति)<BR>1 To possess supreme or superhuman power.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुह
षुह<BR>r. 4th cl. (सुह्यति)<BR>1 To bear, to endure.<BR>2 To be content or satisfied.<BR>3 To be able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षू
षू<BR>(ङ) षूङ् r. 2nd cl. (सूते) r. 4th cl. (सूयते)<BR>1 To bear a child, to bring forth.<BR>2 To produce in general.<BR>r. 6th cl. (सुवति)<BR>To direct, to send, to throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षू
षू<BR>f. (-षूः)<BR>Birth, delivery, child-bearing.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, aff. क्विप्, and the consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूद
षूद<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूदते) r. 10th cl. (सूदयति)<BR>1 To leak, to drop, to flow, to distil.<BR>2 To deposit, to place.<BR>3 To hurt, to wound, to kill or attempt to kill.<BR>4 To promise.<BR>5 (In the causal form,) To hallow, to make holy or pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर
षूर<BR>(ई) षूरी r. 4th cl. (सूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To be stopped or fixed.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर्क्ष
षूर्क्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्षति)<BR>1 To respect, to regard, to treat with reverence or respect.<BR>2 To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर्क्ष्य
षूर्क्ष्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्ष्यति)<BR>1 To envy, to be impatient of another's rise.<BR>2 To be intolerant or impatient of another's faults.<BR>3 To disregard or contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूष
षूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूषति)<BR>To bring forth, to bear; also सूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षृभ
षृभ<BR>(उ) षृभु r. 1st cl. (सर्भति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षृम्भ
षृम्भ<BR>(उ) षृम्भु r. 1st cl. (सृम्भति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेक
षेक<BR>(ऋ) षेकृ r. 1st cl. (सेकते)<BR>To go, to move; preferably सेक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेल
षेल<BR>(ऌ) षेलृ r. 1st cl. (सेलति)<BR>To go, to move; also शेल, and सेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेव
षेव<BR>(ऋ) षेवृ r. 1st cl. (सेवति-ते)<BR>1 To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>2 To rely or depend on.<BR>3 To worship.<BR>4 To follow, to practise, to be addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षै
षै<BR>r. 1st cl. (सायति)<BR>To waste, to wane or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षो
षो<BR>r. 4th cl. (स्यति)<BR>1 To destroy, to put an end to.<BR>2 To be destroyed, to perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडत्|षोडन्त्
षोडत्<BR>m. (-डन्)<BR>A young ox, or one with six teeth.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडश|षोडशः
षोडश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Sixteenth.<BR>E.<BR>शोडशन् sixteen, डट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशक
षोडशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sixteen, (collectively.)<BR>E.<BR>शोडश, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशन्
षोडशन्<BR>mfn. plu. only. (-श)<BR>Sixteen.<BR>E.<BR>षष् six, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशर्त्तुनिशा|षोडशर्तुनिशा
षोडशर्त्तुनिशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Any one of sixteen nights from the commencement of menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>शोडश, and ऋतु menses, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशांश
षोडशांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A sixteenth.<BR>E.<BR>शोडश, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशांशु|षोडशांशुः
षोडशांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The planet VENUS.<BR>E.<BR>शोडश sixteen, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशाङ्घ्रि|षोडशांघ्रि|षोडशाङ्घ्रिः
षोडशाङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>षोडश sixteen, and अङ्घ्रि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशार्च्चिस्|षोडशार्चिस्
षोडशार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>The planet VENUS.<BR>E.<BR>षोडश sixteen, and अर्च्चिस् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडषावर्त्त
षोडषावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A conch shell.<BR>E.<BR>षोडश sixteen, and आवर्त्त a twist or spire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडा
षोडा<BR>ind.<BR>In six ways.<BR>E.<BR>षष six, उ substituted for the final, धा aff., and ध changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टक
ष्टक<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्तकति)<BR>To resist or oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टग
ष्टग<BR>(ए) ष्टगे r. 1st cl. (स्तगति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=871" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टन
ष्टन<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्तनति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टभ
ष्टभ<BR>(इ) ष्टभि r. 1st cl. (स्तम्भते)<BR>1 To stop or hinder, to oppose, to impede, to resist or prevent.<BR>2 To be stupid or dull, to be inanimate or insensible.<BR>3 To be fixed as a post.<BR>4 To be astounded or stupefied.<BR>5 To be paralysed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टम
ष्टम<BR>r. 1st. cl. (स्तमति)<BR>1 To be confused.<BR>2 To be clear or unconfused.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तमयति)<BR>To confuse or annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिघ
ष्टिघ<BR>r. 5th cl. (स्तिघ्नुते)<BR>To assail, to assault, to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिप
ष्टिप<BR>(ऋ) ष्टिपृ r. 1st cl. (स्तेपते)<BR>1 To ooze, to drop, to distil.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिम
ष्टिम<BR>r. 4th cl. (स्तिम्यति)<BR>To be wet or moist, to reek, to steam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टीम
ष्टीम<BR>r. 4th cl. (स्तीम्यति)<BR>To be wet or moist, to reek, to steam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टु
ष्टु<BR>(ञ) ष्टुञ् r. 2nd cl. (स्तौति or स्तुते स्तवीति or स्तवीते)<BR>1 To praise, to eulogise.<BR>2 To hymn, to worship with praises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुच
ष्टुच<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्तोचते)<BR>To be clear, to be bright, to be pellucid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुप
ष्टुप<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तोपयति)<BR>To heap up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुभ
ष्टुभ<BR>(उ) ष्टुभु r. 1st cl. (स्तोभति)<BR>1 To stop, to hinder.<BR>2 To be stupid or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टूप
ष्टूप<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तूपयति)<BR>To heap together, to pile up, to collect into a heap; also स्तूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टृक्ष
ष्टृक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्तृक्षति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टृह
ष्टृह<BR>(उ) ष्टृहु r. 6th cl. (ष्टृहति)<BR>To hurt or kill; also स्तृह, and ष्टृह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टॄह
ष्टॄह<BR>(ऊ) ष्टॄहू r. 6th cl. (स्तृहति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टेप
ष्टेप<BR>(ऋ) ष्टेपृ r. 1st cl. (स्तेपते)<BR>1 To leak, to flow, to distil or drop.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टै
ष्टै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्तायति)<BR>To surround, to encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ट्युम|ष्ट्युमः
ष्ट्युम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ट्यै
ष्ट्यै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्त्यायति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To crowd or swarm.<BR>3 To envelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठग
ष्ठग<BR>(ए) ष्ठगे r. 1st cl. (स्थगति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठल
ष्ठल<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्थलति)<BR>1 To stand.<BR>2 To be firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठस
ष्ठस<BR>(उ) ष्ठसु r. 4th cl. (स्थस्यति)<BR>To dwell in, to inhabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठा
ष्ठा<BR>r. 1st cl. (तिष्ठति)<BR>1 To stand, to stop, to be still, to refrain from moving.<BR>2 To abide, to stay, to be.<BR>(तिष्ठते)<BR>1 To apply or refer to, as an umpire or judge.<BR>2 To indicate or reveal one's thoughts to another.<BR>With अधि prefixed,<BR>(अधितिष्ठति)<BR>1 To excel, to surpass, to overcome.<BR>2 To sit or stand upon or over.<BR>3 To be placed or preside over.<BR>With अनु<BR>(अनुतिष्ठति)<BR>1 To practise as a duty, to obey or follow as a law.<BR>2 To apply or adhere to.<BR>With अव<BR>(अवतिष्ठति-ते)<BR>1 To stay or stand.<BR>2 To attend upon.<BR>With आङ्<BR>(आतिष्ठते)<BR>1 To affirm or assert.<BR>2 To apply;<BR>(आतिष्ठति)<BR>1 To ascend, to mount.<BR>2 To promise or engage.<BR>With उत्<BR>(उत्तिष्ठते)<BR>1 To seek for, to endeavour to obtain;<BR>(उत्तिष्ठति)<BR>To get up, to rise as from a seat, &c.<BR>With उप<BR>(उपतिष्ठति-ते)<BR>1 To propitiate (as a deity.)<BR>2 To praise or hymn, to worship, to adore.<BR>3 To embrace.<BR>4 To treat in a friendly manner, to form a friendship or connexion with.<BR>5 To pass or lie along or near to, that is, as a path or road.<BR>6 To arrive at or near;<BR>(उपतिष्ठते)<BR>To hope to gain or acquire.<BR>With नि<BR>(नितिष्ठते)<BR>To be established.<BR>With परि and अव<BR>(पर्य्यवतिष्ठते)<BR>To be stationary or immovable.<BR>With प्र<BR>(प्रतिष्ठते)<BR>1 To set off, to go forth, to depart.<BR>2 To go to.<BR>With प्र and उत्<BR>(प्रोत्तिष्ठति)<BR>To get up, to rise.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>(प्रतितिष्ठति)<BR>To be erected for holy purposes, to be sacred or consecrated.<BR>With वि<BR>(वितिष्ठते)<BR>1 To stand apart, to be separated.<BR>2 To stay or be.<BR>With वि and अव<BR>(व्यवतिष्ठते)<BR>To decree, to pronounce.<BR>With सम्<BR>(सन्तिष्ठते)<BR>1 To be well.<BR>2 To be close to or together.<BR>3 To be of the same inclinations or opinions, to conform, to agree.<BR>4 To be completed or finished.<BR>With सम and आङ्<BR>(समातिष्ठते)<BR>To perform, to be engaged in.<BR>With सम and उत्<BR>(समुत्तिष्ठति)<BR>To rise or get up.<BR>With सम and प्र,<BR>To go forth or on a journey.<BR>With प्र in the causal<BR>(प्रस्थापयति)<BR>To send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठिव
ष्ठिव<BR>(उ) ष्ठिवु r. 1st cl. (ष्ठीवति) r. 4th cl. (ष्ठीव्यति)<BR>To eject from the mouth, to spit, to sputter, (the radical sibilant is unchanged in this root); also ष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीव
ष्ठीव<BR>(उ) ष्ठीवु r. 1st cl. (ष्ठीवति)<BR>To spit or eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवन|ष्ठीवनं
ष्ठीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Spitting, ejecting saliva.<BR>2 Saliva, spittle.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठीव, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवित्वा
ष्ठीवित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having spitten.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठीव to spit, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठ्युत
ष्ठ्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ejected as saliva, spit.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठीव to spit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णस
ष्णस<BR>(उ) ष्णसु r. 4th cl. (स्नस्यति)<BR>To eject from the mouth, to spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णा
ष्णा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (स्नाति)<BR>To bathe, to purify by ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णिह
ष्णिह<BR>(ऌ ऊ) r. 4th cl. (स्निह्यति)<BR>To bear affection to, love, to regard, to be kind to or pleased with.<BR>r. 10th. cl. (स्नेहयति)<BR>To be unctuous, to be bland or greasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णु
ष्णु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ष्णौति)<BR>To distil, to drop, to ooze or leak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुच
ष्णुच<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्नोचते)<BR>To be clear or pellucid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुस
ष्णुस<BR>(उ) ष्णुसु r. 4th cl. (स्नुस्यति)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To take.<BR>3 To disappear.<BR>4 To eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुह
ष्णुह<BR>(ऌ ऊ) r. 4th cl. (स्नुह्यति)<BR>To be sick, to retch, to throw up, to vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णै
ष्णै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्नायति)<BR>To surround, to encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्मि
ष्मि<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्मयते)<BR>To smile.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्नाययते)<BR>To disrespect:<BR>with वि prefixed,<BR>to surprise or astonish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वक्क
ष्वक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (ष्वक्कते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वञ्ज
ष्वञ्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वजते)<BR>To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वद
ष्वद<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वदते) r. 10th cl. (स्वादयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To be pleasing.<BR>3 To cover; also स्वाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वप
ष्वप<BR>(ञि औ) ञिष्वपौ r. 2nd cl. (स्वपिति)<BR>To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वर्त्त
ष्वर्त्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (ष्वर्त्तयति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To be wretched or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वष्क
ष्वष्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (ष्वष्कते)<BR>To go, to move: the radical sibilant is unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्विद
ष्विद<BR>(ञि आ) ञिष्विदा r. 1st cl. (स्वेदते) r. 4th cl. (स्विद्यति)<BR>1 To perspire, to sweat.<BR>2 To be greasy or unctuous.<BR>3 To be fascinated, to be tempted or deluded.<BR>4 To quit, to yield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स<BR>The thirty-second consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, corresponding to S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स<BR>m. (सः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>5 The abbreviated name of the musical note ष ज्.<BR>6 He, the nominative case masc. of तद the third personal pronoun: before many letters the Visarga is rejected.<BR>f. (सा)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 She, the nominative case fem. of तट्.<BR>n. (सं)<BR>1 Knowledge. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">Page873</a>]<BR>2 Meditation.<BR>3 A carriage road.<BR>4 A fence.<BR>ind.<BR>(In composition,) With, together with; being substituted for सम् or सह; combined with nouns it forms adjectives and adverbs; as सकोपः angry, सकोपम् angrily; सगर्ब्बः proud, सगर्व्वम् haughtily; सविनयः modest, well behaved, सविनयम् respectfully; ससम्भ्रमः flurried, ससम्भ्रमम् flurriedly, &c. सानन्दः joyful,सानन्दं joyfully.<BR>E.<BR>षो to go, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=872" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सं|स|सः
सं<BR>ind.<BR>(In composition,) With, together with, &c.; being the optional form of writing सम् before a consonant: before consonants of the first five classes, the Anusvāra may be again changed to the nasal of the class to which the letter it precedes belongs, as सं for सम्, and कल्प make सङ्कल्प, &c.: before the semivowels, the sibilants, and ह, it preferably remains unaltered; practice however is very arbitrary in this respect, and the change is expressed or not, in all manuscripts according to the pleasure of the writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संय|संयः
संय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The skeleton.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, यस to restrain, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्|संयन्त्
संयत्<BR>mf. (-यत्)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत|संयतः
संयत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Checked, restrained, controuled, suppressed.<BR>2 Bound, confined, fettered, imprisoned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयतात्मन्
संयतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Self-subdued, of well regulated spirit.<BR>E.<BR>संयत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयतेन्द्रिय
संयतेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of subdued or controuled passions and desires.<BR>E.<BR>संयत, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयद्वर|संयद्वरः
संयद्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, ष्वरच् Uṇādi aff.; or संयत् war, वर chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयन्तृ|संयंतृ
संयन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Constraining, a constrainer.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयम|संयमः
संयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Restraint, forbearance.<BR>2 Humanity, avoiding the infliction of pain on others.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमत्
संयमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>Curbing, restraining, subduing, who or what does so.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमन|संयमनं|संयमनः
संयमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Restraining, checking.<BR>2 Forbearance, self-denial or controul.<BR>3 Binding, confinement.<BR>4 Holding, detaining.<BR>5 A religious vow or obligation.<BR>6 A cluster of four houses.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The capital of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying completeness, or entirely, and यम to restrain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमित|संयमितः
संयमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Checked, controuled, restrained.<BR>2 Bound, confined, held, detained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to check, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमिन्
संयमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Who or what checks, restrains, curbs, &c.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A saint, a sage, one who subdues or controuls his passions.<BR>E.<BR>संयम restraint, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयात्रा
संयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>Travelling into another island or continent, voyaging, travelling by water.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before या to go, त्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयान|संयानं|संयानः
संयान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A mould.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Accompanying, going together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, या to go or get, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाम|संयामः
संयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Forbearance, check, controul, restraint.<BR>2 Humanity, abstaining from giving pain to others.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यम to restrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयामवत्|संयामवन्त्
संयामवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Forbearing.<BR>E.<BR>संयाम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाव|संयावः
संयाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A sort of roll, or a thin cake of unleavened bread, fried with Ghee, pounded and again made up into an oblong form with fresh bread, sugar, and spices, and again fried with Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, यु to mix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुक्त|संयुक्तः
संयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Joined with, connected, attached.<BR>2 Mixed, blended.<BR>3 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>4 Accompanied or attended by.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, युज to join, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुग|संयुगः
संयुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Union, mixture.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before युज to join, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुज्
संयुज्<BR>mfn. (-युक्)<BR>1 Possessed of or endowed with good qualities.<BR>2 Connected or associated with.<BR>3 Joined, united.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before युज to join, aff. क्विप्, and the consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुत|संयुतः
संयुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Connected, joined, mixed, blended, attached to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, यु to join, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुयूषु
संयुयूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to mix, join, unite, to bring together in any way.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before यु to join, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोग|संयोगः
संयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Intimate union or association.<BR>2 Living with, being in company with.<BR>3 Adherence, junction.<BR>4 (In grammar,) A conjunct consonant.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before युज to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोगित|संयोगितः
संयोगित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Joined, annexed, connected.<BR>E.<BR>संयोग union, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजन|संयोजनं
संयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Copulation, coition.<BR>2 Joining, uniting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, युज to join, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजित|संयोजितः
संयोजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Joined, attached, annexed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, युज to join, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्त
संरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Inflamed, angry.<BR>2 Empassioned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रञ्ज to be affected, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्ष|संरक्षः
संरक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Care, preservation, protection.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and रक्ष preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षण|संरक्षणं
संरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking care of, protecting, preserving.<BR>E.<BR>मम् before रक्ष to preserve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षित
संरक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken care of, preserved, protected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रक्ष to preserve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्ष्य
संरक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Fit, proper, or necessary to be taken care of, guarded, preserved, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रक्ष to preserve, यत् aff.; also संरक्षणीय and संरक्षितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरब्ध
संरब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Incensed, angry.<BR>2 Agitated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रभि to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भ|संरंभ|संरंभः|संरम्भः
संरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Wrath, rage.<BR>2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>3 Flurry, agitation.<BR>4 Swelling with heat and redness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रभि to sound, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भपरुष
संरम्भपरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Exceedingly harsh, rough, or scurrilous.<BR>E.<BR>संरम्भ, and परुष harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भरस
संरम्भरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Angry, resentful.<BR>E.<BR>संरम्भ, and रस taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भित्व
संरम्भित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Wrath.<BR>2 Pride.<BR>3 Agitation.<BR>E.<BR>संरम्भिन्, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, संरम्भिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भिन्|संरंभिन्
संरम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>1 Proud.<BR>2 Angry.<BR>3 Flurried.<BR>E.<BR>संरम्भ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराग|संरागः
संराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Anger.<BR>2 Affection.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, रञ्ज to be affected, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधन|संराधनं
संराधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Propitiating, pleasing by worship.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before राध to accomplish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=873" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधित
संराधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Propitiated, pleased.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before राध to accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराव|संरावः
संराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रु to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराविन्
संराविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Roaring, shouting, making a noise or uproar.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रु to sound, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुद्ध
संरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Checked, stopped, impeded, curbed, opposed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रुध to obstruct, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरूढ|संरूढः
संरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Confident, audacious, presuming.<BR>2 Budded, blossomed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रुह to grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरोध|संरोधः
संरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Hindering, stopping, opposing, preventing.<BR>2 Impediment, obstruction.<BR>3 Bond, fetter.<BR>4 Curb, check.<BR>5 Throwing, sending.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before रुध to obstruct, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्षण|संलक्षणं
संलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Distinguishing, characterising.<BR>E.<BR>सं before लक्ष to mark, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्षित
संलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Marked, distinguished.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before लक्ष to mark, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्ष्य
संलक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>To be marked with or by.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before लक्ष to mark, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलग्न|संलग्नः
संलग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Joined, united, adherent.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and लग्न attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलज्जमान
संलज्जमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before लस्ज to be ashamed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलय|संलयः
संलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sleep, sleepiness.<BR>E.<BR>सं before ली to join, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलाप|संलापः
संलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Conversation, discourse.<BR>2 In the drama, high discourse, dialogue of profound or occult meaning.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together with, and लप to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापक|संलापकः
संलापक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A species of minor drama, a controversial drama.<BR>E.<BR>संलाप, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापित
संलापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Discoursing, conversing.<BR>E.<BR>संलाप, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापिन्
संलापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Discoursing, who or what discourses.<BR>E.<BR>संलाप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवंहयत्
संवंहयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Increasing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, वहि to grow, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्सर|संवत्सरः
संवत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, completely, and वत्सर a year; or सम् with वस to abide, सर Uṇādi aff., and त substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवद्
संवद्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A year.<BR>2 A year of VIKRAMĀDITYA'S era.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वद to speak, aff. विच्, or सम् before वय to go, क्विप् aff., य rejected, and तुक् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवदन|संवदनं
संवदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Communication of tidings or intelligence.<BR>2 Sight, seeing.<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Subduing by charms, overpowering any thing or person by magical compounds, or drugs, or mystical gems, &c.<BR>2 A charm, an amulet, the article by which the above is effected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with वद to speak, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवनन|संवननं
संवनन<BR>n. (-नं-ना)<BR>Subduing by magical drugs or charms: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वन to ask, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर|संवरं|संवरः
संवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Self-control.<BR>3 Covering, concealing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The name of a demon.<BR>2 Collection, comprehension.<BR>3 Contraction, compression.<BR>4 A mound, a bridge, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृ to choose, aff. अप्, more usually derived from शम्ब or षम्ब to collect, and then written शम्बर or सम्बर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्त|संवर्त|संवर्तः|संवर्त्तः
संवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Destruction of the universe.<BR>2 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>3 The name of a Muni.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 Being, becoming.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृत to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तक|संवर्तक|संवर्तकः|संवर्त्तकः
संवर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 BALADEVA.<BR>2 The plough of BALADEVA.<BR>3 Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृत to be or abide, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तकिन्|संवर्तकिन्
संवर्त्तकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>संवर्त्तक his plough, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्ति|संवर्ति|संवर्तिः|संवर्त्तिः
संवर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृत to be, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तिका|संवर्तिका
संवर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>सम् near, (the stalk,) वृत to be, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धक
संवर्द्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Augmenting, augmentative, prospering, an augmentor, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृद्ध to increase, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धन
संवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Augmenting, increasing.<BR>2 Prospering, thriving.<BR>3 Bringing up, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृद्ध to increase or prosper, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धित
संवर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished, protected, brought up, patronised, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृद्ध to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्म्मित|संवर्मित
संवर्म्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fully armed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and वर्म्म armour, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवलित|संवलितः
संवलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mixed, mingled.<BR>2 Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>3 Having, possessed of.<BR>4 United.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, वल to surround, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवसथ|संवसथः
संवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वस to abide, अथ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाटिका
संवाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवात्
संवात्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वाती-वान्ती-वात्)<BR>Blowing, breathing, (as wind.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वा to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाद|संवादः
संवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Communication of intelligence, information, news.<BR>2 Assent, concurrence.<BR>3 Conformity, correspondence, sameness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, वद to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवार|संवारः
संवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Contraction, diminution.<BR>2 Compression of the lips, &c. in pronunciation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृ to choose, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवास|संवासः
संवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 An open space, either within or without a town, for the meeting and diversion of the townsmen.<BR>3 Company, society.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, वास an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाह|संवाहः
संवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An attendant employed to rub and knead the body.<BR>2 Rubbing the body.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वाह to exert one's self, and अच् aff.; or when the action is implied, वह to obtain or bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहक|संवाहकः
संवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An attendant rubbing and kneading the limbs.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to obtain, (pleasure or ease,) causal form, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहन|संवाहनं
संवाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing the person, kneading the limbs.<BR>2 Bearing, carrying.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to obtain or bear, (causal form,) aff. ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहित
संवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rubbed, kneaded, (as the limbs.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to bear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाह्य
संवाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be rubbed or kneaded.<BR>2 To be borne.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to bear, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविग्न
संविग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Agitated, flurried, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before विज to fear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=874" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविग्नमानस
संविग्नमानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Distracted.<BR>E.<BR>संविग्न, and मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवित्ति|संवित्तिः
संवित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Understanding, intellect.<BR>2 Accommodation, reconciliation.<BR>3 Recognition, recollection of a thing or person previously known.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before विट् to know, aff. क्तिन्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्
संविद्<BR>f. (-वित् or विट्)<BR>1 Intellect, understanding.<BR>2 Promise, assent.<BR>3 Contract, engagement, agreement, covenant.<BR>4 Knowledge.<BR>5 A watch-word, a cry of battle.<BR>6 War, battle.<BR>7 Name, appellation.<BR>8 Sign, signal.<BR>9 Institute, prescribed custom or observation.<BR>10 Pleasing, delighting.<BR>11 Hemp.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together with, विद to know, &c., aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदित|संविदितः
संविदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed.<BR>2 Known, understood.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before विद to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्ध्यतिक्रम
संविद्ध्यतिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Non-performance of agreements.<BR>E.<BR>संविट्, and व्यतिकम departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधान|संविधानं
संविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Mode, rite.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, वि before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधानक|संविधानकं
संविधानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Strange or unusual occurrence.<BR>E.<BR>संविघान, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभक्त
संविभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Parted, divided.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and वि before भज to divide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभाग|संविभागः
संविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Part, portion, share.<BR>2 Distributing, apportioning.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and वि before भज to divide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविषा
संविषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, (Betula?)<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीक्षण|संवीक्षणं
संवीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Search, inquiry, looking for or after any thing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and वि intensitives, ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीत|संवीतं
संवीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, enclosed, encompassed.<BR>2 Covered, clothed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, व्येञ् to surround, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवुवूर्षु
संवुवूर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>Wishing to conceal, disguise, hide, cover, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृ to screen, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत|संवृतः
संवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered.<BR>2 Closed.<BR>3 Contracted, compressed, (as the lips, &c. in pronunciation.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वृ to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्त|संवृत्तः
संवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Covered, concealed, hidden.<BR>2 Furnished with, filled with, possessed of.<BR>3 Being, become.<BR>4 Past, gone.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>VARUṆA, deity of the ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, वृत to be, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्ति|संवृत्तिः
संवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Hiding, concealing.<BR>2 Covering.<BR>3 Possession, endowment.<BR>4 Secret purpose.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, वृत to screen or cover, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेग|संवेगः
संवेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Hurry, flurry, haste proceeding from fear, &c.<BR>2 Haste, speed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, विज to be agitated, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेद|संवेदः
संवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Perception, consciousness.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, with विद to know, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेश|संवेशः
संवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Sleep, sleeping.<BR>2 Dreaming, a dream.<BR>3 Copulation.<BR>4 A stool, a chair, a seat.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before विश to enter, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेशन|संवेशनं
संवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Copulation, coition.<BR>E.<BR>मस् before विश to enter, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यान|संव्यानं
संव्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An upper-garment.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes, vesture.<BR>3 Covering, a covering.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, व्येञ् to cover, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूढ
संव्यूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mixed, united.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and वि before ऊह to reason, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूह|संव्यूहः
संव्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Combination, mixture, union.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and वि before ऊह to reason, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशकला
संशकला<BR>aptote.<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशप्तक|संशप्तकः
संशप्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A picked man or soldier, one of a select band sworn never to recede, and stationed to prevent the flight of the rest, a brother in arms.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together, शप्त sworn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय|संशयः
संशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयस्थ
संशयस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Doubtful, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>संशय, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयात्मन्
संशयात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A sceptic.<BR>E.<BR>संशय, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयान|संशयानः
संशयान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dubious, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शीङ्^1 to sleep, शानच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयापन्न
संशयापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Affected with doubt, hesitating^1, dubious.<BR>2 Doubtful, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>संशय, and आपन्न having.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयापन्नमानस|संशयापन्नमानसः
संशयापन्नमानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Irresolute, dubious, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>संशय doubt, आपन्न affected, and मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयालु|संशयालुः
संशयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Dubious, doubting, sceptic.<BR>E.<BR>संशय doubt, आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयितृ
संशयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Dubious, sceptical, a sceptic.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शीङ्^1 to sleep, तृच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय्य
संशय्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having doubted or deliberated, being in doubt.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शी to sleep, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशरण|संशरणं
संशरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Commencement of a combat, charge, attack.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, शॄ to injure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशित|संशितं
संशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Certain, certified, ascertained, established.<BR>2 Completed, effected, finished.<BR>3 Completing, effecting, diligent and attentive in accomplishing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शो to destroy, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशितव्रत
संशितव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Faithful to a vow or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>संशित completing, व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिश्रीषु
संशिश्रीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to adhere to or depend upon, to serve, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before श्रि to serve, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्ध
संशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pure, purified.<BR>2 Clean.<BR>3 Refined.<BR>4 Discharged, acquitted, (as a debt.)<BR>5 Acquitted, (of a crime.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्धि|संशुद्धिः
संशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Cleaning the body.<BR>2 Purification in general.<BR>3 Correction.<BR>4 Acquittal of debt, &c.<BR>5 Acquittance of charge or crime.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, शुद्धि purification, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुष्क|संशुष्कं
संशुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Dry, dried.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधन|संशोधनं
संशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cleaning, cleansing, purifying the body by ablutions, &c.<BR>2 Correcting.<BR>3 Refining.<BR>4 Discharging, paying.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before शोधन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोध्य
संशोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 To be rectified or purified.<BR>2 To be paid or acquitted (as a debt, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्, शुध to be pure, यत् aff.; संशोधनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चत्
संश्चत्<BR>n. (-श्वत्)<BR>Deceit, trick, illusion, juggling.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चि to collect, Uṇādi aff. अति, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्यान|संश्यानः
संश्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Contracted, rolled up, gathered up, shrunk, collapsed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, श्यै to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रय|संश्रयः
संश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Protection, refuge, asylum.<BR>2 Seeking the alliance of a powerful prince, as a safety against actual or future enemies.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, श्रि to serve, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=875" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रव|संश्रवः
संश्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Promise, assent, agreement.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and श्रु to hear, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्राव
संश्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sprinkling, aspersion, pouring out.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, श्रु to ooze, causal v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रित|संश्रितः
संश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protected, supported.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A servant, a follower, a dependant.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before श्रि to serve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रुत|संश्रुतः
संश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Promised, agreed, assented.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before श्रु to hear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्ट|संश्लिष्टः
संश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Close together, adjoining, touching.<BR>2 Bound, united.<BR>3 Embraced.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before श्लिष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेष|संश्लेषः
संश्लेष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Embrace, embracing.<BR>2 Union, connection^1, junction, contact, association.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, श्लिष to unite, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्वत्
संश्वत्<BR>n. (-श्वत्)<BR>Fraud, trick, cheating, deception.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before श्वि to increase, aff. अति, deriv. irr.; also संश्वत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्त|संसक्तः
संसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Near, adjoining, contiguous.<BR>2 Possessing, endowed with, affected by.<BR>3 Connected or acquainted with.<BR>4 Attached to, intent on.<BR>5 Tied or attached.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before षञ्ज to embrace, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्तयुग
संसक्तयुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Harnessed, yoked.<BR>E.<BR>संसक्त, and युग a yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्ति|संसक्तिः
संसक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Proximity, contact.<BR>2 Union, junction.<BR>3 Acquaintance, intimacy, connection with.<BR>4 Devotion or addiction to.<BR>5 Tying, fastening.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before षञ्ज to embrace or adhere to, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसज्जमान
संसज्जमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Prepared, ready.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, षस्ज to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद्<BR>f. (-सट् or सत्)<BR>An assembly, a meeting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before षद to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरण|संसरणं
संसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going, proceeding in general.<BR>2 Going well or unobstructedly.<BR>3 The unresisted march of troops.<BR>4 The beginning of war or battle.<BR>5 A highway^1, the principal road through a village or town.<BR>6 The world.<BR>7 Birth, the production of living beings.<BR>8 A resting place for passengers near the gates of a city.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, &c., सृ to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ग|संसर्गः
संसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Union, proximity, approximation, contact.<BR>2 Acquaintance, familiarity, intercourse.<BR>2 Co-existence.<BR>4 Sensual attachment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, सृज to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गाभाव|संसर्गाभावः
संसर्गाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Logical nonexistence or annihilation; of three kinds, prior, incidental, and final, or absence of birth or production, destruction of present being, and necessary end or cessation of existence.<BR>E.<BR>संसर्ग union, and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गित्व
संसर्गित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Familiarity, fellowship.<BR>E.<BR>संसर्गिन्, and त्व added; also with तल्, संसर्गिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गिन्
संसर्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्गी-र्गिणी-र्गि)<BR>Familiar, friendly, keeping company, acquainted, an acquaintance.<BR>2 United or mixed with, in contact with, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृज to go, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ज्जन|संसर्जन|संसर्जनं
संसर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>2 Voiding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृज to quit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्प|संसर्पः
संसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>An equable or gentle motion, as the creeping of a snake, the gliding of a stream, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृप to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पिन्
संसर्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि)<BR>Flowing, gliding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive prefix, सृप to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसार|संसारः
संसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The world, the habitation of mortals.<BR>2 Mundane existence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, (mankind,) सृ to go, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारगुरु|संसारगुरुः
संसारगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>संसार the world, and गुरु the spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारमार्ग|संसारमार्गः
संसारमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>संसार the world, (or mankind,) and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारिन्
संसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Worldly, mundane.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An animal or sentient being.<BR>E.<BR>संसार the world, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्ध
संसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Perfected, fully done or accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सिद्ध effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्धि|संसिद्धिः
संसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Nature, disposition, the natural state or quality.<BR>2 Perfection, completion, accomplishment.<BR>3 A passionate or intoxicated woman.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिस्मयिषमाण
संसिस्मयिषमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Wishing or purposing to ridicule, laugh at, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्मि to smile, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिसृक्षु
संसिसृक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to unite.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृज to create, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचन|संसूचनं
संसूचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Telling, informing.<BR>2 Reproaching, scolding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before षूच to inform, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचित
संसूचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Informed, apprised, told.<BR>2 Reproved, scolded.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before षूच to inform, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृति|संसृतिः
संसृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 The world.<BR>2 Flow, stream, current.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and सृ to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्ट|संसृष्टः
संसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 United, joined, connected.<BR>2 Mixed.<BR>3 Reunited, rejoined.<BR>4 Connected as partners or coparceners.<BR>5 Clean dressed, clad in clean garments.<BR>6 Involved in.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृज to leave or make, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टत्व|संसृष्टत्वं
संसृष्टत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Union, association.<BR>2 Re-union.<BR>3 (In law,) The voluntary co-residence or re-union of father and son, or of brothers with each other, after partition of property.<BR>E.<BR>संसृष्ट associated, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टरूप
संसृष्टरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Mixed, adulterated.<BR>E.<BR>संसृष्ट, and रूप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टि|संसृष्टिः
संसृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Uniting, combining.<BR>2 Collecting, assembling.<BR>3 Living together in one family.<BR>4 (In rhetoric,) The use of a number of figures in one passage.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सृज to make, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टिन्
संसृष्टिन्<BR>m. (-ष्टी)<BR>A coparcener, a brother, whether of whole or half blood, who after the partition of the family property continues or returns to reside with his father, his paternal uncle, or his other brothers.<BR>E.<BR>संसृष्ट united or re-united, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवन
संसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Waiting on, serving.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सेव to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवित
संसेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Waited on, served, attended.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before सेव to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कर्त्तृ|संस्कर्तृ
संस्कर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्ती-र्त्तृ)<BR>Who or what polishes, completes, initiates, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृ to make, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कार|संस्कारः
संस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Completing, accomplishing, finishing, perfecting.<BR>2 Apprehension, conception.<BR>3 The power of memory, the faculty of recollection.<BR>4 Faculty in general, one of the twenty-four qualities enumerated by logicians.<BR>5 An essential [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">Page877</a>] and purificatory rite or ceremony amongst the Hindus; as those of the three first classes, commencing with conception and ending with marriage; or गर्भाघानं sacrifice on conception; पुंसवनं on vitality in the fœtus; सीमन्तोन्नयनं in the fourth, sixth, or eighth month; जातकर्म्म giving the infant clarified butter out of a golden spoon to taste, before dividing the navel string; नामकरणं naming the child on the tenth, eleventh, twelfth, or hundred and first day: निःक्रमणं carrying him out to see the moon on the third lunar day of the third light fortnight, or to see the sun in the third or fourth month; अन्नप्राशनं feeding him with rice in the sixth or eighth month, or when he has cut teeth: चूडाकार्य्यं tonsure in the second or third year: उपनयनं investiture with the string in the fifth, eighth, or sixteenth year: विवाहः or marriage is the tenth and last Saṃskāra.<BR>5 Embellishment, decoration, elegance.<BR>6 Purity, perfection.<BR>7 Preparing as an article of medicine or food, cooking, dressing, compounding, &c.<BR>8 Purification, consecration.<BR>9 Impression, form, mould.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying perfection, कृ to make, अण् aff. and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=876" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारज|संस्कारजं|संस्कारजः
संस्कारज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced from a purificatory ceremony, &c.<BR>E.<BR>संस्कार as above, with the power of the fifth case, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारवर्जित|संस्कारवर्ज्जितः
संस्कारवर्जित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Brahman, &c. who has not received the usual initiatory ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>संस्कार purificatory rite, and वर्जित deprived of; also संस्काररहित, संस्कारहीन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारहीन|संस्कारहीनः
संस्कारहीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A man of the three first classes, who has not been invested^1 with the mystic thread, and who has not received the other ceremonies necessary to purification.<BR>E.<BR>संस्कार a rite, &c. हीन lost.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत|संस्कृतं|संस्कृतः
संस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wrought, made, artificially produced.<BR>2 Excellent, best.<BR>3 Decorated, ornamented.<BR>4 Cooked, dressed.<BR>5 Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>6 Purified.<BR>7 Finished, perfect, completed.<BR>8 Consecrated.<BR>9 Initiated.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A word regularly formed, a regular derivative.<BR>2 A learned man.<BR>3 A man of the three first classes who has received all the purificatory rites.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Language formed by perfect grammatical rules, the classical and sacred language of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying completion or perfection, कृत made, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृतात्मन्
संस्कृतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 A man who has undergone the initiatory rites.<BR>2 A sage.<BR>E.<BR>संस्कृत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृतोक्ति|संस्कृतोक्तिः
संस्कृतोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Classical or polished language.<BR>E.<BR>संस्कृत, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत्य
संस्कृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having perfected, polished, adorned, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृ to do, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत्रिम
संस्कृत्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Perfected, polished.<BR>2 Fabricated, made.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृ to make, त्रि aff. and मन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्क्रिया
संस्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Funeral ceremonies, as burning the dead body, &c.<BR>2 Any purificatory rite: see संस्कार.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रिया act, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तर|संस्तरः
संस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bed, a couch.<BR>2 A bed made of leaves, &c.<BR>3 Sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्तृ to spread, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तब्ध
संस्तब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Made firm, rigid, &c.<BR>2 Confirmed, corroborated.<BR>3 Stopped, stayed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्तभि to stop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भ|संस्तंभ|संस्तंभः|संस्तम्भः
संस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Fixing, making firm, (as a post.)<BR>2 Confirming, establishing.<BR>3 Paralysis, muscular rigidity.<BR>4 Stop, stay.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्तभि to stop, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भनीय
संस्तम्भनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be made firm.<BR>2 To be stopped.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्टभि to stop, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तभ्य|संस्तभ्यं
संस्तभ्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having made firm, stable, rigid, &c.<BR>2 Having confirmed or established.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्तभि to stop, aff. ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तव|संस्तवः
संस्तव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>2 Praise.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, ष्टु to praise, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तवान|संस्तवानः
संस्तवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Eloquent, talking fluently and well.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्टु to praise, आनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्ताव|संस्तावः
संस्ताव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The place occupied at a sacrifice by the Brahmans reciting hymns and prayers.<BR>2 Celebrating or hymning in chorus, the repetition of the verses of the Vedas by a number^1 of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, (in chorus,) ष्टु to praise, (the gods,) घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुत|संस्तुतः
संस्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Intimate, acquainted.<BR>2 Praised, hymned, eulogised.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्टु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुति|संस्तुतिः
संस्तुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Praise, celebration.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्टु to praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्याय|संस्त्यायः
संस्त्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Assemblage, collection, heap or number.<BR>2 Vicinity, proximity.<BR>3 Spreading, expansion, diffusion.<BR>4 A house.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ट्यै to crowd, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थ|संस्थः
संस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Staying, stopping, fixed, stationary.<BR>2 Staying with, associated, domesticated.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary.<BR>2 A countryman, a neighbour, a person of the same country, &c.<BR>3 A dweller, an inhabitant.<BR>f. (स्था)<BR>1 Continuance in the right way, correct conduct.<BR>2 State or condition of being, time of life, &c.<BR>3 Occupation, business, profession.<BR>4 Stop, stay.<BR>5 End, completion.<BR>6 Manifestation, appearance.<BR>7 Resemblance, likeness.<BR>8 A sort of sacrifice.<BR>9 Loss, destruction.<BR>10 Death, dying.<BR>11 Form.<BR>12 An assembly.<BR>13 A royal ordinance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying completeness, association, &c., and ष्ठा to stay, affs. क or अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थान|संस्थानं
संस्थान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Like, resembling.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Form, figure, shape.<BR>2 Death, dying.<BR>3 Fabrication, construction.<BR>4 A place where four roads meet.<BR>5 Any place.<BR>6 A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR>7 A heap, a quantity.<BR>8 Primary formation, the aggregation of the primitive atoms.<BR>9 A vicinity, a neighbourhood, a common place of abode.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ठा to stay or stand, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापन|संस्थापनं
संस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Placing, fixing.<BR>2 Establishing.<BR>3 Collecting.<BR>4 Restraining.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ठा to stay, causal v., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापित
संस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed, fixed, deposited.<BR>2 Established.<BR>3 Accumulated.<BR>4 Controuled, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ठा to stay, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थाप्य
संस्थाप्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having placed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ठा to stay, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थित|संस्थितः
संस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead, deceased.<BR>2 Ended, finished.<BR>3 Established, fixed.<BR>4 Staying, stationary.<BR>5 Residing, being in or at.<BR>6 Heaped, collected.<BR>7 Placed in or on.<BR>8 Near or contiguous to.<BR>9 Like, resembling.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ष्ठा to stay, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=877" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थिति|संस्थितिः
संस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Abode, abiding, being or being stationary.<BR>3 Abiding, being or residing with.<BR>4 Duration, continuance.<BR>5 State or condition, (of life.)<BR>6 Contiguity, connexion.<BR>7 Heap, accumulation.<BR>8 Restraint.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्थिति staying: see संस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्श|संस्पर्शः
संस्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Touching, contact, laying hold of.<BR>2 Perception, sense.<BR>f. (-र्शा)<BR>A fragrant plant, commonly Chakawal.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्पृश to touch, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्शज
संस्पर्शज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced by sense, by contact, &c.<BR>E.<BR>संस्पर्श, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृष्ट
संस्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Touched.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्पृश to touch, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फाल|संस्फालः
संस्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्फल to shake, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फुट|संस्फुटः
संस्फुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Blossomed, blown.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्फुट to blow, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फेट|संस्फेटः
संस्फेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्फिट to disrespect, aff. खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोट|संस्फोटः
संस्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्फुट to hurt or kill, aff. घञ्, or with इ aff. संस्फोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरण|संस्मरणं
संस्मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Remembering, calling to mind.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and स्मरण remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृत
संस्मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Remembered, called to mind.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and स्मृ to remember, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृति|संस्मृतिः
संस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Remembering, remembrance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before स्मृ to remember, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्राव|संस्रावः
संस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Flowing, oozing.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to go, with सम् pref. and ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहत|संहतः
संहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strong knit, well limbed.<BR>2 Compact, close.<BR>3 Joined, attached or approximated to.<BR>4 Closed, shut.<BR>5 Collected, assembled.<BR>6 Struck, hurt, wounded, killed.<BR>7 Acting or making effort together, combining, combined.<BR>3 Closely allied.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together with, हन to hurt or strike, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतजानुक|संहतजानुकः
संहतजानुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Knock-kneed.<BR>E.<BR>संहत approximated, close, and जानु the knee, कन् aff.; also without the aff. संहतजानु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहततल
संहततल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The two hands open, and the palms brought together.<BR>E.<BR>संहत closed, ला to get or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतता
संहतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Close approximation or contact, &c.: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>संहत, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतत्व|संहतत्वं
संहतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Compactness.<BR>2 Combination, &c.<BR>3 Approximation, contact.<BR>E.<BR>संहत, and त्व aff.; also संहतता with तल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहति|संहतिः
संहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Assemblage, collection, heap, number, host, multitude, &c.<BR>2 Combination, joint effort.<BR>3 Union, junction.<BR>4 Compactness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, हन to strike or hurt, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहनन|संहननं
संहनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 Rubbing the limbs.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हन to strike or hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरण|संहरणं
संहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Collecting, accumulating.<BR>2 Restraining, checking.<BR>3 Taking, seizing.<BR>4 Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्ष|संहर्षः
संहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 Pleasure, joy.<BR>3 Erection of the hair of the body, either from pleasure, or disease.<BR>4 Envy, emulation.<BR>5 Trituration, rubbing, grinding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हृष to be pleased, or घृष to rub, &c., aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्षयोगिन्
संहर्षयोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Joyful, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>संहर्ष, and योगिन् who joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहवन|संहवनं
संहवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A group of four houses.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, हु to sacrifice, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहात|संहातः
संहात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the twenty-one hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार|संहारः
संहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Destruction, loss.<BR>2 The destruction of the world.<BR>3 A division of Tartarus.<BR>4 Abridgment, abbreviation.<BR>5 Collection, assemblage.<BR>6 Restraining, suppressing.<BR>7 Practice, skill.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहित|संहितः
संहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Attached, joined.<BR>2 Collected, assembled.<BR>3 Placed, fixed.<BR>4 Provided, furnished, equipped.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 An arrangement of the text of the Vedas into short sentences, regulated when the style is verse by the species of verse, and when prose by the subject, and denominated after the person or persons by whom the arrangement was originally made: it is also sometimes considered as synonymous with a Śākhā; a branch or school of the Vedas, of which sixteen are reckoned to the Ṛg-veda, one hundred and one to the Yajuṣ, one thousand in the Sāma, and nine in the Atharvan.<BR>2 A compendium, a collection more or less compressed of laws, legends, &c.<BR>3 (In grammar,) Proximity of two letters without an intermediate pause, Sandhi or junction, though usually considered rather^1 as the state preparatory to the actual junction than the junction itself.<BR>4 A compilation, a code, a digest.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धा to have, aff. क.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूति|संहूतिः
संहूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Clamour, shout, tumultuous exclamation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, हूति calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत|संहृतः
संहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seized, laid hold of.<BR>2 Scuttered, thrown.<BR>3 Destroyed.<BR>4 Compressed, contracted, abridged^1.<BR>5 Curbed, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हृ to take, aff. क्त.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृति|संहृतिः
संहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Destruction, loss, disappearance.<BR>2 Conraction, abridgment.<BR>3 Taking, seizure.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हृ to take, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत्य
संहृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having contracted or reduced in bulk.<BR>2 Having abridged, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्राद|संह्रादः
संह्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ह्रद to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रादिन्
संह्रादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Sounding, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ह्रद to sound, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रीण
संह्रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and ह्री to be ashamed, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक|सकः
सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>He, that man.<BR>E.<BR>स he, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकट|सकटः
सकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Bad, vile.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>स with, कट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकटान्न|सकटान्नं
सकटान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Impure food.<BR>E.<BR>सकट, and अन्न boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकण्टक|सकंटक|सकण्टकः
सकण्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Thorny, prickly.<BR>2 Troublesome, perilous.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् like or with, कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर
सकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Bearing or returning tax or toll.<BR>2 Having rays, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स with, कर tax, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकरुण|सकरुणः
सकरुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Tender, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>स with, करुण compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्ण|सकर्णः
सकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Hearing, listening.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=878" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्म्मन्|सकर्मन्
सकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Performing any act or rite.<BR>2 Following similar business.<BR>E.<BR>स with or same, कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्म्मक|सकर्मक|सकर्म्मकः
सकर्म्मक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>(In grammar,) The transitive verb.<BR>E.<BR>स with कर्म्म act, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
सकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>All, whole, entire.<BR>E.<BR>स with, कला a part, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाकौल
सकाकौल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>One of the twenty-one hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकारण
सकारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having a cause, originating from a cause.<BR>E.<BR>स with, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाल
सकाल<BR>n. adv. (-लं)<BR>Betimes, early in the morning.<BR>E.<BR>स with, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल|सकुलः
सकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having a family, belonging to one, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of fish; also शकुल.<BR>E.<BR>स with, कुल a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल्य|सकुल्यः
सकुल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>1 A kinsman, one of the same family name and common origin: see सगोत्र.<BR>2 A distant kinsman or relation; one who shares a divided oblation, as the grandson's grandson or other descendant as far as three degrees from him, or the offspring of the grandfather's grandfather or other remoter ancestor.<BR>E.<BR>स same, कुल्य of family: some authorities extend the name of Sakulya to the tenth descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>Fæces, ordure: more usually, शकृत्.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Once.<BR>2 With, together with.<BR>3 Always.<BR>E.<BR>सकृत् substituted for एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्प्रज|सकृत्प्रजः
सकृत्प्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>सकृत् once, प्रज progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकोप
सकोप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Angry, displeased.<BR>E.<BR>स with, कोप wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्त|सक्तः
सक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Attached, joined, in contact with.<BR>2 Diligent, attentive, intent.<BR>3 Devoted or addicted to.<BR>E.<BR>षञ्ज to embrace or adhere to, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्ति|सक्तिः
सक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Contact, union, junction, cohesion.<BR>2 Devotion or addiction to.<BR>E.<BR>षञ्ज to embrace or adhere to, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तु|सक्तुः
सक्तु<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>Rice or corn fried and then ground.<BR>E.<BR>षच to moisten, Uṇādi aff. तुन्; also read शक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुक|सक्तुकः
सक्तुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of poison.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुफला
सक्तुफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>सक्तु barley meal, and फल fruit; of a similar white colour; also सक्तुफली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थि
सक्थि<BR>n. (-क्थि)<BR>1 The thigh.<BR>2 Part of the frame of a cart.<BR>E.<BR>षञ्ज to unite, Uṇādi aff. क्थिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखि
सखि<BR>m. (-सखा)<BR>1 A friend.<BR>2 An associate, a companion.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A woman's female friend or companion, a confidante, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान all, (the world,) ख्या to celebrate, aff. इन्, and ङीष् fem. aff.; the masc. noun is irregularly inflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखित्व|सखित्वं
सखित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सखि a friend, and त्व aff.; also सखिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखीजन
सखीजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A female friend or confidante.<BR>E.<BR>सखी, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख्य|सख्यं|सख्यः
सख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A friend.<BR>E.<BR>सखि a friend, य aff. of the property or pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग
सग<BR>(ए) सगे r. 1st cl. (सगति)<BR>To cover; also षग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगन्ध|सगंध|सगन्धः
सगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Fragrant, odoriferous.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A relation, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम same, like, and गन्ध connexion; or स with, and गन्ध smell, scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर|सगरः
सगर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Poisonous.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sovereign of Ayodhyā, the father of ASAMAÑJA by KEŚINĪ, and sixty thousand sons by SUMATI: the latter being turned into a heap of ashes by the sage KAPILA, GARUḌA instructed the king to perform their funeral ceremonies with the waters of Gaṅgā, to be brought from heaven for that purpose; this was finally accomplished by the devotion of BHAGĪRATHA, the great-grandson of ASAMAÑJA, who having led the river to the sea, denominated it Sāgara, in honor of this his ancestor.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, गर poison; being born together with a poison given to his mother by the other wife of his father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ|सगर्भः
सगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A brother by the same father and mother.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान the same, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ्य|सगर्भ्यः
सगर्भ्य<BR>m. (-र्भ्यः)<BR>A brother of whole blood, one by the same father and mother.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, गर्भ embryo, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्व्व|सगर्व
सगर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>1 Proud.<BR>2 Elated.<BR>E.<BR>स with, गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुण
सगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having or endowed with properties, qualities, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स with, गुण a quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगोत्र|सगोत्रं|सगोत्रः
सगोत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Being of one family, of kin, related.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A distant kinsman.<BR>2 A kinsman of the same family name, or one sprung from a common ancestor; one connected by funeral oblations of food and water.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A family, a race or lineage.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान like, common, and गोत्र family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्धि|सग्धिः
सग्धि<BR>f. (-ग्धिः)<BR>Eating together.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् with, अद to eat, क्तिच् aff.; घस is substituted for the root, the स rejected, and घ changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघ
सघ<BR>r. 5th cl. (सघ्नोति)<BR>To hurt, to kill; also षघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कट|संकट|सङ्कटः
सङ्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Narrow, contracted.<BR>2 Crowded.<BR>3 Impassable, impervious.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 Difficulty, trouble.<BR>2 A defile, a pass.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कटाक्ष|संकटाक्ष|सङ्कटाक्षः
सङ्कटाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Winking, leering.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कट contracted, अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथा|संकथा
सङ्कथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Conversation, discourse, talking together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, कथा speech; also सङ्कथन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कर|संकर|संकरः|सङ्करः
सङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mixing, blending, confounding.<BR>2 A mixed caste or race, one proceeding from the promiscuous intercourse of the four tribes in the first instance, and again from their commerce with the descendants of such a connexion, or the indiscriminate cohabitation of those descendants amongst one another: most Hindus of the present age are of one of the many branches of this race, the highest of which is impure and inferior to the Śūdra: under this term two kinds of men are included according to the Rāmāyaṇa; the one denominated योनिसङ्कर, mixed or degraded by birth; and आचारसङ्कर degraded by conduct.<BR>3 Dust, sweepings.<BR>4 The crackling of flame.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कॄ to scatter, or कृ to make, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्करीकरण|संकरीकरण|सङ्करीकरणं
सङ्करीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Reducing to the state of the mixed or outcaste tribes, causing loss of caste.<BR>2 Blending, mixing.<BR>3 Confusion, either in kind, number, or arrangement.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कर a mixed race, च्चि augment, and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्करीकृत
सङ्करीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blended, mixed, confusedly.<BR>2 Outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कर, and कृत made, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कर्षण|संकर्षण|संकर्षणं|सङ्कर्षणं|संकर्षणः|सङ्कर्षणः
सङ्कर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Attracting, drawing.<BR>2 Ploughing, making furrows, &c.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>BALADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृष to plough. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">Page880</a>] &c., aff. युच् or ल्युट्. As applied to the demigod it refers to his removal in embryo from the womb of DEVAKĪ to that of ROHIṆĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=879" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल|संकल|संकलः|सङ्कलः
सङ्कल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Collection, quantity.<BR>2 Addition.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, कल to number, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कलन|संकलन|संकलनं|सङ्कलनं
सङ्कलन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Contact, junction.<BR>2 Blending, clinging, twining, intermixture.<BR>3 Heaping as corn, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Addition, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् with or like, कल to number, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कला|संकला
सङ्कला<BR>aptote.<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कलित|संकलित|सङ्कलितः
सङ्कलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heaped, piled, arranged.<BR>2 Brought in contact, blended, intermixed.<BR>3 Added.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Addition, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कल to number, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्प|संकल्प|संकल्पः|सङ्कल्पः
सङ्कल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 Volition, will, resolve, mental determination.<BR>2 A solemn vow or declaration of purpose.<BR>3 Expectation of desired consequences from any voluntary act.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृप to be able, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पज|संकल्पज|संकल्पजः
सङ्कल्पज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born of, or proceeding from the hope or expectation of advantage.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, and ज born; also सङ्कल्पजन्मन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पजन्मन्|संकल्पजन्मन्
सङ्कल्पजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प volition, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पभव|संकल्पभव|सङ्कल्पभवः
सङ्कल्पभव<BR>m. (वः)<BR>KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प will, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पयोनि|संकल्पयोनि|सङ्कल्पयोनिः
सङ्कल्पयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>KĀMA, the deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प will, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्परूप|संकल्परूप
सङ्कल्परूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Of the nature of or conformable to the will or purpose.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पसम्भव|संकल्पसम्भव|संकल्पसंभव
सङ्कल्पसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced from or arising out of the hope or desire of advantage.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Love or KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, and सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पात्मक|संकल्पात्मक
सङ्कल्पात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Willing, resolving, referring to volition.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, and आत्मक one with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पित|संकल्पित
सङ्कल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Proposed, sought as the result of any act.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कसुक|संकसुक
सङ्कसुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Unsteady, fickle, changeable.<BR>2 Uncertain, doubtful.<BR>3 Weak, feeble.<BR>4 Bad, weak, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कस to go, Uṇādi aff. उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कार|संकार|संकारः|सङ्कारः
सङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Dust, sweepings.<BR>2 The crackling of flame.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A girl recently deflowered, a new bride, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्काश|संकाश|संकाशः|सङ्काशः
सङ्काश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Like, similar, (in composition.)<BR>2 Near.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before काशृ to shine, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्किल|संकिल|संकिलः|सङ्किलः
सङ्किल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A burning torch, a fire-brand.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before किल to be white, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्ण|संकीर्ण|सङ्कीर्णं|संकीर्णः|सङ्कीर्णः
सङ्कीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Crowded, confused.<BR>2 Miscellaneous.<BR>3 Impure.<BR>4 Mixed.<BR>5 Of mixed and consequently impure origin or caste.<BR>6 Contracted, narrow.<BR>7 Spread, diffused.<BR>8 Scattered.<BR>9 Indistinct, confused, (as a writing.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कॄ to scatter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्णचारिन्|संकीर्णचारिन्
सङ्कीर्णचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wandering about, going into all sorts of places.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कीर्ण, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्णयोनि|संकीर्णयोनि
सङ्कीर्णयोनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Of mixed or impure origin.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कीर्ण, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्त्तन|सङ्कीर्तन|संकीर्तनं|सङ्कीर्त्तनं
सङ्कीर्त्तन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Celebrating, praising, honour, glorification.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कॄत to praise, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्त्तित|सङ्कीर्तित|संकीर्तित|सङ्कीर्त्तितः
सङ्कीर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, renowned, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, कॄत to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कु
सङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कुचित|संकुचित|सङ्कुचितं
सङ्कुचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unblown, unopened.<BR>2 Closed, shut.<BR>3 Narrowed, contracted.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कुच to contract, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कुल|संकुल|सङ्कुलं
सङ्कुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Crowded, confused, filled with so as to be impervious.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Inconsistent and contradictory speech.<BR>2 War.<BR>3 A crowd, a mob.<BR>4 A flock, a flight.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, कुल to accumulate, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कृति|संकृति
सङ्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A form of metre, a stanza of four lines, of 24 syllables each.<BR>E.<BR>सम् complete, कृति a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केत|संकेत|संकेतः|सङ्केतः
सङ्केत<BR>r. 10th cl. (सङ्केतयति)<BR>1 To call or invite.<BR>2 To counsel or advise.<BR>3 To fix or appoint a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केत|संकेत|संकेतः|सङ्केतः
सङ्केत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Engagement, agreement, appointment, convention.<BR>2 Condition, provision, the circumstances under which any thing is necessarily or naturally effected.<BR>3 Sign, gesture, gesticulation.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्केत to appoint a time, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केतस्थान|संकेतस्थान
सङ्केतस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Place of assignation.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्केत, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कोच|संकोच|सङ्कोचं|संकोचः|सङ्कोचः
सङ्कोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 Shutting, closing, contracting, contraction.<BR>2 Binding, tying.<BR>3 A sort of fish, a scate, (Raia Sancura, HAM.)<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before कुच to contract, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कोचन|संकोचन|संकोचनं
सङ्कोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Astringing, causing to shrink or close.<BR>E.<BR>मम्, कुच to contract, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रन्दन|संक्रन्दन|संक्रंदन|संक्रंदनः|संक्रन्दनः|सङ्क्रन्दनः
सङ्क्रन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रदि to cry out, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रम|संक्रम|संक्रमः|सङ्क्रमः
सङ्क्रम<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>1 Difficult progress, clambering up rocks, fording torrents, making way through almost impervious or inaccessible passes, &c.<BR>2 The means of effecting such a passage, a causeway, a bridge, &c.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going, moving, travelling.<BR>2 The passage of a planetary body through the zodiac.<BR>3 Passage from one point to another, traversing, transit, transition.<BR>4 Concurrence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रम to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रमण|संक्रमण|संक्रमणं|सङ्क्रमणं
सङ्क्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going from or to, passage, transition.<BR>2 Going with, concurrence.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रमितृ|संक्रमितृ
सङ्क्रमितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who goes or proceeds, who or what passes from one to another.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, क्रम to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रान्त|संक्रांत|संक्रान्त|सङ्क्रान्तः
सङ्क्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Passed, gone from one to another, transferred, &c.<BR>2 Entered (into a new sign).<BR>3 Depicted, imaged, reflected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रम to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रान्ति|संक्रान्ति|संक्रांति|संक्रांतिः|संक्रान्तिः|सङ्क्रान्तिः
सङ्क्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 The actual passage of the sun or other planetary bodies from one sign of the zodiac into another.<BR>2 Passage in general, proceeding from one time or condition of life to another, from one place to another, &c.<BR>3 Going, proceeding in general.<BR>4 Imitation, reflexion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रम to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्राम|संक्राम|संक्रामः|सङ्क्रामः
सङ्क्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Difficult progress or passage over steep rocks, through narrow defiles, &c.<BR>2 A bridge of ropes, &c.: see सङ्क्रम.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रम to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रीडण
सङ्क्रीडण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रीड to play, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=880" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रीडमाण
सङ्क्रीडमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्रीड to play, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रुद्ध|संक्रुद्ध
सङ्क्रुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Violent, enraged.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and क्रुद्ध angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्लेद|संक्लेद|संक्लेदः|सङ्क्लेदः
सङ्क्लेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The fluid secretion which is supposed to form upon conception, and to be the rudiment of the foetus.<BR>2 Moisture, wet, damp.<BR>E.<BR>सम् to gether, and क्लेद moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षय|संक्षय|संक्षयः
सङ्क्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The destruction of the world.<BR>2 Loss, destruction in general.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, क्षि to perish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षिप्त|संक्षिप्त|संक्षिप्तः
सङ्क्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Abridged, abbreviated, concise, compressed.<BR>2 Small, compact.<BR>3 Thrown.<BR>4 Sent.<BR>5 Taken from or away, seized.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्षिप to throw or send, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्तिः
सङ्क्षिप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Abridgment.<BR>2 Throwing.<BR>3 Sending.<BR>4 Ambuscade.<BR>5 Transition from one feeling to another.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, क्षिप to throw, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षीयमाण
सङ्क्षीयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Perishing, being destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्षि to waste, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षेप|संक्षेप|संक्षेपः
सङ्क्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Abridgment, abbreviation, conciseness, compression.<BR>2 Sending.<BR>3 Throwing.<BR>4 Taking away.<BR>5 Assisting in another's duty.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्षिप to throw or send, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षेपण|संक्षेपण|संक्षेपणं
सङ्क्षेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Abridgment, brevity.<BR>2 Sending.<BR>3 Throwing.<BR>4 Taking away.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्षिप to throw or send, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षोभ|संक्षोभ|संक्षोभः
सङ्क्षोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Overturning, upsetting.<BR>2 Shaking, trembling, agitation.<BR>3 Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्षुभ to tremble, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्ष्णुवान
सङ्क्ष्णुवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Whetting, sharpening.<BR>2 Inflaming, exciting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before क्ष्णु to sharpen, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्य|संख्य|संख्यं|सङ्ख्यं
सङ्ख्य<BR>n. (-ङ्ख्यं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>f. (-ङ्ख्या)<BR>1 Number in general, or a number, a numeral.<BR>2 Deliberation, reasoning, reflection.<BR>3 Intellect, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ख्या substituted for चक्ष to speak well, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यता|संख्यता
सङ्ख्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Number, numeration, counting.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also सङ्ख्यत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यात|संख्यात|सङ्ख्यातं
सङ्ख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Numbered, counted, reckoned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ख्या to tell, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यान|संख्यान|संख्यानं|सङ्ख्यानं
सङ्ख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Numbering, numeration, reckoning.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ख्या to tell, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यावत्|संख्यावत्|संख्यावन्त्
सङ्ख्यावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having or being possessed of number, numbered.<BR>2 Intelligent, discriminating.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A learned Brahman, a Paṇḍita, a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ख्या number, &c., and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्येय|संख्येय|सङ्ख्येयं
सङ्ख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Numerable, to be counted or numbered.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ख्या a number, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
सङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Meeting, encountering.<BR>2 Association, intercourse, friendship.<BR>3 Joining, uniting.<BR>4 Desire, wish, cupidity.<BR>5 Addiction or devotion to.<BR>6 Confluence of rivers.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, गम to go, aff. ड, or षंज to embrace. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गणिका|संगणिका
सङ्गणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Incomparable or unequalled discourse.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गण to count, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गत|संगत|सङ्गतं
सङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Apposite, proper, (as speech.)<BR>2 Mixed, united.<BR>3 Met, encountered.<BR>4 Collected, accumulated.<BR>5 In conjunction, (planets.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Friendship, acquaintance.<BR>2 Union, meeting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गति|संगति|संगतिः|सङ्गतिः
सङ्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Meeting, union, mixture.<BR>2 Knowledge.<BR>3 Association, intercourse.<BR>4 Frequenting, going to.<BR>5 Questioning for continued or further information.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गम|संगम|संगमः|सङ्गमः
सङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Meeting, union, mixture, junction, the encounter of persons, the association of friends or lovers, the confluence of rivers, the fitness or adaptation of two things to each other, &c.<BR>2 (In astronomy,) Planetary conjunction.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, like, suitably, गम going: see also सङ्ग, सङ्गत, सङ्गति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गर|संगर|सङ्गरं|संगरः|सङ्गरः
सङ्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>3 Promise, assent, agreement.<BR>4 A bargain, a transaction of sale.<BR>5 Poison.<BR>6 Knowledge.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The fruit of the Śami tree.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गॄ to swallow, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गरहित
सङ्गरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Indifferent, stoical, free from attachment.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग, and रहित free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गवर्ज्जित|सङ्गवर्जित
सङ्गवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Free from worldly attachments or affections.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग, and वर्ज्जित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गविच्युति
सङ्गविच्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Separation from, or dissolution of worldly affection.<BR>2 Disunion.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग, and विच्युति separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिन्|संगिन्
सङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Uniting with, going to or with, attached.<BR>2 Devoted or addicted to, intent on.<BR>3 Libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग union, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिरमाण
सङ्गिरमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Promising.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गॄ to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीत|संगीत|सङ्गीतं
सङ्गीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The exhibition of song, dancing, and music, as a public entertainment.<BR>2 The art or science of music, and dancing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीति|संगीति|संगीतिः|सङ्गीतिः
सङ्गीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Conversation, discourse.<BR>2 The science of music and dancing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, गा to sing, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीर्ण|संगीर्ण|सङ्गीर्णं
सङ्गीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Promised, agreed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गॄ to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गुप्त|संगुप्त|सङ्गुप्तः
सङ्गुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Hidden, concealed.<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गूढ|संगूढ|सङ्गूढः
सङ्गूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Heaped, piled, arranged.<BR>2 United, joined, brought in contact.<BR>3 Contracted, abridged.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गुह to hide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गृहीत|संगृहीत
सङ्गृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken, accepted, seized.<BR>2 Assented to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ग्रह to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गोपन|संगोपन|सङ्गोपनं
सङ्गोपन<BR>mfn. (-नं)<BR>Hiding, concealment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गुप to hide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रह|संग्रह|संग्रहः|सङ्ग्रहः
सङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A compilation and abridgment.<BR>2 A catalogue, a list or summary.<BR>3 Quantity, collection.<BR>4 Restraining, confining.<BR>5 Taking, seizing.<BR>6 Propitiating, pleasing, attaching.<BR>7 Protecting, guarding.<BR>8 A place where any thing is kept.<BR>9 Assent, promise.<BR>10 Elevation, loftiness.<BR>11 Velocity.<BR>12 Clenching the fist.<BR>13 Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ग्रह to take, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रहण|संग्रहण|संग्रहणं
सङ्ग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, accepting, seizing.<BR>2 Sexual intercourse.<BR>3 Hope.<BR>4 Collecting.<BR>5 Compiling.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Diarrhœa, dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ग्रह to take, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राम|संग्राम|संग्रामः|सङ्ग्रामः
सङ्ग्राम<BR>r. 10th cl. (सङ्ग्रामयति-ते)<BR>1 To fight.<BR>2 To make war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=881" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राम|संग्राम|संग्रामः|सङ्ग्रामः
सङ्ग्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग्राम to fight, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रामपटह|संग्रामपटह|संग्रामपटहः|सङ्ग्रामपटहः
सङ्ग्रामपटह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A large military drum.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग्राम war, and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राह|संग्राह|संग्राहः|सङ्ग्राहः
सङ्ग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Laying hold of forcibly, seizing, griping.<BR>2 The fist.<BR>3 Clenching the fist.<BR>4 The gripe of a shield.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ग्रह to seize, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घ|संघ|संघः|सङ्घः
सङ्घ<BR>n. (-ङ्घं)<BR>1 Flock, multitude, number, a collection of living beings either of the same or different species.<BR>2 A heap, a quantity in general.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हन to kill or hurt, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घचारिन्|संघचारिन्
सङ्घचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A fish in general.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्घ a shoal, चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घजीविन्|संघजीविन्
सङ्घजीविन्<BR>m. (-वां)<BR>A hired porter or labourer, a cooly.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्घ a crowd, and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घट्ट|संघट्ट|संघट्टः|सङ्घट्टः
सङ्घट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 Clash, shock, collision.<BR>2 Friction, rubbing together.<BR>3 Meeting, encounter.<BR>4 Embracing.<BR>f. (-ट्टा)<BR>A large creeper.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घट्ट to go, aff. अच्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घट्टन|संघट्टन|संघट्टनं|सङ्घट्टनं
सङ्घट्टन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Meeting, encountering, occurrence.<BR>2 Union, junction, contact, cohesion.<BR>3 Close contact, cleaving or adhering to, the intertwining^1 of wrestlers, the embraces of lovers, &c.<BR>4 Friction, rubbing together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घट्ट to move, aff. युच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घर्ष|संघर्ष|संघर्षः|सङ्घर्षः
सङ्घर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Envy, emulation, rivalry, vieing or contending for superiority.<BR>2 Trituration, rubbing, grinding.<BR>3 Going gently, gliding, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घृष to rub, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घशस्|संघशस्
सङ्घशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Collectively, altogether.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्घ, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घाटिका|संघाटिका
सङ्घाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bawd, a procuress.<BR>2 A pair, a couple.<BR>3 An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>4 Smell.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घट to unite, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घात|संघात|संघातः|सङ्घातः
सङ्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Assemblage, multitude, heap, quantity.<BR>2 Association, combination.<BR>3 Composition of words, formation of compound terms.<BR>4 Killing, striking, hurting.<BR>5 Phlegm.<BR>6 A particular mode of walking in dramatic representation.<BR>7 A division of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before हन to strike or kill, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घातवत्|संघातवत्|संघातवन्त्
सङ्घातवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having or connected with many, a heap, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्घात, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घुष्ट|संघुष्ट|सङ्घुष्टं|संघुष्टः
सङ्घुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Resonant, resounding.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Sound, cry, noise.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घुष to sound, aff. क्त; also optionally with the augment, इट्, सङ्घुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचराचर
सचराचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>All whether animate or inanimate.<BR>E.<BR>स with, चर moving, अचर stationary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचि|सचिः
सचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>Friendship, intimacy, connexion.<BR>f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>षच to be connected, aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added; also शचि, and शची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिल्लक|सचिल्लकः
सचिल्लक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Blear-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, चिल्ल a bad eye, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिव|सचिवः
सचिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A friend, a companion, an associate.<BR>2 A minister, a counsellor.<BR>E.<BR>सचि friendship, वा to go or get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतन
सचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Rational.<BR>2 Conscious, sensible.<BR>E.<BR>स with, चेतन intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतस्
सचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Conscious, reflective, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>स with, चेतस् mind<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेल
सचेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Clothed, dressed.<BR>E.<BR>स with, चेल clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेष्ट|सचेष्टः
सचेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Active, making effort.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The mango, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>स with, चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चरित
सच्चरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Honest, upright.<BR>2 Virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, चरित conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चारा
सच्चारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदंश
सच्चिदंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Intellect, intellectual part or portion.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, चित् intellect, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदानन्द|सच्चिदानंद|सच्चिदानन्दः
सच्चिदानन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>BRAHMA, or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being present, चित् intellect, and आनन्द happiness; the external source of wisdom and happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्छूद्र
सच्छूद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A Śūdra, who has gone through the same ceremonies as the other classes, which though not directed by and indeed contrary to law, is in some places customary.<BR>E.<BR>सत् pure, and शूद्र a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजम्बाल|सजंबाल|सजम्बालः
सजम्बाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Muddy, clayey.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह, with जम्बाल mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजल
सजल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Watery, wet.<BR>E.<BR>स with, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजाति|सजातिः
सजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of the same sort or species, of the same tribe, &c.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The son of a man and woman of the same caste.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजातीय|सजातीयः
सजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Descended from parents of the same tribe or caste.<BR>2 Of the same tribe.<BR>3 Of the same species.<BR>4 Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, जाति sort, kind, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजुस्
सजुस्<BR>mfn. (-जूः-जूः-जुः)<BR>Associated, an associate or companion.<BR>ind. (-जूः)<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>स with जुष to please, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ज|सज्जः
सज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>1 Armed, accoutred.<BR>2 Fortified.<BR>3 Prepared, got ready.<BR>4 Ornamented, decorated.<BR>5 Covered, clothed.<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>1 Dress, decoration.<BR>2 Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>षस्ज to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जन|सज्जनं|सज्जनः
सज्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Of good family, well born.<BR>2 Respectable, reputable.<BR>3 Good, virtuous.<BR>4 Arming, putting on armour.<BR>5 Dressing, preparing.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A guard, a sentry, a picquet.<BR>2 A ferry, a Ghāt.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Caparisoning an elephant.<BR>2 Dress, decoration.<BR>3 Arming, accoutring.<BR>E.<BR>षस्ज to go, aff. युच्, or सत् excellence, जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जमान
सज्जमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Arming.<BR>2 Dressing.<BR>3 Getting ready, preparing.<BR>4 Hesitating, (in speech.)<BR>E.<BR>षस्ज to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जित|सज्जितः
सज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Armed, accoutred.<BR>2 Dressed, decorated, ornamented.<BR>3 Prepared, made.<BR>E.<BR>सज्जा armour, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीकरण
सज्जीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Arming, arraying, preparing, decorating.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ज armed, and करण् making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीकृत
सज्जीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Armed, accoutred, prepared, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ज, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीभूत
सज्जीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Armed, prepared, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ज, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्य
सज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Strung, (as a bow,) having a bowstring.<BR>E.<BR>स with ज्या a bowstring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चकित|संचकित
सञ्चकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Afraid, timid.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and चकित timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चत्|संचत्
सञ्चत्<BR>m. (-ञ्चत्)<BR>Cheating, juggling.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, चि to collect, अति Uṇādi aff. and the radical vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=882" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चय|संचय|संचयः|सञ्चयः
सञ्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Heap, quantity, number, multitude.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, चि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चयन|संचयन|संचयनं|सञ्चयनं
सञ्चयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Collecting, gathering.<BR>2 Collecting the ashes or bones of a body which has been burnt.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, चि to collect, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चयिन्|संचयिन्
सञ्चयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Who or what collects.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, चि to collect, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चर|संचर|संचरः|सञ्चरः
सञ्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A defile, any narrow or difficult pass, a road along the edge of a mountain, or a bridge over a mountain stream, &c.<BR>2 Difficult passage, travelling along almost impracticable routes.<BR>3 A road, a way.<BR>4 The body.<BR>5 Killing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, aff. घ; also सञ्चार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चलन|संचलन|संचलनं|सञ्चलनं
सञ्चलन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चल to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चान|संचानः|सञ्चानः
सञ्चान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bird, a hawk (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चाय्य|संचाय्य|संचाय्यः|सञ्चाय्यः
सञ्चाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A particular sacrifice, at which the juice of the acid Asclepias is drank.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, चि to collect, participial aff. ण्यत् form irr. आय being substituted for the regular change: see सञ्चेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चार|संचार|संचारः|सञ्चारः
सञ्चार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Difficult progress.<BR>2 Difficulty, distress.<BR>3 Leading, guiding.<BR>4 Inciting.<BR>5 Impelling, setting in motion.<BR>6 Contagion, communication or transmission of disease.<BR>7 Course, transition.<BR>8 A gem supposed to be in the head of a serpent.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, aff. घञ्: see सञ्चर, or सम् and चर to go, causal v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारक|संचारक|संचारकः
सञ्चारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A leader, a guide.<BR>2 An instigator.<BR>3 An orator.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, चर to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारजीविन्|संचारजीविन्
सञ्चारजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Indigent, distressed, calamitous, in want of aid or protection.<BR>E.<BR>सञ्चार difficulty, and जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारण|संचारण|संचारणं
सञ्चारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Leading, guiding.<BR>2 Impelling, instigating.<BR>3 Moving, setting in motion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारिका|संचारिका
सञ्चारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A female messenger or go-between.<BR>2 A bawd.<BR>3 A brace, a pair.<BR>4 Smell.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारित|संचारित
सञ्चारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Led, guided.<BR>2 Driven, impelled.<BR>3 Set in motion, moved.<BR>4 Communicated, (as disease.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारिन्|संचारिन्
सञ्चारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Fickle, changeable, not permanent.<BR>2 Moving, going.<BR>3 Difficult, inaccessible.<BR>4 Moving, putting in motion.<BR>5 Transmitted, hereditary, (as disease.)<BR>6 Contagious.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 Incense.<BR>2 A division of the Bhāvas, the same as the व्यभित्रारिन् q. v. or the reverse of the स्थायिन् or fixed and steady sentiments.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चित|संचित
सञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Assembled, accumulated, collected, gathered.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चित्रा|संचित्रा
सञ्चित्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A plant, (Salvainia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, चित्र variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्तन|संचिन्तन|संचिंतनं
सञ्चिन्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Considering, reflecting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चिति to think, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्तित|संचिंतित|संचिन्तित
सञ्चिन्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Deliberated, weighed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, चिति to think, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्त्य|संचिन्त्य
सञ्चिन्त्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered, reflected, thoughtful.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, त्रिति to think, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चूर्णन|संचूर्णन|संचूर्णनं
सञ्चूर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Breaking to pieces, reducing to powder.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, चूर्ण to grind, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चूर्णित|संचूर्णित
सञ्चूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut or broken to pieces, pulverised, comminuted.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before चूर्ण to pound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चेय|संचेय|सञ्चेयं
सञ्चेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be collected or accumulated.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, त्रि to gather, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चोदित|संचोदित
सञ्चोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ordered, commanded.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and चोदित ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छन्न|संछन्न
सञ्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Covered.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, and छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिन्न|संछिन्न
सञ्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Cut, cut off.<BR>2 Dissipated, removed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before छिद to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज|संज|संजः|सञ्जः
सञ्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (सञ्जति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज|संज|संजः|सञ्जः
सञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>A she-goat.<BR>E.<BR>सम् uniformly, all (mankind), जन to be born, (or created by whom,) and ढ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनन|संजनन
सञ्जनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Begetting, causing, producing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before जन to be born, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनयत्
सञ्जनयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Begetting, producing, causing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before जन to be born, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जवन|संजवन|संजवनं|सञ्जवनं
सञ्जवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A group of four houses.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, जु to go, aff. युच्; also संयवन, and सञ्जीवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जात|संजात
सञ्जात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Become.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जानान|संजानान
सञ्जानान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Knowing, observing.<BR>2 Watching, who or what keeps watch.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्ञा to know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जीवन|संजीवन|संजीवनं|सञ्जीवनं
सञ्जीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Animating, bringing to life.<BR>2 A cluster of four houses.<BR>3 A hill.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, जीव to live, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जुघुक्षा|संजुघुक्षा
सञ्जुघुक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Wish or attempt to preserve.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गुह to hide, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जुघुक्षु|संजुघुक्षु
सञ्जुघुक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to preserve, hide, conceal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before गुह to hide, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वर|संज्वर|संज्वरः|सञ्ज्वरः
सञ्ज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Heat, the heat of fire, burning, scorching, a burn.<BR>2 Fever.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्वर to burn, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वरातुर|संज्वरातुर
सञ्ज्वरातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Overcome by or affected with fever, fevered, feverish.<BR>E.<BR>सञ्ज्वर, and आतुर distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वारिन्|संज्वारिन्
सञ्ज्वारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Affected with fever, fevered, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्वर to be feverish, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञ
संज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Knock-kneed.<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 Name, appellation.<BR>2 Thought, mind, intellect.<BR>3 Gesture, sign, gesticulation.<BR>4 The sacred verse or Gāyatrī of the Vedas.<BR>5 One of the wives of the sun.<BR>6 (In grammar,) The technical name of any affix, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्ञा to know, aff. अङ् and टाप्, that by which any thing is known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञप्ति
संज्ञप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Killing, slaying.<BR>2 Apprising, informing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्ञा to know; also, to slay, (causal form,) aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञापन
संज्ञापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Apprising, informing.<BR>3 Teaching.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ज्ञा to know; also to slay, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=883" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ञावत्
सज्ञावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Recovered after insensibility, become sensible.<BR>2 Having a name or denomination.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ञा sign, name, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ञाविषय
सज्ञाविषय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An epithet or attributive.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ञा, and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ञित
सज्ञित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Called, denominated.<BR>E.<BR>सज्ञा, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ञु
सज्ञु<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु)<BR>Knock-kneed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, and ज्ञु for जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट|सटं
सट<BR>r. 1st (सटयति)<BR>To manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट|सटं
सट<BR>mfn. subst. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>An ascetic's clotted hair, or the hair collected into a loose braid and twisted forwards upon the forehead.<BR>2 A mane.<BR>3 A crest.<BR>E.<BR>षट to be a part of, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटाङ्क|सटांक|सटाङ्कः
सटाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>सटा mane, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटि|सटिः
सटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet,) but applied also to the Curcuma amada: see सटि.<BR>E.<BR>षट to be a part of, इन् aff. and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटीक
सटीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Accompanied or explained by a commentary.<BR>E.<BR>स with, टीका a comment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्ट
सट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (सट्टयति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्टक|सट्टकं
सट्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of minor drama in Prākṛta only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सठ|सठः
सठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (साठयति)<BR>1 To finish, to complete.<BR>2 To leave unfinished.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सणसूत्र|सणसूत्रं
सणसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Packthread.<BR>E.<BR>see शणसूत्र, the sibilants being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्ड|संड|सण्डः
सण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A eunuch: see षण्ड, and शण्ड, &c. the sibilants being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डीन|संडीन|संडीनं|सण्डीनं
सण्डीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Perching, alighting, (as a bird.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् before डी to fly, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्|सन्त्|संत्
सत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>1 True.<BR>2 Good, virtuous.<BR>3 Being, existing.<BR>4 Excellent, best.<BR>5 Venerable, respectable.<BR>6 Wise, learned.<BR>7 Firm, steady.<BR>8 Right, proper.<BR>f. (-सती)<BR>1 A virtuous wife; in ordinary use applied especially to the wife who burns herself with her husband's corpse.<BR>2 The goddess UMĀ.<BR>3 A fragrant earth, commonly Surat earth.<BR>4 A species of the Pratiṣṭhā metre.<BR>n. (सत्)<BR>The true God, the always present and all-pervading spirit.<BR>ind. (सत्)<BR>In composition, a particle of reverence or respect, implying, good, right, fit, &c. as सत्क्रिया virtue, doing what is right, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, aff. of the participle of the present tense शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत|सततं
सतत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eternal, continual.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>Eternally, continually.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तन to spread, aff. क्त, and the म rejected optionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत्त्व|सतत्त्वं
सतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>Natural property, nature.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान universal, तत्त्व nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतानन्द|सतानन्दः
सतानन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The sage GAUTAMA, the author of the Nyāya or logical philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>सत् the good, and आनन्द who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सति|सतिः
सति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 End, destruction.<BR>2 Gift, giving.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give or षो to destroy, क्तिन् aff.; also साति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीत्व|सतीत्वं
सतीत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Virtuousness or purity in a wife.<BR>E.<BR>सती, see सत्, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, सतीता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीन|सतीनः
सतीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Peas, or a particular kind of pulse.<BR>E.<BR>सति, from सत् being, life, इन् master, and with कन् added सतीनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीनक|सतीनकः
सतीनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Peas; also सितीनक, and सतीलक, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ|सतीर्थः
सतीर्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A fellow student, the pupil of the same spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह same, तीर्थ a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ्य|सतीर्थ्यः
सतीर्थ्य<BR>m. (-र्थ्यः)<BR>A fellow student: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह the same, तीर्थ a teacher, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतील|सतीलः
सतील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>Peas, pulse, or a particular kind, called Teorā.<BR>E.<BR>सती a good wife, लक्ष to make, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलक|सतीलकः
सतीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Pulse in general, or a particular sort.<BR>E.<BR>सतील wind, कै to utter, aff. ड; also सितीलक, सतीनक, सातीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्
सतृष्<BR>mfn. (-तृट्)<BR>1 Thirsty, greedy, cupidinous.<BR>2 Thirsty, (literally.)<BR>E.<BR>स for सहित with, तृष thirst, literally or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कर्म्मन्|सत्कर्मन्
सत्कर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 A good act, piety, virtue.<BR>2 Hospitality.<BR>3 Funeral obsequies.<BR>4 Expiation.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and कम्मन् act; also सत्, क्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कदम्ब|सत्कदम्बः
सत्कदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A tree, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, कदम्ब the Cadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्काञ्चनार|सत्काञ्चनारः
सत्काञ्चनार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of ebony: see रक्तकाञ्चन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्काण्ड|सत्कांड|सत्काण्डः
सत्काण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A hawk, a kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कार|सत्कारः
सत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Reverence, respect.<BR>2 Hospitable treatment or reception.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृत|सत्कृतः
सत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Worshipped, adored.<BR>2 Respected, revered.<BR>3 Welcomed, saluted.<BR>4 Entertained, treated with hospitality.<BR>5 Done rightly or properly.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Hospitality.<BR>2 Respect.<BR>3 Virtue.<BR>E.<BR>सत् excellent, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृति|सत्कृतिः
सत्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Doing good, acting properly, virtue, morality, &c.<BR>2 Treating with respect.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and कृति act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृत्य
सत्कृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having treated with respect, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and कृत्य having made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्क्रिया
सत्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Funeral or obsequial ceremonies.<BR>2 Any purificatory ceremony.<BR>3 Doing good, charity, virtue, &c.<BR>4 Worship, homage.<BR>5 Respectful treatment.<BR>6 Salutation, welcome, courtesy.<BR>7 Hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तम|सत्तमः
सत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Best, excellent.<BR>2 Very venerable or respectable.<BR>3 Most virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ता
सत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>1 Being, existence.<BR>2 Goodness, excellence.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, तल् aff. of the abstract; also सत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (सत्रयते)<BR>1 To act liberally.<BR>2 To be connected.<BR>3 To spread or extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्र
सत्त्र<BR>n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>1 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 Liberality, munificence.<BR>3 Covering, clothing, concealing.<BR>4 Fraud, roguery, cheating.<BR>5 A wood, a forest.<BR>6 Wealth.<BR>7 A house.<BR>8 A tank, a pond.<BR>E.<BR>सद to go, Uṇādi aff. त्रन्; in writing, one त may be omitted, and it occurs, सत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रशाला
सत्त्रशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An apartment in which Brahmans or mendicants, &c. are presented with food and gifts.<BR>E.<BR>सत्र giving, and शाला a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रा
सत्त्रा<BR>ind.<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, त्रा to preserve, aff. क्विप्; also written, सत्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रि
सत्त्रि<BR>m. (-त्त्रिः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 A victor, a conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, or waste, to destroy, &c. Uṇādi aff. त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिन्
सत्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्त्री)<BR>1 A liberal housekeeper, one constantly performing sacrifice and distributing alms.<BR>2 An embassador, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">Page885</a>] an agent residing in a foreign country.<BR>3 A priest superintending or performing a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्र munificence, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=884" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्व|सत्त्वं|सत्त्वः
सत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>1 One of the three Guṇas or properties of man and nature; the quality of excellence or goodness: that which enlightens, constitutes knowledge, and is the cause of truth, and the predominance of which renders the person, in whom it resides, virtuous, gentle, devout, charitable, chaste, honest, &c., and the thing, pure, mild, &c.<BR>2 Substance, thing, either elementary substance, as earth, air, fire, &c. or any thing of which some property may be predicated.<BR>3 Mind, intellect.<BR>4 Nature, natural property or disposition.<BR>5 Vigour, power.<BR>6 Strength.<BR>7 Self-possession or command.<BR>8 Breath.<BR>9 Being, existence.<BR>10 Essence, substance.<BR>11 Wealth.<BR>12 Certainty.<BR>13 Life, the principle of being.<BR>14 A substantive noun.<BR>15 A demon, a goblin.<BR>mn. (-त्त्वः-त्त्वं)<BR>An animal, a being.<BR>E.<BR>षद to perish, aff. त्वत्, or सत् being, good, excellent, &c. त्व aff. of the abstract; one त being rejected also, it is read सत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वगुण|सत्त्वगुणः
सत्त्वगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The property of goodness; see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and गुण attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वता
सत्त्वता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Purity, goodness, the existence of the Sattva Gauṇa, or property of truth and virtue, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् abstract added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वमेजय
सत्त्वमेजय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Frightening animals, making them tremble.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and एज to shake, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्ववत्|सत्त्ववन्त्
सत्त्ववत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Pure, virtuous, endowed with the quality of goodness.<BR>2 Natural.<BR>3 Existent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वविहित
सत्त्वविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done spontaneously or naturally<BR>2 Virtuous, upright.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and विहित effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंशुद्धि|सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः
सत्त्वसंशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Purity of nature or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and संशुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसम्पन्न|सत्त्वसंपन्न|सत्त्वसम्पन्नः
सत्त्वसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Equable, even-minded, neither elated by prosperity nor depressed by misfortune.<BR>2 Good, excellent.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व the good quality, and सम्पन्न endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वस्थ|सत्त्वस्थः
सत्त्वस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Excellent, holy, pure.<BR>2 Being or existing in the nature of things.<BR>3 Animate, inherent in animals.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वानुरूप
सत्त्वानुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>According to nature or natural quality.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and अनुरूप conformable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वोत्साह|सत्त्वोत्साहः
सत्त्वोत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Natural energy or perseverance.<BR>E.<BR>सत्त्व, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पत्र|सत्पत्रं
सत्पत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पथ|सत्पथः
सत्पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A good road.<BR>2 Correct or virtuous conduct, doctrine, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and पथ a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्परिग्रह|सत्परिग्रहः
सत्परिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Acceptance of gifts from proper persons.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and परिग्रह acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पशु|सत्पशुः
सत्पशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>An animal fit for a sacrifice, a victim.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पात्र
सत्पात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A worthy or virtuous person.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पात्रवर्ष
सत्पात्रवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Judicious liberality, bestowing favours on the worthy.<BR>E.<BR>सत्पात्र, and वर्ष raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुत्त्र
सत्पुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 The father of a son.<BR>2 A virtuous son.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, or good, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुरुष|सत्पुरुषः
सत्पुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A worthy or spirited man.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and पुरुष a male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रतिपक्ष|सत्प्रतिपक्षः
सत्प्रतिपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Contrariety of doctrine or argument, knowledge of the opposite arguments proving the existence or non-existence of a thing.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, प्रतिपक्ष opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्फल|सत्फलः
सत्फल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्य|सत्यं|सत्यः
सत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 True.<BR>2 Sincere, honest, speaking the truth.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Truth.<BR>2 An oath.<BR>3 The first Yuga or age, the golden age, comprising one million seven hundred and twenty-eight thousand years.<BR>4 Demonstrated conclusion.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 RĀMACANDRA.<BR>2 The uppermost of the seven Lokas or worlds, the abode of BRAHMĀ, and heaven of truth.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR>2 The mother of Vyāsa.<BR>3 Speaking the truth, sincerity, veracity.<BR>ind. (सत्यम्)<BR>Indeed, verily, a particle of interrogation, and asseveration.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक|सत्यकं
सत्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>True, veracious.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Ratification of a bargain.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यङ्कार|सत्यंकार|सत्यंकारः|सत्यङ्कारः
सत्यङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Ratification of a bargain.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, कार making, confirming, सम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यङ्कारकृत|सत्यंकारकृत|सत्यङ्कारकृतः
सत्यङ्कारकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Given or deposited in order to bind or ratify a bargain.<BR>E.<BR>सत्यङ्कार as above, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यता
सत्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Truth, trueness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to सत्य; also with त्व, सत्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधन
सत्यधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Virtuous, sincere, upright.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and घन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभामा
सत्यभामा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>One of KṚṢṆA'S wives.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य true, भाम beautiful, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभारत|सत्यभारतः
सत्यभारत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>VYĀSA, the poet.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य true, भारत the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययुग|सत्ययुगं
सत्ययुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The first of the four Yugas or ages, the period of general virtue and purity, or golden age, comprising a term of 1,728,000 years.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययौवन|सत्ययौवनः
सत्ययौवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Vidyādhara or demigod so named.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यरत|सत्यरतः
सत्यरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Honest, sincere.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and रत devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवक्तृ
सत्यवक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>A speaker of truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and वक्तृ who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचन
सत्यवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Speaking truth.<BR>2 Acknowledging or admitting the truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचस्
सत्यवचस्<BR>mfn. (-चाः-चाः-चः)<BR>Speaking truth, veracious.<BR>m. (-चाः)<BR>A Ṛṣi, a saint, a seer.<BR>n. (-चः)<BR>Truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवत्|सत्यवन्त्
सत्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत)<BR>True, possessing or practising truth.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The name of a king.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>1 The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>2 The wife of NĀRADA.<BR>3 The wife of ṚṢIKA, a saint.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवतीसुत|सत्यवतीसुतः
सत्यवतीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>सत्यवती his mother's name, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवद्य
सत्यवद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>True-speaking, veracious.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and वद to speak, with क्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=885" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवाच्
सत्यवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Speaking the truth, veracious, sincere.<BR>m. (-वाक्)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 A Ṛṣi, a saint.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य true, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादित्व
सत्यवादित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Speaking truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्यवादिन्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादिन्
सत्यवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवृत्त|सत्यवृत्तः
सत्यवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Practising or speaking the truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and वृत्त chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यव्रत|सत्यव्रतः
सत्यव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Practising or adhering to the truth, veracious, honest, sincere.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A king, the 25th of the solar dynasty in the second age.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य the truth, व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसङ्काश|सत्यसंकाश|सत्यसङ्काशः
सत्यसङ्काश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Likely, probable, plausible, like the truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and सङ्काश like; also, similar compounds, as सत्यसन्निभ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसङ्गर|सत्यसंगर|सत्यसंगरः|सत्यसङ्गरः
सत्यसङ्गर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>True, veracious.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य the truth, सम् with गॄ to swallow, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसन्ध|सत्यसंध|सत्यसंधः|सत्यसन्धः
सत्यसन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Veracious, adhering to or observing the truth.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 BHARATA, the younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>2 The prince JANAMEJAYA.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the PĀṆḌU princes.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, सम् before धा to have or hold, aff. क<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसाक्षिन्
सत्यसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>An unexceptionable witness.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याकृति|सत्याकृतिः
सत्याकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Ratification of a bargain.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, आङ् before कृ to make, to confirm, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याग्नि|सत्याग्निः
सत्याग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य the truth, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यात्मन्
सत्यात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>True.<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A virtuous and upright man.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and आत्मन् same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानुरक्त
सत्यानुरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Upright, true.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and अनुरक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यान्टत
सत्यान्टत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Commerce, trade, traffick.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य truth, and अन्टत falsehood, a mixed practice of truth and lies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापन|सत्यापनं
सत्यापन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Ratification of a bargain.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य nominal verb, to speak or observe the truth, causal form, सत्याप, and ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योत्कर्ष|सत्योत्कर्षः
सत्योत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Eminence or excellence in truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य, and उत्कर्ष excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योद्य
सत्योद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Speaking the truth.<BR>E.<BR>सत्य the truth, उद्य to be said or uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Sacrifice, &c.; see सत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रप
सत्रप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Ashamed, modest.<BR>E.<BR>स with त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रिजातक|सत्रिजातकं
सत्रिजातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Meat which has been once fried with spices, &c. then soaked and dried, and again dressed with Ghee and condiments.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह, with त्रि three, जातक species of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्व
सत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The quality of excellence or goodness, &c.; see सत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वर|सत्वरं
सत्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, त्वरा dispatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वरता
सत्वरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Quickness, speed.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, सत्वरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संसर्ग|सत्संसर्गः
सत्संसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Association with the good or respectable.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and संसर्ग connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सङ्ग|सत्संग|सत्संगः
सत्सङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Association with the good.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and सङ्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सन्निधान|सत्संनिधान
सत्सन्निधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Association or intercourse with the wise and good.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and सन्निघान propinquity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्समागम|सत्समागमः
सत्समागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Association with the good.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and समागम encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सहाय|सत्सहायः
सत्सहाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Having a friend.<BR>2 Having virtuous friends.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, or good, &c. सहाय a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सार|सत्सारः
सत्सार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A painter.<BR>2 A poet.<BR>E.<BR>सत् excellence, सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कार|सथूत्कारः
सथूत्कार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Sputtering in speech.<BR>E.<BR>स for सहित with, थूत imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशक|सदंशकः
सदंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>स with, दंशक a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशवदन|सदंशवदनः
सदंशवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>स with, दंश a tooth or beak, and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद|सदः
सद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The fruit of trees.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदञ्जन|सदञ्जनं
सदञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, excellence, अञ्जन stibium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन|सदनं
सदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Perishing, decaying.<BR>4 Exhaustion.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go or perish, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदय
सदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Benevolent, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>स with, दया clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर
सदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Fearful, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>स with, दर fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्
सदस्<BR>fn. (-दाः-दः)<BR>An assembly, a meeting.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, (to which,) Uṇādi aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसत्|सदसन्त्
सदसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>1 Existent and non-existent.<BR>2 True and false.<BR>3 Perceptible and non-perceptible.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and असत् untrue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसदात्मक
सदसदात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Being both real and unreal, existent and non-existent, substantial though imperceptible.<BR>E.<BR>सदसत्, and आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसद्विवेक
सदसद्विवेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Discrimination between true and false, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सदसत्, and विवेक judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्य|सदस्यः
सदस्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>1 An assistant or by-stander at a sacrifice, &c. one whose business it is to notice and correct mistakes.<BR>2 Any person present at an assembly, a spectator, an assessor, a member, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सदस् an assembly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदा
सदा<BR>ind.<BR>Always, at all times.<BR>E.<BR>स for सर्व्व all, दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदागति|सदागतिः
सदागति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 Final happiness, emancipation from life.<BR>4 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, गति going, duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचार|सदाचारः
सदाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The traditionary observances of the Hindu castes, as preserved in the land lying between the Sarasvatī and Dṛṣadvatī rivers.<BR>2 Virtuous conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सत् pure, virtuous, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातन|सदातनः
सदातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Eternal.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, ट्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातोया
सदातोया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, and तोय water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदात्मन्
सदात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Good, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदादान|सदादानः
सदादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Liberality, munificence.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The elephant of INDRA.<BR>2 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 An elephant in must.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, दान giving, or the ichor that exudes from the elephant's temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=886" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन्द|सदानंद|सदानन्दः
सदानन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Always happy.<BR>E.<BR>सदा, and आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानर्त्त|सदानर्त|सदानर्तः|सदानर्त्तः
सदानर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, नर्त्त a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानीरवहा
सदानीरवहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A small river in the north of Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, नीर water, वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानीरा
सदानीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The Karatoya, a small river in the north of Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, नीर water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदापुष्प|सदापुष्पः
सदापुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A shrub, gigantic swallow-wort, the white variety.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाफल|सदाफलः
सदाफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The cocoanut tree.<BR>2 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>3 The jack, (Artocarpus integrifolia?)<BR>4 The Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभव्य
सदाभव्य<BR>mf. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Attentive, present.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, भव्य being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभद्रा
सदाभद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A shrub, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदायोगिन्
सदायोगिन्<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, योग union by meditation, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाशिव|सदाशिवः
सदाशिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सदा always, शिव auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाश्रित
सदाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Attached or belonging to the virtuous, pure, good, lovely, &c.<BR>2 Always connected with or dependant on.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, &c., or सदा always, and आश्रित connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदुत्तर
सदुत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A proper or good reply.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्ष|सदृक्षः
सदृक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् same, दृक्ष to see, क्म aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश्
सदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् same, दृश to see, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश|सदृशः
सदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Like, resembling, similar.<BR>2 Fit, proper, right.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् the same, दृश to see, aff. कञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृशता
सदृशता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Likeness, sameness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, सदृशंत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेश|सदेशः
सदेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Of the same country or place.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान the same, and देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गति|सद्गतिः
सद्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Felicity or fortune.<BR>2 Good conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गुण|सद्गुणः
सद्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Good, pure, virtuous.<BR>2 Excellent, eminent.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्धेतु|सद्धेतुः
सद्धेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>(In logic,) The co-existence of cause and effect.<BR>E.<BR>सत् being, हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भाव|सद्भावः
सद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A pure or holy disposition or nature.<BR>2 A good temper.<BR>3 Amiability, kindly feeling.<BR>4 The quality or nature of being, entity.<BR>5 The property of goodness.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भूत|सद्भूतः
सद्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>True.<BR>E.<BR>सत् true, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 Water.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मचिति
सद्मचिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A number of houses.<BR>E.<BR>सद्म, and चिति an assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःकृत|सद्यःकृतं
सद्यःकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done promptly or quickly.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A name, an appellation.<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस् instantly, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःशोथा
सद्यःशोथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस् instantly, and शोथा a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्
सद्यस्<BR>ind.<BR>Instantly, momentarily, at the moment, in an instant.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् the same, and द्यस for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्क|सद्यस्कः
सद्यस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>New, recent.<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस् in the moment, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्युवती
सद्युवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A virtuous maiden.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and युवती a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योजात|सद्योजातः
सद्योजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस् in a moment, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योभाविन्
सद्योभाविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस् in a moment, भाविन् being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु<BR>mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>1 Resting, staying.<BR>2 Going.<BR>E.<BR>सद to go or sit, रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वंश
सद्वंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Of high birth, of a good race.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and वंश a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वसथ|सद्वसथः
सद्वसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, वस to abide, अथच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वृत्त|सद्वृत्तं
सद्वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Amiable, well-behaved.<BR>2 Moral, virtuous.<BR>3 Well rounded, handsomely orbicular.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Amiableness, good or amiable disposition.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, and वृत्त, selected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधन
सधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wealthy, rich.<BR>E.<BR>स with, घन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मन्|सधर्मन्
सधर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Like, equal, resembling.<BR>2 Of the same sect or caste, performing like duties.<BR>3 Of the same or similar properties.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, घर्म्म merit, practice, and अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मचारिणी|सधर्मचारिणी
सधर्म्मचारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A wife, one married with religious rites.<BR>E.<BR>स with, (her husband,) घर्म्म duty, चारिणी who proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मिन्|सधर्मिन्
सधर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>Observing the same customs or laws.<BR>f. (-र्म्मिणी)<BR>A wife wedded according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>स same or with, घर्म्म virtue or duty, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधवा
सधवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A wife, whose husband is living.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, घव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधि|सधिः
सधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स with, धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिस्
सधिस्<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>An ox, a bull.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, Uṇādi aff. इसि, and ह changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्र्यञ्च्|सध्र्यंच्
सध्र्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-ध्र्यङ्-ध्रीची-ध्र्यक्)<BR>Accompanying, going with, a companion.<BR>f. (-ध्रीची)<BR>A woman's female friend, a confidante.<BR>E.<BR>सध्रि substituted for सह with, अञ्च to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन|सनः
सन<BR>mf. (-नः-नी)<BR>The flapping of an elephant's ears.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>2 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 GAURĪ.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>षन to give, to serve, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनक|सनकः
सनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 One of the companions of VIṢṆU, or four sons of BRAHMĀ, inhabiting the Janaloka.<BR>2 An inspired legislator.<BR>E.<BR>षन to serve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
सनत्<BR>m. (-नत्)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>ind.<BR>Always, perpetually.<BR>E.<BR>षन to serve or give, aff. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्कुमार|सनत्कुमारः
सनत्कुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of the four sons of BRAHMĀ, and eldest of the progenitors of mankind.<BR>2 One of the twelve emperors of India according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>सनत् always, कुमार a youth: i. e. continent; retaining the purity of that age, or being devoid of human passion; otherwise, सनत् BRAHMĀ, and कुमार son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्द|सनन्दः
सनन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>One of the four sons of BRAHMĀ, inhabiting the Janaloka.<BR>E.<BR>स with, नन्द pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनपर्णी
सनपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>सन the Asana or Pentaptera, and पर्ण a leaf; more usually असनपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=887" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनस्
सनस्<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>1 Excrement, ordure.<BR>2 ŚIVA'S trident (?)<BR>3 Crystal (?)<BR>E.<BR>षन to give, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनसूत्र|सनसूत्रं
सनसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Packthread, or a net made of it.<BR>E.<BR>see शणसूत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सना
सना<BR>ind.<BR>Always, eternally, perpetually.<BR>E.<BR>षण to serve, आच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातन|सनातनः
सनातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Eternal, continual, perpetual.<BR>2 Firm, fixed, permanent.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 BRAHMĀ.<BR>4 A guest of the Manes, or one who is to be fed whenever he chooses to attend the obsequial ceremonies or Śrāddhas.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>सना always, and द्यु or द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनात्
सनात्<BR>ind.<BR>Always, perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथा
सनाथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>A woman whose husband is living.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, नाथ a lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभि|सनाभिः
सनाभि<BR>mfn. (-भिः-भिः-भि)<BR>1 Like, resembling.<BR>2 Affectionate.<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>1 A kinsman, one of the same family name: it is considered also the same as the Sapiṇḍa or gentile, a relation as far as the seventh degree, and qualified to offer the funeral cake.<BR>2 A uterine brother.<BR>E.<BR>स with or same, नाभि navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामक|सनामकः
सनामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Morunga tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनि|सनिः
सनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 Service, worship.<BR>2 Giving, donation.<BR>mf. (-निः-नी)<BR>Request, solicitation, respectful solicitation as addressed to a spiritual preceptor, &c.<BR>2 Quarter, region, point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>षन to honour, to give, इनि Uṇādi aff., ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठीव|सनिष्ठीवं
सनिष्ठीव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sputtered speech, utterance interrupted by saliva.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह, with, निर् before ष्ठीव to eject saliva, घञ् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठेव|सनिष्ठेवं
सनिष्ठेव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Speech uttered with emission of saliva or sputtered.<BR>E.<BR>स with, नि before ष्ठीव to spit, aff. घञ्; also सनिष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीड|सनीडः
सनीड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, नीड nest or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुतर्
सनुतर्<BR>ind.<BR>Concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त|संत|संतः|सन्तः
सन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The hands opened and joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तत|संतत|सन्ततं
सन्तत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eternal, continual.<BR>2 Spread, extended.<BR>3 Continued, continuous.<BR>4 Much, many.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>Eternally.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तन to spread, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तताभ्यास|संतताभ्यास|सन्तताभ्यासः
सन्तताभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The regular study and perusal of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सन्तत constant, continual, and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तति|संतति|संततिः|सन्ततिः
सन्तति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Race, lineage.<BR>2 A son, a daughter, offspring, progeny.<BR>3 Descent, succession.<BR>4 A continuous line, a row, a range.<BR>5 Extent, expanse, spreading, stretching.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, equally, तन to spread, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्त|संतप्त|सन्तप्तः
सन्तप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Suffering pain or distress, distressed, afflicted, wretched.<BR>2 Suffering from extreme heat.<BR>3 Burnt, scorched.<BR>4 Inflamed with passion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तप to heat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस्|संतमस्
सन्तमस्<BR>n. (-मः)<BR>Great or universal darkness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, तमस् gloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस|संतमस|सन्तमसं
सन्तमस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Darkened, clouded.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and तमस darkness, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्ज्जन|सन्तर्जन|संतर्जन|संतर्जनं
सन्तर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Abusing, reproving, scolding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तज्ज to abuse, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्ज्जित|सन्तर्जित|संतर्जित
सन्तर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abused, scolded, reproved.<BR>E.<BR>सम before तर्ज्ज to abuse, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्पण|संतर्पण|संतर्पणं|सन्तर्पणं
सन्तर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Satisfying, satiating, gratifying.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तृप to be satisfied, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्पित|संतर्पित
सन्तर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Satisfied, satiated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तृप to be satisfied, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तान|संतान|संतानं|संतानः|सन्तानः
सन्तान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Family, race, lineage.<BR>2 Offspring, progeny, a son or daughter.<BR>3 One of the trees of heaven.<BR>4 Spreading, expansion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तन to spread, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तानक|संतानक|संतानकः
सन्तानक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What spreads, scatters, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The tree of heaven.<BR>f. (-निका)<BR>1 Cream, the coagulum of milk, &c.<BR>2 A cobweb.<BR>3 The blade of a knife or sword.<BR>4 Froth, foam.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तन to spread, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तानसन्धि|संतानसंधि|संतानसंधिः
सन्तानसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>Peace cemented by family alliance.<BR>E.<BR>सन्तान, and सन्धि peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप|संताप|संतापः|सन्तापः
सन्ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Heat, burning heat.<BR>2 Affliction, pain, distress.<BR>3 Passion.<BR>4 Repentance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, तप to heat, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापन|संतापन|संतापनः|सन्तापनः
सन्तापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Burning, scorching.<BR>2 Paining, affliction.<BR>3 Exciting passion.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA or love.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तप to heat, causal form, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापहर|संतापहर
सन्तापहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Cooling.<BR>2 Consolatory, consoling.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ताप, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापित|संतापित|सन्तापितः
सन्तापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-तां-तं)<BR>1 Pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR>2 Suffering from heat.<BR>3 Inflamed with passion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तप to burn, causal v., aff. क्त, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप्य|संताप्य
सन्ताप्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having caused to be heated.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, तप to be hot, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ति|संति|संतिः|सन्तिः
सन्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 End, destruction.<BR>2 Gift, giving.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give, क्तिच् aff.; also सति and साति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तुष्ट|संतुष्ट|सन्तुष्टः
सन्तुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Delighted, pleased.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive prefix, तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष|संतोष|संतोषः|सन्तोषः
सन्तोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Joy, pleasure, delight, satisfaction, happiness.<BR>2 Thumb and forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive prefix, तुष to be pleased, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोषण|संतोषण|संतोषणं
सन्तोषण<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pleasing, propitiating.<BR>2 Comforting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तुष to be pleased, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोषित|संतोषित
सन्तोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Consoled, comforted.<BR>2 Gratified.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तुष to be pleased, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष्टव्य|संतोष्टव्य
सन्तोष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be pleased, comforted, gratified, &c. सम्, तुष to be pleased, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष्य|संतोष्य
सन्तोष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having pleased or gratified.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before तुष to be pleased, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यक्त|संत्यक्त
सन्त्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Left, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and त्यज to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यजन|संत्यजन|संत्यजनं
सन्त्यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Leaving, abandoning.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, त्यज to leave, ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रस्त|संत्रस्त
सन्त्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Frightened, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before त्रस to fear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रास|संत्रास|संत्रासः
सन्त्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Fear, alarm.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before त्रस to fear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दंश|संदंश|संदंशः|सन्दंशः
सन्दंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A pair of tongs or nippers.<BR>E.<BR>सम with, दंश biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दंशक|संदंशक|संदंशकः
सन्दंशक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pair of tongs.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pair of nippers, or small shears or tongs.<BR>2 A vice.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दंश to bite or nip, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=888" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दधान
सन्दधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Having, possessing.<BR>2 Being at peace with, making peace.<BR>3 Fixing or placing in or on.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्भ|संदर्भ|संदर्भः|सन्दर्भः
सन्दर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 Weaving garlands, collecting flowers into a wreath or chaplet, &c.<BR>2 Stringing, collecting, arranging.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together, दृभि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शन|संदर्शन|संदर्शनं|सन्दर्शनं
सन्दर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Looking, seeing.<BR>2 Shewing.<BR>3 Appearance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, दर्शन seeing, or सम् before दृश to see, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शयत्
सन्दर्शयत्<BR>mfn. (-न्य-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Shewing, pointing out.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दृश to see, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शित|संदर्शित
सन्दर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shewn, pointed out.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दृश to see, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दान|संदान|संदानं|सन्दानं|संदानः|सन्दानः
सन्दान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A rope, a cord, (for tying cattle especially.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The elephant's temples, or part whence the ichorous fluid issues when the animal is in must.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दो to cut, aff. ल्युट्; or सम् with, दान the temporal juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानित|संदानित|सन्दानितः
सन्दानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दान a rope, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानिनी|संदानिनी
सन्दानिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A cow-house.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दान a rope for tying cattle, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दामितक|संदामितक
सन्दामितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A poem of three stanzas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दाव|संदाव|संदावः|सन्दावः
सन्दाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दु to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्ध|संदिग्ध|सन्दिग्धः
सन्दिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Doubted, questioned, doubtful.<BR>2 Entertaining doubt, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दिह to augment, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धमति|संदिग्धमति|सन्दिग्धमतिः
सन्दिग्धमति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A sceptic, one who is uncertain or doubtful of the results of religious observances, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दिग्ध doubted, doubting, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धनिश्चय|संदिग्धनिश्चय
सन्दिग्धनिश्चय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Confident in a doubtful matter.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दिग्ध, and निश्त्रय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धलेख्य|संदिग्धलेख्य
सन्दिग्धलेख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>A writing or document of doubtful meaning or authority.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दिग्ध, and, लेख्य a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धार्थ|संदिग्धार्थ|संदिग्धार्थः|सन्दिग्धार्थः
सन्दिग्धार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 A disputed debt, either in its amount or existence.<BR>2 Doubtful interpretation or meaning.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दिग्ध doubted, अर्थ property or meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दित|संदित|सन्दितः
सन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दो to cut, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिदर्शयिषु|संदिदर्शयिषु
सन्दिदर्शयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to shew.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दृश to see, causal v., desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिशत्
सन्दिशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शती-शत्)<BR>Informing, telling.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दिश to shew, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिष्ट|संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं|संदिष्टः
सन्दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Told, communicated, related as news or information.<BR>2 Promised, agreed, engaged.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>News, tidings, information.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, दिश to shew, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिष्टार्थ|संदिष्टार्थ|सन्दिष्टार्थः
सन्दिष्टार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A herald, a pursuivant, a royal messenger who communicated oral instructions or orders.<BR>E.<BR>सन्दिष्ट communicated, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिहान|सन्दिहानः
सन्दिहान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-न)<BR>Dubious, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दिह to collect, aff. शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्यमान
सन्दिह्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Doubtful, uncertain, obscure.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दिह to collect, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दी|संदी
सन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>A small bed or couch.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दो to cut, aff. ड, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्य|संदीप्य|सन्दीप्यः
सन्दीप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृष्ट|संदृष्ट
सन्दृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Seen, beheld.<BR>2 Foreseen, anticipated.<BR>E.<BR>सम दृश, to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्यमान
सन्दृश्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being seen or looked at.<BR>2 Being foreseen.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दृश to see, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देश|संदेश|संदेशः|सन्देशः
सन्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>News, tidings, information.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, दिश to shew, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशवाच्|संदेशवाच्
सन्देशवाच्<BR>mf. (-वाक्)<BR>Communication of intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>सन्देश news, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशहर|संदेशहर|संदेशहरः|सन्देशहरः
सन्देशहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador.<BR>E.<BR>सन्देश tidings, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशहारक|संदेशहारक|संदेशहारकः|सन्देशहारकः
सन्देशहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador.<BR>E.<BR>सन्देश news, and हारक who conveys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देह|संदेह|संदेहः|सन्देहः
सन्देह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दिह to collect, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दोह|संदोह|संदोहः|सन्दोहः
सन्दोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Assemblage, multitude.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, दुह to fill, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्राव|संद्राव|संद्रावः|सन्द्रावः
सन्द्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, द्रु to go, to run, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध|संध
सन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>1 Possessing as an integrant part, intimately blended with.<BR>2 Holding, possessing, having placed in or on.<BR>3 Joined, united.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 Promise, assent, agreement.<BR>2 State, condition, the steady continuance in any state, steadiness, fixation.<BR>3 Intimate union or association, identification.<BR>4 Twilight.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, धा to have or hold, aff. क, or अङ् and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धातव्य|संधातव्य
सन्धातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be united or allied with, to be reconciled, to be connected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धा to have, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धान|संधान|संधानं|सन्धानं
सन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Holding together, uniting, joining.<BR>2 Tying, binding.<BR>3 Peace, alliance.<BR>4 Association, company.<BR>5 Supporting, reception, receiving, sustaining.<BR>6 Mixing, joining, intimate union or combination.<BR>7 A relish, something eaten to excite thirst.<BR>8 Sour rice-gruel.<BR>9 Pickles, &c. acid preparation of the Bel and other fruits.<BR>10 Spirituous liquor.<BR>11 Contracting the skin, &c. by astringent applications.<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>Distillation, distilling, the manufacture of spirituous liquors.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A braziery, a foundery, a place where the base metals are stored or wrought.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, धा to hold, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानकरण|संधानकरण
सन्धानकरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Who or what heals, re-unites, allies, connecting, re-uniting, &c.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Uniting, combining.<BR>2 Healing.<BR>3 Allying, making peace.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धान, and करण making, the act or instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानकर्त्तृ|सन्धानकर्तृ
सन्धानकर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Uniting, connecting, healing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धान, and कर्त्तृ what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानित|संधानित|सन्धानितः
सन्धानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bound, tied.<BR>2 Strung together.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धान holding together, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानिनी|संधानिनी
सन्धानिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A cow-house.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धान a binding, इनि and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारण|संधारण|संधारणं
सन्धारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Holding, observing, practising.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धृ to hold, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धार्य्य|सन्धार्य|संधार्य
सन्धार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be observed or followed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धृ to hold, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धि|संधि|संधिः|सन्धिः
सन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>1 Union, junction, connexion, combination.<BR>2 Peace, making peace, pacification.<BR>3 A hole, a chasm. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">Page890</a>]<BR>4 A hole made in a wall or underneath it to enter a building for hostile or felonious purposes, a breach, a mine, &c.<BR>5 Breaking, dividing.<BR>6 The vulva.<BR>7 A division of a drama, apparently applicable to each subject represented or sentiment excited, as considered severally and detached from the rest, though contributing to the connexion of the whole; contrast of incident, change of situation, transition of passion or emotion, &c.<BR>8 An interval, a pause or rest.<BR>9 A joint, an articulation of the body.<BR>10 The union of letters, either at the end and beginning of different words, or in the middle of compound terms, to avoid dissonance or hiatus.<BR>11 A period at the expiration of each Yuga or age, or one-sixth of its duration, intervening before the commencement of the next; a Sandhi, also, of the same length as the Satya Yug, occurs at the end of each Manvantara, and each Kalpa.<BR>12 (In mensuration,) The connecting link of a perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, धा to have or hold, aff. कि of either the act, condition or instrument; whence the word becomes applicable to a chasm, &c. as to an interval, which whilst it divides, also connects, two parts or places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=889" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिका|संधिका
सन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Distillation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, धा to have, aff. क, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिचौर|संधिचौर|सन्धिचौरः
सन्धिचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a breach, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिजीवक|संधिजीवक|संधिजीवकः|सन्धिजीवकः
सन्धिजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who seeks for wealth by dishonest means, especially as a go-between.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि union, (of others,) and जीवक who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित|संधित|सन्धितः
सन्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tied, bound, strung, fastened together.<BR>2 Allied, united, reconciled.<BR>3 Pickled.<BR>(-तं)<BR>Pickles and preparations of various fruits.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धा union, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित्सु|संधित्सु
सन्धित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing to be at peace or in alliance with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धा to have, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिनी|संधिनी
सन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी).<BR>1 A cow with calf, or one which has taken the bull.<BR>2 One who is milked unseasonably.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धा joining, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिबन्ध|संधिबन्ध|सन्धिबन्धः
सन्धिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A flower, (Kæmpferia rotunda.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिबन्धन|संधिबन्धन|संधिबंधन|सन्धिबन्धनं
सन्धिबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A tendon, a nerve, a ligament.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a joint, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिरन्ध्रका|संधिरन्ध्रका
सन्धिरन्ध्रका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A hole or breach in a wall.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a breach, रन्ध्र a hole, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिला|संधिला
सन्धिला<BR>f. (-ला).<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>3 A hole in a wall, a breach.<BR>4 A chasm, a pit, a mine.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a hole, &c. लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविग्रहाधिकार|संधिविग्रहाधिकार
सन्धिविग्रहाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>War ministry, charge of peace and war.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि, विग्रह war, अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविग्रहाधिकारिन्|संधिविग्रहाधिकारिन्
सन्धिविग्रहाधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>Chief political minister.<BR>E.<BR>इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविचक्षण|संधिविचक्षण|संधिविचक्षणः
सन्धिविचक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An able negociator.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि, and विचक्षण skilled; also similar compounds, as सन्धिकुशल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविद्|संधिविद्
सन्धिविद्<BR>m. (-वित्)<BR>A negociator, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिवेला|संधिवेला
सन्धिवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A particular period, and one which connects the part of the day or fortnight, as morning, noon, and evening, new moon, the first or thirteenth day of the fortnight, and full moon.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि union, and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिहारक|संधिहारक|संधिहारकः|सन्धिहारकः
सन्धिहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a breach, and हारक who carries away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षित|संधुक्षित
सन्धुक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lighted, inflamed, kindled.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before घुक्ष to kindle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धेय|संधेय
सन्धेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be joined, united, &c.<BR>2 To be reconciled or at peace with.<BR>3 To be allied, connected, &c., what or who may or ought to be allied, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before धा to have यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्या|संध्या
सन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>1 Twilight, either morning or evening.<BR>2 The period that elapses between the expiration of one Yuga or age, and the commencement of another.<BR>3 A period of time, forenoon, afternoon, or mid-day.<BR>4 Religious abstraction, meditation, repetition of Mantras, sipping water, &c. to be performed by the three first classes of Hindus, at particular and stated periods in the course of every day, especially at sunrise, sunset, and also, though less essentially, at noon.<BR>5 Reflexion.<BR>6 Promise, assent.<BR>7 Boundary, limit.<BR>8 Joining, union.<BR>9 A flower; according to some the tuberose, to others, the jasmine.<BR>10 Twilight, personified as the daughter of BRAHMĀ, and wife of ŚIVA.<BR>11 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धि a joint, (of the day,) and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यांश|संध्यांश|संध्यांशः|सन्ध्यांशः
सन्ध्यांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Twilight.<BR>2 The period at the end of each Yuga.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या as above, and अंश portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यांशु|संध्यांशु|संध्यांशुः
सन्ध्यांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>Twilight.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याकाल|संध्याकाल|संध्याकालः
सन्ध्याकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Twilight.<BR>2 The intervals of a Yuga.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याचल|संध्याचल|सन्ध्याचलः
सन्ध्याचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या twilight, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यात्रय|संध्यात्रय
सन्ध्यात्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The three periods of the day.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यानाटिन्|संध्यानाटिन्
सन्ध्यानाटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या evening twilight, and नाटिन् who dances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याबल|संध्याबल|संध्याबलः|सन्ध्याबलः
सन्ध्याबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An imp, a Rākṣasa, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या evening, and बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याबलि|संध्याबलि|संध्याबलिः|सन्ध्याबलिः
सन्ध्याबलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Any image of NANDĪ, the bull of ŚIVA, either of clay, wood, or stone, placed in a temple of the deity.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या evening, (when ŚIVA is worshipped,) and बलि an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याभ्र|संध्याभ्र|सन्ध्याभ्रं
सन्ध्याभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>A sort of red chalk, that called golden.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या twilight, and अभ्र talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याराग|संध्याराग|सन्ध्यारागं|संध्यारागः
सन्ध्याराग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Redlead.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या twilight, and राग the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याराम|संध्याराम|संध्यारामः|सन्ध्यारामः
सन्ध्याराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या the daughter of the deity, of whom he became enamoured, and आङ् before रम to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यासमय|संध्यासमय|संध्यासमयः
सन्ध्यासमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Evening twilight.<BR>2 The period after each Yuga.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न|सन्नः
सन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Shrunk, diminished.<BR>2 Lost, gone.<BR>3 Still, motionless.<BR>4 Dispirited.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>A little, a small quantity.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नक|सन्नकः
सन्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, commonly Piyāl: see the सन्नकद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नकण्ठ
सन्नकण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>Choking, choked, scarce able to articulate.<BR>E.<BR>सन्न gone, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=890" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नकद्रु|सन्नकद्रुः
सन्नकद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, commonly Piyāl, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>सन्नक said to mean here, sharp, hot, and द्रु a tree; also सन्नक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नत|संनत
सन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, bowed down.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नति|संनति|संनतिः|सन्नतिः
सन्नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Reverence, obeisance, reverential salutation.<BR>2 Humility.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before नम to bow, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नद्ध|संनद्ध|सन्नद्धः
सन्नद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Armed, mailed, accoutred.<BR>2 Arranged, arrayed, prepared for battle.<BR>3 Murderous, felonious, provided with arms for the destruction of others.<BR>4 Wearing amulets, provided with charms, &c.<BR>5 Near, at hand.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before नह to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नय|संनय|संनयः|सन्नयः
सन्नय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Multitude, number, quantity.<BR>2 Rear, rear-guard.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, नी to get or guide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नहर्ष
सन्नहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Destitute of joy, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>सन्न gone, हर्ष joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह|संनाह|संनाहः|सन्नाहः
सन्नाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Armour, mail, either of iron or thick quilted cotton.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before नह to bind, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह्य|संनाह्य|संनाह्यः|सन्नाह्यः
सन्नाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A war elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सन्नाह armour, यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्ष|संनिकर्ष|संनिकर्षः|सन्निकर्षः
सन्निकर्ष<BR>mf. (-र्षः-र्षा)<BR>Proximity, nearness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, नि before कृष to attract, aff. अच्, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्षण|संनिकर्षण|संनिकर्षणं|सन्निकर्षणं
सन्निकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Proximity.<BR>2 Approximation, approximating, bringing or approaching near to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before कृष to make furrows, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकृष्ट|संनिकृष्ट|सन्निकृष्टः
सन्निकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नि prefixed to कृष to make furrows, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निक्षार|संनिक्षार
सन्निक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Piyāl tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नि before क्षर to ooze, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निचय|संनिचय|संनिचयः
सन्निचय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Collected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, निचय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निध|संनिध|सन्निधं
सन्निध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Proximity.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नि before धा to have, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधातृ|संनिधातृ
सन्निधातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Receiving, keeping in deposit or near to, who or what places near to, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नि before धा to have, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधान|संनिधान|संनिधानं|सन्निधानं
सन्निधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Proximity.<BR>2 Appearance, perceptibility.<BR>3 Placing, depositing.<BR>4 Receiving, taking charge of.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and नि before धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधाय
सन्निधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having placed or placed near at hand.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधि|संनिधि|संनिधिः|सन्निधिः
सन्निधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Proximity, approximation.<BR>2 Perceptibility, presence, appearance, becoming or being visible or perceptible.<BR>3 Placing.<BR>4 Receiving.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before धा to have, and कि aff.; also सन्निध and सन्निधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपतित|संनिपतित|सन्निपतितः
सन्निपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Assembled, collected.<BR>2 Mixed, blended.<BR>3 Alighted, descended.<BR>4 Come, arrived.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before पत to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपात|संनिपात|संनिपातः|सन्निपातः
सन्निपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Collection, assemblage, multitude.<BR>2 Union, junction, contact.<BR>3 Mixture, miscellaneous collection.<BR>4 Morbid state of the three humours.<BR>5 Alighting, descending.<BR>6 Arrival.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before पत to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपातक|संनिपातक|संनिपातकः
सन्निपातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Dangerous illness.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबद्ध|संनिबद्ध|सन्निबद्धः
सन्निबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound firmly, fast tied or fettered.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि intensitives, बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्ध|संनिबन्ध|सन्निबंध|संनिबंधः|संनिबन्धः
सन्निबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Binding, tying.<BR>2 Connexion, consequence.<BR>3 Effectiveness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, or सत् good, निबन्ध fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्धन|संनिबन्धन|सन्निबन्धनं
सन्निबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Binding or tying fast.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि intensitives, and बन्धन tying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निभ|संनिभ|सन्निभः
सन्निभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and निभ like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमग्न|संनिमग्न
सन्निमग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Immersed, plunged in.<BR>2 Asleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and निमग्न immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमित्त|संनिमित्त
सन्निमित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>For a good cause, for the sake of the good.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and निमित्त cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियुक्त|संनियुक्त
सन्नियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Appointed, employed.<BR>2 Attached to, connected with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before युज to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियोग|संनियोग|संनियोगः
सन्नियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Attachment or application to, connection or union with.<BR>2 Deputation, appointment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before युज to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरुद्ध|संनिरुद्ध
सन्निरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Stopped, obstructed, checked.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before रुघ to oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरोध|संनिरोध|संनिरोधः
सन्निरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Hindrance, check, obstruction, suppression.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before रुघ to hinder, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निविष्ट|संनिविष्ट|सन्निविष्टः
सन्निविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Near, present, at hand.<BR>2 Entered into.<BR>3 Collected, assembled.<BR>4 Neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before विश to enter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवेश|संनिवेश|संनिवेशः|सन्निवेशः
सन्निवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An open space, either in a town or its vicinity, where the people take exercise or diversion.<BR>2 Vicinity, proximity, neighbourhood.<BR>3 Fabrication, manufacture, construction, preparation.<BR>4 Putting in, causing to enter.<BR>5 Union, junction.<BR>6 Assemblage, collection.<BR>7 The collective form or figure of an asterism.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before विश to enter, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्त|संनिवृत्त
सन्निवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Ceasing, forbearing.<BR>2 Stopped, ceased.<BR>3 Returned, coming back.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before वृत्त to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्ति|संनिवृत्ति|संनिवृत्तिः|सन्निवृत्तिः
सन्निवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Restraint, forbearance, avoiding, forsaking.<BR>2 Returning, coming back.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and निवृत्ति desisting, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निषण्ण|संनिषण्ण
सन्निषण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>Stationary, seated, halted.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before षद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निहित|संनिहित|सन्निहितं
सन्निहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Near, proximate, at hand, present.<BR>2 Staying. being.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, निहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निहितापाय|संनिहितापाय
सन्निहितापाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Transient, brief.<BR>E.<BR>सन्निहित, and अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मान|सन्मानः
सन्मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Respect for the good.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मार्ग
सन्मार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Good or virtuous conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सत्, and मार्ग a way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यसन|संन्यसन|संन्यसनं
सन्न्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abandonment of the world.<BR>2 Entrusting to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before अस to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्त|संन्यस्त|सन्न्यस्तः
सन्न्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Abandoned, deserted.<BR>2 Entrusted or delivered to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्य
सन्न्यस्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having left or abandoned.<BR>2 Having consigned or delivered to.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before अस to throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यास|संन्यास|संन्यासः|सन्न्यासः
सन्न्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Abandonment of all worldly affections and possessions.<BR>2 Abandonment in general.<BR>3 Deposit, trust, or relinquishment to.<BR>5 Sudden death.<BR>6 Indian spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and नि before अस to throw, to cast off, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=891" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यासिन्|संन्यासिन्
सन्न्यासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 The Brahman of the fourth order, the religious mendicant.<BR>2 An ascetic, a devotee.<BR>E.<BR>सन्न्यास abandonment of the world, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपक्ष|सपक्षः
सपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Winged.<BR>2 Having a side or party.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A partisan, a follower, an adherent, one of the same side or party.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same, and पक्ष party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्रकृत
सपत्रकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distressed, afflicted.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A wounded deer or other animal.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, पत्र the leaf, the barb of the arrow, and कृत made; also सपत्राकृत, &c. being metaphorically applied to distress or pain in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकरण|सपत्त्राकरणं|सपत्राकरणं
सपत्राकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Excessive pain: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकृति|सपत्त्राकृतिः|सपत्राकृतिः
सपत्राकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Agony, affliction, excessive pain or distress: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्न|सपत्नः
सपत्न<BR>m. (-त्वः)<BR>An enemy, an adversary.<BR>f. (-त्वी)<BR>A woman whose husband has other wives.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान the same, पति a husband, ङीष् aff. and नुक् augment, अच् added for the masc. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नारि|सपत्नारिः
सपत्नारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A sort of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपदि
सपदि<BR>ind.<BR>1 Instantly, in a moment, at the moment.<BR>2 Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पद to go, इन् aff. and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्य्या|सपर्या
सपर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Worship, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>सपर Kaṇḍvādi root, said to imply worship, यक् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्ड|सपिंड|सपिंडः|सपिण्डः
सपिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kinsman, especially one connected by the offering of the funeral cake to either or all of the manes of the father, grandfather, and great-grandfather, and their wives respectively, as sprung from them in directly collateral lines; the relationship stops with every fourth person, as the fifth cannot perform the offering of a cake to the father even of the deceased. The following are enumerated as Sapiṇḍas; the son, son's son, and son's grandson; widow, daughter and daughter's son; the father, the mother, the brother, brother's son, and brother's grandson; father's daughter's son; father's brother's son and grandson; paternal grandfather's daughter's son; paternal grandfather; paternal grandmother, paternal grandfather's brother, brother's son and grandson; and lastly the great grandfather's daughter's son: these all present oblations in which the deceased is either included, or may participate: other enumerations, including the oblations he was bound to offer, &c. extend the connection of Sapiṇḍa to seven persons both in an ascending or descending line.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान common, and पिण्ड ball of meat, &c. offered to the manes of the deceased ancestors, at the Śrāddhas performed in honor of them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डीकरण|सपिंडीकरणं|सपिण्डीकरणं
सपिण्डीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Offering food to the deceased relatives called Sapiṇḍas: see the last.<BR>2 Investing a person with the rights of relationship, indicated by offering the funeral cake.<BR>E.<BR>सपिण्ड, करण making, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डीकृत
सपिण्डीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Comprehended in the relationship of Sapiṇḍa or offering of a common cake.<BR>E.<BR>सपिण्ड, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीति|सपीतिः
सपीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Drinking together.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, and पा to drink, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तक|सप्तकः
सप्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं)<BR>1 Seven.<BR>2 Seventh.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A collection of seven stanzas of the Ṛg Vedas.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A woman's girdle.<BR>E.<BR>सप्तन् seven, (strings, &c.) कन् and घातु or ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तजिह्व|सप्तजिह्वः
सप्तजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>AGNI, or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and जिह्वा a tongue or flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तज्वाल|सप्तज्वालः
सप्तज्वाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, ज्वाला a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ततन्तु|सप्ततन्तुः
सप्ततन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A sacrifice, an offering or oblation.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, (prayers, or the tongues of AGNI,) तन to spread, aff. तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तति|सप्ततिः
सप्तति<BR>f. sing. (-तिः)<BR>Seventy.<BR>du. (-ती)<BR>Two seventies.<BR>plu. (-तयः)<BR>Many seventies.<BR>E.<BR>सप्तन् seven, डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदश|सप्तदशः
सप्तदश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Seventeenth.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, दशन् seventeen, aff. डट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदशन्
सप्तदशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Seventeen.<BR>E.<BR>सप्तन seven, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदीधिति|सप्तदीधितिः
सप्तदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, दीधिति a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधा
सप्तधा<BR>ind.<BR>In seven ways.<BR>E.<BR>सप्तन् seven, धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधातु
सप्तधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The seven parts of the body, or chyle, blood, flesh, adeps, marrow, bone, and semen.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and घातु element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तन्
सप्तन्<BR>mfn. plu. only (सप्त)<BR>Seven.<BR>E.<BR>षप to be collected, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपर्ण|सप्तपर्णं|सप्तपर्णः
सप्तपर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Seven-leaved.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A tree, (Alstonia scholaris.)<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A sort of sweetmeat, made of the expressed juice of the grape, pomegranate and date, with sugar, spices, honey, and Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपुत्त्रसू
सप्तपुत्त्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of seven children.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, पुत्त्र a child, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तप्रकृति|सप्तप्रकृतिः
सप्तप्रकृति<BR>plu. (-तयः)<BR>The seven constituent parts of a kingdom, or prince, minister, city, country, treasure, force, and ally or friend.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and प्रकृति constituent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तभद्र|सप्तभद्रः
सप्तभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The Sirisha tree, (Acacia Sirisa.)<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तम|सप्तमः
सप्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Seventh.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The seventh day of the fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>सप्तन् seven, डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तरक्त|सप्तरक्तं|सप्तरक्तः
सप्तरक्त<BR>m. plu. (-क्ताः)<BR>The seven external parts of the body of a red colour, or the palms of the hands, the soles of the feet, the corners of the eyes, the tongue, the palate, the lips and nails.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and रक्त red or blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तरात्र
सप्तरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A period of seven nights.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तर्षि
सप्तर्षि<BR>m. plu. (-र्षयः)<BR>The constellation Ursa Major, the seven stars of which are the seven great saints, MARĪCI, ATRI, AṄGIRAS, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, and VASIṢṬHA.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and ऋषि a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तला
सप्तला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Double jasmine, (J. zambac fl. multiplicatis.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR>3 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>4 A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, (leaves, &c.) ला to get or have, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्ति|सप्तसप्तिः
सप्तसप्ति<BR>m. (-प्तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and सप्ति a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तहस्त
सप्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Of seven cubits.<BR>2 Having seven hands, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and हस्त a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तांशुपुङ्गव|सप्तांशुपुंगव|सप्तांशुपुङ्गवः
सप्तांशुपुङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The planet SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, अंशु a ray of light, पुङ्गव eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=892" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताङ्ग
सप्ताङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Having seven members or parts.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तार्च्चिस्|सप्तार्चिस्
सप्तार्च्चिस्<BR>mfn. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>Evil-eyed.<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>1 AGNI or fire.<BR>2 The planet SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and अर्च्चिस् a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताश्व|सप्ताश्वः
सप्ताश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तास्र
सप्तास्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A heptagon.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताह|सप्ताहः
सप्ताह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A week.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त, and अह for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ति|सप्तिः
सप्ति<BR>m. (-प्तिः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>षप to be collected, (in a troop,) ति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफर|सफरः
सफर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A small glistening fish, commonly Punthi, a sort of carp, (Cyprinus sophore, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>श the initial changed to सः see शफर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफल|सफलं
सफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>Productive, fruitful, bearing fruit, yielding a profit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबधूक
सबधूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man with his wife.<BR>E.<BR>स with, बधू a wife, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबलि|सबलिः
सबलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Evening twilight.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, बलि offering of food to evil spirits; the proper hour for such ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध|सबाधः
सबाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Painful, hurtful.<BR>2 Oppressive, extortionary.<BR>E.<BR>स with, बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचर्य्य|सब्रह्मचर्य|सब्रह्मचर्यं
सब्रह्मचर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Studying together, being disciples of one teacher.<BR>E.<BR>स with, ब्रह्मचर्य्य studentship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचारिन्
सब्रह्मचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A fellow student, one engaged in the same studies and observing the same austerities.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, and ब्रह्मचारिन् the religious student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभय
सभय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearing, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>स with, भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभर्त्तृका|सभर्तृका
सभर्त्तृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose husband is alive.<BR>E.<BR>स with, भर्त्तृ a husband, कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभा
सभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 An assembly, a meeting.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह together, भा to shine, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाज
सभाज<BR>r. 10th cl. (सभाजयति)<BR>1 To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>2 To please or satisfy.<BR>3 To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजन|सभाजनं
सभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Courtesy, politeness, civility in receiving or taking leave of a friend.<BR>E.<BR>सभाज to please or gratify, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजित
सभाजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Treated with courtesy, gratified, pleased.<BR>E.<BR>सभाज to please, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभापति|सभापतिः
सभापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>2 The president of an assembly.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, (of gamblers, &c.) and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभावशकर
सभावशकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Influencing or fascinating an assembly.<BR>E.<BR>सभा, and वशकर what subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभासद्
सभासद्<BR>m. (-सत् or सद्)<BR>One of a company, an assistant at an assembly or meeting; (in law,) an assessor.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, and सद् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभास्तार|सभास्तारः
सभास्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An assistant at an assembly, one of a company.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, and स्तृ to cover, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभिक|सभिकः
सभिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, ठक् aff; also with the penultimate vowel made long सभीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीक|सभीकः
सभीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The keeper of a gaming house: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभोचित|सभोचितः
सभोचित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman or teacher.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, and उचित fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्य|सभ्यः
सभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>1 Trusted, confidential, faithful.<BR>2 Relating to an assembly, fit for or suitable to it.<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>1 An assistant at an assembly.<BR>2 An assessor.<BR>3 A person of honourable parentage.<BR>4 The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>E.<BR>सभा an assembly, &c. य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यतम
सभ्यतम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A distinguished person, one who is an ornament of society.<BR>E.<BR>सभ्य, and तमप् affix of superl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यता
सभ्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Politeness, refinement in manners.<BR>E.<BR>सभ्य, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix implying;<BR>1 Union, junction, (with, together.)<BR>2 Assemblage, collection.<BR>3 Beauty or perfection.<BR>4 Intensity. As a prefix it corresponds to con, co, com, &c. Before a consonant the final of this word is changed to Anusvāra, and is written सं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम<BR>mfn. pron. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 All, whole, entire.<BR>(adj.)<BR>2 Like, similar.<BR>3 Good, virtuous.<BR>4 Full, complete.<BR>5 Same, even, equal.<BR>6 Indifferent, impartial.<BR>7 Mean.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A year.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A figure of rhetoric, identity or sameness of objects compared to one another.<BR>2 (In geometry,) A mean; a fourth proportional to the two perpendiculars and the link or segment.<BR>E.<BR>सम to be confused or unconfused, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकन्या
समकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A girl fit to be married.<BR>E.<BR>सम complete, कन्या a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकाल|समकालः
समकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The same time, the same moment.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकोल|समकोलः
समकोल<BR>m. (-लं)<BR>A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्न|समक्नः
समक्न<BR>m. (-क्नः-क्ना-क्नं)<BR>Going or moving equally, kept equal or together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अञ्च to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्ष|समक्षं
समक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Before, in presence or sight of, visible.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with अक्षि the eye, aff. टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समखात|समखातः
समखात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An oblong excavation, thence also a parallelopipedon, (in geometry.)<BR>E.<BR>सम equal, खात dug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समगन्धक|समगन्धकः
समगन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Compounded perfume.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, even, गन्ध smell, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समग्र|समग्रः
समग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>All, entire, whole, full, complete.<BR>E.<BR>सम the whole, ग्रह to take, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समङ्गा|समंगा
समङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>2 A sort of fern, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>3 A sort of sensitive plant.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अगि to go or grow, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचित्त|समचित्तं
समचित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Indifferent, unattached.<BR>2 Equable, even tempered.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and चित्त the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचित्तत्व
समचित्तत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Indifference.<BR>2 Equanimity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, समचित्तता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज|समजं|समजः
समज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A multitude of beasts.<BR>2 A number of blockheads.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A forest, a wood.<BR>E.<BR>सम alike, जन to be born, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्ञा
समज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Fame, reputation.<BR>E.<BR>सम all, ज्ञा to know, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्या
समज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 An assembly, a meeting.<BR>2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अज to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समञ्जस|समंजस|समञ्जसं|समञ्जसः
समञ्जस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Proper, right, fit.<BR>2 Exercised, experienced.<BR>3 Correct, accurate, true.<BR>4 Virtuous, good.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together with, अञ्जसा truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समण्ठ|समण्ठः
समण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A potherb, a sort of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=893" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समता
समता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Sameness, similarity, equality.<BR>E.<BR>सम equal, like, तल् aff.; also समत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम|समतिक्रमः
समतिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Deviating from, transgressing.<BR>2 Going over or beyond.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and अति before क्रम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रान्त
समतिक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Surpassed, exceeded.<BR>2 Gone over or beyond.<BR>3 Transgressed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अति before क्रम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिरिक्त|समतिरिक्तं
समतिरिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Much, exceeding, abundant.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, and अतिरिक्त much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्रिभुज|समत्रिभुजः
समत्रिभुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An equilateral triangle.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and त्रिभुज triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतीत
समतीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Past, gone.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अतीत past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्विष्
समत्विष्<BR>mfn. (-त्विट्)<BR>Equally bright or lovely.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and त्विष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्सर
समत्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Envious, jealous.<BR>E.<BR>स with, मत्सर envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदर्शिन्
समदर्शिन्<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>Impartial, equally viewing both sides.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदुःख
समदुःख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Sympathizing, feeling for another's woe.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and दुःख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिक|समधिकः
समधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Exceeding, abundant, plentiful.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगमन|समधिगमनं
समधिगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Surpassing, overcoming.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अधि before गम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधृत
समधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Equal or equivalent to.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समध्व
समध्व<BR>mfn. (-ध्वः-ध्वा-ध्वं)<BR>Travelling in company.<BR>E.<BR>सम् same, अध्वन् a road, the final dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञात
समनुज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Assented or agreed to, permitted. allowed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and अनु before ज्ञा to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञान|समनुज्ञानं
समनुज्ञान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Permitted, allowed.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Assent, concurrence, permission.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and अनु before ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुव्रत
समनुव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Entirely devoted to.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अनुब्रत devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त|समंत|समन्तः
समन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>All, entire, universal.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Limit, term, boundary, end.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्ततस्
समन्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 All round, on every side.<BR>2 Wholly, altogether.<BR>E.<BR>सम with, अन्त end, term, तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तदुग्धा
समन्तदुग्धा<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>The milk hedge-plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>समन्त every way, दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तभद्र|समंतभद्र|समन्तभद्रः
समन्तभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A Jina or Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>समन्त every way, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तभुज्|समंतभुज्
समन्तभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>समन्त universally, भुज what eats or consumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तात्
समन्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>All around, on every side.<BR>E.<BR>समन्त in the fifth case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्यु|समन्युः
समन्यु<BR>mfn. (-न्युः-न्युः-न्यु)<BR>Fierce, angry, enraged.<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, मन्यु wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वय|समन्वयः
समन्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Connected consequence.<BR>2 Natural succession or order.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अन्वय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वित|समन्वितः
समन्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Possessed of, endowed with, possessing, affected with, full of.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive or conjunctive, and अन्वित endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपाद|समपादं
समपाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet even.<BR>E.<BR>सम even, पाद the foot; also read समपद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समबुद्धि
समबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Philosophical, stoical, looking on all things alike, calm, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभाव|समभावः
समभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Of like nature or property.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Equability.<BR>2 Sameness.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिप्लुत
समभिप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Overwhelmed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अभि before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिसरण|समभिसरणं
समभिसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Seeking, wishing, endeavouring to gain.<BR>2 Approaching, going to or against.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अभि before सृ to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहरण
समभिहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking, seizing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अभि before सृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहार|समभिहारः
समभिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Repetition, reiteration.<BR>2 Excess, surplus.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, अभि before हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभूमि|समभूमिः
समभूमि<BR>f. (-भिः)<BR>Even ground.<BR>E.<BR>सम even, and भूमि ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्यर्च्चन|समभ्यर्चन|समभ्यर्चनं
समभ्यर्च्चन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Worshipping, reverencing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अभि before अर्च्च to worship, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्यर्च्चित|समभ्यर्चित
समभ्यर्च्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Honoured, worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अभि before अर्च्च to respect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समम्
समम्<BR>ind.<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>षम् to be confused or unconfused, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममय
सममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Of like origin, proceeding from the same cause, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममात्र
सममात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Of the same size or measure.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममिति|सममितिः
सममिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Mean measure.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and मिति measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समय|समयः
समय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 Oath, affirmation by oath or ordeal.<BR>3 Established moral or ceremonial custom.<BR>4 Demonstrated conclusion.<BR>5 Agreement, covenant, contract, bargain.<BR>6 Engagement, appointment.<BR>7 Order, instruction.<BR>8 Sign, hint, indication.<BR>9 Religious obligation or observance.<BR>10 Leisure, interval, opportunity.<BR>11 Season, fit or proper time for any thing.<BR>12 Speech, declaration.<BR>13 Limit, boundary.<BR>14 End of trouble or distress, (in dramatic action.)<BR>E.<BR>स for सम with, मी to mete, to measure, aff. अच्, or सम alike, इण् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयकार|समयकारः
समयकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Making an appointment or engagement, fixing a time.<BR>E.<BR>समय an agreement, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयभेद|समयभेदः
समयभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Breaking an agreement.<BR>E.<BR>समय, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयव्यभिचार|समयव्यभिचारः
समयव्यभिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Violating or breaking an agreement.<BR>E.<BR>समय, and व्यभिचार improper conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया<BR>ind.<BR>1 Near.<BR>2 Within, midst.<BR>3 At such a time, at a fixed or appointed time.<BR>4 Duly, seasonably, in due time or season.<BR>E.<BR>सम alike, इण् to go, आ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयाध्युषित
समयाध्युषित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A time at which neither stars nor sun are visible.<BR>E.<BR>समय time, अधि over, उषित abided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर|समरं|समरः
समर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>War, battle, conflict.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together, ऋ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरज्जु
समरज्जु<BR>f. (-ज्जुः)<BR>Mean string or soundings.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and रज्जु a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरमूर्द्धन्
समरमूर्द्धन्<BR>m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>The front or van of battle.<BR>E.<BR>समर, and मूर्द्धन् front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=894" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरूप्य|समरूप्यः
समरूप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Of like or same source or origin.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, रूप्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्च्चन|समर्चन|समर्चनं
समर्च्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worshipping, adoration.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before अर्च्च to worship, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्च्चित|समर्चित
समर्च्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Worshipped, adored, honoured.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before अर्च्च to worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्ण|समर्ण्ण
समर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Asked, solicited.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्द्द to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थ|समर्थः
समर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Strong, powerful.<BR>2 Connected in sense.<BR>3 Fit, proper.<BR>4 Able, adequate to, capable.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>The construction of words.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, अर्थ to ask, aff. अच्, or अर्थ meaning, sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थक|समर्थकं
समर्थक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Aloe wood, (Amyris agallocha.)<BR>E.<BR>समर्थ fit, (for perfume,) कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थता
समर्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Strength, power, prowess.<BR>2 Ability, capability, adequacy.<BR>3 Signification of terms.<BR>E.<BR>तल् aff. of the abstract, added to समर्थ; also समर्थत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थन|समर्थनं
समर्थन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Deliberation, deciding on the propriety or impropriety of any thing; also समर्थना.<BR>2 Perseverance in an arduous undertaking, attempting difficulties or impossibilities.<BR>3 Reconciling differences, allaying a dispute.<BR>4 Objecting, objection.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before अर्थ to ask, or request, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्द्धक
समर्द्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Granting a boon.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ऋधु to augment, aff. खुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्प्पण|समर्पण|समर्पणं
समर्प्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Delivering, consigning, presenting.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्प्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्प्पणीय|समर्पणीय
समर्प्पणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be delivered, presented, made over &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्प्पणीय to be delivered; also समर्प्पयितव्य and समर्प्प्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्प्पित|समर्पित
समर्प्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delivered, made over, consigned.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्प्पित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्प्पितवत्|समर्पितवत्
समर्प्पितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Giving or making over, delivering.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्प्पितवत् delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्य्याद|समर्याद|समर्यादः|समर्य्यादः
समर्य्याद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Bounded, limited.<BR>3 Correct in conduct.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, मर्य्यादा a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समल|समलं
समल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Dirty, muddy, filthy.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Fæces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवतार|समवतारः
समवतार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A place of pilgrimage, as a sacred stream, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, अव below, तृ to cross or pass over, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्ण|समवर्णः
समवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Of the same caste, colour, &c.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Community of caste, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्त्तिन्|समवर्तिन्
समवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती)<BR>YAMA, the ruler of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>सम all, equal, वृत to be or to select, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवनत
समवनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव before णम to bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवश्यात
समवश्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone away, wasted, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव before श्यै to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसर्ग्य
समवसर्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>To be let go or let out.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव before सृज to loose, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाकार
समवाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of dramatic entertainment.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव with आङ्, before कृ to make, aff. घञ्; described, as that in which the chiefs are engaged in mutual conflict or contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्ति|समवाप्तिः
समवाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Obtaining, getting.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव before आप to get, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाय|समवायः
समवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Multitude, assemblage, collection, aggregate, quantity.<BR>2 One of the categories or Padārthas of logic, intimate and constant relation, as of yarn and the cloth made of it.<BR>3 Connection of species in a genus, or parts of a whole.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and अव before अय to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायसम्बन्ध|समवायसंबन्धः
समवायसम्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Inseparable relation, as of properties with substances, material with manufacture, species with genus.<BR>E.<BR>समवाय, and सम्बन्ध connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिन्
समवायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Multitudinous, aggregated.<BR>2 Connected intimately.<BR>n. (-यि)<BR>Intimate and inseparable cause, as earth of pottery, thread of cloth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समवाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिकारण
समवायिकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Inseparable cause or relation, as of material with produce, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समवायिन्, and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवृत्ति|समवृत्तिः
समवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Moderate, equable.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेत|समवेतः
समवेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mixed, mingled, blended.<BR>2 Collected, assembled.<BR>3 Connected with, related to, as properties with things.<BR>4 Comprised in one genus.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अव before इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेध|समवेधः
समवेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Mean depth.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and वेध perforation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्नुवान|समश्नुवानः
समश्नुवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Spreading over, pervading, extending throughout.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, अश to pervade, शातच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्ठिला
समष्ठिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of potherb, said to grow in watery places; according to some authorities, a kind of cucumber, to others a shrub, called commonly गांडरद्धवी.<BR>E.<BR>सम together, स्था to stay, इलच् aff. deriv. irr. or सम with, अस्थि a bone, (a seed,) ला to get or have, aff. क, also समष्ठीला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन|समसनं
समसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Contracting, contraction.<BR>2 Combination, conjunction, formation of compound terms.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अस to throw or direct, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन्धि|समसंधि|समसंधिः
समसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>Alliance or peace on equal terms.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन्धित|समसंधित
समसन्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Allied on equal terms.<BR>2 Bound or connected equally.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and सन्धित bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसुप्ति|समसुप्तिः
समसुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>The end of the Kalpa, and destruction of the universe<BR>E.<BR>सम universal, सुप्ति sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्त|समस्तं
समस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 All, whole, entire, complete.<BR>2 Compound, compounded.<BR>3 Abridged, contracted.<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A whole, the aggregate of all the parts.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अस to throw or direct, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थ|समस्थः
समस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Even, equal, level, uniform.<BR>2 Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>सम even, स्थ what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थल
समस्थल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>Level ground.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The Doab, the country between the Ganges and Jumna rivers.<BR>E.<BR>सम level, स्थल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थलीकृत
समस्थलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Levelled, made level, filled up (as a marsh or river).<BR>E.<BR>समस्थल, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्य
समस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 To be collected together.<BR>2 To be made entire or complete.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Part of a stanza, proposed as a trial of skill to be completed.<BR>E.<BR>सम even or complete, क्यच् affix, and सुक् augment; or सम् together, अस to direct, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=895" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्यार्था
समस्यार्था<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>Part of a stanza to be completed as a trial of skill.<BR>E.<BR>समस्य to be completed, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांश|समांशः
समांश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Entitled to an equal share.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An equal portion, a part.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांशहारिन्
समांशहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Sharing equally, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>समांश, and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांशिन्
समांशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>A coheir entitled to an equal share.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, अंश part or portion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांसमीना
समांसमीना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A cow bearing a calf every year.<BR>E.<BR>समा a year, in the second case, repeated, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्षिन्
समाकर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>Possessing a diffusive fragrance.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and आङ् before कृषि to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुल
समाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Agitated, bewildered, confused.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before कुल to accumulate, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुलत्व
समाकुलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Agitation, anxiety.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, समाकुलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रान्त
समाक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Pervaded, spread.<BR>2 Overcome, surpassed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before क्रम to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>Fame, reputation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् all, आङ् before ख्या to tell or declare, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्यात
समाख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famed, celebrated.<BR>2 Notorious, public.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before ख्या to say, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागत|समागतः
समागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Arrived, approached.<BR>2 Met, encountered.<BR>3 United, joined.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागति|समागतिः
समागति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Arrival, approach.<BR>2 Union, joining.<BR>3 Encountering, meeting.<BR>4 Similar condition or progress.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, or सम् same, आङ् before गम to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम|समागमः
समागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Union, junction.<BR>2 Arrival, approach.<BR>3 Association, acquaintance, intercourse.<BR>4 Encounter, meeting.<BR>5 (In astronomy,) The occultation of a star.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघात|समाघातः
समाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Striking, beating, killing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, आघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचर
समाचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what observes, practices, proceeds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरण|समाचरणं
समाचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Following, practising, observing, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before चर to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरत्
समाचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Following, practising, behaving, proceeding, &c. सम्, and आङ् before चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचार|समाचारः
समाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Equal or like in virtuous conduct.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Proper practice or conduct.<BR>2 Proceeding, going.<BR>3 Information, tradition, news.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छन्न
समाच्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Covered with, involved in.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आच्छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज|समाजः
समाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A multitude, a number, (of any thing except beasts.)<BR>2 An assembly, a meeting.<BR>3 A convivial meeting, a club.<BR>4 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सम् like, and अज to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
समाज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Fame, reputation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् all, आङ् before ज्ञा to know, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादान|समादानं
समादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Receiving suitable donations.<BR>2 Taking.<BR>3 The daily observances of the Jaina sect.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादाय
समादाय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Having accepted.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ before दा to give, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिष्ट
समादिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Enjoined, commanded.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आदिष्ट enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेय
समादेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Acceptable, to be selected or taken.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधान|समाधानं
समाधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Religious meditation, restraining the mind from external objects, and fixing it in profound absorption.<BR>2 Promising, declaring.<BR>3 (In the drama,) The leading incident, that which gives rise sometimes unexpectedly to the whole plot.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and आङ् before धा to have or hold, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधाय
समाधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having fixed upon, (the mind,) being intent upon.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and आङ् before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधि|समाधिः
समाधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Deep and devout meditation, restraining the senses and confining the mind to contemplation on the true nature of spirit, &c.<BR>2 A religious vow or obligation.<BR>3 Silence.<BR>4 Promise, assent, engagement.<BR>5 Composing or reconciling differences, putting a stop to a dispute.<BR>6 Requital, return, retaliation.<BR>7 Attempting impossibilities; exertion or perseverance in extreme difficulties.<BR>8 Storing corn on account of a dearth.<BR>9 A Jaina saint of a future age.<BR>10 A figure of rhetoric; connexion or proximity of two events accidentally connected, and expressed by a common verb and the government of the verb by a double nominative, as उत्कण्ठिता च कुस्तटा जगामास्तञ्च भानुमान् the disloyal woman went sorrowfully, and the sun (went) down.<BR>11 Demonstrated conclusion.<BR>12 The joint of the neck.<BR>13 A tomb, a grave.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, धा to have or hold, with आङ् prefix, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिमत्|समाधिमन्त्
समाधिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Contemplative, engaged in meditation.<BR>2 Making a promise, announcing assent or permission.<BR>E.<BR>समाधि, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिस्थ|समाधिस्थः
समाधिस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Devoted to meditation.<BR>E.<BR>समाधि, and स्थ who is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्मात
समाध्मात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blown or puffed up, inflated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before ध्मा to blow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
समान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Like, similar.<BR>2 Good, virtuous.<BR>3 One, uniform, same.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 One of the vital airs, that which is considered essential to digestion.<BR>2 A corresponding letter of the alphabet, as a long vowel to its short one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम all, अन to breathe, aff. घञ्, or सम् and आङ् before णी to get, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानकालीन|समानकालीनः
समानकालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Occurring or produced at the same period.<BR>E.<BR>समान same, काल time, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानगोत्र
समानगोत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Of the same lineage or family: see सगोत्र.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and गोत्र family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजन्मन्
समानजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Of equal age.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजाति
समानजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of a common tribe, sort, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजातीय
समानजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of the same caste or species.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and जातीय of a caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानता
समानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sameness, equality, likeness.<BR>2 Community of kind or quality.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, aff. समानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=896" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयत
समानयत<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Making equal or like to.<BR>2 Leading, bringing.<BR>E.<BR>समान used as a verb, or सम् and आङ् before णी to get, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयन|समानयनं
समानयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bringing, conducting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before णी to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाधिकरण
समानाधिकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Common or generick property.<BR>2 A predicament or condition including several things or persons.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A generick character.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and अधिकरण possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाधिकार|समानाधिकारः
समानाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Similar or equal duty, office, or government.<BR>2 Generick character.<BR>E.<BR>समान, and अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानित
समानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken, led, conducted.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानीय
समानीय<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before णी to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानोदक|समानोदकः
समानोदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kinsman, one who when distinct from the Sapiṇḍa is next in order and succession, and is connected by oblations of water only, to the manes of common ancestors; this relationship extends to the fourteenth in descent, i. e. the seven first or Sapin'da's presenting water as well as the cakes, are also Samānodakas, whilst the seven next presenting water alone are Samānodakas only.<BR>E.<BR>समान common, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानोदर्य्य|समानोदर्य|समानोदर्यः|समानोदर्य्यः
समानोदर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A brother of whole blood.<BR>E.<BR>समान same, उदर belly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान्त|समान्तः
समान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The end of a year.<BR>E.<BR>समा a year, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप|समापः
समाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Sacrificing, offering oblations to the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सम् same, आप water; in which libations of water are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापक|समापकः
समापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Filling, completing, finishing.<BR>2 Killing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, आप to get, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन|समापनं
समापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Conclusion, completion, finish.<BR>2 A section, a chapter, a division.<BR>3 Killing, destroying.<BR>4 Profound meditation.<BR>5 Gain, acquisition.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, together with, आप to obtain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन्न|समापन्नं
समापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Finished, done, completed, concluded.<BR>2 Got, gained, obtained.<BR>3 Distressed, afflicted.<BR>4 Killed.<BR>5 Accomplished, perfect, (in any branch of study.)<BR>6 Come, occurred, happened.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying completion, &c., आङ् before पद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापित|समापितं
समापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Finished, done, concluded.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before आप to get, aff. क्त, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त|समाप्तः
समाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Finished, done, concluded, completed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before आप to get, aff. क्त, without the augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्ति|समाप्तिः
समाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 End, completion, perfection, conclusion, finish.<BR>2 Reconciling differences, putting an end to disputes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying completion, आप to get or gain, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिक|समाप्तिकः
समाप्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Finite, final, concluding, completing.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 One who has completed a course of holy study.<BR>2 A finisher, an ender.<BR>E.<BR>समाप्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त्यर्था
समाप्त्यर्था<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>Part of a stanza given as a task or trial of skill to be completed.<BR>E.<BR>समाप्ति completion, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लुत
समाप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drenched, drowned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाय|समायः
समाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A visit, arrival.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before या to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत
समायत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lengthened, extended.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before यम to restrain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायात
समायात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Come, arrived.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before या to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुत
समायुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Joined, connected, attached to or united with.<BR>2 Decorated, adorned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before युत joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नाय|समाम्नायः
समाम्नाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Totality, the aggregate.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before म्ना to remember, घञ् and युक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायोग|समायोगः
समायोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Union, junction, connection, association.<BR>2 Heap, multitude, assemblage.<BR>3 Cause, origin, motive, object.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before युज to join, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारब्ध
समारब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Begun, commenced.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रभि to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भ|समारंभ|समारंभः|समारम्भः
समारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Commencement, beginning.<BR>2 Undertaking.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रभि to commence, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारूढ
समारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Ascended, gone up or upon.<BR>2 Mounted.<BR>3 Agreed to, determined.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रुह to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपण|समारोपणं
समारोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Placing or fixing in or on.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रुह to grow, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपित
समारोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Placed in or upon.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रुह to grow, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोह|समारोहः
समारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Going up, ascending.<BR>2 Mounting, riding upon.<BR>3 Agreeing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रुह to rise, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समार्थिन्
समार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 Desirous of equality.<BR>2 Seeking peace.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बन|समालंबनं
समालम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Resting upon, being supported by.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before लवि to depend, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भ|समालंभ|समालंभः|समालम्भः
समालम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Smearing the body with coloured perfumes, as with saffron, sandal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before लभि to sound, aff. अच्; also with ल्युट् aff. समालम्भन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भन|समालंभन|समालंभनं|समालम्भनं
समालम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Smearing the body with coloured fragrant substances: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाली
समाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A collection of flowers, a nosegay, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स for सम् with, माला a garland, affs. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्त्तन|समावर्तन|समावर्तनं|समावर्त्तनं
समावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A pupil's return home after finishing his religious studies.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावाय|समावायः
समावाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A multitude, a number, a heap or quantity.<BR>2 Association.<BR>3 Integral or inseparable aggregation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् implying aggregation, वय to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावास|समावासः
समावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Residence, abode.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before वस to dwell, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावासित
समावासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sojourning, taking up a residence.<BR>E.<BR>समावास, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविष्ट
समाविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Entered or engrossed by, absorbed by, (feeling, passion, &c.) possessed by, (as an evil spirit.)<BR>2 Entered, (as a mansion.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् implying entireness, and विष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत|समावृतः
समावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>2 Covered, inclosed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्त|समावृत्तः
समावृत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A pupil who has completed his studies and taken leave of his preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before वृत to be, aff. क्त; also with कन् added, समावृत्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=897" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेद्य
समावेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be announced or communicated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before विद to know, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेश|समावेशः
समावेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Affection, passion, emotion.<BR>2 Possession by evil spirits.<BR>3 Entrance.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before विश to enter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेशित|समावेशितः
समावेशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed, fixed.<BR>2 Entered, penetrated.<BR>3 Brought in or into.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before विश to enter, causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाशङ्कित
समाशङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Doubtful, fearing, apprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ before शकि to doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रय|समाश्रयः
समाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Protection, refuge.<BR>2 Seeking protection.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित|समाश्रितः
समाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protected, defended, cherished, refuged.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and आश्रित refuged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित्य
समाश्रित्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Depending upon, trusting to.<BR>2 Having engaged in, agreed to, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before श्री to serve, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्त
समाश्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Trusting, confiding in.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before श्वस to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वास|समाश्वासः
समाश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Trust, belief, confidence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before श्वस to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्
समास्<BR>m. (-माः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास|समासः
समास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Contraction, abridgment, conciseness.<BR>2 Composition of words, formation of compound terms, (in grammar.)<BR>3 Composition of differences, reconciling quarrels.<BR>4 Aggregation, assemblage, collection.<BR>5 Whole.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अस to throw or direct, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्त|समासक्तः
समासक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Joined, united.<BR>2 Reached, attained.<BR>3 Marked, affected by, &c.<BR>4 Combined, comprehended.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षञ्ज to be in contact with, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्ति|समासक्तिः
समासक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Union.<BR>2 Comprehension, inclusion.<BR>3 Affection, attachment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षञ्ज to be in contact, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासज्जत्
समासज्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्)<BR>Joining, or connecting with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आ before षञ्ज to unite, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासज्जन
समासज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Joining, uniting, union, combination, connection, contact.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षञ्ज to be in contact with, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासतस
समासतस<BR>ind.<BR>Briefly, summarily.<BR>E.<BR>समास, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासन्न|समासन्नं
समासन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Obtained, attained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् implying union or contiguity, षद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासभावना
समासभावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Composition by the sum of the products.<BR>E.<BR>समास, and भावना contemplating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासवत्|समासवन्त्
समासवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Abridged, contracted.<BR>2 Compounded.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The Tūn tree, (Cedrela Tunna.)<BR>E.<BR>समास, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासर्जण
समासर्जण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Delivering, consigning, abandoning.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before सृज to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादन|समासादनं
समासादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Attaining, effecting, accomplishing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षद to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादित|समासादितः
समासादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done, effected, attained, obtained, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षद to go, causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाद्य|समासाद्यं
समासाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Attainable, what may be obtained or effected.<BR>ind.<BR>Having obtained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before षद to go, aff. ण्यत् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाध्याहार|समासाध्याहारः
समासाध्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>E.<BR>समास, and अध्याहार the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासार्थ
समासार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>The sense of a compound.<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>Part of a stanza to be completed.<BR>E.<BR>समास connexion, composition, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासीन
समासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Sitting, seated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before अस to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासृष्ट
समासृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Left, abandoned, given, made over.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before सृज to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवन
समासेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Following, practising.<BR>2 Serving.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before सेव to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवित
समासेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Followed, practised.<BR>2 Served.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before सेव to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासोक्ति|समासोक्तिः
समासोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A protracted metaphor, (in rhetoric.)<BR>E.<BR>समास, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्या
समास्या<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Interview, colloquy.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, अम to be, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहत
समाहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>सस् and आङ् before हन to strike, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरण|समाहरणं
समाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Uniting, combining, collecting, composition.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, आङ् before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहार|समाहारः
समाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Aggregation, collection, assemblage, either in fact or thought.<BR>2 Contraction, abridgement.<BR>3 Composition of words (in grammar).<BR>4 Conjunction of equal words or sentences, the power of the particle and.<BR>5 A particular form of composition, a subdivision of the class Dvanda, in which several words are joined together, and the compound is a term in the neuter gender, as अहिनकुलं the snake and mungoos.<BR>6 The combination of two letters of the alphabet into a syllable, which designates all the letters intermediate between the two of which it consists.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, आङ् before हृ to take or convey, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहित|समाहितः
समाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed or assented to.<BR>2 Absorbed in meditation, absent, abstracted or having the senses steadily held in subjection.<BR>3 Concluded, demonstrated, following from what has been said.<BR>4 Composed, reconciled, put an end to, as a contest or dispute.<BR>5 Placed, deposited, delivered.<BR>6 Pure, purified.<BR>7 Finished, completed.<BR>8 Cool, collected, firm.<BR>9 Assembled.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>(In rhetoric,) The expression or description of attentiveness.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् implying collection or perfection, धा to have or hold, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृत|समाहृतः
समाहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Accepted, received, taken.<BR>2 Collected, assembled, combined.<BR>3 Compiled.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृति|समाहृतिः
समाहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Compilation, abridgement, an abridgement.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, आङ्, and हृ to take, to bring, aff. क्तिन्: see समाहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्व|समाह्वः
समाह्व<BR>mf. (-ह्वः-ह्वी)<BR>Calling out or to, mutual calling.<BR>2 Acclaim.<BR>2 Defiance.<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A plant, commonly Gojiwha.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before ह्वेञ्^1 to call, क aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=898" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वय|समाह्वयः
समाह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A match, a main, the conflict of animals or birds for sport, cockfighting, &c.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 Calling out.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before ह्वेङ् to call, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वान|समाह्वानं
समाह्वान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Challenge.<BR>E.<BR>समाह्व to call out, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिक|समिकं
समिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pike, a dart.<BR>E.<BR>सम even, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्
समित्<BR>f. (-मित्)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, इ to go, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिता
समिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wheat flour.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before इ to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिति|समितिः
समिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Assembly, company.<BR>3 Association, meeting, union.<BR>4 Sameness, likeness, equality.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, इ to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिथ|समिथः
समिथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, इन् to go, थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिद्ध|समिद्धः
समिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Lighted, kindled, set alight or on fire.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before इन्ध to kindle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्
समिध्<BR>f. (-मित् or मिट्)<BR>Fuel, wood, grass, &c. so employed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, इन्धि to kindle or inflame, क्विप् aff., and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध|समिधः
समिध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and इन्ध to kindle, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धन|समिंधनं|समिन्धनं
समिन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fuel.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, इन्ध to kindle, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धान
समिन्धान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Augmenting, prospering.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before इधि to increase, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिर|समिरः
समिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wind, air.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, ईर to go, aff. क, and the vowel made short; also समीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक|समीकं
समीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 A pike, a dart.<BR>E.<BR>षम to be sad or confused, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकरण|समीकरणं
समीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Equalizing, making equal to.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Equation.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्रिया
समीक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>(In arithmetic,) Equation.<BR>E.<BR>सम, and क्रिया operation, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकृत|समीकृतं
समीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Equalized, made even or equal.<BR>2 Imitated, done in like manner, &c.<BR>3 Added, summed up.<BR>4 Balanced, equipoised.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, even, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष|समीक्षं|समीक्षः
समीक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The Sāṃkhya system of philosophy.<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Nature, essential nature, or according to the Sāṃkhya system, crude matter or any of its twenty-four essential parts.<BR>2 Understanding, intellect.<BR>3 Sight, seeing, inspection, looking.<BR>4 Effort.<BR>5 Search, investigation.<BR>6 A book, a work supplementary to the Vedas, treating of the modes of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ईक्ष to see, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षण|समीक्षणं
समीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Search, looking for, investigation.<BR>2 Seeing, looking at.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive prefix, and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षित
समीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, looked at.<BR>2 Considered, investigated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्यकारिन्
समीक्ष्यकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Acting after due deliberation.<BR>E.<BR>समीक्ष्य having inspected, कारिन् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीच|समीचः
समीच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>1 A deer, a doe.<BR>2 Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before इण to go, Uṇādi aff. चट्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचक|समीचकः
समीचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचीन|समीचीनं
समीचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 True.<BR>2 Right, correct.<BR>3 Fit, proper.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Truth.<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक् true, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीद|समीदः
समीद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Fine wheat flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीन|समीनः
समीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Yearly, annual, relating to a year.<BR>2 Hired for a year.<BR>3 After a year, a year hence, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समा a year, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीनिका
समीनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow calving every year.<BR>E.<BR>समीन a year, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीप|समीपः
समीप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Near, contiguous, proximate, at hand.<BR>E.<BR>सम together, आप water, and ई substituted for आ; analogous to the confluence of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपग
समीपग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Approaching, going or gone near to.<BR>E.<BR>समीप, and ग who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपतस्
समीपतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Before, near.<BR>E.<BR>समीप, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपता
समीपता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Proximity, contiguity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also समीपत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीभूत
समीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Equalised.<BR>2 Identified.<BR>3 Equipoised.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, भूत become, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीय|समीयः
समीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of like cause or origin.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयिवस्
समीयिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वः)<BR>Going to, arriving at, attaining.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before इण् to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर|समीरः
समीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>सम् every way, ईर to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरण|समीरणः
समीरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Marüa.<BR>3 A traveller.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throwing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, ईर to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरित
समीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tossed, thrown.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>3 Sent.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ईर to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीहित
समीहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before ईह to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुख|समुखः
समुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>स with, and मुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुचित|समुचितः
समुचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fit, right, proper.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चय|समुच्चयः
समुच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Assemblage, collection, either in thought or fact.<BR>2 Conjunction of words or sentences, the power of the particle and, or also; but it implies the conjunction of different objects of one act or different acts with the same object, as ईश्वरं गुरुञ्च भजस्व worship GOD, and (or also) the Guru.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before चि to collect, aff. णच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चर|समुच्चरः
समुच्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what goes about or up, traverses, ascends, flies, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before चर to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चरत्
समुच्चरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Going up or about.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छेद|समुच्छेदः
समुच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Destroying, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before छिद to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रय|समुच्छ्रयः
समुच्छ्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Opposition, enmity.<BR>2 Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and उट् up, above, and श्रिञ् to serve, aff. णच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्राय|समुच्छ्रायः
समुच्छ्राय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before श्रि to serve, aff. णच्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रित|समुच्छ्रितः
समुच्छ्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>High, elevated, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before श्रि to serve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रिसित
समुच्छ्रिसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sighing.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A sigh.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before श्वस to breathe, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्वास|समुच्छ्वासः
समुच्छ्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Heavy expiration, sighing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before श्वस to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुञ्झित
समुञ्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Left, abandoned, quitted, resigned.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and उञ्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=899" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रम|समुत्क्रमः
समुत्क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Rise, ascent, going up.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् up, क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रोश|समुत्क्रोशः
समुत्क्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An osprey.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and उत् before क्रुश to cry, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तरत्
समुत्तरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Crossing, passing over or beyond.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before तृ to cross, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तेजन
समुत्तेजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inflaming, inciting, irritating.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before तिज to be sharp, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तेजित
समुत्तेजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inflamed, incited, excited, irritated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before तिज to be sharp, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थ|समुत्थः
समुत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>1 Rising, risen, getting or got up.<BR>2 Born, produced.<BR>3 Occasioned, occuring.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, उट् up, स्था to stand, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थान|समुत्थानं
समुत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Performance of work, occupation, effort, industry.<BR>2 Positive indication or symptom of disease.<BR>3 Rising, getting up.<BR>4 Common growth or increase, (as of size or wealth, &c.)<BR>5 Healing a wound or sore, cure or recovery from any injury.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, उट् up, स्था to stay or be, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थित|समुत्थितः
समुत्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Risen, got up.<BR>2 Increased.<BR>3 Derived or obtained from.<BR>4 Cured, healed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पतन|समुत्पतनं
समुत्पतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Ascending.<BR>3 Making effort, energy, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पत् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पतित
समुत्पतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, gone up, ascended.<BR>2 Exerted, vigorous.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पत to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पत्ति|समुत्पत्तिः
समुत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Origin, production, birth.<BR>2 Occurrence, incidence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पद to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पन्न|समुत्पन्नः
समुत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Born, produced.<BR>2 Occurring, taking place.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पाट|समुत्पाटः
समुत्पाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Detaching, separating from, tearing from, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पट to go, causal v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पाटित
समुत्पाटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Detached or severed from, torn from, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पट to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पादन|समुत्पादनं
समुत्पादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Producing, fabricating.<BR>2 Effecting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पद to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पादित
समुत्पादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Produced, effected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पद् to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिञ्ज|समुत्पिंज|समुत्पिञ्जः
समुत्पिञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>Excessively confused or confounded, bewildered, lost, overcome.<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>An army in great disorder.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before पिजि to hurt, aff. अच्; also समुत्पिञ्जल, and simply पिञ्ज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सर्ग|समुत्सर्गः
समुत्सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Leaving, abandoning.<BR>2 Giving.<BR>3 Evacuation of urine or fæces.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before सृज to abandon, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सव|समुत्सवः
समुत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Festivity.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुक|समुत्सुकः
समुत्सुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sorrowful, regretting, missing or grieving for any one absent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, उत्सुक sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सेध|समुत्सेधः
समुत्सेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before षिघ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदक्त|समुदक्तं
समुदक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Drawn, raised, lifted or thrown up from a deep place.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, and उट् up, अञ्च to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदय|समुदयं|समुदयः
समुदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Multitude, number, heap or quantity.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 Assent, rise.<BR>4 Rising, (as of the sun, &c.)<BR>5 Effort, exertion, perseverance.<BR>6 A day.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before इ to go, aff. णच्; also समुदाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागम|समुदागमः
समुदागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Knowledge in general.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उद् before आगम knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदात्रार
समुदात्रार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Intention, purpose, design, motive.<BR>E.<BR>सम with, उट् and आङ् before चर to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाय|समुदायः
समुदाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Multitude, quantity, number, heap.<BR>3 Rise, ascent.<BR>4 The rear or reserve of an army.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् up, इण् to go, aff. णच्; also समुदय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहरण|समुदाहरणं
समुदाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Declaring, uttering.<BR>2 Illustrating.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहृत
समुदाहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Declared.<BR>2 Illustrated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदित|समुदितः
समुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Risen, ascended.<BR>2 Risen, (as the sun, &c.)<BR>3 Produced, excited, occasioned.<BR>4 Possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and उदित risen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरण|समुदीरणं
समुदीरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Repeating, declaring, speaking, reciting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before ईर to send, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरित
समुदीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, spoken, declared, recited.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before ईर, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग|समुद्गः
समुद्ग<BR>mfn. (-द्गः-द्गा-द्गं)<BR>1 Who or what rises or goes up.<BR>2 Who or what pervades entirely.<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A casket, a covered box.<BR>2 A stanza in which two or more of the Pādas correspond in sound, though in a different sense.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before गम to go, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गक|समुद्गकः
समुद्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A casket, a covered box.<BR>2 A sort of stanza: one, each half of which consists of the very same words but in different acceptations, those of one half being respectively the the attributives or adjectives to those of the other.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before गम to go, aff. ड and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गम|समुद्गमः
समुद्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Rising, ascent.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before गम to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गयमक
समुद्गयमक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>(In rhetoric,) The repetition of the same words in different pādas of a stanza, but in a different sense.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्ग what goes completely, यमक alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गीर्ण|समुद्गीर्णः
समुद्गीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Brought up (as food), vomited.<BR>2 Raised or lifted up (from a depth, &c.)<BR>3 Uttered, exclaimed, raised (as a cry, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before गॄ to swallow, or sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दिष्ट
समुद्दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Pointed out, shewn.<BR>2 Particularised, enumerated.<BR>3 Explained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before दिश to shew, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्देश|समुद्देशः
समुद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Describing.<BR>2 Pointing out.<BR>3 Particularising, explaining, enumerating.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before दिश to shew, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धत|समुद्धतः
समुद्धत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ill-mannered, behaving ill or improperly, conducting one's self discreditably.<BR>2 Raised or drawn up.<BR>3 Upheld, supported.<BR>4 Arrogant, proud, puffed up with pride, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before हन to hurt or kill, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धरण|समुद्धरणं
समुद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Food vomited or thrown up.<BR>2 Drawing up, raising, lifting (as water from a well, &c.)<BR>3 Eradicating a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">Page901</a>] tree, &c. pulling up by the roots.<BR>4 Extricating, lifting out.<BR>5 Taking out from, as a part or share.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=900" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धर्त्तृ|समुद्धर्तृ
समुद्धर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Who or what lifts, raises, extricates, &c.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A redeemer, a deliverer.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धस्त
समुद्धस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Wiped off by the hand.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and उट् before हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धृत|समुद्धृतं
समुद्धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ill-behaved.<BR>2 Thrown up (as food, &c.)<BR>3 Raised or drawn up.<BR>4 Extricated, lifted out or from.<BR>5 Taken as a share, set apart, divided.<BR>6 Seized, possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before धृ to have, or हृ to take, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्भव|समुद्भवः
समुद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Production, origin.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्भूत|समुद्भूतः
समुद्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Born, produced, derived.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before भू to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यत
समुद्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ready, prepared.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, उद्यत active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यम|समुद्यमः
समुद्यम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Commencement, onset.<BR>2 Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र|समुद्रः
समुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Sealed, stamped.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A sea, an ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before उन्दि to be wet, and रक aff.; or स for सह with, and मुद्रा a seal; also thence signifying a limit, (i. e. bounded by continents,) or a jewel, (the receptacle of gems,) or सम with उद्र an otter; or स with, मुद pleasure, or सम् together, उद water, and रा to give or have, aff. क, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रकफ|समुद्रकफः
समुद्रकफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रकान्ता|समुद्रकांता
समुद्रकान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and कान्ता the mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रग|समुद्रगः
समुद्रग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Ocean-going, sea-faring.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A trader by sea.<BR>2 A seaman.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and ग who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रगृह|समुद्रगृहं
समुद्रगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A sort of pleasure or summer house, built in the midst of water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रचुलुक|समुद्रचुलुकः
समुद्रचुलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The saint, AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, चुलुक a pot; having drank up the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रतट
समुद्रतट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The sea coast.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र, and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रतीर
समुद्रतीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The sea shore.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रदयिता
समुद्रदयिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and दयिता beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रनवनीत|समुद्रनवनीतं
समुद्रनवनीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The beverage of immortality.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the ocean, and नवनीत butter: being produced or recovered by the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रफेन|समुद्रफेनः
समुद्रफेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and फेन froth or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रमेखला
समुद्रमेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, मेखला a zone; the sea girt; surrounded by the ocean as by a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रयान|समुद्रयानं
समुद्रयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sea voyage.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र, and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रयायिन्
समुद्रयायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A sailor, a navigator, a merchant trading by sea.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ररसना
समुद्ररसना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and रसना a zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रलवण|समुद्रलवणं
समुद्रलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रवह्नि|समुद्रवह्निः
समुद्रवह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रविजय|समुद्रविजयः
समुद्रविजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The father of the Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and विजय victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रवेला
समुद्रवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A wave of the sea.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र, and वेला a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रान्त|समुद्रांत|समुद्रान्तं|समुद्रान्तः
समुद्रान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 The nutmeg.<BR>2 The sea shore.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A shrub, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>2 The cotton plant.<BR>3 A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and अन्त end or boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्राम्बरा
समुद्राम्बरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and अम्वर vesture; clothed or invested by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रारु|समुद्रारुः
समुद्रारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A shark.<BR>2 A large fabulous fish, perhaps intending the whale, hyperbolically described.<BR>3 RĀMA'S bridge.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, ऋ to go, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रिय|समुद्रियः
समुद्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Marine, oceanic, maritime.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वह|समुद्वहः
समुद्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Who or what lifts or bears up.<BR>2 Moving up and down.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before वह to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वहत्
समुद्वहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>1 Lifting or raising up.<BR>2 Moving up and down.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before वह to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्दन|समुंदन|समुंदनं|समुन्दनं
समुन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Wetness, damp, moisture.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before उन्दि to be moist or wet, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्न|समुन्नं
समुन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Wet, moist, moistened.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before उन्द to be wet, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नत|समुन्नतः
समुन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 High, lofty, elevated.<BR>2 Full, prominent.<BR>3 Exalted, dignified.<BR>4 Proud, arrogant.<BR>5 Lifted up, raised.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before नम to bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नति|समुन्नतिः
समुन्नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Height, elevation.<BR>2 Consequence, rank, dignity, exaltation.<BR>3 Pride, loftiness.<BR>4 Lifting up.<BR>5 Increase, thriving, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before नम to bow, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नद्ध|समुन्नद्धः
समुन्नद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Conceited of learning, thinking one's self learned.<BR>2 Proud, arrogant.<BR>3 Produced, born.<BR>4 Tied up or above.<BR>5 Supreme, lord or master.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before णह to tie, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नय|समुन्नयः
समुन्नय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Occurrence, event, advent.<BR>2 Gaining, attaining.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before णी to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नयत्
समुन्नयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Attaining, gaining.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before णी to get, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपगत
समुपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Approached, approximated.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and उप near, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपगम|समुपगमः
समुपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Approach, approximation, contact.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before गम to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपचित
समुपचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Collected, heaped, accumulated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपजोषम्
समुपजोषम्<BR>ind.<BR>Happily, fortunately.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before जुष to gratify, aff. अम्; also read उपजोषम् and उपयोषम् or समुपयोषम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपविष्ट
समुपविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Seated, sat down.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before विश to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेश|समुपवेशः
समुपवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Welcoming, entertaining, causing to sit down.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before विश to enter, causal v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेशित
समुपवेशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Welcomed, made to sit or rest.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before विश to enter, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=901" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपस्था
समुपस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Proximity, approximation.<BR>2 Happening, befalling.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before ष्ठा to be, अङ् and टाप् affs.; also समुपस्थान and समुपस्थिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपस्थित
समुपस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Attained, acquired.<BR>2 Brought or come near to, approximated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before ष्ठा to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपेक्षित
समुपेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपेत
समुपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Come together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before इ to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपेयिवस्
समुपेयिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वत्)<BR>Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before ई to go, क्वसु aff. of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपोढ
समुपोढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Suppressed, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उप before वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुल्लसत्
समुल्लसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Sporting, wantoning.<BR>2 Shining, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उट् before लस to play, शतृ aff. of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुल्लसित
समुल्लसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sportive, sporting.<BR>2 Brilliant, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and उत् before लस to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूढ|समूढः
समूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Heaped, accumulated, assembled, collected.<BR>2 Crooked, bent.<BR>3 Produced quickly.<BR>4 Accompanying, associated, a companion.<BR>5 Tamed, tranquillized.<BR>6 Married.<BR>7 Purified, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to bear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूर|समूरः
समूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>षम to be confused, aff. ऊर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूरु|समूरुः
समूरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A deer, one of the sorts of which the skin may be used as a student's seat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षम to be confused, ऊरु aff.; also with कन् added समूरुक. According to some, this sort of deer is distinguished by a white mane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूल|समूलं
समूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having a root, joined or in connexion with the root.<BR>E.<BR>स with, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूलघात
समूलघात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Utter destruction or eradication.<BR>E.<BR>समूल radical, घातं killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूह|समूहः
समूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Assemblage, aggregate in general, heap, number, multitude, quantity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, ऊह to reason, or वह to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहकार्य्य|समूहकार्य
समूहकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Interests or business of a number, general affair.<BR>E.<BR>समूह, and कार्य्य affair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहत्
समूहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Collecting, gathering.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before वह to bear, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहनी
समूहनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A broom.<BR>E.<BR>समूह heap (of dirt), णी to take, aff. ड and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूह्य|समूह्यः
समूह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be assembled or collected.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>1 Sacrificial fire.<BR>2 A place prepared for the reception of a sacrificial fire.<BR>ind.<BR>Having collected.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, वह to bear, or ऊह to reason, aff. क्यप् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्ध|समृद्धः
समृद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Happy, prosperous, thriving.<BR>2 Grown, encreased, augmented.<BR>3 Flourishing.<BR>4 Full, entire.<BR>5 Accelerated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, ऋद्ध to increase, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धवेग
समृद्धवेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Very swift.<BR>E.<BR>समृद्ध, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धि|समृद्धिः
समृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Thriving, increase.<BR>2 Prosperity, success.<BR>3 Power, supremacy, sway.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, ऋध to increase, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समेत|समेतः
समेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Near, approximated, approached.<BR>2 Agreed, covenanted.<BR>3 Collected, associated.<BR>4 Having, possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समेधित|समेधितः
समेधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Increased, augmented.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before एधित increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समोदक|समोदकं
समोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mixture of half butter milk and half water<BR>E.<BR>सम equal, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प|संपः|सम्पः
सम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Descending, falling, alighting.<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and पत to fall, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पत्ति|संपत्ति|संपत्तिः|सम्पत्तिः
सम्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Prosperity, success, increase of wealth, power, or happiness.<BR>2 A sort of medicinal root.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying perfection, पद to go, aff. क्तिन्; also सम्पट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद्|संपद्
सम्पद्<BR>f. (-पत् or पट्)<BR>1 Success, prosperity, increase of any favourable kind, or of wealth, fame, power, &c.<BR>2 Advancement in good qualities, perfection, excellence.<BR>3 A necklace of pearls, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पट् to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद|संपद|सम्पदं
सम्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Standing with the feet even.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद्धर
सम्पद्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पद to go, ष्वरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पन्न|संपन्न|संपन्नः|सम्पन्नः
सम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Accomplished, completed, effected, obtained.<BR>2 Prosperous, fortunate, thriving, happy.<BR>3 Possessed of, endowed with.<BR>4 Mature, full grown.<BR>5 Perfectly acquainted with or performing, (duty, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, पद to go, aff. क्त; also with कन् aff. सम्पन्नक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पराय|संपराय|संपरायः|सम्परायः
सम्पराय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Calamity, adversity.<BR>2 Futurity.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>4 A son.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and पर before इण् to go, नच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परायक|संपरायक|संपरायकं|सम्परायकं
सम्परायक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परायिक|संपरायिक|संपरायिकं|सम्परायिकं
सम्परायिक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम्पराय war, ठन् aff.; also सम्परायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परिशोषण|संपरिशोषण
सम्परिशोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A withering or drying up.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and परि implying entirely, शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्क|संपर्क|सम्पर्कं|संपर्कः|सम्पर्कः
सम्पर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 Mixture, mingling, contact, union, junction.<BR>2 Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, वृच to be in contact, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्क्किन्|सम्पर्किन्
सम्पर्क्किन्<BR>mfn. (-र्क्की-र्क्किणी-र्क्कि)<BR>1 Mixed, blended.<BR>2 Connected or united with.<BR>3 In contact with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, पृच् to be in contact, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्कीय|संपर्कीय|सम्पर्कीयः|सम्पर्क्कीय
सम्पर्कीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Liable to come in contact, relating to contact or connexion.<BR>E.<BR>सम्पर्क, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पश्यत्
सम्पश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>Seeing, beholding.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before दृश to see, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाक|संपाक|संपाकः|सम्पाकः
सम्पाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Reasoning, a reasoner, a logician.<BR>2 Impudent, shameless.<BR>3 Small, little, low.<BR>4 Lecherous, libertine.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, पाक ripening or maturing; also शम्पाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाट|संपाट|संपाटः|सम्पाटः
सम्पाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A spindle.<BR>2 The intersection of the prolonged side of a triangle by the perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पट to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पात|संपात|संपातः|सम्पातः
सम्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Descending, falling, coming down.<BR>2 Alighting, (as a bird.)<BR>3 Going, moving.<BR>4 The son of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पत to alight, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाति|संपाति|संपातिः|सम्पातिः
सम्पाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The son of GARUḌA, a fabulous bird.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, पा intensitive, to cherish or drink, अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=902" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पातिक|संपातिक|संपातिकः|सम्पातिकः
सम्पातिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The eldest son of GARUḌA, and like him a sort of fabulous and supernatural bird.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादक|संपादक|सम्पादकः
सम्पादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what fulfils, accomplished, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पद to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादन|संपादन|संपादनं|सम्पादनं
सम्पादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gaining, acquiring, reaching, attaining.<BR>2 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पद to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादित|संपादित|सम्पादितः
सम्पादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Attained, obtained, gained, gotten.<BR>2 Effected, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पद to go, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पिष्ट
सम्पिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pounded, bruised, crushed, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीड|संपीड|संपीडः
सम्पीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Agitating, disturbing.<BR>2 Sending, directing.<BR>3 Pain, torture.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पीड to give pain to, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीडन|संपीडन|संपीडनं|सम्पीडनं
सम्पीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Castigation, punishment.<BR>2 Agitating.<BR>3 Sending.<BR>4 Pressing, squeezing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पीड to give pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीडित|संपीडित
सम्पीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pained, tortured.<BR>2 Punished.<BR>3 Agitated.<BR>4 Sent.<BR>5 Pressed, squeezed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before पीड to pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीति|संपीति|संपीतिः|सम्पीतिः
सम्पीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Drinking in company.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, पा to drink, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पुट|संपुट|संपुटः|सम्पुटः
सम्पुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A casket, a covered box.<BR>2 A flower; also Kuruvaka.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, पुट to contract, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पुटक|संपुटक|सम्पुटकः
सम्पुटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A casket.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with पुट to contract, aff. क, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजन|संपूजन|संपूजनं
सम्पूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Treating with great respect.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and पूज to worship, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजनीय
सम्पूजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be, what may or ought to be respected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and पूज to respect, अनीयर् aff.; also सम्पूजितव्य and सम्पूज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजित|संपूजित
सम्पूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Honoured, respected.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and पूजित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूर्ण|संपूर्ण|सम्पूर्णं|सम्पूर्णः
सम्पूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Whole, entire.<BR>2 Complete, finished.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Any mode of music in which all the notes of the gamut are employed.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Æther, the etherial matter or atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and पूर्ण full, finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूर्णता|संपूर्णता
सम्पूर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fulness, completion.<BR>E.<BR>सम्पूर्ण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, सम्पूर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पृक्त|संपृक्त|सम्पृक्तः
सम्पृक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Mixed, blended, combined, inlaid, interspersed.<BR>2 Joined, untied.<BR>3 Close to, in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, पृच to be in contact, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रकॢप्त
सम्प्रकॢप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Possessed of, having.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before कॢप्त made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणर्द्दित|सम्प्रणर्दित
सम्प्रणर्द्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bellowed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before नर्द्द to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणीत|संप्रणीत
सम्प्रणीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought, conveyed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणेतृ|संप्रणेतृ
सम्प्रणेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what guides, leads, &c.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A judge, a ruler.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before णी to get, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतापन|संप्रतापन|संप्रतापनं
सम्प्रतापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Heating, burning.<BR>2 Afflicting.<BR>3 One of the twenty-one hells.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before तप to heat, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रति|संप्रति|सम्प्रतिः
सम्प्रति<BR>ind.<BR>Now, at present, at this time.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina pontiff, of the last era.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and प्रति with respect to, &c. conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिपत्ति|संप्रतिपत्ति|संप्रतिपत्तिः|सम्प्रतिपत्तिः
सम्प्रतिपत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Agreed, convened, consentient.<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Assent, concurrence.<BR>2 Admission, acknowledgment, confession.<BR>3 Agreement.<BR>4 Co-operation.<BR>5 Presence, company.<BR>6 Assault.<BR>7 Doing, performing, effecting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, प्रतिपत्ति agreement, assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिपन्न|संप्रतिपन्न
सम्प्रतिपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Done, performed.<BR>2 Come, arrived.<BR>3 Agreed, concurred.<BR>4 Attached.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्रति before पद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिरोधक|संप्रतिरोधक|संप्रतिरोधकं|सम्प्रतिरोधकं|संप्रतिरोधकः
सम्प्रतिरोधक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>Durance, actual confinement or restraint.<BR>E.<BR>सम्प्रति present, रोधक what restricts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतीक्षा|संप्रतीक्षा
सम्प्रतीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Expecting, awaiting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्रति before ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतीति|संप्रतीति|संप्रतीतिः|सम्प्रतीतिः
सम्प्रतीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fame, notoriety.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before प्रतीति the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रदान|संप्रदान|संप्रदानं|सम्प्रदानं
सम्प्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 (In grammar,) The dative case.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before दा to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रदाय|संप्रदाय|संप्रदायः|सम्प्रदायः
सम्प्रदाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Traditional doctrine, what has been transmitted from one teacher to another, and is established as of sacred authority.<BR>2 A sect, a schism, a peculiar doctrine and exclusive worship of one divinity.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before दा to give, घञ् aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रधान|संप्रधानं
सम्प्रधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Consideration, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रधारणा|संप्रधारणा
सम्प्रधारणा<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Determination, deliberation, the determining on the propriety or impropriety of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before धृ to have or hold, causal form, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रपद|संप्रपद|सम्प्रपदं|संप्रपदः
सम्प्रपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Roaming, peregrination.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before पद to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयाण|संप्रयाण|संप्रयाणं
सम्प्रयाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Departure.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before या to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयुक्त|संप्रयुक्त
सम्प्रयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Acquainted or connected with.<BR>2 Joined, united with, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before युज to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयोग|संप्रयोग|संप्रयोगः|सम्प्रयोगः
सम्प्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Connexion, relation, mutual proportion, dependance or association.<BR>2 Order, natural and connected series or arrangement.<BR>3 Copulation.<BR>4 Union, joining.<BR>5 Magic.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before युज to join, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयोगिन्|संप्रयोगिन्
सम्प्रयोगिन्<BR>m. (गी)<BR>1 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>2 A catamite.<BR>3 A joiner or uniter, any one who effects a union or connexion.<BR>4 A conjuror.<BR>E.<BR>सम्प्रयोग union in general, or coition, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रवदन|संप्रवदनं
सम्प्रवदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Conversation, talking together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before वद to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रश्न|संप्रश्न|संप्रश्नः
सम्प्रश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>Asking, enquiring civilly.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रवृत्त|संप्रवृत्त
सम्प्रवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Passed, gone by.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before वृत्त been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसाद|संप्रसाद|संप्रसादः
सम्प्रसाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Trust, confidence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before सद to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसाधन|संप्रसाधन|संप्रसाधनं
सम्प्रसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Effecting, accomplishing, performing well or completely.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before साध to accomplish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसारण|संप्रसारण|संप्रसारणं|सम्प्रसारणं
सम्प्रसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The mutual substitution of the letters इ, उ, ऋ, ऌ, and their respective semivowels, ब, य, र, and स्न.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before सृ to go, causal form, aff. ल्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=903" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रस्थान|संप्रस्थान|संप्रस्थानं
सम्प्रस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Setting out on a journey.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रस्थित
सम्प्रस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set forth, gone on a journey.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रहार|संप्रहार|संप्रहारः|सम्प्रहारः
सम्प्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Striking, wounding, killing.<BR>3 Going, motion.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रहास|संप्रहास|संप्रहासः
सम्प्रहास<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Laughter.<BR>2 Joy.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before हस to laugh, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्त|संप्राप्त|सम्प्राप्तः
सम्प्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Attained, obtained, gotten.<BR>2 Effected, accomplished.<BR>3 Become.<BR>4 Arrived, come.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्ति|संप्राप्ति|संप्राप्तिः|सम्प्राप्तिः
सम्प्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Obtaining, getting, acquisition.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before प्राप्ति obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीत|संप्रीत
सम्प्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well pleased, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and प्रीत liking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीति|संप्रीति|संप्रीतिः
सम्प्रीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Attachment, affection.<BR>2 Delight.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before प्रीति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षणं
सम्प्रेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Deliberating, considering, investigating.<BR>2 Looking at, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षित
सम्प्रेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Considered, investigated.<BR>2 Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेषित
सम्प्रेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, ordered.<BR>2 Dismissed, sent away.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before प्रेषित sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रैष|संप्रैष|संप्रैषः|सम्प्रैषः
सम्प्रैष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Ordering, commanding, directing.<BR>2 Dismissing, sending away.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before इष to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षणं
सम्प्रोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>2 Consecrating a temple.<BR>E.<BR>सम and प्र before उक्ष to sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.; see प्रोक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षित
सम्प्रोक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled, wetted, (especially with holy water.)<BR>2 Consecrated.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before उक्ष to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लव|संप्लव|संप्लवः
सम्प्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Falling in various directions.<BR>2 Submerging, inundation.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and प्लु to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फाल|संफाल|संफालः|सम्फालः
सम्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before फल to bear fruit, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फुल्ल|संफुल्ल|सम्फुल्लः
सम्फुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Blown, blossomed, opened, (as a flower.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, and फुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फेट|संफेट|संफेटः
सम्फेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>(In dramatic language) Wrathful encounter, defiance, combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब|संब|संबं|सम्बं
सम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (सम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (सम्बयति)<BR>To unite, to join, to connect or collect; also षम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब|संब|संबं|सम्बं
सम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Twice ploughing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्ब to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बद्ध|संबद्ध|सम्बद्धः
सम्बद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Connected with, endowed with, possessing as a predicate or property.<BR>2 Bound, tied, attached.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, बन्ध to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्ध|संबन्ध|संबंध|संबन्धः|सम्बन्धः
सम्बन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>1 Able, capable.<BR>2 Fit, right, proper.<BR>3 Adjunct, annexed or connected, inherent, &c.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Prosperity, success.<BR>2 Fitness, propriety.<BR>3 Connexion, natural or essential connexion, as of a property with a substance, subject matter with a work, proper meaning with a word, &c.<BR>4 Connexion by birth or marriage, relationship.<BR>5 The application of authority, as of the Upaniṣads to prove a theological assertion, &c.<BR>6 Mental association of objects, conceiving them in connexion with each other.<BR>7 (In grammar,) The possessive case.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धक|संबन्धक|संबंधक|संबन्धकः
सम्बन्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Relating to, concerning.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धिन्|संबन्धिन्|संबंधिन्
सम्बन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>1 Possessing good qualities, learned, amiable, liberal, &c.<BR>2 Having adjoined or connected with, inherent.<BR>3 Related to, a relation, a connexion.<BR>4 Connected with, belonging or relating to.<BR>E.<BR>सम्बन्ध connexion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बर|संबर|सम्बरं|संबरः|सम्बरः
सम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Restraint, forbearance, self-controul.<BR>3 A religious observance of the Bauddhas.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The name of a demon or Daitya.<BR>2 A deer.<BR>3 A sort of fish.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>5 A Jina, one of the pontiffs of the future age.<BR>6 A kind of dramatic entertainment.<BR>7 A bridge, a dam, a causeway.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्ब to accumulate, अरच् aff.; also शम्बर and सम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बल|संबल|संबलं|संबलः
सम्बल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>Provender or stock for travelling expences.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>षम्ब to go, aff. अलच्; also शम्बल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाकृत|सम्बाकृतं
सम्बाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Twice ploughed.<BR>E.<BR>सम्ब a second ploughing, कृत made, डाच् augment; also शम्बाकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाध|संबाध|संबाधः|सम्बाधः
सम्बाध<BR>adj.<BR>m. only, but having the three genders when the last term of a compound adjective.<BR>(-धः)<BR>1 Narrow, contracted, impassible, either from being naturally confined, or from being blocked up or crowded.<BR>2 Crowded.<BR>Subst.<BR>1 The vulva.<BR>2 The road to tartarus or hell.<BR>3 Fear, dread.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before बाध to impede, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधक|संबाधक
सम्बाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Crowding, contracting, pressing upon.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before बाध to obstruct, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधन|संबाधन|संबाधनं|सम्बाधनं
सम्बाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A gate, a barrier.<BR>2 The point of a stake or spit.<BR>3 A door-keeper.<BR>4 Obstructing, opposing.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before बाध to impede, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्ध|संबुद्ध|संबुद्धः|सम्बुद्धः
सम्बुद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>A Jaina deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying perfection, and बुद्ध wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्धि|संबुद्धि|संबुद्धिः|सम्बुद्धिः
सम्बुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Calling or calling to.<BR>2 An epithet.<BR>3 The vocative case.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with बुध to know, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोध|संबोध|संबोधः|सम्बोधः
सम्बोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Explaining, instructing, informing.<BR>2 Throwing, sending.<BR>3 Loss, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, बुध to know, causal form, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधन|संबोधन|संबोधनं|सम्बोधनं
सम्बोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calling, addressing, calling to.<BR>2 The vocative case, (in grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and बुध to know, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भली|संभली
सम्भली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भल to speak, affs. अच् and ङीष्; also शम्भली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव|संभव|संभवः|सम्भवः
सम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Cause, origin, motive.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Mixing, union, combination.<BR>4 Capacity, appropriateness, adaptation, the conformity of the receptacle to the thing received, or supported to the thing supported.<BR>5 Agreement, engagement.<BR>6 Loss, destruction.<BR>7 Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>8 Possibility.<BR>9 Ability, adequacy.<BR>10 Consistency, compatibility.<BR>11 The third Jina of the present age.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying perfection or co-existence, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव्य|संभव्य|संभव्यः|सम्भव्यः
सम्भव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>The wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भव being, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार|संभार|संभारः|सम्भारः
सम्भार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Multitude, number, quantity, heap, assemblage.<BR>2 Maintaining, supporting.<BR>3 Provision, preparation, getting [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">Page905</a>] every thing ready or complete.<BR>4 Fulness, completion.<BR>5 Apparatus, necessaries, things required for any act or affair.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before भृ to maintain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=904" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार्य्य|सम्भार्य|संभार्य
सम्भार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be nourished, a dependant.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भॄ to nourish, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावन|संभावन|संभावनं|सम्भावनं
सम्भावन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Considering, reflecting.<BR>2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>3 Fitness, suitableness.<BR>4 Adequacy, competency, ability.<BR>5 Possibility.<BR>5 Worship, honour.<BR>7 (In grammar,) The sense of the potential mood.<BR>8 (In rhetoric,) The use of the verb in the imperative or potential mood.<BR>9 (In Logic,) Doubt.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before भू to be, causal form, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावित|संभावित|सम्भावितः
सम्भावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Equal or adequate to, suited to or fit for.<BR>2 Possible.<BR>3 Considered, reflected.<BR>4 Satisfied or occupied with.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भू to be, &c., causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावितात्मन्
सम्भावितात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Noble-minded.<BR>E.<BR>सम्भावित equal, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाव्य|संभाव्य
सम्भाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Suitable, to be adapted to, made, or fit for.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भू to be, causal v., यत् aff. also सम्भावनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषण|संभाषण|संभाषणं|सम्भाषणं
सम्भाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Conversation, discourse.<BR>2 War-cry, watchword.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषा|संभाषा
सम्भाषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 War-cry, watch-word.<BR>2 Conversation, discourse.<BR>3 Contract, agreement.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषित|संभाषित
सम्भाषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, spoken.<BR>2 Spoken to, addressed.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before भाष to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भिन्न|संभिन्न|संभिन्नः|सम्भिन्नः
सम्भिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Shaken, agitated.<BR>2 Divided, broken.<BR>3 Combined or united with.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भु|संभु|सम्भुः
सम्भु<BR>m. (-म्भुः)<BR>A parent, a progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with भू to be, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुग्न
सम्भुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Bent, curved.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भुग्न bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूत|संभूत|सम्भूतः
सम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Equal, adequate.<BR>3 Combined with, being together.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भू to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूतविजय|संभूतविजय|सम्भूतविजयः
सम्भूतविजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sacred person peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूति|संभूति|संभूतिः
सम्भूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Combination.<BR>3 Power.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भू to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूय|संभूय
सम्भूय<BR>ind.<BR>Having united or combined.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, भू to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूयकारिन्|संभूयकारिन्
सम्भूयकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A coadjutor, copartner, or colleague.<BR>E.<BR>सम्भूय, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूयसमुत्थान|सम्भूयसमुत्थानं
सम्भूयसमुत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Partnership, association in trade, joint execution of work or conduct of business.<BR>E.<BR>सम्भूय, and समुत्थान performance of work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत|संभृत|सम्भृतः
सम्भृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Collected, assembled.<BR>2 Gained, got, possessed of.<BR>3 Filled, full.<BR>4 Complete, ready, prepared.<BR>5 Nourished, maintained.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before भृ to nourish, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृति|संभृति|संभृतिः|सम्भृतिः
सम्भृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Nourishment, support.<BR>2 Plenitude, fulness.<BR>3 Preparation, provision.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भृ to possess, aff. क्तिन्, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत्य|संभृत्य
सम्भृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be nourished.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भृ to nourish, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भेट्
सम्भेट्<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The confluence of two rivers, or the junction of a river with the sea.<BR>2 Breaking, splitting, bursting.<BR>3 Union, junction.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भिट् to break, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोग|संभोग|संभोगः|सम्भोगः
सम्भोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Enjoyment, pleasure, delight.<BR>2 Coition, copulation.<BR>3 A Jaina or Bauddha Śasana or edict, &c.<BR>4 One branch of the Śṛṅgāra rasa, or sentiment of love, happy or successful love, meeting or union of lovers.<BR>5 A catamite.<BR>6 Use, employment.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोगिन्|संभोगिन्
सम्भोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Sensual, sensualist, &c.<BR>2 Enjoying, as pleasure or property.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>सम्भोग enjoyment, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोजन|संभोजन|संभोजनं
सम्भोजन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Convivial, friendly, (as a dinner, &c.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A meal, &c. partaken together, a convivial party.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, भुज to enjoy, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रम|संभ्रम|संभ्रमः|सम्भ्रमः
सम्भ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Haste, hurry.<BR>2 Fear, terror.<BR>3 Flurry, confusion, haste or hurry arising from joy, fear, &c.<BR>4 Error, ignorance.<BR>5 Turning round, whirling, revolving.<BR>6 Respect, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before भ्रम to revolve, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रान्त|संभ्रांत|संभ्रान्त
सम्भ्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Bewildered, agitated.<BR>2 Flurried.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and भ्रम to err, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मत|संमत
सम्मत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Assented or agreed to, concurred in, approved of.<BR>2 Conformable to.<BR>3 Attached to.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and मन to mind, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मति|संमति|संमतिः|सम्मतिः
सम्मति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Order, command.<BR>3 Agreement, assent, similarity of opinion, or purpose.<BR>4 Approbation.<BR>5 Self or real knowledge.<BR>6 Regard, affection, love.<BR>7 Respect, homage.<BR>E.<BR>सम् implying union or perfection, and मति mind, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मद|संमद|संमदः|सम्मदः
सम्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Happy, glad.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Happiness, joy, pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, मट् to delight, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द्द|सम्मर्द|संमर्दः|सम्मर्द्दः
सम्मर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 Trampling or treading on.<BR>2 Friction, rubbing.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, मृद् to trample, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द्दिन्|सम्मर्दिन्|संमर्दिन्
सम्मर्द्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दी-र्द्दिनी-र्द्दि)<BR>1 Trampling.<BR>2 Rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>सम्मर्द्द, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मातुर|संमातुर
सम्मातुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of a virtuous woman.<BR>E.<BR>सत् good, मातृ a mother, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्माद|संमाद|संमादः|सम्मादः
सम्माद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Phrensy, intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, मद to be mad, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान|संमान|संमानः|सम्मानः
सम्मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Respect, homage.<BR>2 Measure.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and मन to respect, with घञ् aff., or मा to measure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानन|संमानन|संमाननं
सम्मानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worship, homage.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, मन to respect, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानित|संमानित|सम्मानितः
सम्मानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Treated with reverence or respect.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मन to respect, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान्य|संमान्य
सम्मान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Respectable, honourable.<BR>E.<BR>सम्मन् to respect, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जक|संमार्जक|संमार्जकः|सम्मार्ज्जकः
सम्मार्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sweeper.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, मृज to clean, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जन|संमार्जन|संमार्जनं|सम्मार्ज्जनं
सम्मार्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sweeping, brushing, cleaning.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A broom.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मृज to clean, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मित|संमित|संमितं|सम्मितः
सम्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Like, similar, same.<BR>2 Of equal measure or extent.<BR>3 Meted, measured.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, मित measured, compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्र|संमिश्र|सम्मिश्रः
सम्मिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Mixed, mingled, blended, joined.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, and मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुख|संमुख|सम्मुखः
सम्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा or -खी-खं)<BR>Encountering, facing, in front of.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखिन्|संमुखिन्
सम्मुखिन्<BR>m. (-खी)<BR>A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, मुख the face, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=905" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखीन|संमुखीन|सम्मुखीनः
सम्मुखीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Before, in front or in face of.<BR>E.<BR>सम्मुख the same, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुग्ध|संमुग्ध
सम्मुग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Fascinated, bewildered.<BR>2 Stupified, astounded.<BR>3 Beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मुह to fascinate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूढ|संमूढ|सम्मूढः
सम्मूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-टा-ढं)<BR>1 Heaped, accumulated.<BR>2 Produced rapidly.<BR>3 Broken.<BR>4 Foolish, ignorant, senseless.<BR>5 Bewildered, beguiled.<BR>6 Stupified, astounded.<BR>E.<BR>सम् entirely, मुह to be foolish, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूढचेतस्
सम्मूढचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Foolish, infatuated.<BR>E.<BR>सम्मूढ, and चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्च्छन
सम्मूर्च्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Uniform or universal expansion or permeation, pervading, co-extension.<BR>2 Height, elevation.<BR>3 Fainting, insensibility.<BR>4 Increasing, augmenting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मूर्च्छ to faint, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्च्छनोद्भव
सम्मूर्च्छनोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A fish or aquatic animal.<BR>E.<BR>सम्मूर्च्छन insensibility, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृत|संमृत
सम्मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>E.<BR>सम्, and मृत dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृष्ट|संमृष्ट|सम्मृष्टः
सम्मृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Strained, filtered.<BR>2 Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>3 Swept.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, मृष्ट cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोद|संमोद|संमोदः|सम्मोदः
सम्मोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>सम् intensitive, मुद to be happy, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोह|संमोह|संमोहः
सम्मोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Ignorance.<BR>2 Folly.<BR>3 Beguilement, fascination.<BR>4 Stupefaction.<BR>5 Fainting.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मुह to be foolish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोहित
सम्मोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Beguiled, fascinated.<BR>2 Enraptured, overcome with delight, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before मुह to be foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यक्
सम्यक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 All, wholly.<BR>2 Properly, fitly, in the right manner: see सम्यच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यक्त्व
सम्यक्त्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Accuracy, totality.<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यक्दण्डन
सम्यक्दण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inflicting the penalty of the law, punishing in a legal manner.<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक् properly, according to the Śāstras, and दण्डन punishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यच्
सम्यच् or सम्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (सम्यङ् समीची सम्यक्)<BR>1 True, right.<BR>2 Accompanying, going with.<BR>3 Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>4 Same, common, identical, uniform.<BR>5 Accurate, correct.<BR>6 All, entire.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, अञ्च to go, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यगुक्त
सम्यगुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Of equal weight or authority, (a precept.)<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक् proper, उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यग्वर्त्तमान|सम्यग्वर्तमान
सम्यग्वर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Continuing in the discharge of duty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक्, and वर्त्तमान being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यग्वृत्ति|सम्यग्वृत्तिः
सम्यग्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Steady and regular discharge of prescribed duties.<BR>E.<BR>सम्यक्, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्
सम्राज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A paramount sovereign, one who rules-over other princes, and has performed the Rājasūya sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सम् all, राजृ to rule, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयत्न
सयत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Endeavouring, taking pains.<BR>n. adv. (-त्नं)<BR>Vigorously, assiduously.<BR>E.<BR>स with, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोनि|सयोनिः
सयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Proximity to a wife.<BR>3 A pair of nippers for cutting betel-nut.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, or सम् like, and योनि pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what goes, occurring chiefly in composition, as अनुसर, अवसर, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The thick part or coagulum of curds or milk, cream, &c.<BR>2 Going, motion.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 Saltness, salt.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A lake, a pool.<BR>2 Water.<BR>mf. (-रः-रा) or (री)<BR>A cascade, a water-fall; also शर.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरःकाक|सरःकाकः
सरःकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gander.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pool, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरक|सरकं|सरकः
सरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Going, moving, proceeding.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor, especially distilled from sugar, rum.<BR>2 Drinking spirits.<BR>3 A drinking vessel.<BR>4 Distribution of liquor.<BR>5 A continuous line of road.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A lake, a pool.<BR>2 Heaven, sky.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, Uṇādi. aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरघा
सरघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>सर one who is going, हन् to injure, aff. ड, and the radical final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरज|सरजं
सरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>सर cream, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्
सरजस्<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, रजस् the menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट्
सरट्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 (In the language of the Vedas,) A bee.<BR>4 A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अटि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट|सरटः
सरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon, a guana, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अटन् aff.; also शरट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटि|सरटिः
सरटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अटिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटु|सरटुः
सरटु<BR>n. (-टुः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अटु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Going, moving, who or what goes or moves.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Oxidized iron, either in the state of rust or filings.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>f. (-णा or णी)<BR>1 A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>2 A sort of Teori.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. युच्, or ल्युट् fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्; also शरण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणि|सरणिः
सरणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 A road, a path, a way.<BR>2 A straight or continuous line.<BR>3 A disease of the throat.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, Uṇādi aff. अनि, and ङीष् optionally added; also शरणि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्ड|सरंड|सरंडः|सरण्डः
सरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>2 A sort of ornament.<BR>3 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, Uṇādi aff. अण्डन्, more usually शरण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यु|सरण्युः
सरण्यु<BR>m. (-ण्युः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अन्यु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
सरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
सरत्<BR>m. (-रत्)<BR>Thread.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्नि|सरत्निः
सरत्नि<BR>mf. (-त्निः-त्निः)<BR>A short cubit.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, कत्निच् aff.; more commonly रत्नि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरपत्रिका
सरपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The new leaf of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभस
सरभस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Quick, speedy.<BR>2 Delighted.<BR>3 Agitated, distressed.<BR>n. adv. (-सं)<BR>Quickly, delightedly, agitatedly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स with, रभस speed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 The wife of RĀVAṆA'S brother.<BR>2 A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अम aff., or स with रम sport, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयु|सरयुः
सरयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>f. (-युः-यूः)<BR>The Sarju or Saryu river.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अयु Uṇādi aff.: also शरयु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Honest, sincere, candid, upright.<BR>2 Straight.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>2 A bird, (Pavo bicalcarata.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A variety of the plant called Teori.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (to spread fragrance abroad, &.,) कल Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलद्रव|सरलद्रवः
सरलद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A fragrant resin, the exudation of the Saral or pine tree.<BR>E.<BR>सरल as above, द्रव what exudes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=906" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलयायिन्
सरलयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Going in a straight line.<BR>2 Upright, honest.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant with an upright stem.<BR>E.<BR>सरल, and यायिन् who or what goes or grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरव्य|सरव्यं
सरव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A butt or mark for shooting at.<BR>E.<BR>सर an arrow, व्येञ् to cover, aff. ड; also शरव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस्<BR>nf. (-रः-सी)<BR>1 A large pond or pool.<BR>2 A piece of water in which the lotus grows or may grow.<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go (into, to bathe or drink), असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Tasty, juicy, sapid.<BR>2 Comprising the expression of the poetical Rasas or sentiments, (a work, &c.)<BR>3 Impassioned.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>A tank, a pond, a lake.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A sort of Teori.<BR>E.<BR>स with, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसम्प्रत|सरसंप्रत|सरसम्प्रतं
सरसम्प्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A sort of Euphorbia, commonly Tiṅkātā Sij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिक|सरसिकः
सरसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>सरस a pool, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिज|सरसिजं
सरसिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pool, (seventh case,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीरुह|सरसीरुहं|सरसीरुहः
सरसीरुह<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सरसी a pool, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्तीर
सरस्तीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The bank of a lake or pond.<BR>E.<BR>सरस्, and तीर bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वत्|सरस्वन्त्
सरस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>1 Juicy, sapid.<BR>2 Elegant.<BR>3 Sentimental.<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A male river.<BR>3 A buffalo.<BR>f. (-स्वती)<BR>1 The wife of BRAHMĀ, the goddess of speech and eloquence, the patroness of music and the arts, and the inventress of the Sanscrit language and Devanāgarī letters.<BR>2 Speech, the faculty or its exercise.<BR>3 A river, the Sarsooty, which rises in the mountains bounding the north-east part of the province of Dehli, whence it runs in a south-westerly direction, and is lost in the sands of the great desart in the country of the Bhatti; according to the Hindus the river only disappears in this place, and continuing its course under ground, joins the Ganges and Jumna at Allahabad.<BR>4 A river in general.<BR>5 An excellent woman.<BR>6 A crow.<BR>7 The wife of a Muni.<BR>8 A female divinity, peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>9 The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a lake, and मतुप् poss. aff., or स with, रस flavour, taste, and the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
सराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Coloured, tinted.<BR>2 Impassioned.<BR>E.<BR>स with, राग colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराव|सरावः
सराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A lid, or a shallow cup or saucer, used as one: see शराव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरि|सरिः
सरि<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A waterfall.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, इन् aff.; also सर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिका
सरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 A woman going, or moving.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, वुन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित्<BR>f. (-रित्)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 Thread.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, इति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिताम्पति|सरितांपति|सरिताम्पतिः
सरिताम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् a river, (second case plural,) and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्पति|सरित्पतिः
सरित्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् a river, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्वत्|सरित्वन्त्
सरित्वत्<BR>m. (-त्वान्)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् a river, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्सुत|सरित्सुतः
सरित्सुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>BHĪṢMA, the son of GAṄGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् the river, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिद्वरा
सरिद्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् a river, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्नाथ|सरिन्नाथः
सरिन्नाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सरित् a river, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्मुख
सरिन्मुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The source of a river.<BR>E.<BR>सरित्, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिमन्
सरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, इमनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिल|सरिलं
सरिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>see सलिल, the ल being changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिषप|सरिषपः
सरिषप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीसृप|सरीसृपः
सरीसृप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, irr. reiterative form, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरु|सरुः
सरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Thin, small, fine, minute.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूप|सरूपः
सरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Like, resembling.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान like, same, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूपता
सरूपता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Likeness, resemblance.<BR>E.<BR>सरूप like, तल् aff. of the abstract; also सरूपत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोग
सरोग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>स, and रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोगिता
सरोगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>स, and रोगिता sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोज|सरोजं|सरोजः
सरोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A foot (in Prosody,) of six long instants.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pond, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजन्मन्
सरोजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pond, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजल
सरोजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The water of a pond or lake.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pond, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजिन्
सरोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A pond abounding in lotuses.<BR>3 A multitude of lotuses.<BR>E.<BR>सरोज a lotus, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोत्सव|सरोत्सवः
सरोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>सर water, उत्सव pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोध|सरोधः
सरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Loss, destruction.<BR>2 Opposition, obstruction.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, रोघ hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुह्
सरोरुह्<BR>n. (-रुट्)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pond, and रुह् what grows; also with a final vowel सरोरुह n. (-हं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुहासन|सरोरुहासनः
सरोरुहासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सरोरुह a lotus, and आसन a seat; first appearing from the interior of a lotus in order to create the world; the flower is supposed to have sprung from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोवर|सरोवरः
सरोवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lake or large pond, any piece of water deep enough for the lotus to grow.<BR>E.<BR>सरम् a pool, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोष
सरोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Angry, wrathful.<BR>n. adv. (-षं)<BR>Angrily.<BR>E.<BR>स with, रोष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ग|सर्गः
सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Nature, natural property or disposition.<BR>2 Tendency of a thing.<BR>3 Creation.<BR>4 Effort, perseverance.<BR>5 Assent, agreement.<BR>6 Relinquishment, abandoning, letting go or getting rid of.<BR>7 Voiding, as excrement.<BR>8 A chapter, a book, a section.<BR>9 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to quit, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्गबन्ध|सर्गबंध|सर्गबन्धः
सर्गबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A principal or great poem, one comprising many Sargas or Cantos.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ग a section, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्ज|सर्ज|सर्जः|सर्ज्जः
सर्ज्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (सर्ज्जति)<BR>To gain or get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्ज|सर्ज|सर्जः|सर्ज्जः
सर्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>1 The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>2 Another tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>3 The resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to quit, aff. घञ्, and the final consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जक|सर्जक|सर्जकः|सर्ज्जकः
सर्ज्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Pentaptera arjuna.<BR>2 The Śāl tree.<BR>f. (-र्जिका)<BR>1 Natron, alkali.<BR>2 Borax.<BR>E.<BR>वुन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जगन्धा|सर्जगन्धा
सर्ज्जगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, commonly Rasan, supposed to be the serpent Ophioxylon.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्ज the Śāl tree, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=907" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जन|सर्जन|सर्जनं|सर्ज्जनं
सर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The reserve or rear of an army.<BR>2 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>3 Voiding, as excrement.<BR>4 Making, creating.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to abandon, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जमणि|सर्जमणि|सर्जमणिः|सर्ज्जमणिः
सर्ज्जमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Resin in general, or the resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्ज the Śāl, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जरस|सर्जरस|सर्जरसः|सर्ज्जरसः
सर्ज्जरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Resin in general, or the resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्ज the Śāl, and रम juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जि|सर्जि|सर्जिः|सर्ज्जिः
सर्ज्जि<BR>f. (-र्ज्जिः)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to abandon, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जिका|सर्जिका
सर्ज्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Natron, alkali, or the impure carbonate of soda, commonly termed Sejji Mitti or Sejji earth, and used in India as a soap for cleaning linen, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्जि the same, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जिकाक्षार|सर्जिकाक्षार|सर्जिकाक्षारः|सर्ज्जिकाक्षारः
सर्ज्जिकाक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Impure carbonate of soda, alkali, natron.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्जिका the same, and क्षार ashes; also स्वर्ज्जिकाक्षार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जू|सर्जू
सर्ज्जू<BR>m. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>A trader.<BR>f. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 A necklace.<BR>3 Going, following.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ज्ज to gain, Uṇādi aff. ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प|सर्पः
सर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>1 A snake, a serpent.<BR>2 Gentle or twining motion, gliding, flowing, creeping.<BR>f. (-र्पी)<BR>The female of the snake.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, to glide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पकङ्काली
सर्पकङ्काली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, commonly Sāmpkaṅkāli or serpent's skeleton.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, कङ्काल a skeleton, fem. aff. of diminutiveness or comparison, ङीष्; also with कन् added सर्पकङ्कालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पगन्धा
सर्पगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, perhaps the same as the serpent ophioxylon.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पघातिनी
सर्पघातिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant: see सर्पकङ्काली.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and घातिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प्पछत्र|सर्पच्छत्र|सर्पछत्र
सर्प्पछत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प्प, and छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प्पण|सर्पण|सर्पणं
सर्प्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going, gliding.<BR>2 The slow flight of an arrow nearly parallel to the ground.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प्पत्|सर्पत्
सर्प्पत्<BR>mfn. (-र्प्पन्-र्प्पन्ती-र्प्पत)<BR>Going, gliding, creeping.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पदंष्ट्र|सर्पदंष्ट्रः
सर्पदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>1 A snake's tooth.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>A plant, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्प, and दंष्ट्र a tooth^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प्पफणज|सर्पफणज|सर्पफणजः
सर्प्पफणज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The snake-stone, a gem or pearl said to resemble in form the berry of the Abrus precatorius, and to be found in the head of the snake.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प्प a snake, फण hood, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पभुज्
सर्पभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 A crane.<BR>3 A large snake.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पमणि|सर्पमणिः
सर्पमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The snake-stone or carbuncle, or a jewel said to be found in the head of a snake, possessing also alexipharmic properties.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पमाला
सर्पमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, commonly Serpakankali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पराज|सर्पराजः
सर्पराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>VĀSUKI, sovereign of the serpent race, inhabiting Pātāla or the regions under the earth.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and राज a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पसत्रिन्
सर्पसत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A name of the prince JANAMEJAYA, the son of PARIKṢIT.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and सच a sacrifice, इनि aff.; having compelled by Mantras all the snakes to be present at a sacrifice performed for their destruction, in retaliation of the death of his father who was killed by the bite of a snake; all were destroyed on this occasion except a few of the chiefs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पसहा
सर्पसहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant: see सर्पकङ्काली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पहन्
सर्पहन्<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An ichneumon, a mungoose.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and हन who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाक्ष|सर्पाक्षं
सर्पाक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The seed of the Elæocarpus.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A plant, commonly Kaṅkālika.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाख्य|सर्पाख्यः
सर्पाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and आख्या an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाङ्गी
सर्पाङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant, Sarpakaṅkālī or a variety of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाराति|सर्पारातिः
सर्पाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 GARUḌA.<BR>2 An ichneumon.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पारि|सर्पारिः
सर्पारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An ichneumon.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and अरि an enemy, equally applicable to the peacock, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाशन|सर्पाशनः
सर्पाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, and अशत food: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिन्
सर्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि)<BR>Going gently or tortuously, gliding, winding, creeping.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A female serpent.<BR>2 A small medicinal shrub.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प a snake, or going, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्
सर्पिस्<BR>n. (-र्पिः)<BR>Ghee, clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to flow, इस् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्समुद्र
सर्पिस्समुद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The sea of clarified butter, one of the seven seas.<BR>E.<BR>सर्पिस् Ghee, समुद्र the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पेष्ट|सर्पेष्टं
सर्पेष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्ब|सर्ब
सर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (सर्ब्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्ब|सर्ब
सर्ब्ब<BR>mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्ब)<BR>All, whole, entire.<BR>E.<BR>षर्ब्ब to go, aff. अच्; as differently read, with a final semivowel, सर्ब्बं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्बंसह
सर्ब्बंसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Patient, enduring.<BR>2 All-sustaining.<BR>E.<BR>सर्ब्ब all, सह to bear, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्म्म|सर्म|सर्मः
सर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्व|सर्व|सर्वः|सर्व्वः
सर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>All, whole, complete, universal, entire.<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, to pervade, (the world,) and वन् Uṇādi aff.; also according to some authorities preferably सर्ब्ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वंसह|सर्वंसह
सर्व्वंसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Patient, enduring.<BR>2 All-sustaining.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (men,) सह to bear or suffer, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वक|सर्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्व्वक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>All, every.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्त्तृ|सर्वकर्तृ|सर्वकर्त्तृ
सर्व्वकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all (things), कर्त्तृ maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्म्मन्|सर्वकर्मन्
सर्व्वकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>All or every act.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A man of all work.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्म्मीण|सर्वकर्मीण|सर्व्वकर्म्मीणः
सर्व्वकर्म्मीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Performing or conversant with every business, pervading every action, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, कर्म्म act, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकारिन्|सर्वकारिन्
सर्व्वकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>The maker of all things.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकाल|सर्वकाल
सर्व्वकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>All seasons or times.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकालीन|सर्वकालीन
सर्व्वकालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of all times or seasons.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वके|सर्वके
सर्व्वके<BR>ind.<BR>Every where, universally.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व in all, and अकच inserted before the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकेशिन्|सर्वकेशिन्
सर्व्वकेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वक्षार|सर्वक्षार|सर्वक्षारः|सर्व्वक्षारः
सर्व्वक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Any substance of an alkaline or soapy nature, as impure soda, pearl ash or potash, &c. which may be used in cleaning clothes.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and क्षार impure alkali or alkaline salt or ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=908" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वग|सर्वग|सर्वगः|सर्व्वगं|सर्व्वगः
सर्व्वग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going every where, all-pervading.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Water.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 BRAHMA.<BR>3 Soul, spirit.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वगत|सर्वगत
सर्व्वगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Omnipresent, universally diffused.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वगन्ध|सर्वगन्ध|सर्व्वगन्धं
सर्व्वगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A class of four aromatics, or Kakkol, cloves, agallochum, and gum benjamin.<BR>2 A perfume in general.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वग्रन्थिक|सर्वग्रन्थिक|सर्व्वग्रन्थिकं
सर्व्वग्रन्थिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, ग्रन्थि a knot, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वङ्कष|सर्वङ्कष|सर्वंकषः
सर्व्वङ्कष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>All-pervading, diffused, extended.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A rogue, a wicked man.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and कष to go, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वचर्म्मीण|सर्वचर्मीण|सर्व्वचर्म्मीणः
सर्व्वचर्म्मीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Made of every kind of skin or leather.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, चर्म्म skin, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजगत्|सर्वजगत्
सर्व्वजगत्<BR>f. (-त्)<BR>The universe, the whole world.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and जगत् world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजनीन|सर्वजनीन|सर्व्वजनीनः
सर्व्वजनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating to all men, fit for all, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, जन mankind, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजित्|सर्वजित्
सर्व्वजित्<BR>mfn. (-जित्)<BR>1 All-subduing, irresistible.<BR>2 All-surpassing, excellent, incomparable.<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The twenty-first year of the cycle.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, जित् who subdues or surpasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वज्ञ|सर्वज्ञ|सर्व्वज्ञः
सर्व्वज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Omniscient, all-wise.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A Jina or Buddha, or deified sage peculiar to those sects.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वज्ञत्व|सर्वज्ञत्व
सर्व्वज्ञत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Omniscience.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, सर्व्वज्ञता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतःशुभा|सर्वतःशुभा
सर्व्वतःशुभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A plant, (Priyangu.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वतस् wholly, शुभ auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतन्त्र|सर्वतन्त्र|सर्वतन्त्रः|सर्व्वतन्त्रः
सर्व्वतन्त्र<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>A man who has studied the Tantra Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, तन्त्र a Tantra, properly with an affix of derivation. &c., as ठक्, and that again rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतस्|सर्वतस्
सर्व्वतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Every way, all round.<BR>2 Wholly, entirely.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतापन|सर्वतापन|सर्वतापनः|सर्व्वतापनः
सर्व्वतापन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, तापन inflamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतेजस्|सर्वतेजस्
सर्व्वतेजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>All-splendour or power.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and तेजस् light, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतेजोमय|सर्वतेजोमय
सर्व्वतेजोमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made, comprising or consisting of all splendour or power.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वतेजम्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतोभद्र|सर्वतोभद्र|सर्वतोभद्रः|सर्व्वतोभद्रं|सर्व्वतोभद्रः
सर्व्वतोभद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Every where auspicious.<BR>mn. (-द्रः-द्रं)<BR>A temple or palace of a square form, with an entrance opposed to each point of the compass.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 The Nimb tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR>2 The carriage of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A bambu.<BR>4 A form of military array.<BR>5 A square mystical diagram, to be painted on the cloth which on particular occasions covers a sort of altar erected to VIṢṆU.<BR>6 A kind of charade, in which the same word answers several questions.<BR>7 A whimsical form of verse, so contrived that the same meanings and words occur, whether the line be read backwards or forwards, or in several other directions.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>2 An actress or the wife of an actor or dancer, &c.<BR>3 A sort of yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वतस् on every side, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतोमुख|सर्वतोमुख|सर्वतोमुखः|सर्व्वतोमुखं|सर्व्वतोमुखः
सर्व्वतोमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Sky, heaven.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 Soul, spirit.<BR>4 A Brahman.<BR>5 Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वतस् on every side, मुख countenance, or chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्र|सर्वत्र
सर्व्वत्र<BR>ind.<BR>1 Everywhere, in all places.<BR>2 Always, at all times.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and चल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्रग|सर्वत्रग|सर्वत्रगः|सर्व्वत्रगः
सर्व्वत्रग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>All pervading, going every where.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वत्र every where, गम to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्रगामिन्|सर्वत्रगामिन्
सर्व्वत्रगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वत्र always, गामिन् going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वथा|सर्वथा
सर्व्वथा<BR>ind. f. (-था)<BR>1 In all ways, by all means.<BR>2 Assuredly, certainly.<BR>3 Exceeding, mostly.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and श्वाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदमन|सर्वदमन|सर्व्वदमनः
सर्व्वदमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>All-subduing, irresistible.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BHARATA, the son of ŚAKUNTALĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, दमन taming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदर्शिन्|सर्वदर्शिन्
सर्व्वदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>All-seeing.<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>A Buddha in general.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and दर्शिन् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदा|सर्वदा
सर्व्वदा<BR>ind.<BR>Always, at all times.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदुःखक्षय|सर्वदुःखक्षय|सर्वदुःखक्षयः|सर्व्वदुःखक्षयः
सर्व्वदुःखक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Final emancipation from transmigration.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, दुःख pain, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदेवमय|सर्वदेवमय|सर्वदेवमयः
सर्व्वदेवमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of or comprising all the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वदेव, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदेवमुख|सर्वदेवमुख|सर्वदेवमुखः|सर्व्वदेवमुखः
सर्व्वदेवमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, देव a deity, and मुख mouth; being the medium of oblations to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधन|सर्वधन
सर्व्वधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Whole wealth or property.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Total of a sum in progression.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and घन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधर्म्मविद्|सर्वधर्मविद्
सर्व्वधर्म्मविद्<BR>m. (-विट् वित्)<BR>One who knows the duties of all tribes and classes.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and धर्म्म duty, विट् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधारी|सर्वधारी
सर्व्वधारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The twenty-second year of the cycle.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, धृ to hold, अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधुरावह|सर्वधुरावह|सर्व्वधुरावहः
सर्व्वधुरावह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An ox fit for any sort of carriage.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, धुर a burthen, आङ् before वह to bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधुरीण|सर्वधुरीण|सर्वधुरीणः|सर्व्वधुरीणः
सर्व्वधुरीण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An ox, &c. fit for any carriage or draught.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, धुर a burthen, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनामता|सर्वनामता
सर्व्वनामता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The quality or condition of a pronoun.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वनाम, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनामन्|सर्वनामन्
सर्व्वनामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>A pronoun.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and नामन् name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनाश|सर्वनाश
सर्व्वनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Total destruction, destruction of all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and नाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वन्दम|सर्वन्दम|सर्वंदमः|सर्व्वन्दमः
सर्व्वन्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, दम to tame or subdue, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपथ|सर्वपथ
सर्व्वपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Every way, every direction.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and पथ for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपथीन|सर्वपथीन
सर्व्वपथीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>In or of every road or direction, (moving, passing, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वपथ, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपा|सर्वपा
सर्व्वपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The wife of the Daitya BALI.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, पा to drink, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपूर्ण्णत्व|सर्वपूर्णत्व|सर्वपूर्णत्वं|सर्व्वपूर्णत्व|सर्व्वपूर्णत्वं
सर्व्वपूर्ण्णत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Entire completion or fulness, complete preparation or provision.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and पूर्णत्व fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वप्रिय|सर्वप्रिय|सर्व्वप्रियः
सर्व्वप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Generally or universally beloved.<BR>2 Generally friendly, loving all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and प्रिय dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभक्ष|सर्वभक्ष|सर्वभक्षः
सर्व्वभक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Omnivorous, eating all or any thing.<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A female goat.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभक्ष्य|सर्वभक्ष्य
सर्व्वभक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Eating any thing or all things, (a child.)<BR>2 All-devouring, omnivorous.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and भक्ष्य edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=909" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभाव|सर्वभाव|सर्वभावः
सर्व्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Whole disposition, all one's thoughts and purpose.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूत|सर्वभूत
सर्व्वभूत<BR>n. plu. (-तानि)<BR>1 All the elements.<BR>2 All created things.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and भूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतकृत्|सर्वभूतकृत्
सर्व्वभूतकृत्<BR>mn. (-कृत्)<BR>1 The maker of all things.<BR>2 The cause of all elements or beings.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वभूत, and कृत् who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतमय|सर्वभूतमय
सर्व्वभूतमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Comprising or comprehending all elementary matter.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The supreme pervading spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वभूत, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतस्थ|सर्वभूतस्थ
सर्व्वभूतस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Present in all elements or beings.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, भूत an element, and स्थ what stays; also सर्व्वभूतस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतात्मन्|सर्वभूतात्मन्
सर्व्वभूतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>Universal, all-pervading spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वभूत an element, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभृत्|सर्वभृत्
सर्व्वभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Cherishing or supporting all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and भृत् who or what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभोगिन्|सर्वभोगिन्
सर्व्वभोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Enjoying all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and भोगिन् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभोगीण|सर्वभोगीण
सर्व्वभोगीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Good or beneficial for all, to be enjoyed or possessed by all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, भोग enjoyment, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमङ्गला|सर्वमङ्गला|सर्वमंगला
सर्व्वमङ्गला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमय|सर्वमय|सर्व्वमयः
सर्व्वमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>General, universal, comprehensive, comprehending.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमही|सर्वमही
सर्व्वमही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>The whole earth.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and मही earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमूल्य|सर्वमूल्य|सर्व्वमूल्यं
सर्व्वमूल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>A Cowrie or small coin represented by it.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (of all things,) मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमूषक|सर्वमूषक|सर्वमूषकः|सर्व्वमूषकः
सर्व्वमूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Time.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (things,) मूष to steal, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरस|सर्वरस|सर्वरसः|सर्व्वरसः
सर्व्वरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Resin, the exudation of the pine or Śāl.<BR>2 A sort of musical instrument, a kind of lute.<BR>3 A scholar, a learned man.<BR>4 Saltness, salt, saline flavour or taste.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, रस taste, real or figurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरसोत्तम|सर्वरसोत्तम|सर्व्वरसोत्तमः
सर्व्वरसोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The saline flavour, saltness, salt.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, रस a flavour, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरात्र|सर्वरात्र|सर्व्वरात्रः
सर्व्वरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The whole night.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and रात्रि, अच् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरीकर
सर्व्वरीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वरी for शर्व्वरी night, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त|सर्वर्तुपरिवर्त|सर्वर्तुपरिवर्तः|सर्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त|सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्तः
सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, ऋतु a season, and परिवर्त्त a revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वला|सर्वला
सर्व्वला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An iron crow.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, ला to take, aff. अङ् and टाप्; also read शर्व्वला and सर्व्वली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलिङ्गिन्|सर्वलिङ्गिन्|सर्वलिंगिन्
सर्व्वलिङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A heretic, an impostor; one who not belonging to the orthodox faith, wears the dress, and assumes the character of an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, लिङ्ग mark, (of sect or caste,) इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलोक|सर्वलोक|सर्वलोकः
सर्व्वलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The universe.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलोह|सर्वलोह|सर्वलोहः|सर्व्वलोहः
सर्व्वलोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववर्त्तिका|सर्ववर्तिका
सर्व्ववर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववल्लभा|सर्ववल्लभा
सर्व्ववल्लभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and वल्लभा a mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वविद्|सर्वविद्
सर्व्वविद्<BR>mfn. (-वित्)<BR>Omniscient, all-wise.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेद|सर्ववेद|सर्ववेदः|सर्व्ववेदः
सर्व्ववेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A Brahman who has read the four Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, वेद the Veda, and अण् or ठक् aff.; the effects of the aff. being subsequently rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेदस्|सर्ववेदस्
सर्व्ववेदस्<BR>m. (-दाः)<BR>A man who gives away all his property to the priests who have been employed by him at particular sacrifices, of which such a destination of the principal's whole wealth is an essential part.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, विद to gain, causal form, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेदिन्|सर्ववेदिन्
सर्व्ववेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Omniscient.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेशिन्|सर्ववेशिन्
सर्व्ववेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>An actor, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, वेश dress or decoration, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशस्|सर्वशस्
सर्व्वशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Wholly, universally.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशान्तिकृत्|सर्वशान्तिकृत्
सर्व्वशान्तिकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The sovereign of India, BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, शान्ति tranquillity, and कृत् who effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशेष|सर्वशेष
सर्व्वशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 What remains of the whole.<BR>2 What is to continue or to be added to all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसङ्गत|सर्वसङ्गत|सर्वसंगतः|सर्व्वसङ्गतः
सर्व्वसङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>United or meeting with universally.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sort of rice of quick growth.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (by all,) सङ्गत known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसङ्ग्रह|सर्वसङ्ग्रह|सर्वसंग्रहः|सर्व्वसंग्रह
सर्व्वसङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A general or universal collection.<BR>2 Any collection.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and सङ्ग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसन्नहन|सर्वसन्नहन
सर्व्वसन्नहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Assembling, a complete army.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (the parts, or elephants, chariots, horse, and foot,) and सन्नहन arming, accoutring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसन्नाह|सर्वसन्नाह|सर्वसंनाहः|सर्व्वसन्नाहः
सर्व्वसन्नाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The universal and pervading spirit.<BR>2 Arming or assembling a complete army.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and सन्नाह arming, accoutring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसमता|सर्वसमता
सर्व्वसमता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sameness or identity with all things.<BR>2 Equanimity, equal regard for all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and समता sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसह|सर्वसह|सर्वसहः|सर्व्वसहः
सर्व्वसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>All-enduring, bearing all things with patience and firmness.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Bdellium.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, सह to suffer, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसिद्धार्थ|सर्वसिद्धार्थ
सर्व्वसिद्धार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Having every object attained, every wish gratified, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and सिद्ध accomplished, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसिद्धि|सर्वसिद्धि|सर्वसिद्धिः|सर्व्वसिद्धिः
सर्व्वसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Universal success or accomplishment of all.<BR>m. (-द्धिः)<BR>A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्व|सर्वस्व|सर्व्वस्वं
सर्व्वस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>1 Whole property or possessions.<BR>2 Substance, whole essence of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वदण्ड|सर्वस्वदण्ड
सर्व्वस्वदण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Fined in all one's property.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Confiscation of property.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वस्व, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वहरण|सर्वस्वहरण
सर्व्वस्वहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Confiscation of a whole property.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वस्व, and हरण taking; also सर्व्वस्वहार, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वामिन्|सर्वस्वामिन्
सर्व्वस्वामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 A universal monarch.<BR>2 The owner or master of all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and स्वामिन् a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वहार|सर्वहार|सर्वहारः
सर्व्वहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Total confiscation.<BR>2 Seizing the whole.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and हार taking; also सर्व्वहरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाङ्ग|सर्वाङ्ग|सर्वाङ्गः|सर्व्वाङ्गं
सर्व्वाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 The whole body.<BR>2 The Aṅgas or portions of divine knowledge collectively.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अङ्ग a limb, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाङ्गीण|सर्वाङ्गीण|सर्वांगीण|सर्व्वाङ्गीणः
सर्व्वाङ्गीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Spreading throughout the body, diffusive, pervading.<BR>2 Relating or belonging to the Aṅgas, or parts of science collectively.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अङ्ग member, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=910" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाणी|सर्वाणी
सर्व्वाणी<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सव्व ŚIVA, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मक|सर्वात्मक
सर्व्वात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>All-pervading.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and आत्मन् self, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मन्|सर्वात्मन्
सर्व्वात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 The supreme or universal spirit.<BR>2 All beings collectively.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and आत्मन् self or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मभूति|सर्वात्मभूति
सर्व्वात्मभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>All beings collectively.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वात्म, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाधिकार|सर्वाधिकार
सर्व्वाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>General control or superintendence.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाधिकारिन्|सर्वाधिकारिन्
सर्व्वाधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A general or head superintendant.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वाधिकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वानुभूति|सर्वानुभूति|सर्व्वानुभूतिः
सर्व्वानुभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A Jina of the last era.<BR>2 One of the future era.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अनुभूति perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नभक्षक|सर्वान्नभक्षक|सर्व्वान्नभक्षकः
सर्व्वान्नभक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Eating every thing or every where.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अन्न food, and भक्षक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नभोजिन्|सर्वान्नभोजिन्
सर्व्वान्नभोजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Eating all sorts of food.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अन्न food, भुज to eat, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नीन|सर्वान्नीन|सर्व्वान्नीनः
सर्व्वान्नीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Eating all sorts of food.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अन्न food, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसन्धक|सर्वाभिसन्धक
सर्व्वाभिसन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A railer, a cynic, one who abuses all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and अभिसन्धक who calumniates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसन्धिन्|सर्वाभिसन्धिन्
सर्व्वाभिसन्धिन्<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>A cynic, a calumniator or reviler.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अभि and सम् before धा to have, क affix, and इनि possess. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसार|सर्वाभिसार|सर्वाभिसारः|सर्व्वाभिसारः
सर्व्वाभिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Assembling a complete army.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and अभि before सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वार्थ|सर्वार्थ
सर्व्वार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Having every object or sense.<BR>n. adv. (-र्थम्)<BR>For or on account of all.<BR>m. plu. (-र्थाः)<BR>All objects, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वार्थसिद्ध|सर्वार्थसिद्ध|सर्वार्थसिद्धः|सर्व्वार्थसिद्धः
सर्व्वार्थसिद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha faith.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अर्थ object, and सिद्ध perfect: his father's wishes being all fulfilled by his birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वावसर|सर्वावसर|सर्वावसरः|सर्व्वावसरः
सर्व्वावसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, (things,) अवसर interval or cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाशिन्|सर्वाशिन्
सर्व्वाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Eating all things.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाश्रय|सर्वाश्रय|सर्वाश्रयः
सर्व्वाश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Giving shelter or protection to all.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाश्रमिन्|सर्वाश्रमिन्
सर्व्वाश्रमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Belonging or common to every order.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and आश्रमिन् belonging to an Āśrama or order of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वास्त्रा|सर्वास्त्रा
सर्व्वास्त्रा<BR>f. (-स्त्रा)<BR>One of the sixteen Vidyā Devis, or goddesses of learning, according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाह्ण|सर्वाह्ण|सर्व्वाह्णः
सर्व्वाह्ण<BR>m. (-ह्णः)<BR>The whole day.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वीय|सर्वीय|सर्व्वीयः
सर्व्वीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to all, suitable or fit for all, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वेश|सर्वेश|सर्वेशः
सर्व्वेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Supreme or universal monarch.<BR>2 The Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वेश्वर|सर्वेश्वर|सर्वेश्वरः|सर्व्वेश्वरः
सर्व्वेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A universal monarch.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौघ|सर्वौघ|सर्वौघः|सर्व्वौघः
सर्व्वौघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 Assembling a complete army.<BR>2 Great speed or dispatch.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, and च्योघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौषधिगण|सर्वौषधिगण|सर्व्वौषधिगणः
सर्व्वौषधिगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A class of certain principal drugs, consisting of Murā, Valerian Jaṭāmāṃsī, Orris root, Benzoin, Zedoary, Kurh, or Costus speciosus, red saunders, and Cyperus.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, औषधि a drug, and गण a class; also with वर्ग the same, सर्व्वौषधिवर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौषधिरस|सर्वौषधिरस
सर्व्वौषधिरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The juice or infusion of a number of plants as used at a royal inauguration.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, औषधि herb, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षप|सर्षपः
सर्षप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A sort of mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR>2 A kind of poison.<BR>3 A small measure of weight, a mustard seed so considered.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A small bird.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अप Uṇādi aff., and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षपतैल|सर्षपतैलं
सर्षपतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Mustard oil.<BR>E.<BR>सर्षप mustard, and तैलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल|सलं
सल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>षल to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
सलज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>स with, लज्जा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिल|सलिलं
सलिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>षल to go, इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलकुन्तल|सलिलकुन्तलः
सलिलकुन्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>सलिल water, and कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलक्रिया
सलिलक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The funeral rite of washing the corpse.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलज|सलिलजं
सलिलज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलनिधि|सलिलनिधिः
सलिलनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल, and निधि store.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलरय|सलिलरयः
सलिलरय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Current, stream.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल, and रय speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलराशि|सलिलराशिः
सलिलराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>Any piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल, and राशि heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलेन्धन|सलिलेंधन|सलिलेन्धनः
सलिलेन्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>सलिल water, and इन्धन inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
सलील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Wanton, sportive.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, लीला sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लकी
सल्लकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>सल to go, वुन् aff., and the ल doubled; also शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव|सवं|सवः
सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 Offspring, progeny.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 The juice or honey of flowers.<BR>3 Sprinkling the juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, &c., aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवन|सवनं
सवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bathing, as a religious exercise, or preparatory to a sacrifice, purificatory ablution in general.<BR>2 A sacrifice in general.<BR>3 Extracting and drinking the juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR>4 Bearing as children, bringing forth young.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear young, &c., Uṇādi aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवपुष
सवपुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Embodied, having a body or form.<BR>E.<BR>स with, वपुस body, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
सवयस्<BR>mfn. (-याः-याः-यः)<BR>Contemporary, of similar age or duration.<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>A friend, a contemporary.<BR>f. (-याः)<BR>A woman's female friend.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान equal, like, and वयस् age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर|सवरः
सवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA. More properly. शवर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
सवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Like, resembling.<BR>2 Of the same tribe or class.<BR>3 Of the same kind, homogeneous.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A name of CHĀYĀ, one of the wives of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान like, same, वर्ण tribe, colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवहा
सवहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus Turpethum); also read सुवहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=911" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवास
सवास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Scented, perfumed.<BR>2 Having a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>स with, वास abode, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवासस्
सवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Clothed, dressed.<BR>E.<BR>स with, वासम् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्पक
सविकल्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Admitting of an alternative or choice.<BR>2 Doubtful.<BR>E.<BR>स with विकल्प option, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकाश|सविकाशः
सविकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Expanded, extended, extensive.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, विकाश expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविग्रह
सविग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Embodied, having body or form.<BR>2 Meaning, importing.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विग्रह body, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>षू to send or cast, (his rays,) तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृदैवत|सवितृदैवतः
सवितृदैवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The constellation Hastā, the thirteenth of the lunar asterisms.<BR>E.<BR>सवितृ the sun, and दैवत godhead; the sun being the ruling deity of this asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृल|सवितृलः
सवितृल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सवितृ the sun, and ल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्र|सवित्रं
सवित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Cause or instrument of production or generation.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, aff. इत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रिय|सवित्रियः
सवित्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सवितृ the sun, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्री
सवित्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A cow.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth young, तृच् aff., ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविद्य
सविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Learned, wise, versed in science.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविध|सविधः
सविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Of the same kind.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान common, same, विघ manner, sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
सविनय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Modest, well-behaved.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Modestly, respectfully.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विनय propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
सविलास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Wanton, sportive.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विलास sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
सविशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Excellent, superior.<BR>2 Having characteristic qualities.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विशेष excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषण
सविशेषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Distinguished, marked, characterised, individualised by marks or properties.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विशेषण distinguishing property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषतस्
सविशेषतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Particularly, excellently.<BR>E.<BR>स with, विशेषतस् especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मय|सविस्मयः
सविस्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, विस्मय astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृद्धिक
सवृद्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Bearing interest.<BR>E.<BR>स with वृद्धि interest, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेश|सवेशः
सवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं).<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Ornamented, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान common, or सह with, and वेश entrance, decoration, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेष
सवेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Decorated, dressed.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, &c., and वेष entrance or decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Left, left hand.<BR>2 South, southern.<BR>3 Reverse, contrary, backward.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>ष to send, य Uṇādi aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यथ
सव्यथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Suffering pain.<BR>E.<BR>स with, व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचार|सव्यभिचारः
सव्यभिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A reason or argument that is locally incompatible with the conclusion to be drawn from it.<BR>E.<BR>स with, व्यभिचार irrelevancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यसाचिन्
सव्यसाचिन्<BR>m. (-ची)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>सव्य left, षच to be joined or attached, aff. णिनि; drawing the bow with his left hand, as well as his right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याज
सव्याज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Cunning, plausible, pretending.<BR>2 Fraudulent.<BR>E.<BR>स with, व्याज pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठ|सव्येष्ठः
सव्येष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>सव्ये on the left, and स्थ who stands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठृ
सव्येष्ठृ<BR>m. (-ष्ठा)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>सव्ये on the left, स्था to stand, ऋन् Uṇādi aff. with the effect of ड, स, and थ changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रीड
सव्रीड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>स with, व्रीडा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशङ्क
सशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearful, doubtful.<BR>E.<BR>स with, शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्क|सशल्कः
सशल्क<BR>mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्का-ल्कं)<BR>Scaly, (as a fish, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>स, and शल्क scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्य
सशल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Troublesome, difficult.<BR>2 Pierced by a thorn or dart.<BR>E.<BR>स with, शल्य a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशूक|सशूकः
सशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A believer, one who believes the existence of GOD, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशोक
सशोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sorrowful, sad.<BR>n. adv. (-कं)<BR>Sorrowfully.<BR>E.<BR>स with, शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्मश्रु|सश्मश्रुः
सश्मश्रु<BR>f. (-श्रुः)<BR>A woman with a beard.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, श्मश्रु a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रम
सश्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Wearied, fatigued.<BR>E.<BR>स with, श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस
सस<BR>r. 2nd cl. (सलि)<BR>To sleep; also षस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंशय
ससंशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Doubtful, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>स with, संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्वा
ससत्वा<BR>f. (-त्वा)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, सत्व a living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससन|ससनं
ससन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Immolation, offering a living victim.<BR>E.<BR>सस to sleep, &c., aff. ल्युट्; also शसन and शमन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससम्पद
ससम्पद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>स with, सम्पद pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
ससाध्वस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Frightened, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>स with, साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससौष्ठव
ससौष्ठव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Quick, fleet.<BR>2 Excellent.<BR>E.<BR>स with, सौष्ठव speed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्तर
सस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bed of leaves, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान common, and लर spreading, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृह
सस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Desirous, wishing for.<BR>E.<BR>स with, स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
सस्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smiling, laughing.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, स्मित a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्य|सस्यं
सस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 Fruit.<BR>2 Corn, grain.<BR>3 A weapon.<BR>4 A quality, an excellence.<BR>E.<BR>सस to sleep, य Uṇādi aff.; also शस्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
सस्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of precious stone, described as of the colour of the inner fruit of the cocoanut, (Opal?)<BR>2 A sword.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यसंवर|सस्यसंवरः
सस्यसंवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>सस्य fruit, and संवर a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्याद्
सस्याद्<BR>mfn. (-द्)<BR>Fructivorous, granivorous, eating grain or fruit.<BR>E.<BR>सस्य, अद to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्येष्टि|सस्येष्टिः
सस्येष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Sacrifice offered on the ripening of new grain.<BR>E.<BR>सस्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
सस्वेद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Perspiring, exuding.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A virgin deflowered, a girl who has committed a breach of chastity.<BR>E.<BR>स with, स्वेद perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=912" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्त्रि
सस्त्रि<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रिः-स्त्रिः-स्त्रि)<BR>Who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, इ aff., redup. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Patient, enduring, suffering, bearing.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The month Agrahāyaṇa.<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>Strength, power.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The Aloe plant.<BR>3 A sort of bean, commonly Mudgaparṇī.<BR>4 A drug, commonly Nakhi.<BR>5 A plant; also Daṇḍotpalā.<BR>6 Barleria, (the white sort.)<BR>7 The ichneumon plant or Rasan.<BR>8 A medicinal sort of moon plant.<BR>ind.<BR>1 With, together with; a particle implying association, connexion;<BR>2 Union, junction;<BR>3 Increase, addition;<BR>4 Presence, present time;<BR>5 Completeness, entireness;<BR>6 Resemblance, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षह to have patience, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकार|सहकारः
सहकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fragrant sort of mango.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिता
सहकारिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Co-operation, assistance.<BR>E.<BR>सहकारिन्, and तल् aff.; also सहकारित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिन्
सहकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>An implement, an assistant or associate, that or who, by which or whom, any object is effected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, कृ to make, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्
सहकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Assisting, an assister.<BR>E.<BR>सह, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्वन्
सहकृत्वन्<BR>mfn. (-त्वा-त्वा-त्व)<BR>Co-operating, assisting.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, कृ to do, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगत
सहगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Accompanied, associated.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगमन
सहगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going with, accompanying.<BR>2 A woman's burning herself on the funeral pile with her deceased husband.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगामिन्
सहगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going with, accompanying.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman who burns herself with her husband's body.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचर|सहचरः
सहचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Accompanying, going or associating with, &c.<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>Yellow Barleria.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A companion, a follower.<BR>2 A surety.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A wife.<BR>2 A woman's female friend or confidence.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, चर to go, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरत्
सहचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Accompanying, attending.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरित
सहचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Who or what accompanies, attends, associates with, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, चर to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचारिन्
सहचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>A companion, an attendant.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहज|सहजः
सहज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Co-existent, cognate, born or produced together.<BR>2 Innate, inherent, natural.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A brother of whole blood.<BR>2 The natural state or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजमित्र|सहजमित्रं
सहजमित्र<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A friend by birth; as a sister's son, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सहज cognate, मिच friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजारि|सहजारिः
सहजारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A natural enemy, one hostile by birth; as the son of the same father by another mother, the son of a paternal uncle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सहज cognate, अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजेतर
सहजेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Incidental, accidental, not inherent or innate, (in the dual it may imply both innate and adventitious.)<BR>E.<BR>सहज, and इतर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजोदासीन|सहजोदासीनः
सहजोदासीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A person, unconnected by birth, born neither an enemy nor friend.<BR>E.<BR>सहज cognate, उदासीन a stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहत्व|सहत्वं
सहत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं).<BR>1 Sufferance, endurance.<BR>2 Association, union.<BR>E.<BR>सह patient, or with, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, सहता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदेव|सहदेवः
सहदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The youngest of the five Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A plant, a sort of Sida.<BR>2 A twining shrub, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>3 Another plant, also Daṇḍotpala.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A sort of Sida.<BR>2 A shrub, bearing a fragrant seed, Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>सह with देव who or what sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्म्म|सहधर्म|सहधर्मः
सहधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Community of duty, law, property, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्म्मिन्|सहधर्मिन्
सहधर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>1 Following the same law, acknowledging the same obligations.<BR>2 Possessing same or like properties.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A woman married according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, धर्म्म the law, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bearing, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहनर्त्तन|सहनर्तन|सहनर्त्तनं
सहनर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dancing together in a circle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सह together, and नर्त्तन dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपांशुकिल|सहपांशुकिलः
सहपांशुकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A contemporary and friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपान|सहपानं
सहपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Drinking together.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभाविन्
सहभाविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A friend, a companion, an adherent or partisan.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, भाव quality, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभोजन|सहभोजनं
सहभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating in company.<BR>E.<BR>सह together, भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमरण|सहमरणं
सहमरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Concremation, a widow's burning herself with the corpse of her husband.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहयुध्वन्
सहयुध्वन्<BR>mfn. (-ध्वा-ध्वा-ध्व)<BR>Fighting with or along with.<BR>m. (-ध्वा)<BR>A brother in arms.<BR>E.<BR>सह, युध to fight, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहयुध्वान
सहयुध्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fighting with.<BR>E.<BR>सह, युध्वान fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरसा
सहरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A sort of bean; see मुद्गपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरि|सहरिः
सहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>ind.<BR>Resembling HARI or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, or समान same, हरि the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्ष|सहर्षः
सहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Envy, emulation.<BR>2 Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>स with, हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस्<BR>m. (-हां)<BR>1 The month Agrahāyaṇa, (Nov.-Dec.)<BR>2 The winter season.<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>1 Strength, power.<BR>2 Light.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसा
सहसा<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly, precipitately, inconsiderately, without consideration or pause.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, असा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसादृष्ट|सहसादृष्टः
सहसादृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Seen quickly.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>An adopted son.<BR>E.<BR>सहसा quickly, दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसान|सहसानः
सहसान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, असानच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्य|सहस्यः
सहस्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>The month Pauṣa, (Dec.-Jan.)<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्र|सहस्रं
सहस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकिरण|सहस्रकिरणः
सहस्रकिरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and किरण a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकृत्व
सहस्रकृत्व<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly, reiteratedly, a thousand or many times.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and कृत्वसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रद|सहस्रदः
सहस्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Liberal, giving by thousands.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=913" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदंष्ट्र|सहस्रदंष्ट्रः
सहस्रदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus pelorius, BUC.)<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and दंष्ट्र tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदंष्ट्रिन्
सहस्रदंष्ट्रिन्<BR>m. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>A sheat fish: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, दंष्ट्र a tooth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदृश्
सहस्रदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदोस्
सहस्रदोस्<BR>m. (-दोः)<BR>KĀRTAVĪRYA, a prince so named.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and दोस् the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधा
सहस्रधा<BR>ind.<BR>In a thousand ways.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधार|सहस्रधारः
सहस्रधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and धार an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रनयन|सहस्रनयनः
सहस्रनयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रनेत्र|सहस्रनेत्रः
सहस्रनेत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and नेत्र the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपति
सहस्रपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The governor of a district, or of a thousand villages.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपत्र|सहस्रपत्रं
सहस्रपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपाद्
सहस्रपाद्<BR>m. (-त् or -द्)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and पाद् for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपाद|सहस्रपादः
सहस्रपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A sort of duck.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रयुग
सहस्रयुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A period of a thousand ages.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररश्मि|सहस्ररश्मिः
सहस्ररश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररोमन्
सहस्ररोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>A blanket.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवदन|सहस्रवदनः
सहस्रवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, a thousand, and वदन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवीर्य्या|सहस्रवीर्या
सहस्रवीर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A bent grass, (Panicum dactylon, the Agrostis linearis of LINNÆIS.)<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, वीर्य्य splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवेधिन्
सहस्रवेधिन्<BR>n. (-धि)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A sort of cane, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousands, and वेधिन् what pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशस्
सहस्रशस्<BR>ind.<BR>By a thousand or thousands, thousand-fold.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशिखर|सहस्रशिखरः
सहस्रशिखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Vindhya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and शिखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रहर्य्याश्व|सहस्रहर्याश्व|सहस्रहर्य्याश्वः
सहस्रहर्य्याश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The car of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, हरि green, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रांशु|सहस्रांशुः
सहस्रांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्राक्ष|सहस्राक्षः
सहस्राक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Thousand-eyed; used figuratively, vigilant, all-perceiving, all-inspecting, all-powerful.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and अक्ष the eye: INDRA having been covered over with marks resembling the female organ, in consequence of a curse of GAUTAMA, those marks were changed subsequently to eyes by the relenting saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्राधिपति|सहस्राधिपतिः
सहस्राधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The governor of a district or chief over a thousand villages.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रार|सहस्रारः
सहस्रार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The top of the head, the seat of the soul.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and अर a spoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रावर|सहस्रावरः
सहस्रावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fine of from five hundred to a thousand Paṇas.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र, and अवर below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रिन्
सहस्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-स्री-स्रिणी-स्रि)<BR>Having a thousand.<BR>m. (-स्री)<BR>1 A body of a thousand men, &c.<BR>2 Commander or prefect of a thousand.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाचर|सहाचरः
सहाचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A yellow sort of Barleria, (B. prionitis.)<BR>E.<BR>सह with आङ् before चर to go, aff. टच्; also सहचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाय|सहायः
सहाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A companion, a follower, an adherent.<BR>2 A patron, a helper.<BR>3 A sort of drug and perfume, commonly Gahantāpārali.<BR>4 The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, इण् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायता
सहायता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A multitude of companions, a company of associates or followers.<BR>2 Association, assistance, friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सहाय a companion, तल् aff. of number, or the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायत्व|सहायत्वं
सहायत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Fellowship, companionship, friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सहाय a companion, त्व aff. of the quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायवत्|सहायवन्त्
सहायवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Befriended, assisted, accompanied.<BR>E.<BR>सहाय, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार|सहारः
सहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The mango.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, आरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहारोग्य|सहारोग्यः
सहारोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Well, convalescent.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, आरोग्य health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्थ|सहार्थः
सहार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Having one object.<BR>2 Synonymous, having the same meaning.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, अर्थ object, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्द्द|सहार्द|सहार्द्दः
सहार्द्द<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दः-र्द्दा-र्द्दं)<BR>Tender, affectionate.<BR>E.<BR>स with, हार्द्द affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहासन
सहासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sitting on the same seat.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
सहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Accompanied by, in company with, associated with, &c.<BR>2 Borne, endured.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, इतच् aff.; or षह to bear, क्त aff., with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितृ
सहितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Bearing, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित्र|सहित्रं
सहित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Patience, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>षह to suffer, and इत्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Patient, enduring, resigned.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुता
सहिष्णुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Patience, resignation.<BR>E.<BR>तल affix of the abstract, added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरि|सहुरिः
सहुरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, उरिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदय|सहृदयः
सहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Good-hearted.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a learned man.<BR>E.<BR>स with, हृदय a heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेल
सहेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Sportive, playing.<BR>E.<BR>स with हेल sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोक्ति|सहोक्तिः
सहोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A figure of rhetoric; either the employment of a word in a double meaning, or connecting different circumstances in one sentence by the use of the term सह with, along with.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोटज|सहोटजः
सहोटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A hut of leaves, &c. inhabited by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढ|सहोढः
सहोढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>The son of a woman pregnant at the time of her marriage.<BR>1 A thief caught with stolen property upon him.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, ऊढा a bride; or स with, होढ stolen goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढज|सहोढजः
सहोढज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of a woman pregnant at the time of marriage.<BR>E.<BR>स with, ऊढा a bride, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदर|सहोदरः
सहोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A brother of whole blood, one by the same father and mother.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदित
सहोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said or declared, comprehensively or collectively.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A saint, a pure or pious man.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, ओरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोवल
सहोवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Violence, aggression.<BR>E.<BR>सहस् and वल, both meaning power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोषित
सहोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dwelling or abiding with, being together with.<BR>E.<BR>सह, and उषित abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=914" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be borne or suffered.<BR>2 Equal or adequate to.<BR>3 Sweet, agreeable.<BR>4 Powerful, strong.<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>Health, convalescence.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>One of the principal ranges of the mountains of India; the mountainous country on the north-west side of the Peninsula or towards Poonah, &c., and in which the Godāvarī river takes its rise.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा<BR>f. (सा)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 The goddess GAURĪ.<BR>3 She, (the third personal feminine pronoun or the feminine inflection of तद् that, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयाचिक
सांयाचिक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A voyaging merchant, one who trades by sea, &c.<BR>E.<BR>संयात्रा travelling together, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An able leader, a soldier skilled in war.<BR>E.<BR>संयुग war, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविण|सांराविणं
सांराविण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Shout, acclamation, the calling out of a number of people together.<BR>2 Crying or complaining aloud.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, राविन् who calls or cries, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Annual, perennial.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>संवत्सर a year, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिक|सांवत्सरिकः
सांवत्सरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Yearly, annual, relating to a year, produced in a year, &c.<BR>E.<BR>संवत्सर a year, and ठञ् aff.; also with वुञ्, aff. सांवत्सरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A logician.<BR>E.<BR>संवाद dispute, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Dubious, doubtful.<BR>2 Uncertain, irresolute, in doubt.<BR>E.<BR>संशय doubt, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Worldly, of or belonging to the world.<BR>E.<BR>संसार, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Spontaneous, effected naturally.<BR>E.<BR>संसिद्धि perfection, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिक|सांस्थानिकः
सांस्थानिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A countryman, an inhabitant or native of the same place.<BR>E.<BR>सम् together, स्थान place, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम्<BR>ind.<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, अक to go, अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्य|साकल्यं
साकल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>The whole, the entire, all.<BR>E.<BR>सकल all, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकाङ्क्ष|साकांक्ष
साकाङ्क्ष<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षः-ङ्क्षा-ङ्क्ष)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आकाङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकार|साकारः
साकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Having form or shape.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
साकूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Significant.<BR>2 Wanton.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आकूत meaning, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूतस्मित
साकूतस्मित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A wanton glance.<BR>E.<BR>साकूत, and स्मित a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेत|साकेतं
साकेत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The city Ayodhya, or ancient Oude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुक|साक्तुकं|साक्तुकः
साक्तुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barley.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A quantity of fried grain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सक्तु fried or parched grain ground, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Before, in presence, in sight.<BR>2 As, like.<BR>3 Evidently, manifestly.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, अक्ष the eye, अत to go or to be, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिता
साक्षिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Evidence, testimony.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, साक्षित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>1 Witnessing, seeing, an eye-witness.<BR>2 Attesting, testifying, evidence.<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A witness, (in law.)<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, (in presence of,) अक्षि the eye, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिपरीक्षा
साक्षिपरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Examination of a witness's credibility.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and परीक्षा trial; also साक्षिपरीक्षणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिभावित
साक्षिभावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made known by testimony.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and भावित caused to be perceived or known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिमत्|साक्षिमन्त्
साक्षिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Having or requiring evidence.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and कतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिलक्षण
साक्षिलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Defined or proved by testimony.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्य|साक्ष्यं
साक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Testimony, evidence.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्यभाव
साक्ष्यभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Absence or deficiency of witnesses or testimony.<BR>E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखेय|साखेयः
साखेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Friendly, amicable.<BR>E.<BR>सखि a friend, ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साख्य|साख्यं
साख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सखि a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागर|सागरः
सागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A sort of deer.<BR>E.<BR>सगर a king, and अण् aff.; to bathe the bones of SAGARA'S 60,000 sons the Ganges is said to have been led by BHAGĪRATHA, his great-great-grandson, to the ocean, at the place now called Gaṅgā-Sāgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरगामिनी
सागरगामिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the ocean, and गामिनी going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरनेमि|सागरनेमिः
सागरनेमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the sea, and नेमि a circumference; surrounding the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरमेखला
सागरमेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the ocean, and मेखला a zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागराम्बरा|सागरांबरा
सागराम्बरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the ocean, अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरालय|सागरालयः
सागरालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>VARUṆA, deity of the water.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the ocean, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरोत्थ|सागरोत्थं
सागरोत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>E.<BR>सागर the sea, and उत्थ produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निक|साग्निकः
साग्निक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A householder, who maintains a sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अग्नि fire, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कर्य्य|साङ्कर्य|सांकर्य|सांकर्यं
साङ्कर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Mixture, blending.<BR>2 The concurrence of various properties in one subject.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कर mixing, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कल|सांकल|साङ्कलं
साङ्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Effected or produced by addition, collection, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्कल collection, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कुर|सांकुर
साङ्कुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Budding, in bud.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अङ्कुर a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्क्षेपिक|सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
साङ्क्षेपिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Short, summary, concise, contracted, abridged.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्क्षेप abridgement, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
साङ्ख्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्यी-ङ्ख्यं)<BR>1 Numeral, relating to number.<BR>2 Rational, discriminative.<BR>m. (-ङ्ख्यः)<BR>The Sāṃkhya system of philosophy, ascribed originally to the Muni KAPILA.<BR>E.<BR>संख्या number, &c., and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग|सांग
साङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Having all the members.<BR>2 Comprising all the subdivisions.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गतिक|सांगतिक|सांगतिकः
साङ्गतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Social, associating, relating to or derived from encounter or society.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A visitor.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्गति acquaintance, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गम|सांगम|सांगमः|साङ्गमः
साङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Union, meeting.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्गम the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
साङ्ग्रामिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Warlike, martial, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A commander, a general.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग्राम war, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि<BR>ind.<BR>Crookedly, awry, bent.<BR>E.<BR>षच to collect, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिविलोकित
साचिविलोकित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A side glance.<BR>E.<BR>साचि, and विलीकित looked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=915" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्य|साचिव्यं
साचिव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Ministry, administration.<BR>2 Friendship, fellowship.<BR>E.<BR>सचिव a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिस्थित
साचिस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Crooked.<BR>2 Standing or placed unevenly.<BR>E.<BR>साचि, and स्थित stood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचीकृत|साचीकृतं
साचीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made crooked.<BR>2 Seen crookedly or tortuously, distorted, misrepresented.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Prejudice, distortion or perversion of mind.<BR>E.<BR>साचि crookedly, च्चि aff., कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्जन|सांजनः|साञ्जनः
साञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अञ्जन unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
साटोप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Proud, haughty, consequential.<BR>n. adv. (-पं)<BR>Arrogantly, consequentially.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आटोप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात्<BR>n. (सात्)<BR>BRAHMA, GOD.<BR>E.<BR>साति to cause happiness, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
सात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Given.<BR>2 Destroyed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>सत to give, or षो to destroy, aff. क्त, form irr.: see सित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातय|सातयः
सातय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who or what causes pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>साति a Sautra root in the causal form, to cause pleasure, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातला
सातला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A shrub, commonly Carmaghās.<BR>E.<BR>सात pleasure, and ला to give, affs. अङ् and टाप्; also शातला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातवाहन|सातवाहनः
सातवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sovereign SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>E.<BR>सात a Gandharba, changed according to the leg end to a lion, on which this prince was discovered riding when a child, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
साति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 End, conclusion, cessation of action.<BR>2 Destruction.<BR>3 Gift, giving.<BR>4 Sharp pain.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, or षण् to give, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.; also read सति and सन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिसार|सातिसारः
सातिसार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dysenteric, afflicted with dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, अतिसार dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिलक
सातिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Peas; also सतीलक, सतीनक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकि|सात्यकिः
सात्यकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>The charioteer of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवत|सात्यवतः
सात्यवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The poet and sage VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>सत्यवती the mother of the bard, and अण् aff.; also with ढक्, aff. सात्यवतेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत्|सात्वन्त्
सात्वत्<BR>m. (-त्वान्)<BR>1 A worshipper, a follower.<BR>2 A man of the Yādava tribe.<BR>E.<BR>साति to cause happiness, वतु participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत|सात्वतः
सात्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 BALADEVA.<BR>m. plu. (-ताः)<BR>The people of one of the countries of midland India, apparently inhabiting a district in the vicinity of the Pārijātra mountains, said to be descendants from outcaste Vaiśyas.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 One of the four great divisions of the drama, described as the representation of gentle and amiable sentiments or passions.<BR>2 The mother of ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR>E.<BR>सत्वत a proper name, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्विक
सात्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Spontaneous, sincere, (as applied to the actions or signs of the Sātvika Bhāva.)<BR>2 Relating to or proceeding from the Sattva quality, honest, true, good, gentle, amiable, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 One of the Bhāvas or classes into which the affections of the mind or their expression, are distinguished, in poetry and the drama: this class holds a middle place between the Sthāyi, and Vyabhicāri Bhāvas, and implies the honest and spontaneous indication of strong feeling, as evinced especially in eight acts, viz. inability to move whilst the faculties or limbs are unaffected, perspiration, horripilation, inarticulate speech, trembling or tremor, change of colour, tears, and mental absorption or indifference, approaching to loss of sense, to every object but one which engrosses the attention.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सत्व the Sattva Guṇa or quality, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Purity, cleanness.<BR>2 Lassitude, weariness, exhaustion.<BR>3 Perishing, decay.<BR>E.<BR>षट् to decay, to be weary, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन|सादनं
सादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 Dispelling.<BR>3 Destroying.<BR>4 Wearying, exhausting.<BR>5 Exhaustion, decay.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयत्
सादयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Destroying.<BR>2 Exhausting.<BR>3 Expelling, removing, extracting.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयितव्य
सादयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादर
सादर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Respectful.<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Respectfully.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादि|सादिः
सादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>1 A charioteer.<BR>2 A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>षद to be weary, &c., इञ् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादित|सादितः
सादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Destroyed, exterminated.<BR>2 Wearied, exhausted, harassed.<BR>3 Wasted, decayed.<BR>4 Broken, cut.<BR>5 Drawn, dragged.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A horseman, a cavalier.<BR>2 One who rides on an elephant.<BR>3 One who rides on or is mounted in a car.<BR>E.<BR>षद to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्य|सादृश्यं
सादृश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Resemblance, similarity.<BR>E.<BR>सदृश like, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Quick, instantaneous.<BR>E.<BR>सद्यस्, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध
साध<BR>(उ) साधु r. 4th cl. (साध्यति) (औ) साधौ r. 5th cl. (साध्नोति)<BR>To finish, to perfect, to complete, or accomplish; also षाध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Completing, perfecting, finishing, who or what effects or completes.<BR>E.<BR>साघ to finish, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>2 Matter, materials, that of which any thing is composed or consists.<BR>3 Thing, substance.<BR>4 Means, expedient.<BR>5 Instrument, agent.<BR>6 Authority.<BR>7 The premises leading to a conclusion.<BR>8 Cause.<BR>9 Going, motion.<BR>10 Following.<BR>11 Killing, destroying.<BR>12 Obsequies, ceremonies observed after the death of a relative.<BR>13 Drug, medicament.<BR>14 Wealth.<BR>15 An army.<BR>16 The penis.<BR>17 Friendship.<BR>18 Enforcement of the delivery of any thing, especially juridically, as the infliction and levy of a fine, &c.<BR>19 Killing metals, depriving them (especially mercury) by oxidation, &c. of their metallic properties, for medicinal or alchemical purposes.<BR>20 Good works, or the observance of the moral and ceremonial parts of the Hindu religion, as secondary means of obtaining purity and emancipation.<BR>21 Proof, substantiation.<BR>E.<BR>षाघ to accomplish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधननिर्द्देश|साधननिर्देश|साधननिर्देशः
साधननिर्द्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Production or indicative of proof (in law).<BR>2 Establishment of premises, leading to a conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>साधन proof, &c., and निर्द्देश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीय
साधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Perfective, to be perfected, accomplished, proved.<BR>E.<BR>साध to complete, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=916" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन्त|साधंत|साधंतः|साधन्तः
साधन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A beggar, a mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>षाध to accomplish, Uṇādi aff. झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधयत्
साधयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Perfecting, accomplishing.<BR>2 Purifying.<BR>3 Proving.<BR>4 Recovering, (as a debt.)<BR>E.<BR>षाध to accomplish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्म्य
साधर्म्म्य<BR>n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>Community of duty, office, property, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सधर्म्म of one duty, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)<BR>1 Like, similar.<BR>2 Common, belonging to all or many.<BR>3 Generic.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A common rule or precept, one applicable to many persons or things.<BR>2 A specific or generic character, one common to all the individuals of a species, or all the species of a genus, &c.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small bolt or bar.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, धारण a having, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणधर्म्म|साधारणधर्म|साधारणधर्मः|साधारणधर्म्मः
साधारणधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Common or universal duty, conduct to be observed by all castes or orders, as humanity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>साधारण general, and धर्म्म merit, duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणस्त्री
साधारणस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>साधारण common, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण्य|साधारण्यं
साधारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Community, universality.<BR>E.<BR>साधारण, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Deep or sound sleep.<BR>E.<BR>साध to finish, aff. वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधित|साधितः
साधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Amerced, fined, punished by fine, (as the culprit.)<BR>2 Awarded, (as the thing or fine.)<BR>3 Awarded to or in favour of, (as the person to whom the fine is to be paid.)<BR>4 Recovered, (as a debt.)<BR>5 Accomplished, finished.<BR>6 Discharged, fulfilled.<BR>7 Conferred, bestowed, enabled to procure or effect.<BR>E.<BR>साध to accomplish, क्त aff., with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिदैव
साधिदैव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>One with supreme divinity.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अधिदैव superintending godhead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिभूत
साधिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Identified or one with elementary essence.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अधिभूत essential matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधियज्ञ
साधियज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>One with the Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अधियज्ञ the object of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Very hard.<BR>2 Very fit, proper, or right.<BR>E.<BR>साधु good, or considered as irregularly substituted for वाढ heavy, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative; also with इयसुन्, aff. साधीयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधीयस्
साधीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very right or proper.<BR>2 Very hard or firm.<BR>3 Very handsome.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु<BR>mfn. (-धुः-धुः-ध्वी-धु)<BR>1 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>2 Well-born, of honorable descent.<BR>3 Right, fit, proper.<BR>4 Good, virtuous, pious, pure.<BR>5 Pure, classical, (as applied to language.)<BR>6 Excellent, good.<BR>7 Eminent.<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>1 A Muni, a saint, a sage in general, one of subdued passions and contemplative habits.<BR>2 A Jina, a deified saint venerated by the Jainas.<BR>3 A usurer.<BR>4 A derivative or inflected noun.<BR>f. (-धुः or ध्वी)<BR>A virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>साध to accomplish or perfect, Uṇādi aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुक|साधुकः
साधुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A low or degraded tribe.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुज|साधुजः
साधुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Well-born, of respectable family or descent.<BR>E.<BR>साधु the same, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुत्व|साधुत्वं
साधुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Goodness, correctness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to साधु; also with तल्, साधुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुधी
साधुधी<BR>f. (-धीः)<BR>A wife's or husband's mother.<BR>E.<BR>साधु pious, धा to have, affs. क and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुपुष्प|साधुपुष्पं
साधुपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>साधु pure, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुम्मन्य|साधुंमन्य
साधुम्मन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Thinking one's self pure or virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>साधु, and मन to think, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाहिन्
साधुवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A well trained horse.<BR>E.<BR>साधु agreeable, pleasing, वाह bearing, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृक्ष|साधुवृक्षः
साधुवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Cadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>साधु handsome or excellent, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्त|साधुवृत्तः
साधुवृत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A virtuous or pious person.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Virtue, piety.<BR>E.<BR>साधु, and वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्ति|साधुवृत्तिः
साधुवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Virtuous.<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>The institutes or moral and ritual observances of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>साधु excellent, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशील
साधुशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Virtuous, righteous, wisely or virtuously inclined.<BR>E.<BR>साधु, and शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशीलत्व
साधुशीलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Virtuous or righteous inclination or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>साधुशील, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, साधुशीलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधूक्त
साधूक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Said or declared by the good.<BR>E.<BR>साधु, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधृत|साधृतं
साधृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A flock of peacocks.<BR>2 A stall, a shop.<BR>3 An umbrella or parasol.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, आधृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 To be perfected or accomplished.<BR>2 Accomplishable, attainable.<BR>3 To be inferred or concluded, (in logic.)<BR>4 To be proved or demonstrated.<BR>5 To be cured, curable, (in medicine.)<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>An inferior deity or demigod, one of a class of twelve.<BR>2 A deity in general.<BR>3 The twenty-second astronomical Yoga.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>1 Accomplishment, perfection.<BR>2 (In law,) The matter in debate, the thing to be proved.<BR>3 (In logic,) The subject of the proposition.<BR>E.<BR>साध to accomplish, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यमान
साध्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being subjected to, or capable, or in course of proof.<BR>2 Being in course of accomplishment.<BR>3 Being proceeded against, (at law.)<BR>E.<BR>षाध to accomplish, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यवत्|साध्यवन्त्
साध्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Comprehending that which is to be proved.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>(In law,) The party on whom rests the onus probandi.<BR>E.<BR>साध्य, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसाधन
साध्यसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Effecting what is to be or may be done, &c.<BR>E.<BR>साध्य, and साधन accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धि|साध्यसिद्धिः
साध्यसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Proof, conclusion, the establishing of that which was to be proved.<BR>2 Completion, accomplishment, fulfilment.<BR>E.<BR>साध्य to be effected, &c., and सिद्धि perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धिपाद|साध्यसिद्धिपादः
साध्यसिद्धिपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The fourth stage or division of a suit at law, judgment or decision.<BR>E.<BR>साध्य to be proved, सिद्धि conclusion, and पाद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्याभाव|साध्याभावः
साध्याभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Absence of the thing to be proved.<BR>2 Absence of the subject of a proposition.<BR>3 Impossibility of cure.<BR>E.<BR>साध्य, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वनिन्दित
साध्वनिन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unreproached, irreproachable.<BR>E.<BR>साधु the pious, and अनिन्दित not reproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वस|साध्वसं
साध्वस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>साधु a pious man, अस to throw or disperse, aff. अङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=917" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वाचार
साध्वाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>साधु, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्द|सानंद|सानन्दः
सानन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Happy, delighted, enjoying and endowed with happiness.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानल|सानलः
सानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसि|सानसिः
सानसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give, Uṇādi aff. असि, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानिका
सानिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flute, a pipe.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give (pleasure), वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु<BR>mn. (-नुः-नु)<BR>1 Table land, level ground on the top or edge of a mountain.<BR>2 A wood.<BR>3 A road.<BR>4 A gale of wind.<BR>5 Point, end, top.<BR>6 A sage, a learned man or Paṇḍita.<BR>7 A shoot, a sprout.<BR>8 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>षण to give (pleasure,) Uṇādi aff. ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकम्प|सानुकंप
सानुकम्प<BR>mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>Sympathizing, kind.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अनुकम्पा kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक्रोश
सानुक्रोश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अनुक्रोश compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनय
सानुनय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Willing, civil, kind.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Kindly, civilly.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अनुनय assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमत्|सानुमन्त्
सानुमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>सानु a summit, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुराग
सानुराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Attached, passionate, impassioned.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अनुराग affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयिका
सानेयिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flute, or pipe.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to सानेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A flute, a pipe, a fife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तपन|सांतपन|सांतपनं|सान्तपनं
सान्तपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A sort of penance; the lighter kind is feeding on a mixture of curds, &c. for one day and fasting the next; the severer is feeding six successive days, severally, on the same articles, or on cow's urine, cow's ordure, milk, curds, Ghee, and water in which Kuśa grass has been steeped, and fasting on the seventh.<BR>E.<BR>सम् completely, तपन austerity, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर|सांतर|सान्तरं
सान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>With intervals, or interstices.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तराल
सान्तराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Separated, distinct from, apart.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अन्तराल interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिक|सांतानिक|सान्तानिकः
सान्तानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Expansive, (as a shrub, &c.)<BR>2 Relating to descendants, posterity, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman intending to marry for the sake of issue.<BR>E.<BR>सन्तान, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सांत्वः|सान्त्वः
सान्त्व<BR>r. 10th cl. (सान्त्वयति)<BR>1 To appease, to conciliate.<BR>2 To comfort; also षान्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सांत्वः|सान्त्वः
सान्त्व<BR>mn. (-न्त्वः-न्त्वं)<BR>1 Conciliation, reconciling, appeasing.<BR>2 Pleasing and conciliatory language.<BR>3 Cleverness, dexterity.<BR>E.<BR>सान्त्व to console or appease, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वन|सांत्वन|सांत्वनं|सान्त्वनं
सान्त्वन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Conciliation, reconcilement.<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Friendly or affectionate salutation and enquiry.<BR>2 Speaking in a kindly and conciliatory manner.<BR>E.<BR>सान्त्व to console or appease, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वयत्
सान्त्वयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Consoling, appeasing.<BR>E.<BR>सान्त्व to console, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्ववाद|सान्त्ववादः
सान्त्ववाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Speaking in a kindly and affectionate manner.<BR>E.<BR>सान्त्व affection, and वाद speech, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सान्दृष्टिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Immediate consequence.<BR>E.<BR>सम् with, दृष्टि sight, present perception, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्र|सांद्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सान्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं)<BR>1 Thick, coarse, gross.<BR>2 Soft, bland.<BR>3 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>4 Much, abundant.<BR>5 Unctuous, oily.<BR>6 Close, compact, but having interstices.<BR>7 Stout, robust.<BR>8 Clustering, collected.<BR>n. (-न्द्र)<BR>1 A wood, a thicket.<BR>2 A heap, a cluster.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, together, अदि to bind, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रता
सान्द्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Thickness, grossness, viscidity.<BR>E.<BR>सान्द्र, and तल् added; also with त्व, सान्द्रत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रपुष्प|सान्द्रपुष्पः
सान्द्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>सान्द्र thick, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रस्निग्ध|सान्द्रस्निग्धः
सान्द्रस्निग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Thick and unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>सान्द्र thick, and स्निग्ध unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिक|सांधिक|सांधिकः|सान्धिकः
सान्धिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>सन्धा distilling, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्ध्य|सांध्य|सान्ध्यः
सान्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्यी-न्ध्यं)<BR>Produced at or relating to the evening, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सन्ध्या twilight, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सान्नहनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Calling to arms, sounding, (as an alarum, &c.)<BR>2 Bearing or putting on armour.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A squire, an armour-bearer.<BR>E.<BR>सन्नाहन arming, ठक् aff. implying relation or causation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं|सांनाय्यः
सान्नाय्य<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>An intended oblation, the thing to be offered with fire, usually clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>सम् before णी to bring, (to the sacrificial fire,) ण्यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्य|सांनिध्य|सांनिध्यं|सान्निध्यं
सान्निध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR>E.<BR>सन्निध near, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निपातिक|सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सान्निपातिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Complicated, (as disease,) relating to the morbid state of the three humors collectively.<BR>2 Miscellaneous, promiscuous, collective.<BR>E.<BR>सन्निपात collection, mixture, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
सान्वय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Related or of kin to.<BR>2 In connexion with family or descendants.<BR>3 In order or succession.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अन्वय descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिकः
सान्न्यासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A beggar, a Brahman of the fourth or mendicant order.<BR>E.<BR>सन्न्यास abandonment, (of the world,) ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यं|सापत्न्यः
सापत्न्य<BR>m. (-त्न्यः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-त्न्यं)<BR>Plurality of wives, or the condition of the wife of one who has other wives.<BR>E.<BR>सपत्नी a fellow-wife, or सपत्न an enemy, ष्यञ् pleonasm or aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्य|सापत्यः
सापत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Having progeny.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
सापराध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Faulty, offending.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अपराध fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिण्ड्य|सापिंड्य|सापिंड्यं|सापिण्ड्यं
सापिण्ड्य<BR>n. (-ण्ड्यं)<BR>Consanguinity, kindred, connexion, by presenting obsequial offerings to the same persons.<BR>E.<BR>सपिण्ड, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीन|साप्तपदीनं
साप्तपदीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, पद a step or pace, and खञ् aff.; to be formed with any with whom seven paces are walked together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Extending to seven generations, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सप्त seven, पुरुष male, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्य|साफल्यं
साफल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Productiveness, fruitfulness.<BR>E.<BR>स with, फल fruit, प्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साब्दी
साब्दी<BR>f. (-ब्दी)<BR>A sort of grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
साभ्यसूय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Envious, malicious.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अभ्यसूया malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम
साम<BR>r. 10th cl. (सामयति)<BR>1 To conciliate, to appease.<BR>2 To pacify, to tranquillize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=918" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The principal of a debt, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सम equal, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A whet-stone.<BR>E.<BR>षो to pare or whet, वुन् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग|सामगः
सामग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Brahman who chants or recites the Sāma Veda.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>The wife of a Sāma Veda Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>साम the Sāma Veda, गै to sing, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्य|सामग्र्यं
सामग्र्य<BR>nf. (-ग्र्यं-ग्री)<BR>1 Entireness, wholeness, the whole.<BR>2 Train, retinue.<BR>3 Implements, instruments, apparatus.<BR>4 Stock, effects.<BR>E.<BR>समग्र all, whole, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामज|सामजः
सामज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Producing from or produced by the Sāma Veda.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>साम the Veda, and ज born; also सामजात, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामञ्चस्य
सामञ्चस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Fitness, accordance, propriety.<BR>E.<BR>समञ्जस, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The Sāma Veda, the third of the four Vedas, the prayers of which composed in metre, are always sung or chanted: the Chāndogya Upaniṣad belongs to this Veda.<BR>2 Conciliation, reconciling, appeasing.<BR>3 Calming, tranquillizing.<BR>4 Speaking kindly or tenderly.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A rope, for tying cattle.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, (sin,) Uṇādi aff. मनिन्, and ङीष् added for the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्त|सामंत|सामन्तः
सामन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>1 Limitative, boundary, bounding.<BR>2 Bordering, neighbouring.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The chief of a district.<BR>2 A neighbour.<BR>3 An attendant or companion of a chieftain, a leader, a captain, a champion.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>समन्त end, term, अण् aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तवासिन्
सामन्तवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Dwelling in the borders, bordering, neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>सामन्त, and वासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्य|सामन्यः
सामन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A Brahman conversant with the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>सामन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामय
सामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Seasonable, punctual, observing time or season.<BR>2 Precise, exact, stipulated, according to agreement.<BR>3 Conventional, customary.<BR>E.<BR>समय time or engagement, ठञ् or ठक् aff. of relation or possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयोनि|सामयोनिः
सामयोनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Born from or produced by the Sāma.<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सामन् the Veda, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्य|सामर्थ्यं
सामर्थ्य<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>1 Power, strength.<BR>2 Fitness, suitableness.<BR>3 Ability, adequacy.<BR>4 (In grammar,) Mutual relation of words.<BR>5 Sense or force of words.<BR>E.<BR>समर्थ able, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्ष
सामर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Enraged, in wrath.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अमर्ष anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A principal minister or counsellor.<BR>2 The chief of a company or corporation.<BR>E.<BR>समवाय an assembly, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामसंगायक
सामसंगायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chanter of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>साम, and सङ्गायक chanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An assistant or spectator at an assembly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>समाज an assembly, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्य|सामानाधिकरण्यं
सामानाधिकरण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Common office, function, government, &c.<BR>2 The receptacle or substratum of common properties.<BR>E.<BR>समानाधिकरण, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Common, general, generic, universal.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Kind, sort, specific or generic property or character.<BR>2 Common property, generality, community.<BR>3 Public affairs or business.<BR>4 Totality, entireness.<BR>5 A figure of rhetoric, the connexion of different objects by common properties.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A female who is common to all men, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>समान common, (to many individuals,) यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यलक्षण
सामान्यलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A generic or specific character.<BR>E.<BR>सामान्य, and लक्षण mark or description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यशासन|सामान्यशासनं
सामान्यशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A general edict or enactment.<BR>E.<BR>सामान्य common, and शासन a grant, an edict, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Compounded, composite.<BR>2 Comprehensive, collective.<BR>3 Brief, summary.<BR>E.<BR>समास, and ठक् aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि<BR>ind.<BR>1 Half.<BR>2 Blameably.<BR>E.<BR>षाम for षान्त्व to appease, अच् added, and इ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिकृत|सामिकृतः
सामिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Halved, divided.<BR>E.<BR>सामि half, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिभुक्त|सामिभुक्तः
सामिभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Half eaten.<BR>E.<BR>सामि half, and भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिपीत|सामिपीतः
सामिपीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Half drank.<BR>E.<BR>सामि half, and पीत drank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेन्य
सामिधेन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A Mantra or mystical prayer, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A prayer used on adding fuel to the sacrificial fire.<BR>2 Fuel.<BR>E.<BR>समिध् fuel, aff. षेण्यण्^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: cf. WIL1819, Abhyankar Dict. Sans. Grammar..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीची
सामीची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>Praise, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्य|सामीप्यं|सामीप्यः
सामीप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Proximity, nearness.<BR>E.<BR>समीप near, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>Marine, sea, sea-born, &c.<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 A spot or mark on the body.<BR>2 Sea salt.<BR>3 Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A mariner, a voyager.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
सामुद्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to spots on the body, or the circumstance of good or ill fortune supposed to be indicated by them.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An interpreter of spots on the body.<BR>2 A work on the same subject.<BR>E.<BR>समुद्र a spot or mole, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद
सामोद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Fragrant, odoriferous.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आमोद fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
साम्नी<BR>f. (-म्नी)<BR>A sort of metre, one of the classes occurring in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सामन the Sāma Veda, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्परायिक|सांपरायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
साम्परायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Future, of or in a future state of being.<BR>2 Calamitous.<BR>3 Relating to war or battle.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>सम्पराय futurity, &c., and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतम्|सांप्रतम्
साम्प्रतम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Now, at this time.<BR>2 Fitly, properly.<BR>E.<BR>सम् and प्र before तन to spread, aff. डम्, and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ब|सांब|सांबः|साम्बः
साम्ब<BR>r. 10th cl. (साम्बयति)<BR>To join, to connect, to assemble; also सम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बरी|सांबरी
साम्बरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female juggler.<BR>E.<BR>see शाम्बरी; the श being changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भवी|सांभवी
साम्भवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Red Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भस्|सांभस्
साम्भस्<BR>mfn. (-म्भाः-म्भाः-म्भः)<BR>Having or being united with water.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्य|साम्यं
साम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Equality, sameness.<BR>2 Likeness, similarity.<BR>E.<BR>सम same, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यता
साम्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Equality, sameness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, साम्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्य|साम्राज्यं
साम्राज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Imperial rule, dominion, empire.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>The descendant of a prince or man of the military tribe.<BR>E.<BR>सम्राज् an emperor, ष्यञ् aff. of the abstract, or ण्य patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=919" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साय|सायं|सायः
साय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Evening, close of day.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 End, close in general.<BR>E.<BR>षो to end or destroy, &c., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंकाल
सायंकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Eventide, evening.<BR>E.<BR>सायम् evening, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायक|सायकः
सायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A sword.<BR>f. (-यिका)<BR>Standing in order.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन|सायनं
सायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The longitude of a planet reckoned from the vernal equinoctial point.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अयन the equinoctial period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन्तन|सायंतन|सायन्तनः
सायन्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging to the evening.<BR>E.<BR>साय evening, and द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायम्
सायम्<BR>ind.<BR>Evening, close of the day, in the evening. See साय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायमण्डन
सायमण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The place or time of sunset.<BR>E.<BR>साय, and मण्डन embellishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायाह्न|सायाह्नः
सायाह्न<BR>m. (-ह्नः)<BR>The evening, eventide.<BR>E.<BR>सायम् evening, and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिन्
सायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A horseman, a groom.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, अय to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्य|सायुज्यं
सायुज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>1 Likeness, similarity.<BR>2 Identification, intimate union, (especially with the Deity.)<BR>E.<BR>स with, युज what joins, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साये
साये<BR>ind.<BR>In the evening, at the close of the day.<BR>E.<BR>साय evening, the seventh case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Best, excellent.<BR>2 Irrefragable, (as an argument.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The pith or sap of trees, &c.<BR>2 Strength, vigour.<BR>3 The essence of any things, the essential or vital part of it.<BR>4 The substance or material part (of a speech, book, message, &c.)<BR>5 Marrow.<BR>6 Air, wind.<BR>7 Sickness, disease.<BR>8 Firmness, hardness.<BR>9 The coagulum of curds, &c. cream.<BR>10 Fresh butter.<BR>11 Prowess, valour, heroism.<BR>m. (-रः-री)<BR>A man at chess, backgammon, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 Properity, fitness.<BR>4 Steel.<BR>5 (In rhetoric,) Climax.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Dūrbbā grass.<BR>(-री)<BR>The Shalik or Sārikā, (Turdus salica, BUC.)<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगन्ध|सारगंध|सारगन्धः
सारगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>सार essence, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारघ|सारघं
सारघ<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>Honey.<BR>E.<BR>सरधा a bee, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्ग|सारंग|सारङ्गः
सारङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Variegated, of a variegated colour.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Variegated colour.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 A deer.<BR>5 The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>6 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>7 A large kind of crane, (Ardea Sarunga, CAREY.)<BR>8 A peacock.<BR>9 A cloud.<BR>10 A tree.<BR>11 A parasol.<BR>12 A garment, cloth, cloths.<BR>13 Hair.<BR>14 A lotus.<BR>15 A flower.<BR>16 A conch shell.<BR>17 A jewel.<BR>18 Gold.<BR>19 A bow.<BR>20 KĀMADEVA.<BR>21 Sandal.<BR>22 Camphor.<BR>23 The earth.<BR>24 Night.<BR>25 Light.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of fiddle.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, अङ्गच् Uṇādi aff., or सार strength, &c., गम to go, खच् aff.; also शारङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्गिक|सारंगिक|सारंगिकः|सारङ्गिकः
सारङ्गिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird or deer-catcher, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सारङ्ग as above, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारज|सारजं
सारज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>सार cream, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Dysentery, diarrhoea.<BR>2 Hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>3 A counsellor and embassador from RĀVAṆA to RĀMA.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>2 A canal, a small river.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (causal form,) ल्युद aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणि|सारणिः
सारणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 A small river.<BR>2 A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>3 A drain, a canal or water-pipe.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (causal form,) अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिक|सारणिकः
सारणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Travelling, way-faring, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>सरणि a road, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिकघ्न|सारणिकघ्नः
सारणिकघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A robber.<BR>E.<BR>सारणिक a traveller, and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण्ड|सारंड|सारंडः|सारण्डः
सारण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A snake's egg.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (causal form,) अण्डन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतरु|सारतरुः
सारतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The plantain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>सांर sap, तरु a tree, having no timber in the stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतस्
सारतस्<BR>ind.<BR>By or with vigour or essence, vigorously, essentially.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारता
सारता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Strength, substance.<BR>2 Essence.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, सारत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथि|सारथिः
सारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (causal form,) अथिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथ्य|सारथ्यं
सारथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>1 Charioteering, driving.<BR>2 Conveyance.<BR>E.<BR>सारथि, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारदा
सारदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सार essence, (of wisdom and eloquence,) दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभङ्ग|सारभङ्गः
सारभङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Void of pith, substance, real strength, &c.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Destroying vigour, overcoming strength, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभाण्ड|सारभाण्डं
सारभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डः)<BR>A natural vessel, as the bag or skin in which musk is sold, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सार essence, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारमेय|सारमेयः
सारमेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>सरमा a bitch, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयोग
सारयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Possession or application of the essence of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारलोह|सारलोहं
सारलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Steel.<BR>E.<BR>सार, the same, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारव|सारवः
सारव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the Saryu river.<BR>E.<BR>सरयु the river, अण् aff., form special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवत्|सारवन्त्
सारवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Substantial, having pith, substance, strength, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवर्ज्जित|सारवर्जित|सारवर्ज्जितः
सारवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pithless, sapless.<BR>E.<BR>सार substance, and वर्ज्जित deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस|सारसं|सारसः
सारस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a lake or pond, &c.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A woman's zone.<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>The Sāras or Indian crane, male and female, (Ardea Sibirica.)<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सरस् a pond, a lake, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसन|सारसनं
सारसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A woman's zone or girdle, formed of twentyfive strings.<BR>2 A military belt or girdle, worn round the waist or chest, upon the coat of mail, to bind it to the body.<BR>E.<BR>सार strength, and षण to give, aff. अच्, or अस to diffuse, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत|सारस्वतः
सारस्वत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>1 Relating to the goddess SARASVATĪ, or to the river, &c.<BR>2 Eloquent, learned.<BR>m. plu. (-ताः)<BR>1 The people of the Saraswata country, or the north-west part of the province of Delhni.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A staff of the Vilva tree.<BR>2 The north-west part of the province of Delhi or part of the Punjab.<BR>3 A saint, sprung according to the legend, indirectly from the personified Sarasvatī river.<BR>4 A Brahman of a particular family, called Sārasvata, from his coming from that country, or supposed descent from the sanctified person last mentioned.<BR>E.<BR>सरस्वती the goddess, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=920" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साराल|सारालः
साराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासार
सारासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Strength and weakness, substance and emptiness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सार, and असार want of vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारि|सारिः
सारि<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A man at chess or backgammon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, causal form, इन् aff.; also शारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिका
सारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of bird, (Turdus Salica, BUC.) but applied also to the Maina, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. ण्वुल, also शारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिवा
सारिवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>see शारिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्य|सारूप्यं
सारूप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>1 Identity of form.<BR>2 Close resemblance.<BR>3 (In the drama,) Surprise at seeing an object or its likeness previously seen elsewhere.<BR>E.<BR>स with, रूप form, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थ|सार्थः
सार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Opulent, wealthy.<BR>2 Of like meaning or purport.<BR>3 Significant, importing, having meaning.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 A multitude of similar animals.<BR>2 A company of traders, a caravan, &c.<BR>3 A number or multitude in general.<BR>4 A wealthy man.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, causal form, थन् Uṇādi aff., or स for सह, &c., and अर्थ wealth, or meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवत्|सार्थवन्त्
सार्थवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Meaning, intending.<BR>2 Numerous in company.<BR>E.<BR>सार्थ, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवाह|सार्थवाहः
सार्थवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A merchant, a trader.<BR>2 The leader of a caravan.<BR>E.<BR>सार्थ a company, a caravan, and वह to bear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थिक|सार्थिकः
सार्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A merchant, a trader.<BR>E.<BR>सार्थ, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्र|सार्द्रं
सार्द्र<BR>mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं)<BR>Wet, moist, damp.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, and आर्द्र wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्ध
सार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं)<BR>Joined with half, (used chiefly in composition, as सार्द्धशतं a hundred and a half, i. e. fifty.)<BR>E.<BR>स with, अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्धम्
सार्द्धम्<BR>ind.<BR>With, together with.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, ऋद्ध increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Dressed, &c. with Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>सर्पिस् Ghee, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष्क|सार्पिष्कं
सार्पिष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Cooked or dressed with Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>सर्पिस् Ghee, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प्प|सार्प|सार्पः
सार्प्प<BR>mfn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पी-र्प्पं)<BR>Relating to a snake.<BR>f. (-र्प्पी)<BR>The ninth lunar asterism, of which the serpents are the presiding deities.<BR>E.<BR>सर्प्प a snake, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्व|सार्व|सार्वः|सार्व्वः
सार्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>Suitable to or fit for all, relating to all, &c.<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all (knowledge, &c.), and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वकालिक|सार्वकालिक
सार्व्वकालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of all times or seasons.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वकाल, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वजनिक|सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्व्वजनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging, fit or suited to all men.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वजन all men, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वजनीन|सार्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीनः
सार्व्वजनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating, fit or suited to all men, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वजन all mankind, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वत्रिक|सार्वत्रिक
सार्व्वत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Suited to, or belonging to every place.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वच every where, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वदैवत्य|सार्वदैवत्य
सार्व्वदैवत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-ती-त्यं)<BR>Presided over by, or sacred to all the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, देवता a god, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वधातुक|सार्वधातुक
सार्व्वधातुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Applicable to the whole of a radical term, (an affix, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, and धातु a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वभौतिक|सार्वभौतिक
सार्व्वभौतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to all elements, being, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्वभूत, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वभौम|सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्व्वभौम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Relating to or consisting of the whole earth, known throughout the earth, &c.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The elephant of KUVERA, as regent of the north.<BR>2 An emperor, a universal monarch.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, भूमि earth, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्व्वलौकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Universally known, prevailing throughout the universe.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, लोक a world, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्ववर्णिक|सार्ववर्णिक
सार्व्ववर्णिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Of every kind or sort.<BR>2 Belonging or relating to every tribe, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्ववर्ण, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वविभक्तिक|सार्वविभक्तिक
सार्व्वविभक्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Applicable or belonging to all the cases of a noun.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व, विभक्ति inflection, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्ववेद्य|सार्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्यः
सार्व्ववेद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A Brahman conversant with all the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सर्व्व all, वेद a Veda, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Mustard, made of or from mustard.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Mustard oil.<BR>E.<BR>सर्षप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल|सालः
साल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A wall surrounding a building, &c.<BR>2 A tree in general.<BR>3 The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>4 A fish (Ophiocephalus Wrahl, HAM.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A house; more usually शाला.<BR>E.<BR>षल to go, घञ् aff.; also शाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालग्राम
सालग्राम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A stone, a species of ammonite common in the Gandhak river, and worshipped by the Vaiṣṇavas, as a type of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अर a ring, ग्राम multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालन|सालनः
सालन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The resin of the Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालनिर्य्यास|सालनिर्यास|सालनिर्यासः
सालनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>साल the tree, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालपर्णी
सालपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum); also शालपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालपुष्प|सालपुष्पं
सालपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis).<BR>E.<BR>साल the Śāl tree, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालभञ्जिका|सालभंजिका
सालभञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>साल the Śāl tree or its wood, भञ्ज to rub, वुन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालरस|सालरसः
सालरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The resinous juice of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>साल the Śāl, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालवाहन|सालवाहनः
सालवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sovereign SĀLAVĀHANA.<BR>E.<BR>साल the Śāl tree, and वाहन a vehicle: see शालवाहन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालवेष्ट|सालवेष्टः
सालवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Turpentine, or the resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>साल the tree, and वेष्ट exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालशृङ्ग|सालशृंग|सालशृङ्गं
सालशृङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The upper part or coping of a wall.<BR>E.<BR>साल a wall, and शृङ्ग horn or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालाकरी
सालाकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female overcome or won in battle.<BR>E.<BR>साला a house, कृ to make, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालातुरीय|सालातुरीयः
सालातुरीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of PĀṆINI.<BR>E.<BR>also read शालातुरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालार|सालारं
सालार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A pin, a bracket, or shelf, projecting from a wall.<BR>E.<BR>साल a wall, ऋ to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालावृक|सालावृकः
सालावृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A wolf.<BR>3 A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>साला a house, and वृक a wolf, more usually शालावृक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालूर|सालूरः
सालूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>षल to go, ऊरच् aff.; the first vowel made long, and the initial changed; also शालुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालेय|सालेयं|सालेयः
सालेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of fennel or dill, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>see शालेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्य|सालोक्यं
सालोक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Habitation with, residing with, (especially with the deity.)<BR>E.<BR>स with, लोक world, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्यता
सालोक्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Habitation, state of abiding or dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=921" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्व|साल्वः
साल्व<BR>mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वी-ल्वं)<BR>Belonging to the Sālva country: the word is more usually read, शाल्व.<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>1 The name of a demon, the enemy of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The name of a country or place.<BR>m. pl. (-ल्वाः)<BR>The people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वहन्
साल्वहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>साल्व a demon, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्विक|साल्विकः
साल्विक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावक|सावकः
सावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-विका-कं)<BR>1 Generative, productive, causing birth, &c.<BR>2 Obstetric, parturient.<BR>f. (-विका)<BR>A midwife.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear young, causal form, षुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावज्ञ
सावज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Despising, disdainful.<BR>E.<BR>स with अवज्ञा disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधान|सावधानः
सावधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Careful, cautious.<BR>2 Dilligent.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Natural, (in astronomy) as Sāvana Dina, a natural day, from sunrise to sunrise.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The conclusion of a sacrifice, the ceremonies by which it is terminated.<BR>2 An employer of priests for a sacrifice.<BR>3 The deity VARUṆA.<BR>4 A month of thirty solar days.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear or produce, aff. ल्युट्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर|सावरः
सावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Lodh tree.<BR>2 Sin, crime.<BR>3 Fault, offence.<BR>E.<BR>see शावर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण|सावर्णः
सावर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The second Manu.<BR>E.<BR>सवर्ण the father of this person, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णि|सावर्णिः
सावर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 The second Manu.<BR>2 A name applied to the 8th, 9th, 10th, 11th, and 12th Menus, or Brahma Sāvarṇi, Dakṣa Sāvarṇi, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सवर्ण, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णलक्ष्य|सावर्णलक्ष्यं
सावर्णलक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्य|सावर्ण्यं
सावर्ण्य<BR>n. (-र्ण्यं)<BR>Identity of caste, class, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सवर्ण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
सावशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>2 Leaving a residue or remainder.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अवशेष remains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
सावहेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Despising, disdaining.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अवहेल disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 A Vasu or demigod so named.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>5 The embryo or foetus.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 UMĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The holy verse of the Vedas, the repetition of which forms an essential part of the ceremonies, enjoined to the Brahman, as daily observances: the prayer is personified as the wife of BRAHMĀ, and mystical mother of the Hindu classes, which are regenerated by investiture with the sacrificial string.<BR>3 The wife of SATYAVĀN.<BR>4 A beam of light, a cluster of solar rays.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The sacrificial string.<BR>E.<BR>सवित्र the sun, and अण् aff. of reference: the prayer is in fact addressed to that luminary, and the deities, &c. are manifestations of the planet or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपतित|सावित्रीपतितः
सावित्रीपतित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A man of the three first classes, not invested at the proper time with the sacrificial cord.<BR>E.<BR>सावित्री, and पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्ट|सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टः
सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A man of the three first classes, not invested with the string at the proper season.<BR>E.<BR>सावित्री, and परिभ्रष्ट broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीसूत्र|सावित्रीसूत्रं
सावित्रीसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The sacrificial or characteristic cord of the three first classes.<BR>E.<BR>साविची the sacred text, (the repetition of which forms part of the ceremony of investiture,) and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविष्कार
साविष्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>2 Manifest.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आविष्कार manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशयन्दक|साशयंदक|साशयंदकः|साशयन्दकः
साशयन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशूक|साशूकः
साशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्य्य|साश्चर्य
साश्चर्य्य<BR>n. adv. (-र्य्यं)<BR>With surprise.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आश्चर्य्य astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रुधी
साश्रुधी<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>A wife's or husband's mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासहि
सासहि<BR>mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि)<BR>Able to bear much.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, intens. v., कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्थिताम्रार्द्ध|सास्थिताम्रार्द्धं
सास्थिताम्रार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>Bell-metal.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अस्थि substance, ताम्र copper, and अर्द्धं a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना<BR>f. (-स्ना)<BR>The dewlap of an ox.<BR>E.<BR>सस to sleep, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
सास्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>1 Weeping, in tears.<BR>2 Cornered, angular.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अस्र a tear, or an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहङ्कार|साहंकार
साहङ्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Proud, arrogant.<BR>2 United with the principle of egotism.<BR>E.<BR>स with, अहङ्कार pride, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्य्य|साहचर्य|साहचर्यं|साहचर्य्यं
साहचर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Company, association, society, fellowship.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, चर going, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहन|साहनं
साहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sufferance, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहय|साहयः
साहय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Causing or enabling to endure.<BR>E.<BR>षह to bear, causal form, साहि, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहयक
साहयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Friendship, fellowship.<BR>E.<BR>साहय a friend, aff. वुञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस|साहसं|साहसः
साहस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Punishment, chastisement, fine.<BR>2 Violence, the perpetration of any act of rapine or aggression.<BR>3 Oppression, cruelty.<BR>4 Hatred.<BR>5 Rape, ravishment.<BR>6 Boldness, daring.<BR>7 Rashness.<BR>8 Oblation with fire.<BR>E.<BR>सहस् strength, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाङ्क|साहसांक|साहसाङ्कः
साहसाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A name of VIKRAMĀDITYA.<BR>E.<BR>साहस violence, अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक|साहसिकः
साहसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Castigatory, inflicted as punishment.<BR>2 Perpetrated by violence.<BR>3 Violent, felonious, rapacious, brutal, cruel.<BR>4 Impetuous, rash.<BR>5 Bold, daring.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A robber, a free-booter.<BR>E.<BR>साहस violence, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिन्
साहसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Violent, ferocious.<BR>2 Rash.<BR>3 Daring, bold.<BR>E.<BR>साहस, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसैकरसिक
साहसैकरसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Intent on violence, brutal, ferocious.<BR>E.<BR>साहस, एक alone, रस taste, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्री-स्रं)<BR>1 Bought with a thousand.<BR>2 Paid per thousand, as interest, duty, &c.<BR>3 Relating or belonging to a thousand.<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>An army or detachment, a thousand strong.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>An aggregate of many thousands.<BR>E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्य|साहाय्यं
साहाय्य<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>1 Friendship, fellowship.<BR>2 Help, succour.<BR>3 Alliance.<BR>E.<BR>सहाय a friend, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्य|साहित्यं
साहित्य<BR>nf. (-त्यं-ती)<BR>Society, association, connexion, combination.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Poetry, belles-lettres.<BR>E.<BR>सहित with, together with, aff. ष्यञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्य|साह्यं
साह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>Society, conjunction.<BR>E.<BR>सह with, together with, aff. of the abstract ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्यकृत्
साह्यकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A companion.<BR>E.<BR>साह्य society, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=922" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वय|साह्वयः
साह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Fighting animals, (as cocks, &c.) for sport or money.<BR>E.<BR>स with, आह्वय challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंह|सिंहः
सिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 LEO, the sign of the zodiac.<BR>3 (In composition) Pre-eminent.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>1 The egg-plant, (Solanum Melongena.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Justicia.)<BR>3 A prickly nightshade.<BR>4 The mother of RĀHU.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, क Uṇādi aff. ह substituted for the final, and नुम् inserted; or हिसि to injure or kill, अच् aff., and the radical consonants transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेलि|सिंहकेलिः
सिंहकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A Bauddha saint, also named MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेशर|सिंहकेशरः
सिंहकेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A lion's mane.<BR>2 A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and केशर a mane, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतल|सिंहतलः
सिंहतल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The open hands joined.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and तल the open palm; also read संहतल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतुण्ड|सिंहतुंड|सिंहतुण्डः
सिंहतुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of fish.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह, and तुण्ड face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहद्वार|सिंहद्वारं
सिंहद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A gate, an entrance, especially the chief gate of a mansion or palace.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह chief, and द्वार a door-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहध्वनि|सिंहध्वनिः
सिंहध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 The roar or sound of a lion.<BR>2 A war cry.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनर्द्दिन्|सिंहनर्दिन्
सिंहनर्द्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दी-र्द्दिनी-र्द्दि)<BR>Roaring like a lion.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह, and नर्द्दिन् who or what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनाद|सिंहनादः
सिंहनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>War-cry, war-hoop, shouting or roaring upon making an onset.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and नाद cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनादक|सिंहनादकः
सिंहनादक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The roar or yelp of a lion.<BR>2 War-cry.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, नाद sounding, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहपर्णी
सिंहपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहपुच्छी
सिंहपुच्छी<BR>f. (-च्छी)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and पुच्छ tail; also with कन् added, सिंहपुच्छिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहयाना
सिंहयाना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहरथा
सिंहरथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and रथ a vehicle, mounted on that animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहविक्रान्त|सिंहविक्रान्तः
सिंहविक्रान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and विक्रान्त valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहल|सिंहलं|सिंहलः
सिंहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Tin.<BR>2 Brass.<BR>3 Cassia bark.<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>Ceylon.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, &c., ला to give or get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलास्थान|सिंहलास्थानः
सिंहलास्थान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, apparently a sort of palm.<BR>E.<BR>सिंहला Ceylon, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहसहनन
सिंहसहनन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Handsome and well-shaped.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह the beast, सहनन rivalling or surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाढ्य
सिंहाढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>Abounding with lions.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह, and आद्य wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाण|सिंहाणं
सिंहाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rust of iron; also सिंहान.<BR>2 The mucus of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहान|सिंहानं
सिंहान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rust of iron.<BR>2 The mucus of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>शिधि, to smell, आनक् aff., form irr.; also शिङ्घाण, सिंहाण, सिङ्घाण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासन|सिंहासनं|सिंहासनः
सिंहासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A throne.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, (supported by lions, &c. wrought in gold,) and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहास्य|सिंहास्यः
सिंहास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, and आस्य the face; to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The mother of RĀHU.<BR>E.<BR>सिंही a lioness, कन् aff. of comparison, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिकासूनु|सिंहिकासूनुः
सिंहिकासूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>सिंहिका the mother of RĀHU, and सूनु son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकता
सिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sandy soil.<BR>2 Gravel or stone, (the disease.)<BR>m. plu. (-ताः)<BR>Sand.<BR>E.<BR>सिकि Sautra root, to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतामय|सिकतामयं
सिकतामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sandy.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A sand bank, or an island with sandy shores.<BR>E.<BR>सिकप्ता sand, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतावत्|सिकतावन्त्
सिकतावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sandy, (in general.)<BR>E.<BR>सिकत sand, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतिल|सिकतिलः
सिकतिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Sandy, as a soil or country.<BR>E.<BR>सिकता sand, aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त|सिक्तः
सिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Sprinkled, wetted.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त्वा
सिक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having sprinkled, effused, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थ|सिक्थं|सिक्थः
सिक्थ<BR>m. (-क्थः)<BR>1 A handful or mouthful of boiled rice.<BR>2 Boiled rice.<BR>n. (-क्थं)<BR>1 Bee's wax.<BR>2 Indigo.<BR>E.<BR>षिच् to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थक|सिक्थकं
सिक्थक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्ष्य|सिक्ष्यः
सिक्ष्य<BR>m. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Crystal, glass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घाण|सिंघाण|सिंघाणं|सिङ्घाणं
सिङ्घाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The mucus of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>शिघि to smell, Uṇādi aff. आनक्, and the last syllable of the aff. optionally rejected; also सिंघाणक. n. (-कं) सिंहाण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घाणक|सिंघाणकं|सिङ्घाणकं
सिङ्घाणक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The mucus of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घिनी
सिङ्घिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>शिघि to smell, affs. इनि and ङीप्, and the initial changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
सिच्<BR>f. (सिक्)<BR>Clothes.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिचय|सिचयः
सिचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Cloth, clothes.<BR>2 Old or ragged raiment.<BR>E.<BR>षिचि to cause to sprinkle, aff. श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्यमान
सिच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>षिच् to sprinkle, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चत्
सिञ्चत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्)<BR>Sprinkling, throwing water.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, शतृ aff. of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चता
सिञ्चता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Long-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्जा|सिंजा
सिञ्जा<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>The sound of metallic ornaments, jingling, ringing, tinkling; more usually शिञ्जा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or -ती-तं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Bound, tied.<BR>3 Finished, destroyed.<BR>4 Completed, concluded.<BR>5 Known.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 The planet VENUS.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 Sandal.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>2 Arabian jasmine.<BR>3 A sort of Clitoria.<BR>4 Bent grass with white blossoms.<BR>5 Moonlight.<BR>6 Spirituous liquor.<BR>7 A handsome or well made woman.<BR>E.<BR>षि to tie or bind, aff. क्त; or षो to destroy, क्त aff., and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितकुञ्जर|सितकुञ्जरः
सितकुञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितचिह्न|सितचिह्नः
सितचिह्न<BR>m. (-ह्नः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Lacerta scincus.)<BR>E.<BR>सित white, चिह्न a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितछच
सितछच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A white umbrella, especially as one of the emblems of royalty.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and छच an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितछद|सितच्छद|सितच्छदः
सितछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A goose.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>White Dūrbbā grass.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and छद a feather or leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितदीधिति|सितदीधितिः
सितदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and दीधिति a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=923" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितदूर्व्वा|सितदूर्वा
सितदूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A bent grass with white blossoms.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and दूर्व्वा Doob grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितद्रु|सितद्रुः
सितद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Moraṭā.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितधातु|सितधातुः
सितधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितपक्ष|सितपक्षः
सितपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, पक्ष a feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितपुष्प|सितपुष्पं|सितपुष्पः
सितपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A sort of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A sort of tree, the Tagara tree.<BR>2 A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमरिच|सितमरिचं
सितमरिच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>White pepper.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and मरिच pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमाष|सितमाषः
सितमाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and माष pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितरञ्जन|सितरञ्जनः
सितरञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Yellow, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितरश्मि|सितरश्मिः
सितरश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशिम्बिक|सितशिम्बिकः
सितशिम्बिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and शिम्बिका an awn; also read शितशिम्बिक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशिव|सितशिवं
सितशिव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and शिव auspicious; also शितशिवं, सितसिवं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशूक|सितशूकः
सितशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>शित white, and शूक an awn or ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसप्ति|सितसप्तिः
सितसप्ति<BR>m. (-प्तिः)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and सप्ति a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसर्षप|सितसर्षपः
सितसर्षप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>White mustard.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and सर्षप mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसिन्धु|सितसिन्धुः
सितसिन्धु<BR>f. (-न्धुः)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसिव
सितसिव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and सिव for शिव auspicious; also सितशिव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितांशु|सितांशुः
सितांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सित, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताखण्ड|सिताखण्डः
सिताखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Clayed sugar, said to be prepared from honey.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, आखण्ड sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताङ्क|सिताङ्कः
सिताङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A kind of fish, (Lacerta scincus.)<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अङ्क a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताग्र|सिताग्रः
सिताग्र<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितादि|सितादिः
सितादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>Treacle, molasses.<BR>E.<BR>सिता sugar, before दा to give, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितानन|सिताननः
सितानन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितापाङ्ग|सितापांग|सितापाङ्गः
सितापाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अपाङ्ग the angle of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताब्ज|सिताब्जं
सिताब्ज<BR>n. (-ब्जं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अब्ज a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताभ|सिताभः
सिताभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, आङ् before भा to shine, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताभ्र|सिताभ्रः
सिताभ्र<BR>mn. (-भ्रः-भ्रं)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अभ्र a cloud, also with कन् added, सिताभ्रक n. (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताम्बर|सिताम्बरः
सिताम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ascetic wearing white garments.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताम्भोज|सिताम्भोजं
सिताम्भोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अम्भोज a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितालता
सितालता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Doob or Dūrbbā grass with white blossoms.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and लता a creeper^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताश्व|सिताश्वः
सिताश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितालिका
सितालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockle.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, आलि a line, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितासित|सितासितः
सितासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White and black.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of BALADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, (skin,) and असित black, (rainment.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
सिति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Black.<BR>E.<BR>सि to bind, aff. क्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिमन्
सितिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Whiteness.<BR>E.<BR>सिति white, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिवासस्
सितिवासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>BALADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सिति black, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितेतर|सितेतरः
सितेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Black.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, इतर reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितेतरगति|सितेतरगतिः
सितेतरगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सितेतर black, (smoke,) गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोदर|सितोदरः
सितोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and उदर the belly; the deity is properly of a black colour, but is whitened by a leprous taint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोपल|सितोपलं|सितोपलः
सितोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Chalk, or a mineral substance of similar appearance, considered as a variety.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Crystal.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोष्णवारण
सितोष्णवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A white umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>सित, and उष्णवारण keeping off the heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Accomplished, effected, completed.<BR>2 Liberated, emancipated.<BR>3 Always, eternal.<BR>4 Celebrated, famous.<BR>5 Judged, decided, terminated, (as a law suit.)<BR>6 Valid, (in law.)<BR>7 Adept, initiated, in alchymy or magic.<BR>8 Demonstrated, proved, (in logic.)<BR>9 Finished.<BR>10 Cooked, dressed.<BR>11 Prepared, compounded, (in medicine.)<BR>12 Shining, splendid.<BR>13 Discharged, settled, (as a debt.)<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 A divine personage of undefined attributes or character; a sort of demigod or spirit, inhabiting, together with the Vidyādharas, Munis, &c. the middle air, or the region between the earth and sun.<BR>2 An inspired or prophetic writer, as VYĀSA and others, or one to whom the past, present, and future, are supposed to be known, a sage, a seer.<BR>3 The twenty-first of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>4 An adept, a magician, one who by the performance of certain mystical and magical rites has acquired superhuman powers.<BR>5 An ascetic, who by mystical and austere practices has effected one or all of five purposes, viz. the affluence, the form, or the society of the gods, residence in the divine Lokas, or identification with a deity.<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>E.<BR>षिध to effect, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धगङ्गा|सिद्धगंगा
सिद्धगङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध a spirit of midheaven, and गङ्गा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धजल|सिद्धजलं
सिद्धजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sour rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध perfect, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धदेव|सिद्धदेवः
सिद्धदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध a saint, and देव deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धधातु|सिद्धधातुः
सिद्धधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध adept, (in alchymy,) and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धरस|सिद्धरसः
सिद्धरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Mineral, metallic, &c.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>2 An alchymist.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध perfect, or perfected by alchymical operation, and रस fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसङ्घ|सिद्धसंघ
सिद्धसङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>A company of saints or the beings called Siddhas.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध, and सङ्घ a company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसलिल|सिद्धसलिलं
सिद्धसलिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sour rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध perfect, and सलिल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधन|सिद्धसाधनं|सिद्धसाधनः
सिद्धसाधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>White mustard.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The performance of magical rites, &c. or the materials employed in magical or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">Page925</a>] alchemical processes.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध perfect, adept, &c., and साधन accomplishing, (the act or instrument.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=924" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाध्य|सिद्धसाध्यः
सिद्धसाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Effected, proved.<BR>2 Having done what was to be done.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Demonstrated proof or conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध, and साध्य to be proved, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसिन्धु|सिद्धसिंधु|सिद्धसिन्धुः
सिद्धसिन्धु<BR>f. (-न्धुः)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध a divine being or sage, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसेन|सिद्धसेनः
सिद्धसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The deity of war, KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध a divine being, and सेना an army; commanding the hosts of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्त|सिद्धांत|सिद्धान्तः
सिद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Demonstrated conclusion, established truth: it may be either the result of an argument in which one opinion is refused and another undeniably established; or the concurrent doctrine of all the authorities on any subject similarly interpreted.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध completed, perfect, and अन्त end, conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्तिन्|सिद्धांतिन्
सिद्धान्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A follower of the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR>2 A demonstrator, one who establishes his conclusions.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्धान्त demonstrated conclusion, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धापगा
सिद्धापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध a divine being, and अपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धायिका
सिद्धायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>One of the tutelary goddesses of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थ|सिद्धार्थः
सिद्धार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Successful, prosperous.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 The father of the last and most celebrated Jina or Jaina teacher of the present era.<BR>2 White mustard.<BR>3 A name of Sāhyasiṃha or Buddha.<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>The mother of the fourth Jina.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्ध complete, &c., and अर्थ meaning or wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धि|सिद्धिः
सिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Fulfilment, accomplishment, the entire completion of any undertaking or attainment of any object.<BR>2 A Yoga, either the sixteenth of the astronomical periods termed Yogas, or the nineteenth of the twenty-eight astrological Yogas.<BR>3 Final emancipation from existence, supreme felicity.<BR>4 Prosperity, success.<BR>5 Knowledge, understanding.<BR>6 Accuracy, correctness, indisputable conclusion or position.<BR>7 Validity (in law.)<BR>8 Acquittance, discharge, (of a debt.)<BR>9 Concealment, secreting, covering.<BR>10 The result or fruit of the adoration of the gods or of ascetic severities.<BR>11 The supposed acquirement of supernatural powers by the completion of magical, mystical, or alchemical rites and processes.<BR>12 A wooden shoe or slipper, especially one over which some mystical formulæ have been repeated, and which will then, it is supposed, convey the wearer every where safely and rapidly.<BR>13 A medicinal root; also Ṛddhi.<BR>E.<BR>षिध to accomplish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिली
सिद्धिली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A small ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्म|सिध्मं
सिध्म<BR>n. (-ध्मं)<BR>A blotch, a scab.<BR>E.<BR>षिध to go, (on the body,) मक् aff.; also सिध्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मन्
सिध्मन्<BR>n. (-ध्म)<BR>A blotch, a scab.<BR>E.<BR>षिध to go, मनिन् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Scabby.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Dried or salt fish.<BR>2 A scab.<BR>3 A sort of leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>सिध्म a scab, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मवत्|सिध्मवन्त्
सिध्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Scabby, pocky.<BR>E.<BR>सिध्म a blotch, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्य|सिध्यः
सिध्य<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>The asterism Puṣya, stars in Cancer.<BR>E.<BR>षिध to accomplish or to be accomplished, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>1 A pious or virtuous man.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>षिघ to be perfect, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रका
सिध्रका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, so named.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रकावण|सिध्रकावणं
सिध्रकावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A garden of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सिध्रका a plant, and वन a wood, न changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन|सिनं|सिनः
सिन<BR>mf. (-नः-नी)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A mouthful, or such a quantity bound together.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, नक् Uṇādi aff. or षि to bind, क्त aff. in this particular application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनीवाली
सिनीवाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The day preceding that of new moon, or that on which the moon rises scarcely visible.<BR>2 The goddess UMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सा good fortune, इनि aff., fem. form, सिनी a digit of the moon, वल to contain, aff. अण्, fem. aff. ङीष्; several other etymologies occur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुक|सिंदुक|सिंदुकः|सिन्दुकः
सिन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to ooze, aff. उ, and कन् added; the semivowel of the root changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुवार|सिंदुवार|सिंदुवारः|सिन्दुवारः
सिन्दुवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>E.<BR>सिन्दु oozing, (as before,) वृ to screen or choose, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूर|सिंदूर|सिन्दूरं|सिंदूरः|सिन्दूरः
सिन्दूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Red lead, minium.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of tree.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Red cloth or clothes.<BR>2 Rocani, (a sort of Crinum.)<BR>3 A plant, (Lythrum fruticosum.)<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to ooze, Uṇādi aff. ऊरन्; also read सिन्दुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरकारण|सिन्दूरकारणं
सिन्दूरकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्दूर minium, and कारण origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरतिलक|सिन्दूरतिलकः
सिन्दूरतिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose forehead is marked with minium.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्दूर red lead, and तिलक the mark on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरिका|सिंदूरिका
सिन्दूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्दूर, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरित|सिंदूरित
सिन्दूरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reddened, made red.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्दूर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धु|सिंधु|सिंधुः|सिन्धुः
सिन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>1 The ocean, the sea.<BR>2 The Indus.<BR>3 The country along the Indus or Sindh.<BR>4 The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples.<BR>5 An elephant.<BR>6 A division of a Rāga or musical mode.<BR>7 A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>f. (-न्धुः)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to trickle or flow, उ Uṇādi aff., the form. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुक|सिंधुक|सिंधुकः|सिन्धुकः
सिन्धुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Marine.<BR>2 Born or produced in Sindh.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, implying place of origin or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुकफ|सिन्धुकफः
सिन्धुकफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुखेल|सिन्धुखेलः
सिन्धुखेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The country of Sindh.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the Indus, खिल to go or sport, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुज|सिंधुज|सिन्धुजं|सिन्धुजः
सिन्धुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 River or sea-born, marine, aquatic.<BR>2 Born or produced in Sindh.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the country or river, &c., and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुजन्मन्
सिन्धुजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>The moon.<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, &c., and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुनन्दन|सिन्धुनन्दनः
सिन्धुनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the ocean, and नन्दन the son; being produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुनाथ|सिन्धुनाथः
सिन्धुनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु a river, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुपुत्त्र
सिन्धुपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A sort of ebony.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, &c., and पुत्त्र offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुपुष्प|सिन्धुपुष्पः
सिन्धुपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A conch.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=925" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुमन्थज|सिन्धुमन्थजं
सिन्धुमन्थज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धुमन्थ the ocean churning, (a mountain,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुर|सिंधुर|सिंधुरः|सिन्धुरः
सिन्धुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to ooze, (the ichor from his temples,) उरच् aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुरद्वैषिन्
सिन्धुरद्वैषिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धुर an elephant, and द्वैषिन् enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुलवण|सिन्धुलवणं
सिन्धुलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु Sindh, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवार|सिंधुवार|सिंधुवारः|सिन्धुवारः
सिन्धुवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A horse of a good breed, brought probably from Sindh or the borders of India and Persia.<BR>2 A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the country or the sea, वृ to choose or screen; aff. घञ्; also सिन्दुवार in the second sense, and with कन् added, सिन्धुवारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवारित|सिन्धुवारितः
सिन्धुवारित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, and वारित selected or chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवेषण|सिन्धुवेषणः
सिन्धुवेषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुशयन|सिन्धुशयनः
सिन्धुशयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the ocean, and शयन a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुसङ्गम|सिन्धुसंगम|सिन्धुसङ्गमः
सिन्धुसङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The mouth of a river, or its point of junction with the sea.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु the sea, and सङ्गम confluence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धूद्भव|सिन्धूद्भवं
सिन्धूद्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु Sindh, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धूपल|सिंधूपल|सिन्धूपलं
सिन्धूपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु Sindh, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिप्र|सिप्रं|सिप्रः
सिप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>1 Perspiration, sweat.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>f. (-प्रा)<BR>1 The Sipra, a river near Oujein.<BR>2 A woman's zone.<BR>3 A female buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम|सिमः
सिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>All, entire.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बा|सिंबा
सिम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा-म्बिः or -म्बी)<BR>A legume, a pod: see शिम्बा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बिका
सिम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Grain in pods, as pulse, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सिम्बा a pod, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिर|सिरः
सिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The root of long-pepper.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Any tubular vessel of the body, or one so considered, as a nerve, a vein, an artery, a tendon, &c.<BR>2 A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, aff. रक्, form irr.; also शिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराजाल
सिराजाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plexus of vessels.<BR>2 Enlargement of the vessels of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>सिरा, and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिरामोक्ष|सिरामोक्षः
सिरामोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Venesection.<BR>E.<BR>सिरा a vein, and भोक्ष loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराव्यध|सिराव्यधः
सिराव्यध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Venesection.<BR>E.<BR>सिरा, and व्यध piercing; also सिराव्यधनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराहर्ष
सिराहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Flow of discoloured tears.<BR>E.<BR>सिरा, and हर्ष joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिरोत्पात|सिरोत्पातः
सिरोत्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Redness and inflammation of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>सिरा, and उत्पात affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिल्लकी
सिल्लकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>see सल्लकी, the इ being substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषङ्ग्रामयिषु|सिषंग्रामयिषु
सिषङ्ग्रामयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing or intending to make war.<BR>E.<BR>सङ्ग्राम to make war, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषा
सिषाधयिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Wish or purpose to effect, prove, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षाध to accomplish, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषु
सिषाधयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous to accomplish, to prove, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षाध to accomplish, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षा
सिसृक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Wish or purpose to create.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षु
सिसृक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing or purposing to create.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिहुण्ड|सिहुंड|सिहुंडः|सिहुण्डः
सिहुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्ण
सिह्ण<BR>m. (-ह्णः)<BR>Incense, gum Benjamin or Olibanum, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to be affectionate, to love, लक aff., form irr.; also with कन् added, सिह्णक. m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्णकी
सिह्णकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The Olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>सिह्ण incense, कन् added, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्णभूमिका
सिह्णभूमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>सिह्ण incense, भूमि place, site, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक
सीक<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>1 To touch.<BR>2 To bear.<BR>(ऋ) सीकृ r. 1st cl. (सीकति)<BR>To sprinkle, to shed or shower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीकर|सीकरः
सीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Thin drizzling rain.<BR>E.<BR>सीक to scatter, (as water,) अरन् aff.; also शीकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीता
सीता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A furrow, the track of the plough-share.<BR>2 The daughter of JANAKA and wife of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>3 One of the four great branches into which the Ganges, after having fallen on mount Meru, is fabled to divide: the eastern branch, flowing into the Varṣa Bhadrāśva.<BR>4 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>5 UMĀ the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>6 A goddess presiding over fruits, &c. an Indian FLORA or POMONA.<BR>7 Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, (the earth,) क्त aff., form irr.; it is then applicable to the princess as having been turned up in the soil by a plough-share; and to the goddess, as they may be supposed to have been incarnate in the wife of RĀMA; also, as differently derived शीता, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतापति|सीतापतिः
सीतापति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The hero RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सीता the princess, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतायाःपति|सीतायाःपतिः
सीतायाःपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सीता in the poss. case, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतीनक|सीतीनकः
सीतीनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Pease: see सतीलक, सतीनक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कार|सीत्कारः
सीत्कार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Uttering an inarticulate sound, such as is made with the lips when a person shivers with cold, or in fainting, sighing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सीत् imitative sound, and कार making; also सीत्कृत n. (-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कृत|सीत्कृतं
सीत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uttered as an inarticulated sound.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>An inarticulate sound: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सीत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्य|सीत्यं
सीत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Ploughed, tilled.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Corn, grain, rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सीता a furrow, यत् aff.; also शीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीदत्
सीदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>1 Sorrowing, grieving, desponding.<BR>2 Decaying.<BR>3 Suffering from, distressed or pained by.<BR>4 Going.<BR>E.<BR>षद to wane, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधु|सीधुः
सीधु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>Spirit, distilled from molasses.<BR>E.<BR>see शीधु, the sibilant being changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुगन्ध|सीधुगंध|सीधुगन्धः
सीधुगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A plant, (Mimusopa elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>सीधु rum, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुप
सीधुप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Drinking spirits.<BR>E.<BR>सिधु, and पा to drink, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीध्र|सीध्रं
सीध्र<BR>n. (-ध्रं)<BR>The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्
सीमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A boundary, a limit, a landmark, or mound, &c. serving to fix the limits of estates, &c.<BR>2 A field.<BR>3 The nape of the neck.<BR>4 The scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>षिञ् to bind, इमनिन् Uṇādi aff.; also with the aff. डाष्, or a final vowel, fem. form, सीमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त|सीमंत|सीमंतः|सीमन्तः
सीमन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A separation of the hair on each side, so as to leave a distinct line on the top of the head.<BR>mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>सीमन् limit, of the hair, and अन्त end, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=926" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तक|सीमंतक|सीमन्तकं|सीमंतकः|सीमन्तकः
सीमन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An infernal being.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Red lead, a mark with which is sometimes made along the division of the hair.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तिनी|सीमंतिनी
सीमन्तिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman in general.<BR>E.<BR>सीमन्त the separation of the hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तोन्नयन|सीमंतोन्नयन|सीमन्तोन्नयनं
सीमन्तोन्नयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>One of the Saṃskāras, or a purificatory and sacrificial ceremony, observed by women in the fourth, sixth, or eighth month of their pregnancy.<BR>E.<BR>सीमन्त partition of the hair, and उन्नयन arranging; this forming an essential part of the rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त्यमान
सीमन्त्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being parted or divided.<BR>E.<BR>सीमन्त used as a passive verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमा
सीमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A boundary, a limit.<BR>2 A field.<BR>3 A bank, a shore.<BR>4 Rectitude, observance of due bounds in morals, &c.<BR>5 The nape of the neck.<BR>6 The scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>see सीमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमालिङ्ग|सीमालिंग
सीमालिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A land or boundary mark.<BR>E.<BR>सीमा, and लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाविवाद|सीमाविवादः
सीमाविवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Litigation or dispute respecting boundaries.<BR>E.<BR>सीमा, and विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमावृक्ष|सीमावृक्षः
सीमावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree serving as a boundary mark.<BR>E.<BR>सीमा, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमासन्धि|सीमासंधि|सीमासंधिः
सीमासन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>The meeting of two boundaries.<BR>E.<BR>सीमा, and सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमीक
सीमीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of tree.<BR>E.<BR>ष्यम to sound, and कीकन् Uṇādi aff., य changed to इ, and that made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर|सीरः
सीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A plough.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, Uṇādi aff. रन्, and the vowel made long; also शीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरक|सीरकः
सीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरपाणि|सीरपाणिः
सीरपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>BALADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरिन्
सीरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, and इणि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीवन|सीवनं
सीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sewing, stitching.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The frenum of the prepuce.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, ल्युट् aff.; also सेवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीस|सीसं
सीस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, क्विप् aff., सी a binding, षो to destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसक|सीसकं
सीसक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसपत्रक|सीसपत्रकं
सीसपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीहुण्ड|सीहुंड|सीहुंडः|सीहुण्डः
सीहुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सी for सिद्ध complete, and हुण्ड a heap, from हुडि to collect, aff. घञ्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु<BR>r. 1st cl. (सवति)<BR>1 To bring forth, as young.<BR>2 To possess power.<BR>3 To go: see षु and षू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix analogous to good, well, or the Greek Eu, and implying,<BR>1 reverence, worship, honour;<BR>2 Assent;<BR>3 Encrease, prosperity;<BR>4 Excess, exceeding;<BR>5 Pain, distress;<BR>6 Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>षु to go, aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकण्टका
सुकण्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Aloe plant.<BR>E.<BR>सु good or much, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकण्डु|सुकंडु|सुकण्डुः
सुकण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>Psora, itch.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, कण्डु the same disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकन्द|सुकंद|सुकन्दः
सुकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 The onion.<BR>2 A yam.<BR>3 A sort of grass, (Scirpus kyssoor.)<BR>4 An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकन्दक|सुकंदक|सुकन्दकः
सुकन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An onion.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, कन्द a root, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर|सुकरः
सुकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Easy, practicable, attainable.<BR>2 Doing well or becomingly.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Doing good to, charity, benevolence.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A tractable cow.<BR>E.<BR>सु pleasure, कृ to make or confer, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर्णिका
सुकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, कर्ण an ear, कन् aff. of comparison, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर्म्मन्|सुकर्मन्
सुकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Virtuous, good, acting virtuously, doing what is right and fit.<BR>2 Active, diligent.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 The artist or architect of the gods.<BR>2 One of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, कर्म्मन् act, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकल|सुकलः
सुकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Liberal, both in giving and using.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, कल to call, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकाण्डिन्|सुकांडिन्
सुकाण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, काण्ड a shrub, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकालिन्
सुकालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A progenitor of a particular class considered as those of the Śūdra tribe.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, काल time, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुन्दक|सुकुंदक|सुकुन्दकः
सुकुन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An onion; also सुकन्दक, मुकुन्दक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुमार|सुकुमारः
सुकुमार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Soft, smooth, tender.<BR>2 Youthful, young.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A variety of the sugar-cane.<BR>3 A sort of grain, (Panicum colonum, &c.)<BR>4 A wild kind of Champak.<BR>5 The name of a Daitya.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Double jasmine.<BR>2 Great-flowered jasmine.<BR>3 The plantain.<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, exceedingly, कुमार soft, young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृत्
सुकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious.<BR>2 Fortunate, well-fated.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृत|सुकृतं
सुकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious.<BR>2 Befriended, assisted, treated with kindness.<BR>3 Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>4 Done well, properly, ably, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>2 Fortune, auspiciousness.<BR>3 Kindness, bounty, friendly aid or assistance.<BR>4 Any kind or friendly act.<BR>5 Reward, recompense, especially heaven as the reward of virtue.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and कृत made or done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृति|सुकृतिः
सुकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Virtue, well-doing.<BR>2 Kindness, acting in a friendly or kindly manner.<BR>3 The practice of religious austerities, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and कृति action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृतिन्
सुकृतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Fortunate, well-fated.<BR>2 Virtuous, pious, good.<BR>3 Benign, benevolent.<BR>4 Learned, wise.<BR>E.<BR>सुकृत auspiciousness, &c. इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकोली
सुकोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Kṣīrakākolī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुक्रिया
सुक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A good action, a good work; a moral or religious observance.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख<BR>r. 10th cl. (सुखयति)<BR>To make happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 Happy, joyful, delighted.<BR>2 Virtuous, pious.<BR>3 Easy, practicable.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Happiness, pleasure, delight.<BR>2 Heaven, paradise.<BR>3 Water.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The capital of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, ख an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखकर|सुखकरः
सुखकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Conferring happiness.<BR>2 Doing any thing easily.<BR>3 Done easily.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखङ्घुण|सुखंघुण|सुखंघुणः|सुखङ्घुणः
सुखङ्घुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of weapon or staff with which ŚIVA is armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखचार|सुखचारः
सुखचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An excellent horse.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, चर to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखछेद्य|सुखच्छेद्य
सुखछेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Easily to be cut or destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and छेद्य to be cut or cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=927" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखजात|सुखजातः
सुखजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Happy, taking pleasure.<BR>2 Born or produced easily.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखद|सुखदं|सुखदः
सुखद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Conferring or affording pleasure, &c.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The seat of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, दा to give, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखदोह्या
सुखदोह्या<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A cow easily milked.<BR>E.<BR>सुख (with) pleasure, दोह्य to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखप्रतीक्ष
सुखप्रतीक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Hoping or expecting happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and प्रति before ईक्ष to see, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभाग
सुखभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Happiness, good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभागिन्
सुखभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>सुखभाग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभेद्य
सुखभेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Easily broken or disunited.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and भेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखमय
सुखमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Full or consisting of happiness, delightful.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवर्च्चक|सुखवर्चक|सुखवर्चकः|सुखवर्च्चकः
सुखवर्च्चक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, बर्च्च to shine, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवासन|सुखवासनः
सुखवासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Perfume for the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, and वासन perfuming; also मुखवासन and शुभवासन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवेदन
सुखवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Consciousness of pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and वेदन knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसन्दुह्या|सुखसंदुह्या
सुखसन्दुह्या<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A tractable and gentle cow, one easily milked.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसन्दोह्या|सुखसंदोह्या
सुखसन्दोह्या<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A tractable cow, one easily and quickly milked.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, सम् before दुह to milk, ण्यत् aff.; also with क्यप् aff. सुखसंदुह्या as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसाध्य
सुखसाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Easy of accomplishment or attainment.<BR>2 Easy of cure.<BR>3 Easy to be discomfited.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and साध्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखस्पर्श
सुखस्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Gratifying, agreeable to the touch or feelings.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and स्पर्श touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाधार|सुखाधारः
सुखाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Svarga, the heaven of INDRA, and paradise of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, and आधार a receptacle or reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखानुभव
सुखानुभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Anticipation or consciousness of pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and अनुभव perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखान्त
सुखान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Wishing well, friendly, attached.<BR>2 Subversive of happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखायत|सुखायतं|सुखायतः
सुखायत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An excellent and well-trained horse.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, and आयत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखायन|सुखायनः
सुखायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A good horse.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखार्थ|सुखार्थः
सुखार्थ<BR>n. adv. (-र्थं)<BR>For the sake of ease, happiness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and अर्थम् on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखार्थिन्
सुखार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Seeking or wishing for happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and अर्थिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखावतीश्वर|सुखावतीश्वरः
सुखावतीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A deified teacher of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखावह|सुखावहः
सुखावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Conferring pleasure, delighting, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, आङ् before वह to convey, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाश|सुखाशः
सुखाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 VARUṆA, deity of water.<BR>2 A cucumber, (Cucumis sativus.)<BR>3 Eating with pleasure, feeding on dainties, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, अश to eat, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाशक|सुखाशकः
सुखाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The common cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>सुखाश the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखासीन
सुखासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Seated or sitting at ease.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखास्वाद|सुखास्वादः
सुखास्वाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Well-flavoured.<BR>2 Delightful, agreeable.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Enjoyment.<BR>2 Flavour.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and आस्वाद taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाहर
सुखाहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Conferring pleasure, agreeable, delightful.<BR>E.<BR>सुख and आङ् before हृ to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिन्
सुखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>Happy, pleasant, possessing happiness or pleasure.<BR>m. (-खी)<BR>A Yati or religious ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिस्वभाव
सुखिस्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A happy or contented disposition.<BR>E.<BR>सुखिन्, and स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखेच्छा
सुखेच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>Hope or desire of happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखैषिन्
सुखैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Wishing well to, seeking another's happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and एषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोत्सव|सुखोत्सवः
सुखोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>सुख pleasure, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोदय|सुखोदयः
सुखोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Realization or occurrence of pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and उदय arising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोदर्क
सुखोदर्क<BR>mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>Yielding or leading to happiness or pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and उदर्क consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोद्य
सुखोद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be uttered easily or agreeably.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and उद्य to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोपविष्ट
सुखोपविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Seated comfortably or at ease.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and उपविष्ट seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोपसर्प्य
सुखोपसर्प्य<BR>mfn. (-र्प्यः-र्प्या-र्प्यं)<BR>Easy of access.<BR>E.<BR>सुख, and उपसर्प्य to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्यात
सुख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Celebrated, famous.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and ख्यात renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्याति
सुख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग|सुगं|सुगः
सुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Graceful, elegant, going well or elegantly.<BR>2 Well rid of.<BR>3 Plain, intelligible.<BR>4 Easy of access.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Fæces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, good, गम to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगण्
सुगण्<BR>mfn. (-गण्)<BR>Counting well, a ready reckoner, or of easy calculation.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, easily, गण to number, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगणित
सुगणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Easily or accurately calculated.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and गणित counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगत|सुगतः
सुगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Passed, gone.<BR>2 Well-bestowed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Buddha in general, one of the generic terms for a deified sage, and teacher of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and गत gone or known, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्ध|सुगंध|सुगन्धं|सुगन्धः
सुगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>1 Small cummin seed.<BR>2 A fragrant grass; also कत्तृण.<BR>3 The blue lotus.<BR>4 Sandal.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Fragrance, odour.<BR>2 Sulphur.<BR>3 A sort of Morinda.<BR>4 A trader, a dealer.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 The ichneumon plant.<BR>2 Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>3 A fragrant grass.<BR>4 A sort of line.<BR>5 Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>6 Jasmine, (of various sorts.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धक|सुगंधक|सुगन्धकः
सुगन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sulphur.<BR>2 The orange.<BR>3 A sort of gourd, (Momordica mixta.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धि|सुगंधि|सुगन्धिः
सुगन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>1 Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>2 Virtuous, pious.<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>1 A perfume, a fragrance.<BR>2 A fragrant sort of mango.<BR>n. (-न्धि)<BR>1 A drug and perfume, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>2 The root of long-pepper.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">Page929</a>]<BR>4 Another sort, (Scirpus kyssoor.)<BR>5 Coriander seed.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, well, गन्ध smell, and इ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=928" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिक|सुगंधिक|सुगन्धिकं|सुगन्धिकः
सुगन्धिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A large sort of rice.<BR>2 Incense.<BR>3 Sulphur.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सु pleonasm, गन्ध smell, ठक् aff.; also सौगन्धिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिकुसुम|सुगन्धिकुसुमः
सुगन्धिकुसुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of Nerium with yellowish flowers.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्धि fragrant, and कुसुम flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिता
सुगन्धिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fragrance, pleasing scent, such as is produced by the trituration of perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्धि fragrant, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिमूल|सुगन्धिमूलं
सुगन्धिमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Rasan, the ichneumon plant.<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्धि fragrant, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिमूषिका
सुगन्धिमूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The musk rat or shrew.<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्धि fragrant, and मूषिका a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगम|सुगमः
सुगम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Accessible, good, (as a road.)<BR>2 Easy, practicable^1.<BR>3 Plain, intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, ready, and गम going.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगहन|सुगहनः
सुगहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Thick, close, impervious.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>An enclosure round a place of sacrifice, to exclude profane access or sight.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, much or thoroughly, गह to be thick, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगुप्त
सुगुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Secret, well hidden or kept secret.<BR>n. adv. (-प्तं)<BR>Secretly, privily.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगुप्ति
सुगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Closeness, secrecy.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and गुप्ति secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृह|सुगृहः
सुगृह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The tailor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.)<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome or good, and गृह a house or nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृहीत|सुगृहीतः
सुगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Held fast or firmly, seized, grasped.<BR>2 Taken or applied properly or auspiciously.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृहीतनामन्
सुगृहीतनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>An epithet of YUDHIṢṬHIRA, and others, whose names it is auspicious to invoke early in the morning.<BR>E.<BR>सु auspicious, and गृहीत taken, and नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्राह्य
सुग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Easily apprehensible, easy to be laid hold of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and ग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्रीव|सुग्रीवः
सुग्रीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Handsome-necked.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 One of the horses of KṚṢṆA'S car.<BR>2 A monkey king, the son of the sun, and sovereign of Kiṣkindhya, and friend and confederate of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>3 The father of the ninth Jina of the present age.<BR>4 ŚIVA.<BR>5 INDRA.<BR>6 A goose.<BR>7 A hero.<BR>8 A piece of water.<BR>9 The name of a mountain.<BR>10 A sort of weapon.<BR>11 The countenance of a friend.<BR>12 A serpent of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, and ग्रीवा a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्रीवेश|सुग्रीवेशः
सुग्रीवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सुग्रीव the monkey king, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्ल|सुग्लः
सुग्ल<BR>mfn. (-ग्लः-ग्ला-ग्लं)<BR>1 Very weary.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, ग्लै to be weary, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघटित
सुघटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well contrived or devised, well arranged or managed.<BR>2 Well joined or united.<BR>3 Brought into agreeable contact.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and घटित contrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघोर
सुघोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hideous, terrific.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, घोर fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघोष|सुघोषः
सुघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A pleasant sound.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and घोष sound or cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचक्षुस्
सुचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>1 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>2 A wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचरित
सुचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well conducted, well behaved.<BR>2 Well managed or pursued.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Good conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and चरित gone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचरित्र
सुचरित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Good or virtuous course of life.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and चरित्र custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचारु|सुचारुः
सुचारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>1 Very beautiful.<BR>2 Pleasing, delightful.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, चारु lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचारुस्वन
सुचारुस्वन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Melodious, mellifluous.<BR>E.<BR>सुचारु, and स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिचक
सुचिचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kingfisher.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, चिचक variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्तन
सुचिन्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Deliberate consideration.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and चिति to think, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्ता|सुचिंता
सुचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Due reflection or consideration.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and चिन्ता thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्तित
सुचिन्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well weighed, well considered.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, चिति to think, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिरम्
सुचिरम्<BR>ind.<BR>Very long, (a time.)<BR>E.<BR>सु much, and चिरम् long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिरायुस्
सुचिरायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A god, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, चिर a long time, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचुटी
सुचुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A pair of nippers or tongs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, चुट to cut, aff. क, and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचेलक|सुचेलकः
सुचेलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cloth or fine cloth.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, चेल cloth, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुच्छची
सुच्छची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The Satlej river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजन|सुजनः
सुजन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Virtuous, good, respectable.<BR>2 Kind, benevolent.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The charioteer of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनता
सुजनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Goodness, benevolence.<BR>2 A number of respectable persons.<BR>E.<BR>सुजन, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनत्व
सुजनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Kindness, benevolence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to सुजन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजन्मन्
सुजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Legitimate, of respectable birth.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजल|सुजलं
सुजल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having clear or sweet water.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Good water.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजाति
सुजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of a good tribe or species.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and जाति tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजीर्ण
सुजीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Well-digested.<BR>2 Decayed, worn out.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and जीर्ण digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजीवित
सुजीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lived well or to some purpose.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A lucky or happy life.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, जीवित living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुट्ट
सुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (सुट्टयति)<BR>1 To disregard, to despise.<BR>2 To be low, small, or shallow; also षुट्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत|सुतः
सुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A prince.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>षु to bear or bring forth, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतङ्गम|सुतंगम|सुतंगमः
सुतङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The father of a son.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, गम to obtain, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुज्ञात
सुज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well or easily known.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतनु|सुतनुः
सुतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-न्वी-नु)<BR>Very thin or delicate.<BR>f. (-नुः or -न्वी)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, तनु thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतपस्
सुतपस्<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>1 A hermit, an ascetic.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, profoundly, तपस् religious austerity, or तप to heat, असि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतप्त
सुतप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Hot, very hot.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=929" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतराम्
सुतराम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Better, more excellently.<BR>2 Consequently, of course.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and तराम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतर्द्दन|सुतर्दन|सुतर्दनः|सुतर्द्दनः
सुतर्द्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Coïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, तर्द्द to hurt, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतल|सुतलः
सुतल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A division of the lower regions, the sixth in descent.<BR>2 The basement or foundation of a large building (?)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and तल deep, profound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवत्|सुतवन्त्
सुतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having children.<BR>m. (-वान)<BR>1 A drinker of the Asclepias juice.<BR>2 The father of a son.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवस्करा
सुतवस्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The mother of seven children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतश्रेणी
सुतश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>सुत offspring, and श्रेणी a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतस्नेह|सुतस्नेहः
सुतस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Paternal affection.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, and स्नेह affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतात्मज|सुतात्मजः
सुतात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A grandson.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A grand-daughter.<BR>E.<BR>सुत a son, or सुता a daughter, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतारका
सुतारका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of tutelar goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतार्थिन्
सुतार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Desirous of having a son.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, and अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिक्तक|सुतिक्तकः
सुतिक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR>2 The coral tree.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, तिक्त bitter, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिन्
सुतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A father, one who has a son.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A mother, the mother of a son.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, and इनि aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीक्ष्ण|सुतीक्ष्णः
सुतीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Very sharp.<BR>2 Very pungent.<BR>3 Acutely painful.<BR>m. (-क्ष्णः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>सु exceedingly, and तीक्ष्ण sharp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतुङ्ग|सुतुंग|सुतुङ्गः
सुतुङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Very lofty or tall.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, तुङ्ग tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतेजस्
सुतेजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>1 Very bright, splendid.<BR>2 Potent.<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>One of the Jinas of the last age.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, तेजस् light or glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतोत्पत्ति|सुतोत्पत्तिः
सुतोत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Birth of a son.<BR>E.<BR>सुत, and उत्पत्ति birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्या
सुत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Religious bathing.<BR>E.<BR>षु to bear, क्यप् aff., form irr., more usually सूत्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्रामन्
सुत्रामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, चा to preserve, (the world,) मनिन् aff.; also सूत्रामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्वन्
सुत्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>A student who has performed his ablutions subsequent, or according to some, preparatory to a sacrifice.<BR>2 A drinker of the Asclepias juice.<BR>3 An offerer of the same.<BR>E.<BR>षु to bring forth, क्वनिप् aff., तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदक्षिण
सुदक्षिण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sovereign of Vidarbha.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The wife of DILĪPA.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दक्षिण clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदत्|सुदन्त्
सुदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Having handsome teeth.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, and दतृ for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदत्त
सुदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Well or properly given.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदन्त|सुदंत|सुदन्तः
सुदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An actor, a dancer.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>The female elephant of the N. W. quarter.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, handsome, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदम
सुदम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Easy to be subdued.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and दम taming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदर्शन|सुदर्शनं|सुदर्शनः
सुदर्शन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>Handsome, good looking.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The discus of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 Mount Meru.<BR>3 The rose-apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>4 The father of the eighteenth Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR>5 One of the nine Śuklabalas or BALARĀMAS of the Jainas.<BR>6 A vulture.<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>The city of INDRA.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A drug.<BR>2 Order, command.<BR>3 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>4 A woman, a handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, दर्शन sight or appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदान्त|सुदान्तः
सुदान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A follower of Śākya Muni, the teacher of the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and दान्त tamed, (whose passions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदामन्
सुदामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 INDRA'S elephant.<BR>4 The name of a cowherd.<BR>5 The sea.<BR>6 A poor Brahman raised to wealth and honours by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and दामन् a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदाय|सुदायः
सुदाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A special gift, as alms to a student at his initiation, a nuptial present, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु auspicious, and दाय a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदारु|सुदारुः
सुदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Pāriyātra mountains, part of the Vindhya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदि
सुदि<BR>ind.<BR>The light half of the lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिन|सुदिनं
सुदिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fine day, fine weather.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिनाह|सुदिनाहं
सुदिनाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A fine day.<BR>E.<BR>सुदिन fair weather, and अह for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिव
सुदिव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Happy daily, passing pleasant days.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and दिव a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदीर्घ|सुदीर्घः
सुदीर्घ<BR>mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं)<BR>Very long, (in space or time.)<BR>E.<BR>सु very, and दीर्घ long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदीर्घघर्म्मा|सुदीर्घघर्मा
सुदीर्घघर्म्मा<BR>f. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A plant, (Marsilia quadrifolia).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुराचार
सुदुराचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very wicked, abandoned, a profligate.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुराचार bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुरारुह
सुदुरारुह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Inaccessible.<BR>E.<BR>सु and दुर with आङ before रुह to mount, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्जय
सुदुर्जय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Difficult to be overcome.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुर्जय difficult to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्द्दर्श|सुदुर्दर्श
सुदुर्द्दर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Difficult to be beheld.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुर्द्दर्श difficult to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्लभ|सुदुर्ल्लभः
सुदुर्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Difficult to be attained, unattainable, impracticable.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुर्लभ difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुश्चर|सुदुश्चरः
सुदुश्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Very arduous or painful, difficult to be performed or attained.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुश्चर arduous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुष्कर|सुदुष्करः
सुदुष्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Very difficult.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुष्कर difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्तर|सुदुस्तरः
सुदुस्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Impassable, difficult to be passed or crossed.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुर् difficult, तॄ to cross, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्सह
सुदुस्सह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Very difficult to be endured.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, दुस्सह unendurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदूर
सुदूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very distant.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, and दूर remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदृश्
सुदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Having handsome eyes.<BR>f. (-दृक्)<BR>A pretty woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, and दृश् sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदृढ|सुदृढं
सुदृढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Solid, firm.<BR>n. adv. (-ढं)<BR>Very hard or firm.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, and दृढ hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन्वन्
सुधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>1 An archer, a bowman.<BR>2 VIŚVAKARMA, the artist of the gods.<BR>3 A prince so named.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and धनुम् a bow, अनङ् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधर्म्म|सुधर्म|सुधर्म्मः
सुधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>One of the principal disciples of Mahāvīra, the last Jina of the present age; he survived his master, and the different ascetics or candidates for holiness are traced from him in regular succession; none of the other ten disciples of Mahāvīra having left successors.<BR>f. (-र्म्मी)<BR>A council of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=930" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधर्म्मन्|सुधर्मन्
सुधर्म्मन्<BR>mf. (-र्म्मा)<BR>The council or assembly of the gods.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A man attentive to the proper maintenance of his family.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, धर्म्म virtue, अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधा
सुधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 Nectar, the beverage of immortality and sustenance of the gods.<BR>2 The nectar or honey of flowers.<BR>3 Juice.<BR>4 Plaster, mortar.<BR>5 A brick.<BR>6 The Ganges.<BR>7 Water.<BR>8 Lightning.<BR>9 The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum, &c.)<BR>10 A plant, (Aletris Hyacinthoides.)<BR>11 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>12 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>सु pleasure, धे to drink, or धा to have, to support, (life,) अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशु|सुधांशुः
सुधांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and अंशु a ray of light, the moon being the supposed repository of the beverage of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशुतैल|सुधांशुतैलं
सुधांशुतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Camphorated oil.<BR>E.<BR>सुधांशु Camphor, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशुरत्न|सुधांशुरत्नं
सुधांशुरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>सुधांशु the moon, and रत्न a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाकर|सुधाकरः
सुधाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाङ्ग|सुधाङ्गः
सुधाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाजीविन्
सुधाजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा plaster, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधवलित
सुधाधवलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White-washed, stuccoed, plastered.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा, and धवलित whitened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधार|सुधाधारः
सुधाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and आधार a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधानिधि|सुधानिधिः
सुधानिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and निधि a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधापाणि|सुधापाणिः
सुधापाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The divine physician, DHANVANTARI.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, पाणि hand, bearing in his hands the beverage of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभवन
सुधाभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A stuccoed house.<BR>2 The fifth Muhūrta or hour after noon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा, and भवन mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभुज्
सुधाभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A deity, an immortal.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, भुज to enjoy, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभृति|सुधाभृतिः
सुधाभृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and भृति cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामय|सुधामयः
सुधामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Made of plaster, &c.<BR>2 Consisting of nectar.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A palace, a mansion, a brick or stone building.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा mortar or a brick, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्ष|सुधावर्षः
सुधावर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A shower of ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्षिन्
सुधावर्षिन्<BR>m. (-र्षी)<BR>1 A Buddha or deified sage of the Bauddha religion.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and वर्षिन् raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावृष्टि
सुधावृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A shower of ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाश्रवा
सुधाश्रवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The uvula or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar or water, श्रु to distil, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधासूति|सुधासूतिः
सुधासूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, सूति birth, production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्यन्द
सुधास्यन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी-न्दं)<BR>Shedding ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा, and स्यन्द what sheds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहर|सुधाहरः
सुधाहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and हर who steals; having on one occasion stolen the moon for the sake of the Amṛta which was to be communicated to the serpent children of KADRU, in consideration of which his mother VINATĀ was to be released from a state of servitude to KADRU, the wife, as well as herself, of the sage KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहृत्
सुधाहृत्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and हृत् taking, stealing; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधिति|सुधितिः
सुधिति<BR>mf. (-तिः-तिः)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, धि to hold, क्तिन् aff.; more correctly स्वधितिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधी
सुधी<BR>m. (-धीः)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a learned man or teacher.<BR>2 An intelligent person.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, ध्यै to think, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधोद्भव|सुधोद्भवः
सुधोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>DHANVANTARI, the physician of Svarga.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Chebulic myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>E.<BR>सुधा nectar, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनन्द|सुनन्दं|सुनन्दः
सुनन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Pleasing, delighting.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The club of BALARĀMA.<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>1 The goddess UMĀ.<BR>2 A sort of pigment and drug: see गोरोचना.<BR>3 A woman.<BR>4 One of UMĀ'S female companions.<BR>5 A plant, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, thoroughly, नदि to please, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनय|सुनयः
सुनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Policy.<BR>2 Good conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and णी to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनयन|सुनयनः
सुनयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deer.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाकुत
सुनाकुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाभ|सुनाभः
सुनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A mountain; part of the ranges of southern India, personified as the son of Himālaya, and Menā.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनार|सुनारः
सुनार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The udder of a bitch.<BR>2 The egg of a snake.<BR>3 A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनालक|सुनालकः
सुनालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनासीर|सुनासीरः
सुनासीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, नासीर the van of an army, the leader of the celestial hosts; also शुनासीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिग्रह
सुनिग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Easily restrained.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and निग्रह confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिद्रा
सुनिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Sound sleep.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिभृत
सुनिभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very lonely or private.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and निभृत lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिभृतम्
सुनिभृतम्<BR>ind.<BR>Privately, very secretly.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and निभृतम् privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिरूपित
सुनिरूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well observed or inspected.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and निरूपित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिश्चित|सुनिश्चितः
सुनिश्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ascertained, determined.<BR>2 Commended, approved.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A deified sage, according to the Jainas or Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, thoroughly, and निश्चित ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिषण्णक|सुनिषण्णकं|सुनिषण्णकः
सुनिषण्णक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A potherb, (Marsilia quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, निषण्ण depression of spirits or drowsiness, कन् aff.; also without the final, सुनिषण्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिष्टप्त|सुनिष्टप्तः
सुनिष्टप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Burnished.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, thoroughly, and निष्टप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीत
सुनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well behaved.<BR>2 Politic.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Good conduct.<BR>2 Policy.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, णी to guide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीति|सुनीतिः
सुनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Propriety of behaviour, good manners.<BR>2 The mother of DHRUVA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and नीति morals or manners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीथ|सुनीथः
सुनीथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Virtuous, moral, good, of proper disposition or conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, नी to obtain, aff. थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=931" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनील|सुनीलं|सुनीलः
सुनील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very black or blue, dark.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The pomegranate tree.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, नील blue or black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीलक|सुनीलकः
सुनीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The blue shrike.<BR>2 The emerald or sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, नील blue or black, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दर|सुंदर|सुन्दरं|सुन्दरः
सुन्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A handsome woman.<BR>2 A small timber tree, (Heritiera minor.)<BR>3 Turmeric.<BR>4 A species of metre.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, दृ to respect, aff. अप्; or सु, with उन्दि to moisten, aff. अरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्वत्|सुन्वन्त्
सुन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वती-न्वत्)<BR>Sacrificing, offering sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>षुञ् to sacrifice, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपक्व|सुपक्वः
सुपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Ripe, mature.<BR>m. (-क्वः)<BR>A sort of mango.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, thoroughly, and पक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपच
सुपच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and पच leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपथ|सुपथः
सुपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A good road.<BR>2 Good conduct.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, पथिन् a road, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपथिन्
सुपथिन्<BR>m. (-न्थाः)<BR>1 A good road.<BR>2 A country, &c. having good roads.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपद्मा
सुपद्मा<BR>f. (-द्मा)<BR>Orris root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपरीक्षण
सुपरीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Examining or trying well or thoroughly.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and परीक्षण trying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपरीक्षित
सुपरीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well examined or tried.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and परीक्षित tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्ण|सुपर्णः
सुपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>3 A cock.<BR>4 A being of a superhuman character, or GARUḌA, and other birds of an equally fanciful description; one of those classes first created by the BRAHMĀDIKAS, and included in the daily presentation of water to deceased ancestors, &c.<BR>f. (-र्णा or र्णी)<BR>1 The mother of GARUḌA.<BR>2 A number of lotuses, or a pool abounding with them.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, and पर्ण a leaf or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णक|सुपर्णकः
सुपर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>2 A small tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>3 A bird of superhuman character: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, पर्ण a wing, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णकेतु|सुपर्णकेतुः
सुपर्णकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सुपर्ण GARUḌA, and केतु symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णाख्य
सुपर्णाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>सुपर्ण Cassia, and आख्य appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णीतनय|सुपर्णीतनयः
सुपर्णीतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सुपर्णी a name of VINATĀ, and तनय a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्व्वन्|सुपर्वन्
सुपर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 A god, a deity.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A bambu.<BR>4 A lunar day, in which religious ceremonies are particularly performed, as the new moon, and the eighth and the fourteenth days of each fortnight.<BR>5 Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>सु good or much, and पर्व्वन् a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्य्याप्त|सुपर्याप्त
सुपर्य्याप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Extensive, vast.<BR>2 Comprehensive.<BR>3 Well laid out, (as a palace with all sorts of buildings.)<BR>E.<BR>सु, and पर्य्याप्त complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपलायित
सुपलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Completely fled or run away.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A total rout or retreat.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and पलायित fled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपात्र|सुपात्रं
सुपात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 An able or clever man.<BR>2 A vessel of earthen ware, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपाद्
सुपाद्<BR>mfn. (-पात् or पाद्)<BR>Having a handsome foot.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and पाद् for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपान|सुपानः
सुपान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Drinking well, easily, or deeply.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, षा to drink, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपार्श्व|सुपार्श्वः
सुपार्श्व<BR>m. (-र्श्वः)<BR>The seventh Jina or Jaina deified teacher of the present era.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, पार्श्व side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपार्श्वक|सुपार्श्वकः
सुपार्श्वक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The third Jina of the future era.<BR>2 The veined leaf^1 fig, (Ficus venosa.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, पार्श्व a side, कन् added.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपीडन
सुपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rubbing and kneading the hands and feet.<BR>E.<BR>सु pleasantly or intensely, पीड to pain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुत्त्र
सुपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>An excellent son.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुष्प|सुपुष्पं|सुपुष्पः
सुपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 The coral tree.<BR>2 The Śirīṣa tree, (Mimosa Sirisha.)<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>1 The plantain.<BR>2 A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa and panmorium.)<BR>3 A flower, (Clitoria ternatea, the white sort.)<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूर|सुपूरः
सुपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and पूर what is full, (of seeds.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूरक|सुपूरकः
सुपूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्त|सुप्तं|सुप्तः
सुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Sleeping, asleep.<BR>2 Senseless, numbed.<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>Sleep, deep or sound sleep.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, क्त aff., and the semivowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तघातक|सुप्तघातकः
सुप्तघातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mischievous, murderous.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त asleep, and घातक killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तजन|सुप्तजनः
सुप्तजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त asleep, and जन mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तज्ञान|सुप्तज्ञानं
सुप्तज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dreaming, a dream.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त asleep, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तत्वच्
सुप्तत्वच्<BR>mfn. (-त्वक्)<BR>Benumbed, paralytic.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त, and त्वच the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तविज्ञान|सुप्तविज्ञानं
सुप्तविज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A dream, dreaming.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त sleeping, and विज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्ति|सुप्तिः
सुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Sleep, sleeping.<BR>2 Numbness, insensibility, paralysis.<BR>3 Drowsiness, sleepiness.<BR>4 Trust, confidence.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रकाश
सुप्रकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Manifest, apparent.<BR>2 Public.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, प्रकाश apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिभा
सुप्रतिभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्ठा
सुप्रतिष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 Consecration, erection, (as of a temple or idol.)<BR>2 Fame.<BR>3 A form of metre, a stanza of four lines, containing five syllables each.<BR>E.<BR>सु and प्रति intensitives, ष्ठा to stay or be, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्ठित|सुप्रतिष्ठितः
सुप्रतिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Consecrated.<BR>2 Celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and प्रतिष्ठा to consecrate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्णात
सुप्रतिष्णात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Certain, ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>सु and प्रति before ष्णा to bathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतीक|सुप्रतीकः
सुप्रतीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Well-made, handsome.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The elephant of the north-east quarter.<BR>2 KĀMADEVA.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, प्रतीक form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभ|सुप्रभः
सुप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Splendid, brilliant, glorious.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>One of the nine Śuklabalas or BALARĀMAS of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent or excessive, and प्रभा light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभात|सुप्रभातं
सुप्रभात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Enlightened.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and प्रभात shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयुक्त|सुप्रयुक्तः
सुप्रयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Joined, attached, closely connected or in contact.<BR>2 Well managed, as an instrument or weapon.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and प्रयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=932" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयोग|सुप्रयोगः
सुप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Dexterity, expertness.<BR>2 Contact, approximation.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, प्रयोग junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयोगविशिख|सुप्रयोगविशिखः
सुप्रयोगविशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A good archer.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, प्रयोग possessing, managing, and विशिख an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलम्भ|सुप्रलम्भः
सुप्रलम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>Easy of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, प्र before लभ to get, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलाप|सुप्रलापः
सुप्रलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Eloquence, elegant discourse, speaking or discoursing well.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and प्रलाष speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रसन्न|सुप्रसन्नः
सुप्रसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Well-pleased, favouring, favourable.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and प्रसन्न pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रसाद|सुप्रसादः
सुप्रसाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Kind, complacent, auspicious.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, good, and प्रसाद favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रात
सुप्रात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dawning finely, (as the day.)<BR>E.<BR>सु, प्रातर dawn, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रिय|सुप्रियः
सुप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Agreeable, pleasant, liked, loved.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>(In prosody,) A foot of two short syllables, a Pyrrhic.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुफल|सुफलः
सुफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bearing good fruit, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The wood apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>2 The pomegranate.<BR>3 Jujube.<BR>4 A sort of bean, (Phaseolus Mungo.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Colocynth.<BR>2 A pumpkin gourd.<BR>3 The plantain.<BR>4 The brown grape.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुफेन|सुफेनः
सुफेन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, फेन froth or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबन्ध|सुबंध|सुबन्धः
सुबन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Well-secured, having a good binding.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबुद्धि
सुबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Wise, clever, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and बुद्धि intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबोध|सुबोधः
सुबोध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Easily taught.<BR>2 Of easy apprehension.<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>2 Waking.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and बोध making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुब्रह्मण्य|सुब्रह्मण्यः
सुब्रह्मण्य<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and ब्रह्मण्य the Brahmanical order, of whom he is the special guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभग|सुभगः
सुभग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Pleasing to the eye, grateful to the sight.<BR>2 Beloved, liked.<BR>3 Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Borax.<BR>2 The Asoca tree.<BR>3 The Champac, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>1 A woman beloved by her husband, a favourite wife.<BR>2 A respectable and auspicious mother.<BR>3 A wild variety of Arabian jasmine.<BR>4 Turmeric.<BR>5 Holy basil.<BR>6 A shrub, (Hedysarum Gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and भग fortune, beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभगम्भावुक|सुभगंभावुक
सुभगम्भावुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Become pleasant or agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>सुभग, भू to be, खुकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभगासुत|सुभगासुतः
सुभगासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The son of an auspicious mother.<BR>E.<BR>सुभगा as above, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभङ्ग|सुभंग|सुभङ्गः
सुभङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Separating or dividing easily.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभट|सुभटः
सुभट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A champion, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and भट a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्र|सुभद्रः
सुभद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious, fortunate.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 The sister of JAGANNĀTHA, whose image is worshipped with those of that deity, and his brother BALARĀMA, and carried in procession with them in the Raṭh Yātra, or annual movement of the car of JAGANNĀTHA; she is the wife of ARJUNA.<BR>2 A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>3 A plant, commonly Ghṛtamaṇḍā.<BR>E.<BR>सु exceedingly, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्रक|सुभद्रकः
सुभद्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A car of the gods.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्राणी
सुभद्राणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant and drug, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्रेश|सुभद्रेशः
सुभद्रेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>सुभद्रा the sister of JAGANNĀTHA, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभर
सुभर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Heavily burthened.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and भर bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाञ्जन|सुभाञ्जनः
सुभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>a various reading of शुभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाषित|सुभाषितः
सुभाषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spoken well or eloquently.<BR>2 Wellspoken, speaking or discoursing well.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Eloquence.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A deified sage, according to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, excellent, भाषा speech, इतच् aff., or भाष to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभिक्षा
सुभिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, भिक्ष to beg, or obtain by begging, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभीरक|सुभीरकः
सुभीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभूम|सुभूमः
सुभूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A name of KĀRTAVĪRYA, as the eighth Cakravartī, or universal emperor, according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, भूमि land, domain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृत
सुभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished, protected.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृश|सुभृशं
सुभृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Much, exceeding.<BR>n. adv. (-शं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>सु insensitive prefix, and भृश much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभोगीन
सुभोगीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Desirable, fit to be enjoyed.<BR>E.<BR>सु, भोग enjoyment, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभैरव
सुभैरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Very fearful, terrific.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and भैरव the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभ्रु|सुभ्रुः
सुभ्रु<BR>f. (-भ्रुः or भ्रूः)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, and भ्रु or भ्रू an eyebrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम|सुमं|सुमः
सुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A flower.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, मा the goddess LAKṢMI; prized by her, &c.: see कुसुम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमङ्गल
सुमङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very fortunate or auspicious.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, commonly Ghṛtamaṇḍā.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमत|सुमतः
सुमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Friendly, well or kindly disposed.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, मन to mind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमति|सुमतिः
सुमति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The fifth Jina or Jaina teacher of the present era.<BR>2 One of the Jainas of the past era.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Friendship, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and मति intelligence or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमद
सुमद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Very drunk, mad, or empassioned.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and मद madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमदात्मजा
सुमदात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>An Apsaras or courtesan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, मद intoxication, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमधुर|सुमधुरं
सुमधुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Pleasant, gentle, soothing, (speech or discourse.)<BR>2 Sweet, saccharine.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, and मधुर sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमध्यमा
सुमध्यमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A woman with a handsome waist.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and मध्यम middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन|सुमनः
सुमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Wheat.<BR>2 The thorn-apple, (Datura metel,)<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Great-flowered jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, मन to think, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनःफल|सुमनःफलं|सुमनःफलः
सुमनःफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस् a flower, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनस्
सुमनस्<BR>m. (-नाः)<BR>1 A god, an immortal.<BR>2 A Paṇḍita, a learned man or teacher.<BR>3 A student of the Vedas, and supplementary [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">Page934</a>] sciences.<BR>4 A plant, (Cæsalpinia Bonducella.)<BR>5 Wheat.<BR>6 The Nimb tree.<BR>mn. (-नाः-नः) or fem. but then always plur. even in the singular acceptation. (-सः)<BR>A flower in general.<BR>f. sing. (-नाः)<BR>Great-flowered jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, excellent, मन to think, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=933" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोभर
सुमनोभर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Ornamented with or having flowers.<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस्, and भर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोरजस्
सुमनोरजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>The pollen of a flower.<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस् a flower, and रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोहर
सुमनोहर<BR>mn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very agreeable, pleasing, beautiful, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and मनोहर grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्त्रित
सुमन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well or wisely counselled, well-advised.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Wise counsel.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and मन्त्रित advised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्तु|सुमन्तुः
सुमन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A saint and legislator so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहत्|सुमहन्त्
सुमहत्<BR>mfn. (-हान्-हती-हत्)<BR>Very large or abundant.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and महत् great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्र|सुमित्रः
सुमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The father of the twentieth Jina of the present era.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, and the mother of LAKṢMAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्रभू
सुमित्रभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 SAGARA, as one of the Cakravartīs or emperors of the Jainas.<BR>2 The twentieth Jina of the present period.<BR>E.<BR>सुमित्र a proper name, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्राभू
सुमित्राभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>LAKṢMAṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमुख|सुमुखं|सुमुखः
सुमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा or खी-खं)<BR>1 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>2 Lovely, handsome-faced.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 The son of GARUḌA.<BR>2 One of the serpents of Pātāla.<BR>3 A kind of potherb.<BR>4 A Paṇḍita, a learned man or teacher.<BR>5 GAṆEŚA.<BR>6 GARUḌA.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The mark or scratch of a finger nail.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A species of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR>f. (-खा or -खी)<BR>1 A handsome woman.<BR>2 A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, मुख countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमुखसू
सुमुखसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सुमुख his son, and सू producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमू
सुमू<BR>mfn. (-मूः-मूः-मु)<BR>Who or what binds well.<BR>E.<BR>सु, मू to bind, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमेधस्
सुमेधस्<BR>mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः)<BR>Sensible, intelligent, of good capacity or understanding.<BR>f. (-धाः)<BR>Heart pea.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, मेघस् apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमेरु|सुमेरुः
सुमेरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Best, excellent.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The sacred mountain Meru: see मेरु.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, मि to shed or scatter, (radiance,) रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्नयु|सुम्नयुः
सुम्नयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A chanter of hymns.<BR>E.<BR>सुम्न a particular hymn, used as a verb, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्पलुण्ठ|सुम्पलुण्ठः
सुम्पलुण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma Zerumbet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्भ|सुम्भः
सुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A country so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयन्त्रित
सुयन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-governed or regulated.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and यन्त्रित restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयामुन|सुयामुनः
सुयामुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A prince, sovereign of Kauśāmbī; also named VATSA.<BR>3 A palace.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, यमुना the river, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयुद्ध
सुयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>A well fought war or battle.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयोधन|सुयोधनः
सुयोधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of DURYODHANA, the chief of the Kuru family and confederates.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, or with pleasure, युध to combat, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर|सुरः
सुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (सुरति)<BR>1 To possess supreme or superhuman power.<BR>2 To shine; also षुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर|सुरः
सुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A god, a deity.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A sage, a learned man.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor in general personified: also as a nymph, produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR>2 A drinking vessel.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>षु to possess power, Uṇādi aff. रक्, or षुर to be radiant, क affix, or सुरा wine (whose, that falling to the share of the gods,) or सु excellent, राज to shine, aff. ड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्त|सुरक्तः
सुरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Deeply or well coloured or dyed.<BR>2 Deep red, crimson.<BR>3 Strongly affected or impassioned.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रञ्ज to dye, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्तक|सुरक्तकः
सुरक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A variety of red chalk, that called golden.<BR>2 A fruit tree, apparently a sort of mango, bearing a small red fruit.<BR>E.<BR>सुरक्त very red, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्षण
सुरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking good care of, protecting, preserving.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्षित
सुरक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-preserved or protected.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रक्षित preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरगण|सुरगणः
सुरगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A class or company of divinities.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरगुरु|सुरगुरुः
सुरगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, regent of Jupiter and preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and गुरु spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरग्रामणी
सुरग्रामणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>INDRA, the ruler of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and ग्रामणी leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्ग|सुरंग|सुरङ्गं|सुरंगः|सुरङ्गः
सुरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The orange.<BR>2 Bright or good colour or dye.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Red sanders.<BR>2 Vermilion.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A hole cut in a wall to break into a house, &c.; see सुरुङ्गा.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>3 Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and रङ्ग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गद|सुरङ्गदं
सुरङ्गद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Red sanders.<BR>E.<BR>सुरङ्ग good colour, and द what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गधातु|सुरंगधातु|सुरङ्गधातुः
सुरङ्गधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>सुरङ्ग good or much colour, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गयुज्
सुरङ्गयुज्<BR>m. (-युक्)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>सुरङ्ग a hole in a wall, and युज् who joins or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरजःफल|सुरजःफलः
सुरजःफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The jack-fruit tree.<BR>E.<BR>सुरजस् abundant farina, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरजनी
सुरजनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रजनी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरज्येष्ठ|सुरज्येष्ठः
सुरज्येष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and ज्येष्ठ elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरञ्जन|सुरंजन|सुरञ्जनः
सुरञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and रञ्जन pleasing, affecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरत|सुरतं
सुरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compassionate, tender.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Copulation, coition.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Godhead, divinity.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रम to sport or play, aff. क्त, or सुर a deity, and तल् aff. of state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतताली
सुरतताली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A female messenger, a go-between.<BR>2 A chaplet, a garland for the head.<BR>E.<BR>सुरत coition, and ताल tune, &c., aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतोषक|सुरतोषकः
सुरतोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The jewel worn by KṚṢṆA on his breast.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, तुष to please, खुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरदारु
सुरदारु<BR>n. (-रु)<BR>A sort of Pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>मुर a deity, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरदीर्घिका
सुरदीर्घिका^1<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and दीर्घिका a pond or pool.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20230605. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/1229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्विप|सुरद्विपः
सुरद्विप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An elephant of the gods, either that of INDRA or of either of the other rulers of the different quarters.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and द्विप an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=934" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्विष्
सुरद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>An Asura, an infernal being, the natural enemy of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and द्विष् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्रुम|सुरद्रुमः
सुरद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The Deodar Pine.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरधनुस्
सुरधनुस्<BR>n. (-नुः)<BR>The rain-bow.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and धनुस् a bow; the bow of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरधूप|सुरधूपः
सुरधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Resin, turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरनदी
सुरनदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरनिम्नगा
सुरनिम्नगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and निम्नगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरन्दला
सुरन्दला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A river so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपति|सुरपतिः
सुरपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>INDRA, ruler of Svarga, and sovereign of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपथ|सुरपथं
सुरपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपर्ण|सुरपर्णं
सुरपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A drug, probably a leaf, commonly called Machi perṇi, and described as pungent and bitter, anthelmintic, stomachic, and a remover of phlegm and catarrh.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपर्णिका
सुरपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपुरी
सुरपुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The capital of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and पुरी a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरप्रिय|सुरप्रियः
सुरप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>3 The Elœocarpus.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and प्रिय beloved by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभि|सुरभिः
सुरभि<BR>mfn. (-भिः-भिः or भी-भि)<BR>1 Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>2 Pleasing, beloved.<BR>3 Friendly, a friend.<BR>4 Celebrated, famous.<BR>5 Wise, learned.<BR>6 Handsome.<BR>7 Good, virtuous.<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>1 A fragrance, a perfume, a sweet-smelling substance.<BR>2 The Michelia Champaca.<BR>3 Nutmeg.<BR>4 Spring.<BR>5 The month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>6 Resin.<BR>f. (-भिः or भी)<BR>1 The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>2 Murā, a sort of drug and perfume.<BR>3 One of the divine Mātṛs.<BR>4 A cow.<BR>5 A fabulous cow, the cow of plenty, granting every wish.<BR>6 Spirituous liquor.<BR>7 The earth.<BR>8 A holy basil.<BR>9 Jasmine, of several sorts.<BR>n. (-भि)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, excellently, रभ to begin, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिगन्धि|सुरभिगन्धिः
सुरभिगन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, गन्ध smell, इ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभित
सुरभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perfumed, rendered fragrant.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभित्वच्
सुरभित्वच्<BR>n. (-त्वक्)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, त्वच् bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिवल्कल|सुरभिवल्कलं
सुरभिवल्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The Laurus Cassia, or its bark.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिवाण
सुरभिवाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि a fragrance, a flower, and वाण an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिस्रवा
सुरभिस्रवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The gum Olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि a fragrance, and स्रव what distils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभीपचा
सुरभीपचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>The rose-apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>E.<BR>सुरभी fragrant, and पचा leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभीरसा
सुरभीरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>सुरभी fragrant, रस juice, टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभूय
सुरभूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The condition of a deity, deification, apotheosis.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and भूय becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरर्षि|सुरर्षिः
सुरर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi, or sage of divine order, as NĀRADA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरला
सुरला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 Another river so named.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and ला to get or have, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरलोक|सुरलोकः
सुरलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Svarga, the heaven of INDRA, and residence of the celestials.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरवर्त्मन्
सुरवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>Heaven, sky, ether, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a divinity, and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरविद्विष्
सुरविद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>An Asura, a titan.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and विद्विष् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरवैरिन्
सुरवैरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An Asura, an infernal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a city, and वैरिन् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरशत्रु|सुरशत्रुः
सुरशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>An Asura, an infernal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरस|सुरसं|सुरसः
सुरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Sweet.<BR>2 Well-flavoured, sapid, juicy.<BR>3 Elegant, (as a composition.)<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Vitex trifolia.)<BR>nf. (-सं-सा)<BR>Holy basil.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 The mother of the Nāgas.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Rasan, a kind of Ophiorrhiza, (Ophiorrhiza mangos.)<BR>3 A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>4 The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>5 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>6 A species of the Atidhṛti metre.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Gum myrrh.<BR>2 Cassia bark.<BR>3 Fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, रस juice or flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसङ्घ|सुरसंघ
सुरसङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>A company, a number of gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and सङ्घ a troop, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसद्मन्
सुरसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसमिति
सुरसमिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An assemblage of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and समिति assembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसरित्
सुरसरित्<BR>f. (-रित्)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and सरित् a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसाष्ट|सुरसाष्टः
सुरसाष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A class of eight plants, the Vitex trifolia, acid Asclepias, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सुरसा a juicy plant, and अष्ट eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसिन्धु|सुरसिंधु|सुरसिन्धुः
सुरसिन्धु<BR>f. (-न्धुः)<BR>The river Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसुन्दरी|सुरसुंदरी
सुरसुन्दरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 An Apsaras or courtesan of heaven.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and सुन्दरी a beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराकर|सुराकरः
सुराकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा vinous spirit or Toddy, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराङ्गना|सुरांगना
सुराङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>An Apsaras or courtesan of heaven, a nymph, a sylph, a fairy.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and अङ्गना a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराचार्य्य|सुराचार्य|सुराचार्यः|सुराचार्य्यः
सुराचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and आचार्य्य a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजक|सुराजकः
सुराजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Eclipta prostrata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजा
सुराजा<BR>m. (-जा)<BR>A divinity.<BR>E.<BR>सु particle of eminence, राज to shine, aff. टाप् and अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजीव|सुराजीवः
सुराजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and आजीव livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजीविन्
सुराजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा spirits, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरात्रि
सुरात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः)<BR>A fine night.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराधिप|सुराधिपः
सुराधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सुर, and अधिप chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराध्वज|सुराध्वजः
सुराध्वज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A tavern flag or sign.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and ध्वज a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराप|सुरापः
सुराप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Drinking spirits.<BR>(-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Wise.<BR>2 Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>3 Preserving spirits.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा vinous liquor, or सुर a deity, पा to drink or cherish, with or without the prefix आङ्, and ठक् or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापगा
सुरापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and अपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=935" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापाण|सुरापाणं
सुरापाण<BR>m. plu. (-णाः)<BR>The inhabitants of eastern India.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा vinous liquor, and पान drinking; the final changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापान|सुरापानं
सुरापान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Drinking spirituous liquors.<BR>2 Eating any thing to excite thirst and promote drinking.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा spirits, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापिन्
सुरापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>Drinking wine.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and पा to drink, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापीत
सुरापीत<BR>mf. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drinking wine.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा and पीत drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराभाग|सुराभागः
सुराभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Yeast, barm.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा spirits, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराभाजन
सुराभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A wine cup.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरामण्ड|सुरामंड|सुरामण्डः
सुरामण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The upper part or froth of vinous liquor during fermentation, yeast, barm.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा wine, and मण्ड scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरारि|सुरारिः
सुरारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 An Asura, an infernal being opposed to the gods.<BR>2 A sprite, a goblin, a Piśāca or Yakṣa.<BR>3 The chirp of the cricket.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्च्चन|सुरार्चन
सुरार्च्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worshipping.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and अर्च्चन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्ह|सुरार्हं
सुरार्ह<BR>n. (-र्हं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a god, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरालय|सुरालयः
सुरालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The sacred mountain Meru, the extremity of the world's axis, and residence of the gods.<BR>2 Svarga or paradise.<BR>3 A tavern.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, or सुरा spirituous liquor, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराष्ट्र|सुराष्ट्रः
सुराष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A country on the western side of India, Surat.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and राष्ट्र district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराष्ट्रज|सुराष्ट्रजं|सुराष्ट्रजः
सुराष्ट्रज<BR>nf. (-जं-जा)<BR>A fragrant earth.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A sort of bean, a black variety of the Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>2 A kind of poison.<BR>E.<BR>सुराष्ट्र Surat, and ज born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरासव|सुरासवः
सुरासव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Spirituous liquor, the produce of rapid distillation.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा, and आसव spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराह्व|सुराह्वः
सुराह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>A kind of Pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and आह्व appellation; being generally called the tree or timber of the gods, or देवद्रु, देवदारु; also सुराह्वय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुङ्ग|सुरुङ्गः
सुरुङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A hole made under ground, or through the walls of a building, for military or felonious purposes; a mine, a breach, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रञ्ज to be intent on, aff. अच्, and उ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुङ्गाहि|सुरुङ्गाहिः
सुरुङ्गाहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>सुरुङ्गा a hole in the wall, and अहि a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुज
सुरुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Sick, unwell.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, रुज sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूढ
सुरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Prominent, standing well up or out.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and रूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूप|सुरूपं|सुरूपः
सुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा or -पी-पं)<BR>1 Handsome, well-formed.<BR>2 Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूहक|सुरूहकः
सुरूहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse of the colour of an ass.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रूह to mount, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेज्य|सुरेज्यः
सुरेज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, teacher of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and इज्य a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्र|सुरेन्द्रः
सुरेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्रजित्
सुरेन्द्रजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सुरेन्द्र INDRA, and जित् victor; having beaten off that deity, when pursued by him to recover the nectar which GARUḌA had stolen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्रलोक
सुरेन्द्रलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The heaven of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सुरेन्द्र, and लोक a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेभ|सुरेभं|सुरेभः
सुरेभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रेभ to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेवट|सुरेवटः
सुरेवट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of betel-nut tree, (Areca gracilis or triandra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेश्वर|सुरेश्वरः
सुरेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA, or a personification of him, especially as one of the eleven Rudras.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेष्ट|सुरेष्टः
सुरेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>2 The Śāl tree.<BR>3 A kind of Punnag or Rottleria.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरै
सुरै<BR>mf. (-राः)<BR>An opulent person.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, रै wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोत्तम|सुरोत्तमः
सुरोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोत्तर|सुरोत्तरः
सुरोत्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, and उत्तर excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोद|सुरोदः
सुरोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>सुरा wine, and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षण
सुलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ascertaining, determining.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>One of DURGĀ'S female companions.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षित
सुलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-determined or ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलभ|सुलभः
सुलभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Easy, feasible, attainable, of easy acquisition or attainment, not difficult to be obtained or effected.<BR>E.<BR>सु ready, and लभ acquiring; opposed to दुर्लभ or difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुललित
सुललित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sporting gracefully.<BR>2 Pleased, happy.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>Delightedly, easily.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and ललित sported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोचन|सुलोचनः
सुलोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fine-eyed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A deer.<BR>2 DURYODHANA.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोहक|सुलोहकं
सुलोहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, लोह iron, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोहित
सुलोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or हिणी-तं)<BR>Very red.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>One of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, लोहित red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचन|सुवचनं
सुवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eloquence, speaking well or elegantly.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचस्
सुवचस्<BR>mfn. (-चाः-चाः-चः)<BR>Speaking much, and eloquently or well.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवन|सुवनः
सुवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>षु to produce, Uṇādi aff. क्युन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्च्चक|सुवर्चक|सुवर्चकः|सुवर्च्चकः
सुवर्च्चक<BR>mf. (-र्च्चका-र्च्चिका)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, वर्च्च to shine, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्च्चला|सुवर्चला
सुवर्च्चला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A wife of the sun.<BR>2 Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A country so named.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, वर्च्च to shine, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्ण|सुवर्णं|सुवर्णः|सुवर्ण्ण
सुवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Of a good tribe or caste.<BR>2 Brilliant, bright.<BR>3 Of a good colour.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A sort of Sandal wood.<BR>3 A kind of red chalk or ochre.<BR>4 Wealth, property.<BR>5 A flower, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>mn. (-र्णः-र्णं)<BR>A weight of gold, equal to sixteen Māṣas, which at five Rattis to each Māṣa makes the Suvarṇa equal to about 175 grains Troy.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>2 A sort of sacrifice.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>1 Aloe wood, the black kind.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>3 A bitter gourd, (Colocynth.)<BR>4 Sida, (Cordifolia, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, वर्ण tribe or colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णक|सुवर्णकं|सुवर्णकः
सुवर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=936" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकदली
सुवर्णकदली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of plantain bearing a bright yellow fruit.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and कदली the plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकर्त्तृ|सुवर्णकर्तृ
सुवर्णकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण, and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकार|सुवर्णकारः
सुवर्णकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and कार a workman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकृत्
सुवर्णकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णगणित
सुवर्णगणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>(In arithmetic,) Allegation medial.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण, and गणित calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णगैरिक|सुवर्णगैरिकं
सुवर्णगैरिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A variety of red chalk, a sort of ochre.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and गैरिक red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णचौर
सुवर्णचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A stealer of gold.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and चौर theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णयूथी
सुवर्णयूथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णवत्|सुवर्णवन्त्
सुवर्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Golden, having or being of gold.<BR>2 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>ind. (-वत्)<BR>Like gold.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णवर्णा
सुवर्णवर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णविन्दु
सुवर्णविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण, gold, and विन्दु a dot or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णस्तेय
सुवर्णस्तेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Stealing gold.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण, and स्तेय theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णाख्य|सुवर्णाख्यः
सुवर्णाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A flower, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, and आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवल्लि|सुवल्लिः
सुवल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः-ल्ली)<BR>A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, and वल्ली a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवस्
सुवस्<BR>mfn. (-वः)<BR>What covers or clothes well.<BR>E.<BR>सु, वस to clothe, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन्त|सुवसन्तः
सुवसन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Chaitra, a festival in honour of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, वसन्त spring; being in March-April.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन्तक|सुवसन्तकः
सुवसन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A large creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>2 A festival in honour of KĀMADEVA in the month of Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, वसन्त the spring, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवह|सुवहः
सुवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Bearing or conveying well or pleasantly.<BR>2 Pleasant of burthen, to be borne with pleasure.<BR>3 Patient, enduring.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>3 Rasan, conjectured to be the ichneumon plant, (Ophiorrhyza mangos.)<BR>4 A scandent shrub, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>5 The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>6 A Vinā, or lute.<BR>7 A medicinal plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, much, or pleasantly, and वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवास|सुवासः
सुवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A pleasant or reputable dwelling.<BR>2 An agreeable perfume.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and वास abode, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवासिन्
सुवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Dwelling in a comfortable or respectable abode.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman married or unmarried, residing in her father's house.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, वास abode, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविक्रम
सुविक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Prowess, valour.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विक्रम power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविक्रान्त|सुविक्रांत|सुविक्रान्तः
सुविक्रान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A hero.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Heroism, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विक्रान्त valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचक्षण
सुविचक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Very clever.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विचक्षण intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचार
सुविचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Deliberate or due consideration.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विचार consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचारित
सुविचारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-weighed, deliberately considered.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विचारित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदित
सुविदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-known or understood.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, विदित known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद्
सुविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a learned man.<BR>f. (-विद्)<BR>A shrewd or clever woman.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, विद to know, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद|सुविदः
सुविद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, विद to know, aff. क; also सौविद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदत्
सुविदत्<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>सुविट् a Paṇḍita, अत to associate with, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदत्र
सुविदत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Related, of kin, a kinsman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, विद to know, कचन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदल्ल|सुविदल्लं|सुविदल्लः
सुविदल्ल<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>A haram, a seraglio.<BR>f. (-ल्ला)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>सुविदत् a king, ला to be or have, aff. ड, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविध
सुविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of a good kind, in a good or easy way.<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Easily.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविधि|सुविधिः
सुविधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ninth Jaina deified teacher of the present age.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and विधि a precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविनीत
सुविनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-trained, properly behaved.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A tractable cow.<BR>E.<BR>सु exceeding, and विनीत well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविलय
सुविलय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Easily fusible, liquefying.<BR>E.<BR>सु and वि before ली to melt, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविश्वस्त
सुविश्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Trusty, confidential.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विश्वस्त trusted in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तर
सुविस्तर<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Fully, at length.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विस्तर expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तीर्ण
सुविस्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Well spread or laid out.<BR>2 Very broad.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and विस्तीर्ण spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीरक|सुवीरकं
सुवीरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A collyrium, prepared from the Amomum anthorhizon.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, वीर power, efficacy, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीराम्ल|सुवीराम्लं
सुवीराम्ल<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sour rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, वीर essence, अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीर्य्य|सुवीर्य|सुवीर्य्यं
सुवीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Great vigour.<BR>2 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and वीर्य्य essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवृत्त|सुवृत्तः
सुवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Virtuous, good.<BR>2 Well or handsomely round.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and वृत्त practised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेल|सुवेलः
सुवेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Bowed, bent, stooping.<BR>2 Tamed, humble, quiet.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A mountain; also called Trikūṭa.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and वेल to move or shake, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेश|सुवेशः
सुवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Well-dressed.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and वेश attire; also सुवेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेषिन्
सुवेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Well-dressed, ornamented, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, वेष ornament, decoration, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्यक्त
सुव्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Plain, manifest.<BR>n. adv. (-क्तं)<BR>Evidently, clearly.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and व्यक्त manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्यस्त
सुव्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Dispersed.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and व्यस्त scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्रत|सुव्रतः
सुव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Virtuous, strict, rigidly observing any religious vow or obligation.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The twentieth Jina of the present age; also named Munisuvrata.<BR>2 One of the Jainas of the future era.<BR>3 The religious student.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The mother of the fifteenth Jaina of the present age.<BR>2 A cow easily milked, one of a tractable and gentle disposition.<BR>3 A virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, good, व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशक
सुशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Easily made or done.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and शक able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=937" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशर्म्मन्|सुशर्मन्
सुशर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-म्मा-म्मा-म्म)<BR>Exquisitely happy.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>The name of a prince.<BR>E.<BR>सु exceeding, शर्म्मन् pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशवी
सुशवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>2 A sort of spice, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, शव to go, aff. अच् and ङीष्; also सुषवी, सुसवी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशासित
सुशासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-governed.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and शासित governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशिख|सुशिखः
सुशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सु handsome, and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशिरस्
सुशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Having a fine head.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and शिरस् head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीत|सुशीतं|सुशीतः
सुशीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very cold or cooling.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A yellow fragrant sort of Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीतल|सुशीतलं
सुशीतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very cold or cooling, frigid, freezing.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A fragrant sort of grass; also कत्तृण.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, शीतल cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीम|सुशीमः
सुशीम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Cold, frigid.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Cold, coldness.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, श्यै to go, aff. मन्, more usually read सुषीम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशील|सुशीलः
सुशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Well-disposed, of good temper or disposition.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The wife of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and शील nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीलता
सुशीलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Natural amiability, excellence of temper or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also सुशीलत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीविका
सुशीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्रुत|सुश्रुतः
सुश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well-heard.<BR>2 Versed in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्लिष्ट
सुश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Closely united or adhering to.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and श्लिष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्लेष|सुश्लेषः
सुश्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Close or intimate union.<BR>2 A close embrace.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and श्लेष embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषम|सुषमः
सुषम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome, pleasing.<BR>2 Same, even, all.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Exquisite beauty.<BR>2 A period of time peculiar to the Jainas, the second division or Ara of a large period, containing six such portions, and that in which steady happiness is enjoyed by mankind: (the word however more usually occurs written सुखमा, as derived from सुख pleasure.)<BR>E.<BR>मु handsome, सम even, all, and the स changed after this particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषवी
सुषवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A sort of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>2 Black cumin-seed, generally confounded with Kalonji, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>3 Cumin-seed.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, षु to send or direct, aff. अच्, fem. aff. ङीष्; also सुशवी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषामन्
सुषामन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Sweet or kindly spoken.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and सामन् calming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषि|सुषिः
सुषि<BR>f. (-षिः)<BR>1 A hole.<BR>2 Drying.<BR>3 A tube or pipe.<BR>E.<BR>स substituted for श; see शुषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषिर|सुषिरं
सुषिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Perforated, pierced.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A hole.<BR>2 A wind instrument.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Nali, a perfume.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>स substituted for शः see शुषिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषीम|सुषीमः
सुषीम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Cold, frigid.<BR>2 Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Cold.<BR>2 A sort of snake.<BR>3 The moon gem.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, सीमा a limit; also read सुषिम and सुशीम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्त|सुषुप्तं
सुषुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Fast asleep.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, ष्वप to sleep, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्ति|सुषुप्तिः
सुषुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Deep sleep, profound repose, entire insensibility.<BR>E.<BR>स well, ष्वप to sleep, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्सु
सुषुप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Wishing to sleep.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप, to sleep, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषेण|सुषेणः
सुषेण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A fruit, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 The physician of the monkey chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>4 A cane or reed, the ratan.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, सेना a host or cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषेणिका
सुषेणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Black Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्ठु
सुष्ठु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Much, very much.<BR>2 Well, excellent.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, स्था to stay, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्म
सुश्म<BR>n. (-श्मं)<BR>A rope, a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंस्कृत|सुसंस्कृतं
सुसंस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dressed, seasoned, prepared with condiments, sauces, &c.<BR>2 Entirely perfected, very highly finished, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, संस्कृत made perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंस्थित
सुसंस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well situated or placed.<BR>2 Being or doing well.<BR>3 Circumscribed, well defined.<BR>E.<BR>मु and सम् before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंहत
सुसंहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well compacted or united, well knit.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and संहत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसङ्गृहीत|सुसंगृहीत
सुसङ्गृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well kept or preserved.<BR>2 Well abridged.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and सङ्गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसवी
सुसवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A sort of pungent seed, either a black species of cumin-seed or the Nigella Indica: see सुषवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसम्पद्|सुसंपद्
सुसम्पद्<BR>f. (-म्पद् or म्पत्)<BR>Fortune, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, and सम्पद् prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसह|सुसहः
सुसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Easily borne or suffered.<BR>2 Bearing or enduring well.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and सह suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसार|सुसारः
सुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>सु good, सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसारवत्|सुसारवन्त्
सुसारवत्<BR>n. (-वत्)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, सार essence, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसीमा
सुसीमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The mother of the sixth Jaina teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसेवित
सुसेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Assiduously served or attended upon.<BR>2 Much addicted to.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and सेवित served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थ|सुस्थः
सुस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Well, healthy.<BR>2 Happy, faring or living well.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and स्थ being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थता
सुस्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Health.<BR>2 Welfare, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुस्थ being well, तल् aff. of condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थयत्
सुस्थयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Setting at rest, appeasing, consoling.<BR>E.<BR>सुस्थ being well, used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थित
सुस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Living well or happily.<BR>2 Being well, in health or condition.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and स्थित who or what stays in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थिति|सुस्थितिः
सुस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Well being, welfare.<BR>2 Health, convalescence.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थिर|सुस्थिरः
सुस्थिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Firm, steady, stable.<BR>2 Resolute, cool.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and स्थिर steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मूर्षमाण
सुस्मूर्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Wishing or trying to recollect.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्वप्न
सुस्वप्न<BR>n. (-प्नं)<BR>A lucky or good dream.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and स्वप्न a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्नात|सुस्नातः
सुस्नात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well bathed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A student, who has performed his ablutions preparatory or subsequent to a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सु auspiciously, स्नात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मित
सुस्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smiling.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman with a pleasing or smiling countenance.<BR>E.<BR>मु well, pleasant, and स्मित smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=938" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहसानन
सुहसानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having a cheerful smiling face.<BR>E.<BR>सु, हस laughing, आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहस्ति
सुहस्ति<BR>m. (-स्तिः)<BR>One of the ten persons called Pūrbadharas by the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहित|सुहितः
सुहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Satiate, satisfied.<BR>2 Fit, right, suitable.<BR>3 Kindly, friendly.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>One of the tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, हित placed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृत्तम
सुहृत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Friendly, cordial, kind.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृत् a friend, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृत्ता
सुहृत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Friendship, affection.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृत्, and तल् aff.; also सुहृत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्
सुहृद्<BR>m. (-हृद् or हृत्)<BR>1 A friend.<BR>2 An ally.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, kind, हृद् heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृदय|सुहृदयः
सुहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Good hearted.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्बल
सुहृद्बल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The army of an ally.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृद्, and वल an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्भेद
सुहृद्भेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The separation of friends.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृद्, and भेद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 Sending, ordering, dispatching.<BR>2 Bearing, parturition.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear or send, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक|सूकः
सूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, क्विप् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूकर|सूकरः
सूकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A potter.<BR>3 A sort of deer, (the hog deer.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of moss, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>स substituted for श; see शूकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्त|सूक्तं
सूक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Well or properly said.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A hymn in the Ṛk Veda.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>The Śārika or Maina.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, उक्त spoken, (by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्षण
सूक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष to disrespect, aff. ल्युट्, and the र rejected; also सूर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्म|सूक्ष्मं|सूक्ष्मः
सूक्ष्म<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)<BR>1 Little, small.<BR>2 Minute, atomic.<BR>3 Fine, delicate.<BR>4 Ingenious, subtle.<BR>m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR>1 An atom.<BR>2 Clearingnut plant, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 The Supreme Soul, the subtle and invisible spirit that pervades all existence.<BR>2 Fraud, cheating.<BR>3 Fine thread, &c.<BR>4 A figure of rhetoric, the delicate or subtle expression of act or intention.<BR>5 Subtlety, ingenuity, craft.<BR>f. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>1 A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>2 Small cardamoms.<BR>3 A perfume, consisting of a substance in small grains: see Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>सूच् to inform or make known, स्मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मतण्डुला|सूक्ष्मतंडुला
सूक्ष्मतण्डुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Long-pepper.<BR>2 A sort of grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म fine, तण्डुला grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मत्व
सूक्ष्मत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Fineness, subtilty.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, सूक्ष्मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदर्शिन्
सूक्ष्मदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Acute, quick, sharp-sighted, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, fine, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदारु
सूक्ष्मदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A thin plank of wood.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म fine, small, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मपच
सूक्ष्मपच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 Coriander seed.<BR>2 A wild kind of cumin.<BR>3 A sort of mustard.<BR>4 A red sort of sugar-cane.<BR>5 The gum Arabic tree, (Mimosa Arabica.)<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म fine, small, and पच a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मपर्णी
सूक्ष्मपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>Rāmadūtī, a plant so called.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मफला
सूक्ष्मफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, and फल a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मबुद्धि|सूक्ष्मबुद्धिः
सूक्ष्मबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>1 Sharp, shrewd, intelligent, acute.<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Mental acumen.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म, and बुद्धि understanding^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्ममक्षिका
सूक्ष्ममक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A musquito, a gnat.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मवस्त्र|सूक्ष्मवस्त्रं
सूक्ष्मवस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Fine cloth.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म fine, वस्त्र cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशरीर
सूक्ष्मशरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The subtle body invested by and the archetype of the grosser and perceptible frame.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशालि|सूक्ष्मशालिः
सूक्ष्मशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A small and fine kind of rice.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मषट्चरण|सूक्ष्मषट्चरणः
सूक्ष्मषट्चरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sort of tick or louse breeding at the roots of the eye-lashes.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, and षद्परण an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मीकृत
सूक्ष्मीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made thin or minute.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मीभूत
सूक्ष्मीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become fine, subtle, minute.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म, भूत become, and च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच|सूचः
सूच<BR>r. 10th cl. (सूचयति)<BR>To give information, to espy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच|सूचः
सूच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The shoot of the Kuśa grass.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A needle. see सूचि.<BR>(-चा)<BR>1 Gesticulation.<BR>2 Sight, seeing.<BR>3 Piercing.<BR>E.<BR>सिव to sew, चट् Uṇādi aff., and ऊ substituted for the final, or सूच to make known, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचक|सूचकः
सूचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spy, an informer.<BR>2 A teacher, an instructor.<BR>3 A needle.<BR>4 A dog.<BR>5 A crow.<BR>6 A cat.<BR>7 A scoundrel, a villain.<BR>8 The manager or chief actor of a company.<BR>9 A Buddha.<BR>10 A Siddha.<BR>11 A demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to make known, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचन|सूचनं
सूचन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Information, informing.<BR>2 Teaching, shewing, describing.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Piercing.<BR>2 Wickedness.<BR>3 Gesture, gesticulation, conveying any intimation by signs.<BR>4 Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to make known, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचि|सूचिः
सूचि<BR>f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>1 A needle.<BR>2 Piercing, perforating.<BR>3 Indication of a passion or feeling by signs, gesture, gesticulation.<BR>4 A mode of dancing.<BR>5 A mode of array, a sharp file or column.<BR>6 A triangle formed by the sides of a trapezium produced to the point of meeting.<BR>7 A cone, a pyramid.<BR>8 (In astronomy,) The earth's disc in computing eclipses.<BR>9 An index, a catalogue.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to make known, aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added; or सिव to sew, &c., Uṇādi aff. चट; see सूच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिक|सूचिकः
सूचिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tailor.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An elephant's trunk.<BR>2 A needle.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, ठक् aff., or कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिकाधर|सूचिकाधरः
सूचिकाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सूचिका a trunk, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिखात|सूचिखातः
सूचिखात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sharp pyramid or pyramidal excavation.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि, and खात a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिकामुख|सूचिकामुखं
सूचिकामुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>A shell, a conch.<BR>E.<BR>सूचिका a needle, and सुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचित|सूचितः
सूचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Communicated, told, made known.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to make known or inform, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिता
सूचिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Needle-work.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिन्
सूचिन्<BR>mfn. (-ची-चिनी-चि)<BR>1 Spying, informing.<BR>2 Piercing.<BR>m. (-ची)<BR>A spy, an informer.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A needle.<BR>2 Night.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to make known, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=939" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिपुष्प|सूचिपुष्पः
सूचिपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिरोमन्
सूचिरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, (a bristle,) and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिवत्|सूचिवन्त्
सूचिवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, (a beak,) and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिवदन|सूचिवदनः
सूचिवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The mungoose.<BR>2 A musquito.<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, (a sharp nose or proboscis,) and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचीपुष्प|सूचीपुष्पः
सूचीपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle, a thorn, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचीमुख|सूचीमुखं|सूचीमुखः
सूचीमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The diamond.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle or a beak, and मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचीभेद्य
सूचीभेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Palpable, tangible.<BR>2 To be pierced, or penetrated by a needle.<BR>E.<BR>सूची, and भेद्य to be pierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचीरोमन्
सूचीरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle, (a bristle,) and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्य
सूच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Informable, communicable.<BR>E.<BR>सूच to inform, यत् aff.; also सूचनीय and सूचितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यग्र
सूच्यग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The point of a needle.<BR>E.<BR>सूची, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यग्रस्थूलक|सूच्यग्रस्थूलकः
सूच्यग्रस्थूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>सूचि a needle, अग्र a point, and स्थूलक thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यास्य|सूच्यास्यः
सूच्यास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
सूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, engendered.<BR>2 Sent, dispatched.<BR>3 Drank.<BR>4 Gone, departed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A charioteer.<BR>2 A carpenter.<BR>3 A man of a mixed race, descended from a Kṣatriya father, and mother of the sacerdotal tribe; his occupation is managing horses and driving cars.<BR>4 A bard, an encomiast.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman lying in.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतक|सूतकं|सूतकः
सूतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Impurity from child-birth or miscarriage.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>f. (-का-तिका)<BR>A woman recently delivered.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतपुत्त्र
सूतपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A name of KARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सूत the sun, and पुत्त्र son; also सूतपुत्त्रक and similar compounds, as सूततनय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
सूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Birth, production, delivery, parturition, bringing forth.<BR>2 Offspring, progeny.<BR>3 Sewing.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, as young, or सिव to sew, क्तिच् aff.; in the latter ऊ is substituted for the finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिकागृह|सूतिकागृहं
सूतिकागृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A part of a house appropriated to the women, or to a lying-in woman especially.<BR>E.<BR>सूतका or सूतिका a lying-in woman. and गृह house or room; hence also सूतकागृह n. (-हं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिकाभवन|सूतिकाभवनं
सूतिकाभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The lying-in chamber: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>सूतिका a lying-in woman, and भवन a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिगृह|सूतिगृहं
सूतिगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The lying-in chamber: see सूतिकागृह.<BR>E.<BR>सूति delivery, child-birth, गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतीगृह|सूतीगृहं
सूतीगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The lying-in chamber.<BR>E.<BR>सूति delivery, and गृह a house, and the vowel made long: see सूतिकागृह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतीमास
सूतीमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The last month of pregnancy.<BR>E.<BR>सूति delivery, and मास month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्कार|सूत्कारः
सूत्कार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Snorting, roaring, any sound expressive of impatience or aversion.<BR>E.<BR>सूत् imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्तर
सूत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Superior.<BR>2 Northern.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, उत्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्त
सूत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Well or entirely given.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and दत्त given, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्थान|सूत्थानः
सूत्थान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dexterous, clever.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, उत्थान exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्पर|सूत्परं
सूत्पर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Distilling spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्या
सूत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Religious bathing, ablution, preparatory or subsequent to a sacrifice.<BR>2 Drinking the juice of the acid Asclepias at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सू to bear, (fruit or offspring,) क्यप् aff., तुक् augment, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्याशौच|सूत्याशौचं
सूत्याशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Impurity from child-birth, continuing for ten days, or if in consequence of a miscarriage, for as many days as months had passed since conception.<BR>E.<BR>सूति child-bearing, अशौच impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (सूचयति)<BR>To bind, to thread, to string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र<BR>m. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A thread in general.<BR>2 A rule, a precept, in morals or science; a short, obscure, and technical sentence, enjoining some observance in law or religion, or intimating some rule in grammar, logic, &c.; in each case it is the fundamental and primitive part of Hindu learning, and is the form in which the works of the early and supposed inspired writers appear; the ingenuity and labour of subsequent authors having expanded and explained the original Sūtras in various commentaries and glosses.<BR>3 An opinion or decree in law.<BR>4 A string, a collection of threads, as that worn by the three first classes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff., and इव changed to ऊ, or सूत्र to string, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रकण्ठ|सूत्रकंठ|सूत्रकण्ठः
सूत्रकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A wagtail.<BR>3 A dove, a pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रकोण|सूत्रकोणः
सूत्रकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A small hour-glass-shaped drum, struck by a string and button fastened to it.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a string, and कोण corner; also with कन् added, सूत्रकोणक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रगण्डिका|सूत्रगंडिका
सूत्रगण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A stick used in spinning the threads to be employed in weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रग्रह
सूत्रग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Who holds thread, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र, and ग्रह to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रग्राह
सूत्रग्राह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Who or what takes, but does not hold thread, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र, ग्रह to take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रण|सूत्रणं
सूत्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Arranging, putting in order.<BR>2 Stringing.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र used as a verb, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रतर्कुटी
सूत्रतर्कुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A distaff, a spindle.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, and तर्कुटी a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रतन्तु|सूत्रतन्तुः
सूत्रतन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A thread.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, and तन्तु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रधार|सूत्रधारः
सूत्रधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The principal actor or manager of a company, and chief interlocutor in the prologue or prelude to a drama.<BR>2 A carpenter.<BR>3 The author of a set of rules or axioms.<BR>4 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a rule, &c., and धार who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रपुष्प|सूत्रपुष्पः
सूत्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The cotton plant.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र thread, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रभिद्
सूत्रभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद् or -भित्)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र thread, and भिद् who breaks or cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रमध्यभू
सूत्रमध्यभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>Incense.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र thread, मध्य amidst, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रयन्त्र|सूत्रयंत्र|सूत्रयन्त्रं
सूत्रयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 A shuttle.<BR>2 A loom.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, and यन्त्र a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=940" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रला
सूत्रला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A spindle or distaff.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र thread, ला to get, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रवीणा
सूत्रवीणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A sort of lute.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, and वीणा a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रवेष्टन|सूत्रवेष्टनं
सूत्रवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A weaver's shuttle.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र thread, and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रामन्
सूत्रामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, चै to preserve, मनिन् aff., and the vowel of the prefix, optionally long; also सुत्रामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्राली
सूत्राली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A necklace or chain worn round the neck.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रित
सूत्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Arranged, methodised.<BR>2 Ruled, directed in Sūtras.<BR>3 Strung.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र used as a vest, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिन्
सूत्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>Having threads, rules, &c.<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद|सूदः
सूद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A cook.<BR>2 Sauce, seasoning.<BR>3 A made dish, any thing seasoned.<BR>4 Split pease.<BR>5 Mud, mire.<BR>E.<BR>षद to leak or distil, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदन|सूदनं
सूदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Destructive, destroyer.<BR>2 Dear, beloved.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Destroying, killing.<BR>E.<BR>षूद to injure or kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदशाला
सूदशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>सूद a cook, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदाध्यक्ष|सूदाध्यक्षः
सूदाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Superintendant of the kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>सूद a cook, अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदित
सूदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Destroyed, killed.<BR>E.<BR>षूद to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदितृ
सूदितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-ती-तृ)<BR>Destroyer, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>षूद, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून|सूनं|सूनः
सून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Blown, budded, (as a flower.)<BR>2 Empty, vacant.<BR>3 Born, produced.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bringing forth, (as young,) parturition.<BR>2 A flower.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 The uvula.<BR>3 A shambles, a slaughter-house.<BR>4 A place or utensil in a house, where, or by which, insects may be killed, as the hearth, the slab, the pestle and mortar, the broom, and the water-pot.<BR>5 Hurting, injuring.<BR>6 Inflammation of the glands of the neck.<BR>7 A zone, a girdle.<BR>8 A ray.<BR>9 A river.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, &c., aff. क्त, or षु the same, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनवत्
सूनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Budding.<BR>2 Bearing.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनिन्
सूनिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>A butcher, a hunter, one who practices the death of animals.<BR>E.<BR>सूना a slaughter-house, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनु|सूनुः
सूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A younger brother.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A daughter's son.<BR>f. (-नुः or -नूः)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, (as children,) नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनृत|सूनृतं
सूनृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 True.<BR>2 Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>3 Agreeable, pleasant, (as speech.)<BR>4 Dear to, beloved by.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Agreeable discourse or speech, but also true.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, नृत to dance, (or excel,) घञ् aff., and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्मद|सून्मदः
सून्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Mad, crazy, insane.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, उन्मद mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्माद|सून्मादः
सून्माद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Mad, insane.<BR>E.<BR>सु much, उन्माद madness, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूप|सूपः
सूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Sauce, condiment.<BR>2 Soup, broth.<BR>3 A cook.<BR>4 A vessel.<BR>5 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>षु to bear, प Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपकार|सूपकारः
सूपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>सूप sauce, कार maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपत्
सूपत्<BR>ind.<BR>Excellently, well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपधूपन|सूपधूपनं
सूपधूपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>सूप sauce, and धूपन perfuming; also सूपधूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपपर्णी
सूपपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपाङ्ग|सूपाङ्गं
सूपाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>सूप sauce, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूम|सूमं|सूमः
सूम<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>1 Sky, heaven.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर|सूरः
सूर<BR>(ई) सूरी r. 4th cl. (सूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To be stupid or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर|सूरः
सूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The father of the 17th Jaina of the present era.<BR>3 A Paṇḍita, a learned man.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, क्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरण|सूरणः
सूरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर to hurt, aff. ल्युट्; also शूरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरत|सूरतः
सूरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Compassionate, tender.<BR>2 Tranquil, calm.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, रम to sport or rest, क्त Uṇādi aff., and the vowel of the prefix made long; also सुरत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरसूत|सूरसूतः
सूरसूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>ARUṆA, the personification of the dawn, as the charioteer of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सूर the sun, and सूत charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरि|सूरिः
सूरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a learned man.<BR>2 A title commonly given to Jaina teachers.<BR>3 KṚṢṆA.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, Uṇādi aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरिन्
सूरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a scholar, a learned man.<BR>E.<BR>सूर to injure, to dispel (ignorance, &c.), णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्षण|सूर्क्षणं
सूर्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disrespect, contumely, contempt.<BR>E.<BR>षूर्क्ष to treat with disrespect, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य|सूर्क्ष्यः
सूर्क्ष्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्ष्यति)<BR>1 To envy, to be impatient of another's success.<BR>2 To be intolerant; also षूर्क्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य|सूर्क्ष्यः
सूर्क्ष्य<BR>m. (-र्क्ष्यः)<BR>A kind of bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर्क्ष to disrespect, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्प्प|सूर्प|सूर्पः
सूर्प्प<BR>mn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पं)<BR>A winnowing basket.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्प्प to measure, aff. घञ्; or शृ to injure, प Uṇādi aff., and the vowel and initial changed: this word and its compounds are hence more usually written शूर्प्प, &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्प्पनखा|सूर्पनखा
सूर्प्पनखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The sister of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्प्प, and नख a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्म्मि|सूर्मि|सूर्मिः
सूर्म्मि<BR>f. (-र्म्मिः-र्म्मी)<BR>1 An image of metal, chiefly of iron.<BR>2 The pillar of a house.<BR>E.<BR>श changed to स, see शूर्म्मी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्य|सूर्य|सूर्यः|सूर्य्यः
सूर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Gigantic swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>3 The son of BALI.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 The wife of the sun.<BR>2 A drug, a bitter gourd.<BR>3 A new bride.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, (in the heavens,) क्यप् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकान्त|सूर्यकान्त|सूर्यकांत|सूर्यकान्तः|सूर्य्यकान्तः
सूर्य्यकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A gem, sometimes applied to crystal, but usually to a stone of fabulous existence and properties.<BR>2 A tree, (Hibiscus phoeniceus,) the red sort.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and कान्त a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकान्ति|सूर्यकान्ति|सूर्यकांति|सूर्यकान्तिः|सूर्य्यकान्तिः
सूर्य्यकान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 The flower of the Sesamum.<BR>2 Sun-shine.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and कान्ति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकाल|सूर्यकाल|सूर्यकालः|सूर्य्यकालः
सूर्य्यकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Day.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यग्रह|सूर्यग्रह|सूर्यग्रहः|सूर्य्यग्रहः
सूर्य्यग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 An eclipse of the sun.<BR>3 The personified ascending and descending node, or KETU and RĀHU.<BR>4 The bottom of a water-jar.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and ग्रह a planet; or seizing, laying hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यज|सूर्यज|सूर्यजः|सूर्य्यजः
सूर्य्यज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The monkey SUGRĪVA.<BR>2 The hero KARṆA.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The Yamunā river.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=941" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यतनय|सूर्यतनय|सूर्यतनयः|सूर्य्यतनयः
सूर्य्यतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 KARṆA.<BR>2 SUGRĪVA.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The Jumna or Yamunā river.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and तनय child; also similar compounds, as सूर्य्यपुत्त्र, सूर्य्यसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यतेजस्|सूर्यतेजस्
सूर्य्यतेजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>The radiance or heat of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य, and तेजस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यपुत्त्र|सूर्यपुत्र|सूर्यपुत्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्त्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्र
सूर्य्यपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 VARUṆA.<BR>2 ŚANI or Saturn.<BR>3 YAMA.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 The Yamunā river.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and पुत्त्र the child; applicable also to KARṆA, SUGRĪVA, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यभक्त|सूर्यभक्त|सूर्यभक्तः|सूर्य्यभक्तः
सूर्य्यभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Devoted to, or worshipping the sun especially.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A flower, (Pentapetes phoenicea.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and भक्त a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यभक्तक|सूर्यभक्तक|सूर्य्यभक्तकः
सूर्य्यभक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A flower, (Pentapetes phœnicea.)<BR>2 A worshipper of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यमणि|सूर्यमणि|सूर्यमणिः|सूर्य्यमणिः
सूर्य्यमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A tree, (Hibiscus phoeniceus.)<BR>2 The sunstone, a crystal lens or a fabulous sort of gem.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यमण्डल|सूर्यमण्डल|सूर्यमंडल|सूर्य्यमण्डलं
सूर्य्यमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The orb or disc of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यलता|सूर्यलता
सूर्य्यलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Cleome viscosa.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यवल्ली|सूर्यवल्ली
सूर्य्यवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A plant, (Cleome pentaphylla.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and वल्ली a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसङ्क्रम|सूर्यसङ्क्रम|सूर्यसंक्रमः
सूर्य्यसङ्क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The passage of the sun from one sign to another.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य, and सङ्क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसङ्क्रान्ति|सूर्यसङ्क्रान्ति|सूर्यसंक्रांति
सूर्य्यसङ्क्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>The sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य, and सङ्क्रान्ति transit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसज्ञ
सूर्य्यसज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and सज्ञा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसारथि|सूर्यसारथि|सूर्यसारथिः|सूर्य्यसारथिः
सूर्य्यसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>The charioteer of the sun, ARUṆA or the personified dawn.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and सारथि a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यालोक|सूर्यालोक|सूर्यालोकः|सूर्य्यालोकः
सूर्य्यालोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sunshine.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and आलोक light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यावर्त्त|सूर्यावर्त|सूर्यावर्तः|सूर्य्यावर्त्तः
सूर्य्यावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्त)<BR>1 A plant, (Cleome viscosa.)<BR>2 A sun-flower, (Helianthus indicus.)<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यावेक्षण|सूर्यावेक्षण
सूर्य्यावेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Looking at the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य, and अवेक्षण looking at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याश्मन्|सूर्याश्मन्
सूर्य्याश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>The sun gem.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याश्व|सूर्याश्व|सूर्याश्वः|सूर्य्याश्वः
सूर्य्याश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A horse of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यास्त|सूर्यास्त|सूर्य्यास्तं
सूर्य्यास्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>Sun-set.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and अस्त setting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याह्व|सूर्याह्व|सूर्याह्वः|सूर्य्याह्वं|सूर्य्याह्वः
सूर्य्याह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गम|सूर्येन्दुसङ्गम|सूर्येंदुसंगम|सूर्येन्दुसंगमः|सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गमः
सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Day of new moon, when the moon rises invisible.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, इन्दु the moon, सङ्गम conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्योढ|सूर्योढ|सूर्योढः|सूर्य्योढः
सूर्य्योढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>An evening guest, one who claims hospitality after sun set.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and ऊढ borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्योदय|सूर्योदय|सूर्योदयः|सूर्य्योदयः
सूर्य्योदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sun-rise.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्य्य the sun, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष
सूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (सूषति)<BR>To bring forth, to bear; also षूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृ
सृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (सरति) r. 3d cl. (ससर्त्ति)<BR>To go.<BR>1st cl. (सरति or धावति)<BR>To go fast, to run, (धै being substituted for the root.)<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>1 To follow.<BR>2 To conform to.<BR>With अप,<BR>To go back, to withdraw or remove.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To spread out or abroad.<BR>2 To go to or with, to accompany or attend, or to meet upon appointment.<BR>With उप,<BR>To approach, to advance;<BR>With निर्,<BR>To go forth or out.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To proceed.<BR>2 To extend.<BR>3 To project.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To go separately or apart.<BR>2 To come or arrive.<BR>3 To forego, to quit or leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक|सृकः
सृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, कक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकण्डु|सृकंडु|सृकण्डुः
सृकण्डु<BR>f. (-ण्डुः)<BR>Itch, psora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकाल|सृकालः
सृकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, कालन् aff., and कुक् augment; also सृगाल, शृकाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कन्
सृक्कन्<BR>n. (-क्क)<BR>The corner of the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to quit, (saliva,) कनिन् aff., form irr.; this word has various forms, as with a final vowel सृक्क n. (-क्कं) with क्वन्, or क्वनिन्, सृक्व n. (-क्वं) or सृक्वन् (-क्व) with कि or क्वि aff.: सृक्वि n. (-क्वि) or सृक्वि n. (-क्वि) with इनि, सृक्किन् n. (-क्कि) or सृक्विन् (-क्वि) and with ङीष् added, fem. form, सृक्विणी, सृक्विणी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृग|सृगः
सृग<BR>m. (-गा)<BR>A short arrow, thrown with the hand or shot through a tube.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. गक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृगाल|सृगालः
सृगाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>2 A Daitya or demon.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to let go, कालन् aff.; more usually शृगाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज
सृज<BR>r. 4th cl. (सृज्यते) r. 6th cl. (सृजति)<BR>1 To leave, to quit.<BR>2 To be left or abandoned.<BR>2 To create, to make.<BR>With उत् or वि prefixed,<BR>To abandon, to quit, to reject.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To unite, to be in alliance or contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
सृज्<BR>m. (सृक् or सृग् सृट् or सृड्)<BR>A creator.<BR>E.<BR>सृज् to create, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजिकाक्षार|सृजिकाक्षारः
सृजिकाक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR>E.<BR>see सर्ज्जिकाक्षार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणि|सृणिः
सृणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>A hook used to drive an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, नि Uṇādi aff., and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्यमान
सृज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being made or created.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to quit, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणिका
सृणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Saliva.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, नि added, and कन् aff., or सृ as before. With ईकन् Uṇādi aff., and नुम augment, सृणीका f. (-का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत|सृतः
सृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृति|सृतिः
सृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A road, a path, a way.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 Hurting, injuring.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वर|सृत्वरः
सृत्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, क्वरप् aff., तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदर|सृदरः
सृदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, दर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदाकु|सृदाकुः
सृदाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>4 The disk or orb of the sun.<BR>f. (-कुः)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, काकु Uṇādi aff., and दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप
सृप<BR>(ऌ) सृपॢ r. 1st. cl. (सर्पति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>With अप,<BR>To go from, to depart.<BR>With उप,<BR>To go near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाट|सृपाटः
सृपाट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A measure.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, पाट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाटिका
सृपाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The beak of a bird.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, पाट aff., कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्त
सृप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Gone, going.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्र|सृप्रः
सृप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>सृप to go, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमर|सृमरः
सृमर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Going, going well or quickly.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of animal; according to some authorities, a young deer.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, क्मरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट|सृष्टं
सृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Created, made.<BR>2 Much, many.<BR>3 Ascertained.<BR>4 Joined, attached, connected.<BR>5 Ornamented, adorned.<BR>6 Left, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=942" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टवत्
सृष्टवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Creating, making.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टि|सृष्टिः
सृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Creation, creating.<BR>2 Nature, natural property or disposition.<BR>3 The absence of properties.<BR>4 The existence of properties or qualities.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create or abandon, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट्वा
सृष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having created.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सॄ
सॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (सृणाति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक<BR>(ऋ) सेकृ r. 1st cl. सेकते<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sprinkling, aspersion, as of a fluid, or of Ghee on the sacrificial fire, &c.<BR>2 Seminal effusion.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकपाच
सेकपाच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR>E.<BR>सेक sprinkling, and पाच vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकिम|सेकिमं
सेकिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A radish.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तृ
सेक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>Sprinkling, aspergent, who or what sprinkles.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्त्र|सेक्त्रं
सेक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>A bucket.<BR>E.<BR>षिच् to sprinkle, aff. ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sprinkling, a sprinkler.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचन|सेचनं
सेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR>2 Dripping, oozing.<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR>E.<BR>षिच to sprinkle, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेटु|सेटुः
सेटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 The water-melon.<BR>2 A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR>E.<BR>षिट to disregard, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 A mound, a bank, a causeway, an elevated piece of ground separating fields, and serving, during their inundation in the rains, for the passage of travellers, &c.<BR>2 A bridge.<BR>3 A pass, a defile, a road practised in mountainous countries, and places of difficult access.<BR>4 A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, तुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुक|सेतुकः
सेतुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>2 A causeway, a pass.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुबन्ध|सेतुबंध|सेतुबन्धः
सेतुबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 The ridge of rocks extending from the south extremity of the Coromandel coast towards the island of Ceylon, supposed to have been formed by HANUMĀN by command of RĀMA, as a bridge for the passage of his forces, when going against RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 Any dyke or dam, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सेतु a bridge, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुभेदिन्
सेतुभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुवृक्ष|सेतुवृक्षः
सेतुवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>E.<BR>सेतु the same, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेत्र|सेत्रं
सेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A ligament, a fetter.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधा
सेधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>A porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 An army.<BR>2 A goddess, the personified armament of the gods, the wife of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>3 The mother of the third Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, नक् and टाप् affs., or स with, इन a lord or leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाङ्ग|सेनांग|सेनाङ्गं
सेनाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A component part or member of an army, as elephants, chariots, cavalry or infantry.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, and अङ्ग limb or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाचर|सेनाचरः
सेनाचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>A soldier, a camp-follower, &c. one belonging to or who accompanies an army.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानी
सेनानी<BR>m. (-नीः)<BR>1 A general, the commander of an army.<BR>2 KĀRTTIKEYA, the military deity of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, णी to lead, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापति|सेनापतिः
सेनापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A general, the commander of an army.<BR>2 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापतित्व
सेनापतित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Generalship.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनामुख|सेनामुखं
सेनामुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 A division of an army or battalion, a company or three Pattis, consisting of three elephants, three chariots, nine horse, and fifteen foot.<BR>2 A mound or covered way in front of a city gate.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, and मुख commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनारक्ष|सेनारक्षः
सेनारक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A guard, a piquet, a centinel, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, and रक्ष what protects or guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफ|सेफः
सेफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>श changed to सः see शेफ, शेफस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराह|सेराहः
सेराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of a milk-white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Binding, tying.<BR>E.<BR>षि to bind, रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल
सेल<BR>(ऋ) सेऌ r. 1st cl. (सेलति)<BR>To go or move; preferably षेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेलु|सेलुः
सेलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A tree, (Cordia myxa): see शेलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव|सेवं
सेव<BR>(ऋ) सेवृ r. 1st cl. (सेवते)<BR>To serve, to gratify by service: preferably षेवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Servile, dependant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sack.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>षेव to serve, or षिव to sew, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवकालु|सेवकालुः
सेवकालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Dugdhapeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A divine treasure, a substance considered as the treasure of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>सेव service, धा to have, aff. कि; also शेवधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
सेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sewing, darning, stitching.<BR>2 A sack.<BR>3 Service.<BR>4 Using, practising, following, being addicted to, or fond of.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A needle.<BR>2 (In anatomy,) A peculiar union of parts, of which seven instances occur in the body: viz. the five sutures of the cranium, the frenum of the tongue, and that of the glans penis.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, or षेव to serve, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनीय
सेवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be served, waited on, or honoured.<BR>2 To be followed or practised.<BR>E.<BR>सेव to serve, अनीयर् aff.; also सेवितव्य and सेव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवमान
सेवमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Serving, attending on.<BR>2 Pursuing, practising, being addicted to.<BR>E.<BR>सेव, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 Service, servitude.<BR>2 Worship, homage.<BR>3 Addition to.<BR>E.<BR>षेव to serve, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित|सेवितः
सेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Served, obeyed, honoured, worshipped, adored.<BR>2 Protected, preserved.<BR>3 Pursued, practised, used.<BR>E.<BR>षेवृ to gratify by service, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितृ
सेवितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Who or what serves, worships, &c.<BR>2 Addicted or devoted to.<BR>E.<BR>सेवृ to serve, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित्व
सेवित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Serving, devotion.<BR>E.<BR>सेविन् who serves, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविन्
सेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Serving, obeying.<BR>2 Pursuing, practising, using.<BR>E.<BR>षेव to serve, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्य|सेव्यं|सेव्यः
सेव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be served or obeyed, to be worshipped or honoured.<BR>2 What ought or may be practised, used, &c.<BR>3 To be taken care of.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>षेवृ to gratify by service, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=943" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यता
सेव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rank, eminence.<BR>E.<BR>सेव्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, सेव्यत्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यमान
सेव्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being served, waited, attended on.<BR>2 Being practised or used.<BR>E.<BR>सेव to serve, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सै
सै<BR>r. 1st cl. (सायति)<BR>To waste, to decline; also षै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंह|सैंहः
सैंह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Lion, leonine, lion-like.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह a lion, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिक|सैंहिकः
सैंहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Lion, leonine.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>सिंह, and ठक् aff.; or सिंहिका the mother of RĀHU, (by adoption,) and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकेय|सैंहिकेयः
सैंहिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>सिंहिका the reputed mother of this being, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकत|सैकतं|सैकतः
सैकत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Sandy in general.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A sand-bank or an island with sandy shores.<BR>E.<BR>सिकता sandy soil, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिक|सैकतिकं|सैकतिकः
सैकतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Living in doubt and error.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A religious mendicant.<BR>2 An ascetic.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A thread worn round the wrist or neck, &c. to secure good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>सिकता sand, &c., ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैतवाहिनी
सैतवाहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Bāhudā river.<BR>E.<BR>सित white, अण् aff. and वाहिनी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैद्धान्तिक|सैद्धांतिक|सैद्धान्तिकः
सैद्धान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Connected with or relating to a demonstrated truth, one who knows the truth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सिद्धान्त an established conclusion, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनापत्य|सैनापत्यं
सैनापत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>The command of an army, the dignity or duty of a general.<BR>E.<BR>सेनापति a general, and यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनिक|सैनिकः
सैनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to an army, drawn up as an army, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A guard, a centinel, a piquet.<BR>2 A body of forces in array.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an array, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धव|सैंधव|सैन्धवं|सैन्धवः
सैन्धव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Produced or born in Sindh.<BR>2 Marine, aquatic, ocean or river-born.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A horse.<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>Rock salt.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>In dramatic literature, musical expression of disappointment with Prākṛta words.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>E.<BR>सिन्धु a river, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवघन|सैंधवघन|सैन्धवघनः
सैन्धवघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A lump of salt.<BR>E.<BR>सैन्धव, and घन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्य|सैन्यं|सैन्यः
सैन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>An army.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 A soldier under arms, one drawn up in array.<BR>2 A guard, a centinel.<BR>E.<BR>सेना an army, and ण्य or ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्याधिपति
सैन्याधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A general.<BR>E.<BR>सैन्य, and अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्याध्यक्ष
सैन्याध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A commander, a general.<BR>E.<BR>सैन्य, and अध्यक्ष supervisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैमन्तिक|सैमंतिक|सैमंतिकं|सैमन्तिकं
सैमन्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Red-lead.<BR>E.<BR>सीमन्त the parting of the hair, (where a red mark is often made with minium,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरन्ध्री|सैरंध्री
सैरन्ध्री<BR>f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>1 A female artist.<BR>2 A name of DRAUPADĪ. see सैरिन्ध्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिक|सैरिकः
सैरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating or belonging to a plough, &c.<BR>2 Having furrows.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Ploughman.<BR>2 A plough-ox, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्र|सैरिंध्र|सैरिंध्रः|सैरिन्ध्रः
सैरिन्ध्र<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>A menial servant, one employed to dress and decorate the person and perform all servile offices; also who may be employed in the chase, snaring animals, &c. the offspring of a Dasyu by an Ayogava female.<BR>f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>1 An independant female artisan working in another person's house.<BR>2 A female attendant in the women's apartments.<BR>3 A woman of one of the mixed and degraded classes.<BR>4 DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the Pāṇḍu princes, and who upon the temporary servitude of her husbands, became workwoman in the house of the Rāja of Virāṭa.<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, धृ to hold or take, aff. क, and मुक् augment, अण् added, and the penultimate vowel changed optionally to इ; whence also सैरन्ध्री, or स्वैर independent, धृ to hold or be, aff. कन्, fem. aff. ङीष्, and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिभ|सैरिभः
सैरिभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 Svarga, INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>E.<BR>सीर the plough or the sun, इभ an elephant, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरीय|सैरीयः
सैरीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Barleria cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>सीर a plough, अण् aff., सैर relating to a plough, (turned up by it, &c.) and छ added; also with कन् added सैरीयक, and with ढक् aff. सैरेय or सैरेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरीयक|सैरीयकः
सैरीयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barleria: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरेय|सैरेयः
सैरेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A shrub, (Barleria cristata); see सैरीय; also with कन् added सैरेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैसक
सैसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Leaden, lead.<BR>E.<BR>सीसक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सो
सो<BR>f. (-सोः)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढ|सोढः
सोढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Borne, suffered, endured.<BR>2 Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढृ
सोढृ<BR>mfn. (-ढा-ढ्री-ढृ)<BR>1 Patient, enduring.<BR>2 Able, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>सह to bear, &c., aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्कण्ठ|सोत्कंठ|सोत्कण्ठः
सोत्कण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>Regretting, bewailing, grieving.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उत्कण्ठा sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्प्रास|सोत्प्रासं|सोत्प्रासः
सोत्प्रास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Excessive, much, violent.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A horse-laugh.<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>Irony, sneering praise and covert censure.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उत्प्रास excess or effort; it is also read सोत्प्राश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्साह
सोत्साह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Vigorous, energetic, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदक
सोदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having or containing water.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदय|सोदयं
सोदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Accumulated, augmented, with interest, with profit.<BR>E.<BR>स for सह with, उदय increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदर|सोदरः
सोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A brother of whole blood.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान common, same, and उदर belly or womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदर्य्य|सोदर्य|सोदर्यः|सोदर्य्यः
सोदर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A brother of whole blood.<BR>E.<BR>स for समान same or common, उदर belly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोद्योग
सोद्योग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Active, diligent, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उद्योग effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोनह|सोनहः
सोनह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोन्माद|सोन्मादः
सोन्माद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Mad, insane.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उन्माद madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपकार|सोपकारः
सोपकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Equipped, stocked, furnished or provided with necessary means or implements.<BR>2 Assisted, abetted, befriended.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उपकार an instrument or assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपप्लव|सोपप्लवः
सोपप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sun or moon in eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उपप्लव a portent, an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपवास|सोपवासः
सोपवास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Tasting, keeping a fast.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उपवास fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाक|सोपाकः
सोपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of a degraded caste, the son of a Cāṇḍāla by a Pukkasī female, and only to be employed as a public executioner, &c.<BR>E.<BR>see श्वपाक, the sibilants being irregularly transposed, व changed to उ, and that to the usual Guṇa letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=944" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाधिक
सोपाधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Restricted, limited, qualified, special.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उपाधि discrimination, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपान|सोपानं
सोपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Stairs, steps or a staircase.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उप above, up, and अन a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोभाञ्जन|सोभाञ्जनः
सोभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga); see शोभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम|सोमं|सोमः
सोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>3 A monkey chief.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>5 YAMA.<BR>6 One of the demigods called VASUS.<BR>7 ŚIVA.<BR>8 The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida, or Sarcostema viminalis.)<BR>9 The acid juice of the Sarcostema.<BR>10 A drug of supposed magical properties.<BR>11 Water.<BR>12 Nectar, the liquor of immortals.<BR>13 Camphor.<BR>14 A deified progenitor.<BR>15 A mountain or mountainous range, the mountains of the moon.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Rice-water or gruel.<BR>2 Heaven, sky, æther.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bear, (as young,) or to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमगर्ब्भ
सोमगर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and गर्ब्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमज|सोमजं|सोमजः
सोमज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमतीर्थ|सोमतीर्थं
सोमतीर्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A place of pilgrimage in the west of India.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and तीर्थ a holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमदैवत्य
सोमदैवत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Presided over by SOMA.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and दैवत्य deification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमधारा
सोमधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, धारा having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमन्
सोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>षू to bring forth, (as young,) and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमप|सोमपः
सोमप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The performer of a sacrifice, or a sacrificer, who drinks the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the plant, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपत्र|सोमपत्रः
सोमपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>सोम the Sarcostema, and पच a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपा
सोमपा<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>1 A drinker of the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>2 A Pitṛ or progenitor of a certain class, or those who are especially the Pitṛs of the Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the acid Sarcostema, and पा to drink, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपान
सोमपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Drinking the juice of the acid Sarcostema, an essential part of sacrifices according to the Veda ritual.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपीतिन्
सोमपीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A drinker of the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the juice of the plant, पीति beverage, इनि aff.; it is also read सोमपीथिन् and सोमपीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमबन्धु|सोमबंधु|सोमबन्धुः
सोमबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The white esculent water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and बन्धु friend; expanding at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमभू
सोमभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 One of the persons called VĀSUDEVAS, by the Jainas.<BR>2 The son of SOMA, BUDHA, the regent of MERCURY, and supposed founder of the lunar dynasty.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयाग|सोमयागः
सोमयाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Offering or sacrifice in which the acid Sarcostema juice is drank.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and याग sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयाजिन्
सोमयाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A sacrificer who drinks at the ceremony the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the plant, यज to sacrifice, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयोनि|सोमयोनिः
सोमयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A sort of Sandal of yellow colour and great fragrance.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमराजिन्
सोमराजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, राज to shine, aff. णिनि, or with अच् and ङीष् added, सोमराजी; and again with कन् added, सोमराजिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमराजी
सोमराजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>1 A medicinal plant: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमलता
सोमलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The moon-plant or acid Sarcostema, (S. viminalis.)<BR>2 The Godāvarī river.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवंश|सोमवंशः
सोमवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>2 The lunar dynasty, or series of princes supposed to descend through BUDHA from SOMA, or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and वंश family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवत्|सोमवन्त्
सोमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Lunar, having the moon.<BR>2 Having the Sarcostema juice.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवत्|सोमवन्त्
सोमवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like the moon.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्क|सोमवल्कः
सोमवल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>1 A white kind of Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>3 A plant, (Guilandina bonduccella.)<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and वल्क bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्लरि|सोमवल्लरिः
सोमवल्लरि<BR>f. (-रिः-री)<BR>The moon-plant, (Sarcostema viminalis.)<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and वल्लरी a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्ली
सोमवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A twining plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>3 The moonplant.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवार|सोमवारः
सोमवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Monday.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमविक्रयिन्
सोमविक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A vender of the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the plant, विक्रय selling, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवृक्ष|सोमवृक्षः
सोमवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, (Kayaphal.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसज्ञ
सोमसज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and सज्ञ appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसद्
सोमसद्<BR>m. (-सद्)<BR>A Pitṛ or progenitor of a peculiar class, the progenitor of the celestial beings called Sādhyas.<BR>E.<BR>सोम, and सद् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिद्धान्त|सोमसिद्धान्तः
सोमसिद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 One of the Buddhas.<BR>2 A rationalist of a sect of Śaivas.<BR>3 A particular doctrine, a system of theological philosophy, followed by a branch of the worshippers of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, (as the teacher of the doctrine,) and सिद्धान्त truth, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिद्धान्तिन्
सोमसिद्धान्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>A follower of a branch of the Śaivas.<BR>E.<BR>सोमसिद्धान्त the doctrine, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिन्धु|सोमसिंधु|सोमसिन्धुः
सोमसिन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुत्
सोमसुत्<BR>m. (-सुत्)<BR>A priest or sacrificer who sprinkles the juice of the acid Sarcostema at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the plant, षु to sprinkle, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुत्वन्
सोमसुत्वन्<BR>mfn. (-त्वान्-त्वती-त्वत्)<BR>Having sprinklers of Soma juice, (a hermitage, a sacrifice, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>सोमसुत्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुता
सोमसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The Narmadā or Nerbudda river.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाख्य|सोमाख्यं
सोमाख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, and आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाल|सोमालः
सोमाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Soft, bland.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, अल to resemble, aff. अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमोद्भवा
सोमोद्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The Narmadā or Nerbudda river.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, (for the lunar race,) and उद्भव born; or सोम nectar, उद्भव production, (from it,) by conferring paradise on those who bathe in it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोराष्ट्रिक
सोराष्ट्रिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>सुराष्ट्र Surat, and ठक् aff.; also सौराष्ट्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठ|सोल्लुंठ|सोल्लुंठः|सोल्लुण्ठः
सोल्लुण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>Irony, ridicule: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=945" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठन|सोल्लुंठन|सोल्लुंठनं|सोल्लुण्ठनं
सोल्लुण्ठन<BR>n. (-न)<BR>Apparent praise and covert censure, irony.<BR>E.<BR>स with, उल्लुण्ठन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर|सौकरः
सौकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Hoggish, swinish.<BR>2 Relating to a hog.<BR>E.<BR>सूकर a hog, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरिक|सौकरिकः
सौकरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>सूकर a boar, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्य्य|सौकर्य|सौकर्यं|सौकर्य्यं
सौकर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Facility, ease of effecting any thing.<BR>2 Easy and extempore composition, or preparation of food or medicine.<BR>3 Hoggishness, swinishness, the condition or qualities of a hog.<BR>E.<BR>सुकर doing easily, or सूकर a hog, &c., aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकुमार्य्य|सौकुमार्य|सौकुमार्यं
सौकुमार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Youthfulness.<BR>2 Delicacy, tenderness.<BR>E.<BR>सुकुमार, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्म्य|सौक्ष्म्यं
सौक्ष्म्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्म्यं)<BR>Minuteness, subtility.<BR>E.<BR>सूक्ष्म small, fine, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखसुप्तिक|सौखसुप्तिकः
सौखसुप्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bard, a minstrel, one whose duty it is to waken the prince in a morning with music and song.<BR>E.<BR>सुखसुप्त sleeping pleasantly, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौख्य|सौख्यं
सौख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Pleasure, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>सुख happiness, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगत|सौगतः
सौगत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A Saugata, a heretic, an atheist.<BR>2 A Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>सुगत the supposed teacher of these doctrines, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतिक|सौगतिकः
सौगतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>2 The mendicant Brahman.<BR>3 Doubt, unbelief, scepticism.<BR>4 An atheist, an unbeliever.<BR>E.<BR>सुगत the founder of the sect, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं|सौगन्धः
सौगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass: see कत्तृण.<BR>2 Fragrance.<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्ध fragrant, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं|सौगन्धिकः
सौगन्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fragrant, odorous.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The white water-lily, (Nymphæa lotus.)<BR>2 A fragrant grass: see कत्तृण.<BR>3 A ruby.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sulphur.<BR>2 A dealer in perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>सु pleasant, गन्ध smell, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध्य|सौगंध्य|सौगंध्यं|सौगन्ध्यं
सौगन्ध्य<BR>n. (-न्ध्यं)<BR>Odour, fragrance.<BR>E.<BR>सुगन्ध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचि|सौचिः
सौचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचिक|सौचिकः
सौचिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>सूची a needle, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजन्य|सौजन्यं
सौजन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Kindness, compassion.<BR>2 Friendship.<BR>3 Goodness.<BR>E.<BR>सुजन, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौण्डी|सौंडी
सौण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>Long-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्र|सौत्रः
सौत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Preceptive, formulary, according to rule or precept.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A radical, the only application of which is to form derivative nouns, and not like other roots, capable of conversion into a verb.<BR>E.<BR>सूत्र a thread, a rule, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामनी
सौदामनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 A courtesan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>3 Part of the Śudāman mountain: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामिनी
सौदामिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 One of the Apsarasas or nymphs of Svarga.<BR>3 A particular sort of lightning.<BR>4 A city so named.<BR>E.<BR>सुदामन् a cloud, a mountain, or INDRA'S elephant, अण् and ङीष् affs. with the augment इक्; also omitting the augment, सौदामनी, and dropping the penultimate vowel, सौदाम्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदाम्नी
सौदाम्नी<BR>f. (-म्नी)<BR>Lightning: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिक|सौदायिकं
सौदायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Received by a woman at her marriage from her father or mother or any relative as a mark of regard, and thence her own property.<BR>E.<BR>सुदाय a nuptial gift, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौध|सौधः
सौध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>1 A mansion, a palace.<BR>2 Silver.<BR>3 Opal.<BR>E.<BR>सुधा plaster, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधार|सौधारः
सौधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One of the fourteen parts of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधाल|सौधालं
सौधाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A temple of ŚIVA, or in the form of Īśāna.<BR>E.<BR>सौध a palace, अल equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन|सौनः
सौन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a slaughter-house, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Butcher's meat.<BR>E.<BR>सूना, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्द|सौनंद|सौनंदं|सौनन्दं
सौनन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The club of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्दिन्|सौनंदिन्
सौनन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>BALARĀMA the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>सौनन्द his club, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनिक|सौनिकः
सौनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender of the flesh of beasts or birds.<BR>E.<BR>सून a place of slaughter, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन्दर्य्य|सौन्दर्य|सौंदर्य|सौंदर्यं|सौन्दर्य्यं
सौन्दर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Beauty, loveliness.<BR>E.<BR>सुन्दर handsome, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्ण|सौपर्णं
सौपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Dry ginger.<BR>2 The emerald.<BR>E.<BR>सुपर्ण GARUḌA, and ठक् aff. of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णेय|सौपर्णेयः
सौपर्णेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>सुपर्णा the mother of this being, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिक|सौप्तिकं
सौप्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Connected with or relating to sleep, somnolent, somniferous, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Nocturnal combat.<BR>E.<BR>सुप्त sleep, (or the hour of sleep,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ|सौभं
सौभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA suspended in mid-air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्र|सौभद्रः
सौभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 The son of SUBHADRĀ.<BR>2 A war occasioned by the carrying off of SUBHADRĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुभद्रा sister to KṚṢṆA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्रेय|सौभद्रेयः
सौभद्रेय<BR>m. (-या)<BR>1 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>2 ABHIMANYU, the son of SUBHADRĀ.<BR>E.<BR>सुभद्रा the sister of KṚṢṆA, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेय|सौभागिनेयः
सौभागिनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of an auspicious mother.<BR>E.<BR>सुभगा an auspicious mother, ढक् aff., and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्य|सौभाग्यं
सौभाग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>1 Auspiciousness, good fortune.<BR>2 The fourth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>3 Redlead.<BR>E.<BR>सुभग auspicious, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्|सौभाग्यवन्त्
सौभाग्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>सौभाग्य, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्ता
सौभाग्यवत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Auspiciouness, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, सौभाग्यवत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाञ्जन|सौभाञ्जनः
सौभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga): see शोभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिक|सौभिकः
सौभिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्र|सौभ्रात्रं
सौभ्रात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Brotherhood, fraternity.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, भ्रातृ a brother, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>1 Floral, flowery, relating to flowers.<BR>2 Agreeable, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्य|सौमनस्यं
सौमनस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस् content, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यायनी
सौमनस्यायनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The blossom of the great-flowered jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सुमनस् the plant, फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Lunar, relating to SOMA or the moon.<BR>2 Performed with the Sarcostema juice, relating to it, &c.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A sacrifice performed on the day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्र|सौमित्रः
सौमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>LAKṢMAṆA, the younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>सुभित्रा the wife of DAŚARATHA, and mother of this prince, and अण् aff.; also with इञ्, aff. सौमित्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेचक|सौमेचकं
सौमेचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिक|सौमेधिकः
सौमेधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sage, a seer, one possessing supernatural knowledge or power.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, मेधा apprehension, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=946" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुक|सौमेरुकं
सौमेरुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>सुमेरु the mountain, with कन् added, and अण् aff. of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या or मी-म्यं)<BR>1 Handsome, pleasing.<BR>2 Mild, gentle, placid.<BR>3 Sacred or belonging to SOMA or the moon.<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>1 BUDDHA, regent of MERCURY, and son of SOMA or the moon.<BR>2 One of the nine Khaṇḍas or divisions of the known continent.<BR>3 A term applied to a pupil when addressing instruction to one.<BR>4 (In anatomy,) The blood before it receives the red particles, the serum.<BR>m. plu. (-म्याः)<BR>Five stars in Orion's head.<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>1 A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>2 Heart-pea.<BR>3 The Abrus precatorious.<BR>4 The moon-plant, (Sarcostema acida.)<BR>5 Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>6 Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>सोम the moon, ण्यत् or यत् aff., or द्यण् aff., when the word takes ङीप् in the feminine form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यकृच्छ्र|सौम्यकृच्छ्रः
सौम्यकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>A religious penance, subsisting for five days, severally, on sesamum after expression, the water of boiled rice, butter-milk mixed with water, water, and parched grain, and fasting on the sixth day.<BR>E.<BR>सौम्य relating to the moon, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यत्व
सौम्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Beauty.<BR>2 Gentleness, placidity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to सौम्य; also with तल्, सौम्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यधातु|सौम्यधातुः
सौम्यधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic humor.<BR>E.<BR>सौम्य lunar, and घातु element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Solar.<BR>2 Celestial.<BR>3 Spirituous.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The planet SATURN.<BR>2 A month, consisting of thirty rising and settings of the sun, a solar month.<BR>3 A solar day, whilst the sun is in one degree of the ecliptic.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, &c., मूर the sun, अण् aff., or सूर्य्य the sun, and ङीष् aff. for the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 Fragrance.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An ox.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभी the cow of plenty, (the parent cow,) and ढक् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यं|सौरभ्यः
सौरभ्य<BR>n. (-भ्यं)<BR>1 Pleasingness, agreeableness, beauty.<BR>2 Fragrance, odour.<BR>3 Fame, character, reputation of learning or other merit.<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, pleasing, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेय|सौरसेयः
सौरसेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of SKANDA.<BR>E.<BR>सुरसा DURGĀ, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैन्धव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Gangetic, relating or belonging to the Ganges river.<BR>E.<BR>सुरसिन्धु the river of the gods, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>Surat.<BR>f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>A fragrant sort of earth.<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>सु good or much, राष्ट्र dominion, अञ् aff.; or सुराष्ट्र the same, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं|सौराष्ट्रकः
सौराष्ट्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of white or bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>सौराष्ट्र Surat, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रिक|सौराष्ट्रिकं
सौराष्ट्रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of poison, (that of a kind of snake according to some, but according to others, a vegetable or mineral.)<BR>E.<BR>सुराष्ट्र the country, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरि|सौरिः
सौरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>सूर the sun, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिक|सौरिकः
सौरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Celestial.<BR>2 Spirituous, vinous.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 A vender of spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>सुर a deity, or सुरा wine, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौल्विक|सौल्विकः
सौल्विक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A copper-smith, more usually शौल्विक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौव|सौवं
सौव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>An edict, &c. in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, proper, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर|सौवरं
सौवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-र)<BR>Produced or existing in a note of music, relating to it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्च्चल|सौवर्चल|सौवर्च्चलं
सौवर्च्चल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Sochal salt.<BR>2 Natron, alkali.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्च्चल a district, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्ण|सौवर्णं|सौवर्णः
सौवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>1 Golden, made or consisting of gold.<BR>2 Weighing a Suvarṇa.<BR>E.<BR>सुवर्ण gold, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्णभेदिनी
सौवर्णभेदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, commonly, Priyangu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवस्तिक|सौवस्तिकः
सौवस्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Salutatory, benedictory.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A family Brahman or priest.<BR>E.<BR>स्वस्ति a term of salutation, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवास्तव|सौवास्तवः
सौवास्तव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Pleasantly situated, erected on a good site.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, वास्तु a site, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविद|सौविदः
सौविद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A guard or attendant of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>सुविद the same, and अण् pleonasm, or सुविद् a woman, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविदल्ल|सौविदल्लः
सौविदल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A guard or attendant of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>सुविदल्ला a female, अण् aff., or सुविदन् a king, ला to get or have, सुविदल्ल a haram, and अण् aff.; also with कन् added, सौविदल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर|सौवीरं|सौवीरः
सौवीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>2 Antimony.<BR>3 Sour gruel.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A district, in the west of India, connected with the country along the Indus.<BR>m. pl. (-राः)<BR>The people of Suvīra.<BR>E.<BR>सुवीर the country so called, and अण् pleonasm or aff. of derivation; also with यञ्, aff. सौवीर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौष्ठव|सौष्ठवं
सौष्ठव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Excess, exceedingness, much.<BR>2 Excellence.<BR>3 A part of a drama.<BR>4 Lightness, fleetness.<BR>E.<BR>सुष्ठु excellent, &c., and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्द|सौहार्द|सौहार्दः|सौहार्द्दं|सौहार्द्दः
सौहार्द्द<BR>n. (-र्द्दं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>The son of a friend.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृद् a friend, अण् aff., and both vowels changed; also with ष्यञ्, aff. सौहार्द्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्य|सौहार्द्यं
सौहार्द्य<BR>n. (-र्द्यं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सुहद् a friend, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहित्य|सौहित्यं
सौहित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>2 Fulness, completion.<BR>E.<BR>सुहित satisfied, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद|सौहृदं
सौहृद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृद a friend, अण् aff.; also from सुहृदय, सौहृदय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद्य|सौहृद्यं
सौहृद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>सुहृद् a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कद
स्कद<BR>(इ) स्कदि r. 1st. cl. (स्कन्दते)<BR>1 To leap, to jump.<BR>2 To inundate.<BR>2 To lift up.<BR>3 To shed or spill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कंदः|स्कन्दः
स्कन्द<BR>(इर) स्कन्दिर r. 1st cl. (स्कन्दति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To be dry or arid.<BR>3 To effuse or emit.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>To assail, to assault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कंदः|स्कन्दः
स्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 SKANDA, or KĀRTTIKEYA, the son of ŚIVA, and military deity of the Hindus.<BR>2 A king, a prince.<BR>3 The body.<BR>4 The bank of a river.<BR>5 A clever or learned man.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to go, (to fly before whom; the enemies of the gods,) and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दन|स्कंदन|स्कंदनं|स्कन्दनं
स्कन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 Purging, looseness.<BR>3 Effusion.<BR>4 Suppressing bleeding by cold applications.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दयत्
स्कन्दयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Effusing, pouring out.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to effuse, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दित
स्कन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Effused, shed, emitted.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to emit, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध|स्कंध|स्कंधः|स्कन्धः
स्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 The shoulder, the head of the humerus.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 The trunk of a tree.<BR>4 A king, a prince.<BR>5 A sort of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">Page948</a>] metre.<BR>6 A multitude, a quantity.<BR>7 War, battle.<BR>8 Any article essential to the coronation of a king, as a jar filled with holy water, a parasol, a Chowri, &c.<BR>9 Part of an army or a form of array.<BR>10 Any one of five branches of human or mundane knowledge, or objects of understanding.<BR>11 A road, a way.<BR>12 A heron.<BR>13 An engagement, an agreement.<BR>14 A wise old man.<BR>15 A learned man, a teacher.<BR>16 Match or equality in the humps of a pair of draft oxen.<BR>17 The five objects of sense, or form, taste, smell, &c.<BR>18 A book, a section, a chapter.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 A branch.<BR>2 A creeper.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, and धा to hold, aff. क, and सुट् initial augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=947" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धचाप|स्कंधचाप|स्कन्धचापः
स्कन्धचाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A sort of yoke for carrying burthens by a sling attached to either end.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the shoulder, and चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धज|स्कन्धजः
स्कन्धज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A tree which grows from a principal stem.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धतरु|स्कंधतरु|स्कन्धतरुः
स्कन्धतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध a stem, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धदेश|स्कंधदेश|स्कन्धदेशः
स्कन्धदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The withers of an elephant, or part where the rider sits.<BR>2 The shoulder.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the shoulder, and देश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धफल|स्कंधफल|स्कन्धफलः
स्कन्धफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The cocoanut tree.<BR>2 The Vilva or Bel.<BR>3 The glomerous fig.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the trunk, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धबन्धना|स्कंधबंधना
स्कन्धबन्धना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium.)<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the stem, and बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धमल्लक|स्कंधमल्लक|स्कन्धमल्लकः
स्कन्धमल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धरुह|स्कंधरुह|स्कन्धरुहः
स्कन्धरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध a principal stem, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाह|स्कंधवाह|स्कन्धवाहः
स्कन्धवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An ox of burthen.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the shoulder, and वाह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाहक|स्कंधवाहक|स्कन्धवाहकः
स्कन्धवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ox of burthen.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, or स्कन्ध the shoulder, with वह to bear, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशाखा|स्कंधशाखा
स्कन्धशाखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The fork or principal branch of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the trunk, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशृङ्ग|स्कंधशृंग|स्कन्धशृङ्गः
स्कन्धशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the shoulder, and शृङ्ग the horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्|स्कंधस्
स्कन्धस्<BR>n. (-न्धः)<BR>1 The shoulder.<BR>2 The trunk of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्कदि to go or collect, aff. असुन्, and द changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धाग्नि|स्कन्धाग्निः
स्कन्धाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The stem of a tree on fire in consequence of attrition.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धानल|स्कन्धानलः
स्कन्धानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The stem of a tree or any large piece of timber on fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धावार|स्कंधावार|स्कन्धावारः
स्कन्धावार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An army, or a division of it attached to the person of the king.<BR>2 A royal capital.<BR>3 A camp.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध a king or an army, and आङ् before वृ to screen or guard, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कंधिकः|स्कन्धिकः
स्कन्धिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ox of burthen.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध the shoulder, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिन्|स्कंधिन्
स्कन्धिन्<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध a stem, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धोपनेय
स्कन्धोपनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be carried on the shoulders.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A form of peace-offering, in which fruit or grain is presented as a mark of submission.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्ध, and उपनेय to be conveyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्न|स्कन्नं
स्कन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Fallen, fallen down or from.<BR>2 Oozed, trickled out or down.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कभ
स्कभ<BR>(इ) स्कभि r. 1st cl. (स्कम्भते) r. 9th and 5th cls. (स्कभ्नाति स्कभ्नोति)<BR>To stop or hinder, to impede, to block, to obstruct, &c.<BR>2 To be dull or stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु<BR>r. 9th and 5th cls. (स्कुनाति-स्कुनीते स्कुनोति-स्कुनुते)<BR>1 To go by leaps.<BR>2 To cover.<BR>3 To raise or lift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुद
स्कुद<BR>(इ) स्कुदि r. 1st cl. (स्कुन्दते)<BR>1 To jump, to go by leaps or jumps.<BR>2 To raise, to lift up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुम्भ
स्कुम्भ<BR>(उ) स्कुम्भु r. 5th and 9th cls. (स्कुभ्नोति-स्कुभ्नाति)<BR>1 To stop or hinder.<BR>2 To be dull or insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद
स्खद<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्खदते)<BR>1 To defeat, to discomfit.<BR>2 To cut.<BR>3 To make firm.<BR>4 To destroy, to hurt or kill.<BR>5 To fatigue, to exhaust.<BR>6 To eat, to taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खदन|स्खदनं
स्खदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Defeating, discomfiting.<BR>2 Injury, hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>स्खद to defeat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल
स्खल<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्खलति)<BR>1 To move, to go.<BR>2 To slip, to stumble or fall.<BR>3 To gather, to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलत्
स्खलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Stumbling, tripping, (either in motion, conduct, or speech.)<BR>E.<BR>स्खल to stumble, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलद्वाक्य
स्खलद्वाक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Blundering, making mistakes in speaking.<BR>E.<BR>स्खलत्, and वाक्य speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन्मति
स्खलन्मति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Erring in judgment, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>स्खलत्, and मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन|स्खलनं
स्खलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Stumbling, slipping, tripping.<BR>2 Stumbling or falling from virtue.<BR>3 Tripping in speech, making a mistake or blunder in speech or pronunciation.<BR>4 Knocking or falling together, shock, collision.<BR>5 Striking or rubbing one thing against another.<BR>E.<BR>स्खल to go, to drop, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Slipped, fallen.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>3 Shaken, agitated, disturbed.<BR>4 Shaking, wavering, unsteady, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>5 Drunk.<BR>6 Stuttering, hesitating, (in speech.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Circumvention, stratagem, (in war.)<BR>2 Falling, tumbling.<BR>3 Falling or deviating from virtue or truth.<BR>E.<BR>स्खल to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन|स्तनः
स्तन<BR>(स्तनति) r. 1st and 10 cls. (स्तनयति)<BR>To sound, to thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन|स्तनः
स्तन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The female bosom or breast.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनकुद्मल
स्तनकुद्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन, and कुद्मल a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनन|स्तननं
स्तनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sound, noise in general.<BR>2 The grumbling of clouds.<BR>3 Breathing hard, groaning as a person in pain.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन to sound, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनन्धय|स्तनंधय|स्तनंधयः|स्तनन्धयः
स्तनन्धय<BR>mf. (-यः-या or यी)<BR>An infant, one at the breast.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, धेट् to drink, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपा
स्तनपा<BR>mf. (-पाः)<BR>An infant at the breast.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and पा who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनभर|स्तनभरः
स्तनभर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man with a breast like a woman's.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन a pap, and भर who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमण्डल
स्तनमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन, and मण्डल a globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमुस्व
स्तनमुस्व<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and मुख point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नु|स्तनयित्नुः
स्तनयित्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 Thunder, the muttering of clouds.<BR>3 Lightning.<BR>4 Sickness.<BR>5 Death.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन to sound, in the tenth cl. इत्नुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनवृन्त|स्तनवृंत|स्तनवृन्तः
स्तनवृन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and वृन्त a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनशिखा
स्तनशिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and शिखा the crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाग्र|स्तनाग्रं|स्तनाग्रः
स्तनाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=948" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनान्तर|स्तनांतर|स्तनान्तरं
स्तनान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The heart, or its site, placed however immediately under the centre bone of the sternum.<BR>2 A mark on the breast, indicative of future widowhood.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन the breast, and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाभोग|स्तनाभोगः
स्तनाभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A man with a large bosom, or one like a female's.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन a breast, and आभोग who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनित|स्तनितं
स्तनित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The rattling of thunder, the grumbling of thunder clouds.<BR>2 The noise of clapping the hands.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन to sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्य|स्तन्यं
स्तन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>स्तन a breast, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Stopped, blocked, or shut up.<BR>2 Firm, hard, stiff, rigid.<BR>3 Stupid, dull, insensible.<BR>4 Paralysed.<BR>E.<BR>स्तभि to stop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धकर्ण
स्तब्धकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Having the ears erect.<BR>E.<BR>स्तब्ध, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धरोमन्
स्तब्धरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>स्तब्ध firm, and रोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीकरण
स्तब्धीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Stiffening, making rigid, paralysing.<BR>E.<BR>स्तब्ध, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीकृत
स्तब्धीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stiffened, rigid, paralysed.<BR>E.<BR>स्तब्ध, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ|स्तभः
स्तभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A goat.<BR>2 A ram.<BR>E.<BR>see स्तुभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तंबः|स्तम्बः
स्तम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A shrub, a plant that has no particular or decided stem.<BR>2 A clump of grass, a sheaf of corn, &c.<BR>3 The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>1 A post, a pillar in general.<BR>2 Stupidity, insensibility.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand or abide, अम्बच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरि|स्तंबकरि|स्तम्बकरिः
स्तम्बकरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Corn or rice.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्ब a cluster, and कृ to make, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकार|स्तम्बकारः
स्तम्बकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Making or forming a heap or cluster.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्ब a cluster, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघन|स्तंबघन|स्तम्बघनः
स्तम्बघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A small hoe for weeding or eradicating clusters of gramineous plants.<BR>2 A sickle or instrument for cutting corn.<BR>3 A basket for holding the heads of wild rice, &c. when cut.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्ब a cluster, (of stalks,) a sheaf, हन to destroy, and अप् aff.; also with कच्, aff. स्तम्बघ्न, in each case घ being substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघ्न|स्तंबघ्न|स्तम्बघ्नः
स्तम्बघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Turf-destroying.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A hoe or sickle, &c.: see the last; also स्तम्बघात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बपुर्
स्तम्बपुर्<BR>f. (-पूः)<BR>A city so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बहनन|स्तम्बहननः
स्तम्बहनन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A hoe or sickle for eradicating weeds, cutting or reaping corn, &c.: see स्तम्बधन.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्ब a cluster, a sheaf, and हनन destroying; also स्तम्बहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बेरम|स्तंबेरम|स्तंबेरमः|स्तम्बेरमः
स्तम्बेरम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्बे in a clump, (of high grass,) रम to sport, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तम्भ<BR>(उ) स्तम्भु r. 5th cl. (स्तभ्नोति) 9th cl. (स्तभ्नाति)<BR>1 To stop, to block, to hinder.<BR>2 To be stupid or insensible; also ष्टम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A post, a pillar, a column.<BR>2 A stalk, a stem.<BR>3 Stupidity, insensibility.<BR>4 Stupefaction from fear, joy, grief, &c.<BR>5 Coldness, (corporeally,) want of feeling or excitability, paralysis.<BR>6 The suppression of any faculty by magical means.<BR>7 Hindrance, obstruction.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टभि to stop, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकर|स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तम्भकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fence, a railing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्भ opposing, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकिन्|स्तंभकिन्
स्तम्भकिन्<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A musical instrument, covered with leather.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्भक stopping, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Stopping, hindering, obstruction.<BR>2 Suppression of any of the bodily faculties by magical incantations.<BR>3 Stoppage of flow of blood, &c.<BR>4 Any article so employed, a styptic, an astringent.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टभि to stop, aff. युच् or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भित|स्तंभित|स्तम्भितः
स्तम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stupefied, paralysed.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्भ to be stupid, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what spreads, extends, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A layer, a stratum.<BR>2 A bed.<BR>E.<BR>स्तृ to spread, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरिमन्
स्तरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A bed, a couch.<BR>E.<BR>स्तृ to spread, इमनिच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरी
स्तरी<BR>f. (-रीः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>स्तृ to cover, Uṇādi aff. ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तव|स्तवः
स्तव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Praise, eulogium, panegyric, celebrating as a hero or hymning as a deity.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>2 A multitude in general.<BR>3 Praise, eulogium.<BR>4 A panegyrist, a praiser.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. वुन्, or स्था to stay, अवक Uṇādi aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकाचित
स्तवकाचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>In blossom, covered with blossoms.<BR>E.<BR>स्तवक, and आचित heaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवरक|स्तवरकः
स्तवरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fence, a railing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवेय्य|स्तवेय्यः
स्तवेय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, एय्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावक|स्तावकः
स्तावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A praiser, a panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमित|स्तिमितः
स्तिमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wet, moist.<BR>2 Unsteady, shaking. wavering, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्टिम to be moist, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्भि|स्तिम्भिः
स्तिम्भि<BR>m. (-म्भिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 An obstacle, an impediment.<BR>E.<BR>स्तम्भ to stop, Uṇādi aff. इ, and the radical vowel changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्व्वि<BR>m. (-र्व्विः)<BR>A priest versed in the Yajur Veda.<BR>E.<BR>स्तॄ to cover, Uṇādi aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत|स्तुतः
स्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, penegyrised, hymned, glorified.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुति|स्तुतिः
स्तुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Praise, eulogy.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिपाठक|स्तुतिपाठकः
स्तुतिपाठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bard, one who accompanies a chief or an army, to recite the titles and praises of the one, and to inspire the other by chaunting martial exploits, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्तुति praise, and पाठक a reader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिव्रत|स्तुतिव्रतः
स्तुतिव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A bard, a herald: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>स्तुति praise, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्य|स्तुत्यः
स्तुत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be praised, laudable, praise-worthy.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनक|स्तुनकः
स्तुनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ|स्तुभः
स्तुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A he-goat.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टुभ to stop, aff. क; also read स्तभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुम्भ
स्तुम्भ<BR>(उ) स्तुम्भु r. 5th cl. (स्तुभ्नोति) 9th cl. (स्तुभ्नाति)<BR>1 To stop.<BR>2 To be stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुषेप्य|स्तुषेप्यः
स्तुषेप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Excellence, preferableness, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, क्मेप्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप|स्तूपः
स्तूप<BR>r. 4th cl. (स्तूप्यति) r. 10th cl. (स्तूपयति)<BR>To heap, to pile, to collect; also ष्टूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप|स्तूपः
स्तूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A heap, a pile of earth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टूप to heap, aff. घञ्, or ष्टू to praise, प Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=949" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूयमान
स्तूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being praised.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृंह
स्तृंह<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्तृंहति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ<BR>(स्तृ,) r. 5th cl. (स्तृणोति स्तृणुते)<BR>To cover, to clothe, to spread on or over, to strew.<BR>With वि prefixed.<BR>1 To spread widely, to extend.<BR>2 To be diffuse or prolix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष
स्तृक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तृक्षति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृणत्
स्तृणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णती-णत्)<BR>Strewing, spreading over or upon, covering.<BR>E.<BR>स्तृ to strew, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह
स्तृह<BR>(ऊ) स्तृहू r. 6th cl. (स्तृहति)<BR>To hurt, to kill; also ष्टृह, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ<BR>(स्तॄ) r. 9th cl. (स्तृणाति स्तृणीते)<BR>To clothe, to cover, to spread on or over: see स्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄह
स्तॄह<BR>(ऊ) स्तॄहू r. 6th cl. (स्तृहति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन|स्तेनं|स्तेनः
स्तेन<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तेनयति)<BR>To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन|स्तेनं|स्तेनः
स्तेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 Thieving, stealing.<BR>E.<BR>स्तेन to steal, aff. अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप
स्तेप<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तेपयति)<BR>To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेम|स्तेमः
स्तेम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Wetness, moisture.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टिम to be wet, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेय|स्तेयं
स्तेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>E.<BR>स्तेन to steal, यत् aff., the final न rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A goldsmith.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>स्तेय theft, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन|स्तैनं
स्तैन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>E.<BR>स्तेन a thief, अञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्य|स्तैन्यं|स्तैन्यः
स्तैन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>स्तेन to steal, ष्यञ् or ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Little, small.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>2 A drop of water.<BR>n. adv. (-कं)<BR>A little.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टुच to be clear or bright, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकक|स्तोककः
स्तोकक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>स्तोक a little, and कै to sound or cry, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोककाय
स्तोककाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Diminutive, dwarfish.<BR>E.<BR>स्तोक, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be praised, deserving or requiring praise.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-ची-तृ)<BR>Praising, a praiser, a panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्र|स्तोत्रं
स्तोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, aff. ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभ|स्तोभं|स्तोभः
स्तोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Stopping, obstructing.<BR>2 Disrespect, contumely.<BR>3 A division of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टुभ to stop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तोमयति)<BR>1 To praise, to eulogise.<BR>2 To flatter, to wheedle, to coax.<BR>3 To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Crooked, bent.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A heap, a number, a multitude, a quantity.<BR>2 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>3 Praise, eulogium.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 Grain, corn.<BR>4 A stick or staff bound with iron.<BR>E.<BR>ष्टु to praise, मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौपिक|स्तौपिकं
स्तौपिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The small broom carried by a Jaina ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>स्तूप a heap, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Bland, soft, unctuous, smooth.<BR>2 Thick, bulky, gross.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Thickness, grossness, massiveness.<BR>2 Idleness, sloth.<BR>3 Echo.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्यै to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्येन|स्त्येनः
स्त्येन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 Amṛta, nectar.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्यै to sound, &c., इनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्त्यायति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To collect, to crowd; also ष्ट्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A woman or female in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्यै to sound, ड्रट् Uṇādi aff., ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकार्य्य|स्त्रीकार्य
स्त्रीकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Attendance on women, or the women's apartments.<BR>2 The business of women.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and कार्थ्य business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीक्षीर
स्त्रीक्षीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Mother's milk.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगवी
स्त्रीगवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A milch-cow.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a female, गो a cow, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघ्न|स्त्रीघ्नः
स्त्रीघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A woman's murderer.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघोष|स्त्रीघोषः
स्त्रीघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Dawn, daybreak.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचित्तहारिन्
स्त्रीचित्तहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Pleasing or delightful to the female sex.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, चित्त heart or mind, हारिन् what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचिह्न|स्त्रीचिह्नं
स्त्रीचिह्न<BR>n. (-ह्नं)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a female, and चिह्न mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचौर|स्त्रीचौरः
स्त्रीचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A libertine.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजननी
स्त्रीजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The mother of a daughter.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजित|स्त्रीजितः
स्त्रीजित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A henpecked husband.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman or wife, and जित overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीता
स्त्रीता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Womanhood, feminineness.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, तल् aff.; also with त्व, aff. स्त्रीत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधन|स्त्रीधनं
स्त्रीधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Woman's separate property, which is held to be of six kinds: 1. Adhyagnikam, what is given before the sacrificial fire; 2. Adhyāvāhanikam, what is presented during the bridal procession; 3. Ādhivedanikam, what is given on her husband's marrying another wife; 4. Prītidattam, what is given through affection; 5. Śulkam, her dower allowed or perquisites made during marriage; 6. Anvādheyam, a gift from her own or husband's relatives after marriage. Other varieties are enumerated, as the pitṛ, mātṛ, suta, bhrātṛ dattam, what is given by her parents, son, or brother; bandhu dattam, what is given by her kindred; and some enumerate acceptance generally, and inheritance, amongst a woman's titles to property.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्म|स्त्रीधर्म|स्त्रीधर्मः|स्त्रीधर्म्मः
स्त्रीधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Duty of woman.<BR>2 The menstrual excretion.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and धर्म्म peculiar property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्मयोग|स्त्रीधर्मयोग
स्त्रीधर्म्मयोग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Laws or institutes concerning women.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्रीधर्म्म, and योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी|स्त्रीधर्मिणी
स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्रीधर्म्म menstruation, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधव|स्त्रीधवः
स्त्रीधव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A man, a male.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and धव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनिबन्धन|स्त्रीनिबंधन
स्त्रीनिबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A woman's peculiar province or domestic duty, housewifery.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and निबन्धन conferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपर|स्त्रीपरः
स्त्रीपर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A libertine, a lover, a lecher.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंधर्म्म|स्त्रीपुन्धर्म|स्त्रीपुंधर्मः|स्त्रीपुंधर्म्मः
स्त्रीपुंधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Reciprocal duty of husband and wife, or man and woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and पुम् male, धर्म्म law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रिय|स्त्रीप्रियः
स्त्रीप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Liked or loved by women.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a female, and प्रिय dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमत्|स्त्रीमन्त्
स्त्रीमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A husband, a wedded man.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरञ्जन|स्त्रीरंजन|स्त्रीरञ्जनं
स्त्रीरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pān, the mixture of betel-nut, Pān leaf, &c. chewed by the Hindus, and by women especially.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and रञ्जन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरत्न
स्त्रीरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>An excellent woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=950" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीराज्य
स्त्रीराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>The kingdom of women, a country placed by some in the direction of Bhot.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and राज्य kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलिङ्ग|स्त्रीलिंग
स्त्रीलिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Feminine gender.<BR>2 Female organs.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and लिङ्ग mark, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवश|स्त्रीवशः
स्त्रीवश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Subjection to women.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and वश subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविधेय
स्त्रीविधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Uxorious.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and विधेय to be ruled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविवाह|स्त्रीविवाहः
स्त्रीविवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marrying a woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवृत
स्त्रीवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Attended by women.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and वृत surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंग्रहण
स्त्रीसंग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Adultery, seduction.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and संग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसभ
स्त्रीसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>An assembly of women, a number of females.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, सभा- an assembly, neuter in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसम्बन्ध|स्त्रीसंबन्ध|स्त्रीसंबंध|स्त्रीसंबन्धः
स्त्रीसम्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Marriage.<BR>2 Connexion by marriage.<BR>3 Relation or reference to women.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and सम्बन्ध union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसेवा
स्त्रीसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Libertinism.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and सेवा addiction to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वभाव|स्त्रीस्वभावः
स्त्रीस्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An attendant of the women's apartments, a eunuch.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री female, स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहत्या
स्त्रीहत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Murder of a woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहन्तृ
स्त्रीहन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>A woman's murderer.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and हन्तृ who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहरण
स्त्रीहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Carrying off a woman, ravishment.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहारिन्
स्त्रीहारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A ravisher, one who carries off a woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and हृ to take, धिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 Female, feminine.<BR>2 Suited to or good for women.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Womanhood.<BR>2 The nature of woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री a woman, and नञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याजीव|स्त्र्याजीवः
स्त्र्याजीव<BR>m. (वः)<BR>One who lives by his wife's labours or prostitution.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and आजीव subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याभिगमन
स्त्र्याभिगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sexual intercourse.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्री, and अभिगमन going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Staying, abiding, what or who is or stays.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, aff. क; this deriv. most usually occurs in composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग<BR>(ए) स्थगे r. 1st cl. (स्थगति)<BR>To cover; also ष्ठग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Fraudulent, dishonest, a rogue, a cheat.<BR>2 Shameless, abandoned.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>A betel box.<BR>E.<BR>स्थग to cover or hide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगन|स्थगनं
स्थगन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Covering, concealment.<BR>E.<BR>स्थग to cover, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगित|स्थगितं
स्थगित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, hidden, concealed.<BR>E.<BR>स्थग to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगु|स्थगुः
स्थगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>A hump or protuberance on the back, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थग to cover, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिल|स्थंडिल|स्थंडिलं|स्थण्डिलं
स्थण्डिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A level square piece of ground, prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>2 A boundary, a limit, a land mark.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठल to be situated, इलच् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलशायिन्|स्थंडिलशायिन्
स्थण्डिलशायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A devotee who, as an act of mortification or penance, sleeps on the ground which has been prepared for sacrificial purposes.<BR>E.<BR>स्थण्डिल as above, शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलसितक|स्थंडिलसितक|स्थण्डिलसितकं
स्थण्डिलसितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An altar.<BR>E.<BR>स्थण्डिल levelled ground for a sacrifice, षो to destroy, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलेशय|स्थंडिलेशय|स्थण्डिलेशयः
स्थण्डिलेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An ascetic sleeping on the ground: see स्थण्डिलशयिन्.<BR>E.<BR>स्थण्डिल on the ground, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Chief, best, principal.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The performer of the VṚHASPATI sacrifice.<BR>2 A guard or attendant of the women's apartments.<BR>3 A sovereign, a chief.<BR>4 An architect, a master carpenter or builder.<BR>5 A carpenter, a wheel-wright.<BR>6 A charioteer.<BR>7 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>स्थ who is or who is placed, and पति master, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Distressed, living in difficulty or distress.<BR>2 Bent with pain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थ what stands, or is, पुट to contract, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल|स्थलं
स्थल<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्थलति)<BR>To stand, to be firm; also ष्ठल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल|स्थलं
स्थल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>Place, site, soil, dry or firm ground.<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A spot of dry ground prepared by art or drained and raised, &c.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A tent, a house of cloth.<BR>2 A mound, a hillock.<BR>3 Point, case, subject (of a description or discussion.)<BR>4 Part (of a book.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठल to be firm, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलचर
स्थलचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what goes on land, terrene.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल, and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलज
स्थलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Terrene, terrestrial, what is produced on land.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्म|स्थलपद्मं|स्थलपद्मः
स्थलपद्म<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थल dry ground, and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्मिनी
स्थलपद्मिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थल dry ground, and पद्मिनी a cluster of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलमञ्जरी
स्थलमञ्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थल dry ground, and मञ्जरी a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलविग्रह|स्थलविग्रहः
स्थलविग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Battle on plain or level ground.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल, and विग्रह war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलशृङ्गाट|स्थलशृङ्गाटः
स्थलशृङ्गाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, (Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थल dry ground, and शृङ्गाट a sort of trapa; also with कन् added, स्थलशृङ्गाटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलसीमन्
स्थलसीमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A boundary, a land-mark.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल dry ground, and सीमन् a boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीदेवता
स्थलीदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A terrestrial demigod, as a faun, a dryad, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थली the dry land, and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीय
स्थलीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to dry ground.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशय|स्थलेशयः
स्थलेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An amphibious animal, as the tortoise, otter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थले on dry ground, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवि|स्थविः
स्थवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to stay, Uṇādi aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Old, aged.<BR>2 Fixed, firm, steady.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 An old man.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, (a long time, &c.) किरच् Uṇādi aff., and स्थव substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्टं)<BR>Very fat or corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल bulky, इष्ठन् superlative affix, the final of the adjective dropped, and vowel changed; also with ईयसुन् similar aff. स्थवीयम् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु<BR>mfn. (-णुः-णुः-णु)<BR>Firm, fixed, steady, stable.<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A stake, a pin.<BR>3 A post.<BR>4 A spear, a dart.<BR>5 A nest of white ants.<BR>mn. (-णुः-णु)<BR>1 The trunk of a tree of which the branches have been lopped off.<BR>2 The trunk of any tree.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand, Uṇādi aff. नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुछेद|स्थाणुच्छेद|स्थाणुच्छेदः
स्थाणुछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>One who cuts down or clears away timber.<BR>E.<BR>स्थाणु, and छेद who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=951" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थांडिलः|स्थाण्डिलः
स्थाण्डिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An ascetic sleeping on the bare ground, or ground prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>2 A mendicant, a religious beggar.<BR>E.<BR>स्थण्डिल ground, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातव्य|स्थातव्यं
स्थातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be placed or fixed.<BR>2 To be appointed or determined, to be ordained or agreed upon.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what stays or stands.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, aff. तृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थान|स्थानं
स्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Place, spot, site, situation.<BR>2 Stay, staying, continuance, being fixed or stationary and exempt from increase or diminution.<BR>3 Likeness, resemblance.<BR>4 Leisure, interval.<BR>5 An open place in a town, a green, a plain, a square.<BR>6 A house, a dwelling.<BR>7 A section, a chapter, a book.<BR>8 One of the three objects of government, the middle state, as neither loss nor gain, nor discomfiture nor success, nor expenditure nor accumulation, &c.<BR>9 A town, a city.<BR>10 Office, appointment.<BR>11 Degree, station.<BR>12 Halt.<BR>13 Firmness of troops, keeping in array.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, to be fixed, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानक|स्थानकं
स्थानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A basin or trench dug for water at the root of a tree.<BR>2 A town, a city.<BR>3 A bubble or a bead on spirits or wine.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानचञ्चला
स्थानचञ्चला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Ocimum pilosum.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थान place, चञ्चला trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानपाल|स्थानपालः
स्थानपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A guard, a keeper, a watchman.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान a place, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानभ्रष्ट|स्थानभ्रष्टः
स्थानभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Displaced, out of place, fallen or removed from the natural or usual situation.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान place, and भ्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानयोग|स्थानयोगः
स्थानयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Assignment of suitable places.<BR>2 Proper mode or place for preserving articles.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान, and योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानाध्यक्ष|स्थानाध्यक्षः
स्थानाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The superintendant or governor of a place or post.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान a place, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानासेध|स्थानासेधः
स्थानासेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Confinement to a place, imprisonment, arrest.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान, and आसेध durance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Local, belonging to place or site.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The governor, or superintendant of any place or district.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान a place, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Having place or fixation, placed, abiding, permanent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान place, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or suitable to any place, fit for or belonging to it, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A city, a town.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान place, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाने
स्थाने<BR>ind.<BR>1 Properly, suitably, fitly.<BR>2 Because, on account of.<BR>3 Like, resembling, similarly.<BR>4 Truly.<BR>E.<BR>स्थान place, in the seventh case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Placing, fixing, regulating, ordering.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The director of the stage business, a stage manager.<BR>2 A founder, the erector of a temple or image, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to be or stand, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्य|स्थापत्यः
स्थापत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A guard of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>स्था who stays, (in the haram, the wife or concubine of a man of rank,) and पति master, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापन|स्थापनं
स्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Placing, founding, fixing, erecting.<BR>2 Ordering, directing.<BR>3 Fixing or concentrating the thoughts upon the object of meditation, abstraction, mental controul.<BR>4 A ceremony performed in the month of utero-gestation.<BR>5 A dwelling, a habitation.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Ordering or arranging as a drama, stage management.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, causal form, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयत्
स्थापयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Fixing, placing, establishing.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयित्वा
स्थापयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having placed, fixed, erected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापित|स्थापितं
स्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deposited, placed.<BR>2 Ordered, directed.<BR>3 Certain, established, ascertained.<BR>4 Firm, steady.<BR>5 Set up, erected.<BR>6 Founded, endowed.<BR>7 Placed in a post or situation.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or be, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापितवत्
स्थापितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Placing, having placed.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to place, causal v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Strength, power.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand or stay, Uṇādi aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Steady, firm, unchangeable, invariable.<BR>2 Who or what stays, or is, &c.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A class of those feelings or passions which are the objects of poetic description: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, णिनि aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिभाव|स्थायिभावः
स्थायिभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Fixed or permanent condition.<BR>2 A feeling or passion, which is the object of poetical or dramatic description, and is classed sometimes as one of three, but more usually as one of two orders of such objects; this order being opposed especially to the Vyabhicārī Bhāvas: the feelings or conditions termed Sthāyi are eight, viz. desire, mirth, sorrow, heroism, anger, fear, aversion, and astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>स्थायिन् fixed, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Stationary.<BR>2 Steady, firm.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The overseer of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand or be, उकञ् aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाल|स्थालं
स्थाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A caldron.<BR>2 Any culinary utensil.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 An earthen pot or boiler.<BR>2 The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suaveolens.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand, Uṇādi aff. आलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपक्व|स्थालीपक्वं
स्थालीपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Boiled, dressed in a pot or boiler.<BR>E.<BR>स्थाली a pot, पक्व cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीविल
स्थालीविल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The interior or hollow of a boiler.<BR>E.<BR>स्थाली a pot, and विल vacuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीविलीय
स्थालीविलीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit to be boiled or dressed.<BR>E.<BR>स्थालीविल the interior of a pot, छ aff.; also with यत् aff. स्थालीविल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Fixed, stationary, stable, immoveable.<BR>2 Regular, established.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A bow-string.<BR>2 Immoveable property, land or houses.<BR>3 Family property, jewels, &c. which have been long in a family, and which ought not to be sold or given away.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Old age, any time after seventy in men, and fifty in women.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, (a long time,) किरच् Uṇādi aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासक|स्थासकः
स्थासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Perfuming the person, smearing the body with fragrant unguents, as of Sandal, &c.<BR>2 A bubble of water or any fluid.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, स aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=952" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु<BR>n. (-सु)<BR>Bodily strength or capability.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, or be, सु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु<BR>mfn. (-स्नुः-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>1 Firm, stable.<BR>2 Durable, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, स्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नुता
स्थास्नुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Firmness, stability.<BR>E.<BR>स्थास्नु, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिक|स्थिकः
स्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A buttock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Steady, firm, immovable.<BR>2 Stayed, stopped.<BR>3 Determined, resolved, decreed, established.<BR>4 Upright, virtuous, steady in conduct.<BR>5 Agreed, engaged, contracted, promised.<BR>6 Risen, got up.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितधी
स्थितधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Firm, unmoved, calm.<BR>E.<BR>स्थित, and धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रज्ञ|स्थितप्रज्ञः
स्थितप्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Calm, content, free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>स्थित, and प्रज्ञा wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रेमन्
स्थितप्रेमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A faithful friend.<BR>E.<BR>स्थित established, and प्रेमन् affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितवत्|स्थितवन्त्
स्थितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Staying, abiding, stationary.<BR>2 Waiting, attending.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिति|स्थितिः
स्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Stay, staying, being fixed or stationary.<BR>2 Correctness of conduct, continuance in the path of duty.<BR>3 Limit, boundary, term.<BR>4 Stop, cessation, pause.<BR>5 Determination, order, decree.<BR>6 Honor, dignity.<BR>7 (In astronomy,) Duration of an eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमत्|स्थितिमन्त्
स्थितिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Firm, stable.<BR>2 Steady, (in purpose, or conduct,) upright, firm, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिस्थापक|स्थितिस्थापकः
स्थितिस्थापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what fixes, places, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Elasticity.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिति, and स्थापक what causes to stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित्वा
स्थित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having stayed, stood, stopped, been, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to stay, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Firm, fixed, steady, immovable.<BR>2 Hard, solid.<BR>3 Permanent, durable, lasting.<BR>4 Firm, steady, (morally,) uninfluenced by pleasure or pain, &c.<BR>5 Cool, collected.<BR>6 Constant, faithful.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A deity, an immortal.<BR>2 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A tree.<BR>5 Final emancipation from existence.<BR>6 The planet SATURN.<BR>7 A bull.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>3 A medicinal root, commonly Kākolī.<BR>4 Silk-cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or be, Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरगन्ध|स्थिरगंध|स्थिरगन्धः
स्थिरगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 The Pandanus odoratissimus.<BR>2 Trumpet flower.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरचक्र|स्थिरचक्रः
स्थिरचक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A Bauddha saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरचेतस्
स्थिरचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तं)<BR>Firm, resolute, steady, constant.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरच्छद|स्थिरच्छदः
स्थिरच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch tree of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरच्छाय|स्थिरच्छायः
स्थिरच्छाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tree by the road side, &c. giving shelter to travellers or persons passing.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरजिह्व|स्थिरजिह्वः
स्थिरजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर immovable, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरजीविता
स्थिरजीविता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The silk-cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting (a long time), and जीवित alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरतर|स्थिरतरः
स्थिरतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Firm, fixed, stationary.<BR>2 Permanent, durable, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरता
स्थिरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Stability, firmness.<BR>2 Moral firmness, fortitude.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर with तल् added; also with त्व, स्थिरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरदंष्ट्र|स्थिरदंष्ट्रः
स्थिरदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 VIṢṆU in the boar Avatāra.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर hard, and दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरपत्र|स्थिरपत्रः
स्थिरपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The marshy date tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरपुष्प|स्थिरपुष्पः
स्थिरपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2 The Bakul, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरमति|स्थिरमतिः
स्थिरमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Steady, firm, deliberate.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरयोनि|स्थिरयोनिः
स्थिरयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A large tree, one that gives shade and shelter.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, lasting, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरयौवन|स्थिरयौवनः
स्थिरयौवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Vidyādhara, a peculiar kind of demi-god.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर perpetual, यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिररङ्गा
स्थिररङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 Indigo.<BR>2 Dār-haldi, a sort of Curcuma.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, and रङ्ग colour or dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरांह्रिप
स्थिरांह्रिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The marshy date tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर hard or lasting, and अंह्रिप tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरात्मन्
स्थिरात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>1 Firm, resolute, unmoved.<BR>2 Stable, steady.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरायु|स्थिरायुः
स्थिरायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर lasting long, and आयु or आयुस् life, whence also स्थिरायुस् m. (-युः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुड
स्थुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्थुडति)<BR>To clothe or cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुरिन्
स्थुरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A packhorse, a horse carrying loads: see स्थौरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूणा
स्थूणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The post of pillar of a house.<BR>2 An iron image.<BR>3 An anvil.<BR>4 A disease.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, न Uṇādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूर|स्थूरः
स्थूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay, ऊरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिन्
स्थूरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A packhorse or one carrying loads on his back.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल bulk, size, इनि affix, and ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्थूलयते)<BR>To increase, to fatten, to become big or bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Fat, corpulent, bulky.<BR>2 Stupid, dull, ignorant.<BR>3 Large, great.<BR>4 Coarse.<BR>5 Clumsy.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A heap, a quantity.<BR>2 A tent.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A sort of pepper, (Pothos officinalis)<BR>2 A pumpkin gourd.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The jack fruit tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल to be large or fat, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक|स्थूलकः
स्थूलक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Large, bulky.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल the same, कन added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकङ्गु|स्थूलकङ्गुः
स्थूलकङ्गु<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>A wild sort of kidney-bean.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and कङ्गु coix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकण्टिका
स्थूलकण्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The silk-cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, कण्ट a thorn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकन्द|स्थूलकन्दः
स्थूलकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>2 Another sort, (Arum Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाय
स्थूलकाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Large bodied, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाष्ठधह्
स्थूलकाष्ठधह्<BR>m. (-धक्)<BR>The trunk of a tree or any piece of timber on fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, काष्ठ wood, and दह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाष्ठाग्नि|स्थूलकाष्ठाग्निः
स्थूलकाष्ठाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A large piece of wood on fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, काष्ठ wood, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=953" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक्ष्वेड|स्थूलक्ष्वेडः
स्थूलक्ष्वेड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and क्ष्वेड a bambu rod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलचाप|स्थूलचापः
स्थूलचाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A bow used in cleaning cotton.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलजीरक|स्थूलजीरकः
स्थूलजीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Kalonji, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and जीरक cumin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलता
स्थूलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Coarseness, bulkiness.<BR>2 Dulness, stupidity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to स्थूल; also with त्व, स्थूलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदण्ड|स्थूलदण्डः
स्थूलदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A sort of reed, (Arundo.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, दण्ड a stick or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदर्भ|स्थूलदर्भः
स्थूलदर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A kind of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and दर्भ Poa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदला
स्थूलदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Aloe plant.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलधी
स्थूलधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Dull, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनाल|स्थूलनालः
स्थूलनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large kind of reed.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and नाल a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनास|स्थूलनासं|स्थूलनासः
स्थूलनास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and नास for नासिका nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनासिक|स्थूलनासिकः
स्थूलनासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hog, a boar.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, नासिका the nose, made masc. in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपट्ट|स्थूलपट्टः
स्थूलपट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>Cotton.<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Coarse cloth.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and पट्ट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपट्टाक|स्थूलपट्टाकः
स्थूलपट्टाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Coarse cloth.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, पट्ट cloth, अक to be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपाद|स्थूलपादः
स्थूलपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपुष्प|स्थूलपुष्पः
स्थूलपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A flower, a sort of mountain Clitorea.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलबुद्धि
स्थूलबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Stupid, dull.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलभद्र|स्थूलभद्रः
स्थूलभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>One of the sacred personages called Śrutā Kevalīs by the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलमरिच|स्थूलमरिचं
स्थूलमरिच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A fragrant medicinal berry, commonly Kakoli.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and मरिच black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष|स्थूललक्षः
स्थूललक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Munificent, liberal.<BR>2 Learned, well. read.<BR>3 Remembering both benefits and offences.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, much, and लक्ष mark or note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष्य|स्थूललक्ष्यः
स्थूललक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Munificent, liberal.<BR>2 Dealing profusely or indiscriminately.<BR>3 Recollecting benefits and injuries.<BR>4 Taking careless aim.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल a heap, (of wealth,) and लक्ष्य to be remarked or seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष्यत्व
स्थूललक्ष्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Liberality.<BR>2 Aiming carelessly.<BR>3 Retentiveness of benefits and injuries.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूललक्ष्य, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलवर्त्मकृत्
स्थूलवर्त्मकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलवल्कल|स्थूलवल्कलः
स्थूलवल्कल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Red Lodh, a tree, the bark of which is used as an astringent in tanning, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल thick, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशरीर
स्थूलशरीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Large bodied.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The external or material body.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशाटक|स्थूलशाटकः
स्थूलशाटक<BR>mf. (-टकः-टका or -टिका)<BR>Thick or coarse cloth.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल thick, and शाटक cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशाटि|स्थूलशाटिः
स्थूलशाटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>Coarse cloth.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and शाटि cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशिरस्
स्थूलशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Large-headed.<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A large head or summit.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल bulky, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशीर्षिका
स्थूलशीर्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A large headed ant.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, शीर्ष the head, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलहस्त|स्थूलहस्तः
स्थूलहस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>An elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलास्य|स्थूलास्यः
स्थूलास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>स्थल large, and आस्य face or head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलिन्
स्थूलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलीभूत
स्थूलीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thick, bulky.<BR>2 Stupid.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and भूत become, with च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलोच्चय|स्थूलोच्चयः
स्थूलोच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Incompleteness, deficiency, defect.<BR>2 The middle pace of an elephant, neither quick nor slow.<BR>3 Pimples on the face.<BR>4 A hill at the foot of a mountain, or a rocky fragment detached from its primitive site and forming a separate projection or promontory.<BR>5 A hollow at the root of the elephant's tusks.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, and उच्चय lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेमन्
स्थेमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Fixedness, firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेय|स्थेयः
स्थेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be fixed or determined.<BR>2 To be placed.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A judge, an arbitrator, one who decides upon a dispute between two parties.<BR>2 A domestic priest.<BR>E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेयस्
स्थेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Firm, stable, fixed.<BR>2 Eternal, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative, and स्था substituted for the adjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेष्ठ|स्थेष्ठः
स्थेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Firm, stable, fixed, durable.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर firm, इष्ठन् aff., and स्था substituted for the primitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य|स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Firmness, stability.<BR>2 Firmness of mind, resolution, fortitude.<BR>E.<BR>स्थिर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थोरिन्
स्थोरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A pack-horse: see स्थोरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेय|स्थौणेयं|स्थौणेयः
स्थौणेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूणा an image, ढक् aff.; also with कन् added, स्थौणेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौर|स्थौरं
स्थौर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Strength, power.<BR>2 A load for a horse or ass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, bulky, अण् aff., and ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरिन्
स्थौरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A pack-horse, one that carries burthens on his back like an ox or ass.<BR>2 A strong horse.<BR>E.<BR>स्थौर strength, इनि aff., or according to some authorities स्थुरा a pack-saddle, इनि aff., deriv. irr.; it is also read स्थूरिन्, स्थुरिन्, and स्थोरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौलशीर्ष|स्थौलशीर्षं
स्थौलशीर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Large-headed, having or relating to a large head or summit.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल large, शिरस् the head, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल्य|स्थौल्यं
स्थौल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Bulk, size, coarseness, largeness.<BR>E.<BR>स्थूल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ्यूम
स्थ्यूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Light, lustre.<BR>2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bathing, ablution.<BR>2 Washing, sprinkling, wetting.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe or purify by bathing, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपित|स्नपितः
स्नपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sprinkled, wetted, bathed, washed.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नव|स्नवः
स्नव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Oozing, dripping, trickling.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णु to distil or ooze, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नसा
स्नसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A tendon, a muscle.<BR>E.<BR>स्नस to eject, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्
स्नात्<BR>mfn. (-स्नान्-स्नान्ती-स्नात्)<BR>Bathing, performing ablution.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात|स्नातः
स्नात<BR>m. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bathed, washed, purified, (by ablution.)<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An initiated householder: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=954" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातक|स्नातकः
स्नातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An initiated householder, a man of the three first classes, who having completed the term prescribed for his studies becomes a housekeeper: if at the end of this period, he has not acquired a knowledge of the Veda, he is called Vratasnātaka; if he has acquired that knowledge earlier, he is termed Vidyāsnātaka; and if he finishes his regular studies at the same time that the period of study expires, he is named Ubhayasnātaka.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्वा
स्नात्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having bathed.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नान|स्नानं
स्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bathing, ablution, purification by bathing.<BR>2 Any thing proper for ablution, water, perfumed powder for the body, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानतृण|स्नानतृणं
स्नानतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Kuśa, grass.<BR>E.<BR>स्नान ablution, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानवस्त्र
स्नानवस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A cloth put on at or after bathing.<BR>E.<BR>स्नान, and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानशील
स्नानशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bathing, performing ablution, (especially in sacred waters.)<BR>E.<BR>स्नान, and शील practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानीय|स्नानीयं
स्नानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Ablutionary, fit or proper for bathing in, or to be used at bathing, as perfumed powders, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Water or other article proper for bathing.<BR>E.<BR>स्नान ablution, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापक|स्नापकः
स्नापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A servant who brings water, or who applies it in bathing.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायिन्
स्नायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>A bather, a performer of ablutions.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, णिनि aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायु|स्नायुः
स्नायु<BR>f. (-युः)<BR>A tendon, a muscle, described as a tubular vessel attached to the bones at either end, and carrying vital air.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णा to bathe, उण् Uṇādi aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाव|स्नावः
स्नाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A tendon, a muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निट
स्निट<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्नेटयति)<BR>1 To be greasy or unctuous.<BR>2 To fuse or melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध|स्निग्धं|स्निग्धः
स्निग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Smooth, oily, unctuous, greasy.<BR>2 Amiable, kind, affectionate.<BR>3 Coarse, thick.<BR>4 Cooling, emollient.<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>A friend.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>Marrow.<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>1 Bees's wax.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 Thickness, coarseness.<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>1 A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>2 Another kind, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to be unctuous, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धता
स्निग्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Affection, kindness.<BR>2 Unctuousness, oiliness.<BR>E.<BR>स्निग्ध affectionate, तल् aff. of the abstract; also स्निग्धत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धतण्डुल|स्निग्धतंडुल|स्निग्धतण्डुलः
स्निग्धतण्डुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Rice of quick growth.<BR>E.<BR>स्निग्ध oily, तण्डुल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धदारु|स्निग्धदारुः
स्निग्धदारु<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>1 A pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>2 Another kind, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>स्निग्ध unctuous, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धपत्र|स्निग्धपत्रः
स्निग्धपत्र<BR>mf. (-त्रः-त्रा)<BR>The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>E.<BR>स्निग्ध unctuous, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु<BR>mn. (-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>Table land, the level summit or edge of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णु to trickle, (the water or snow from it,) डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुत|स्नुतः
स्नुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Flowing, dropping, oozing, trickling, distilled.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णु to ooze, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A daughter-in-law.<BR>2 The milk-hedge plant.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णु to distil, Uṇādi aff. स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह्<BR>f. (-स्नुक्)<BR>The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्णुह to vomit, (its milk being used as an emetic,) aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added, स्नुहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहि|स्नुहिः
स्नुहि<BR>f. (-हिः-ही)<BR>A plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum.)<BR>E.<BR>ष्णुह to vomit, (see the last,) कि aff., and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेह|स्नेहः
स्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Affection, kindness.<BR>2 Oil, unguent, grease, any unctuous or greasy substance.<BR>3 Oiliness, lubricity, viscidity.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णीह to be unctuous, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहछेद|स्नेहच्छेद|स्नेहच्छेदः
स्नेहछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Cessation or loss of regard.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and छेद severing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन्
स्नेहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>1 A friend.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A disease.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to be affectionate, &c., कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन|स्नेहनं
स्नेहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Unctuousness, being or becoming oily, &c.<BR>2 Anointing, unction, rubbing with unguents, oil, &c.<BR>3 An emollient, an unguent, or liniment.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to be unctuous, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहपक्व
स्नेहपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Dressed with oil.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and पक्व cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहप्रिय|स्नेहप्रियः
स्नेहप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह oil, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभू
स्नेहभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The phlegmatic humor.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह oily substance, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभूमि|स्नेहभूमिः
स्नेहभूमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 An object of affection.<BR>2 Any substance yielding oil or grease.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहरङ्ग|स्नेहरंग|स्नेहरङ्गः
स्नेहरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह oil, रङ्ग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहवत्|स्नेहवन्त्
स्नेहवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Affectionate.<BR>2 Unctuous, oily.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहविद्ध|स्नेहविद्धं|स्नेहविद्धः
स्नेहविद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह oil, and विद्ध pierced, impregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहाक्त
स्नेहाक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Oiled, greased, lubricated.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and अक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहानुवृत्ति|स्नेहानुवृत्तिः
स्नेहानुवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Affectionate or friendly intercourse.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह, and अनुवृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहाश|स्नेहाशः
स्नेहाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह oil, and अश what consumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित|स्नेहितः
स्नेहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Kind, affectionate.<BR>2 Beloved, the object of affection.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A friend.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह affection, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिन्
स्नेहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Affectionate, friendly.<BR>2 Oily, unctuous.<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>1 A friend.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>E.<BR>स्नेह affection, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहु|स्नेहुः
स्नेहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to be unctuous, उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध्य|स्नैग्ध्यं
स्नैग्ध्य<BR>n. (-ग्ध्यं)<BR>1 Oiliness, smoothness, lubricity.<BR>2 Affectionateness.<BR>E.<BR>स्निग्ध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पद
स्पद<BR>(इ) स्पदि r. 1st cl. (स्पन्दते)<BR>1 To quake, to shake, to tremble slightly, to throb, to beat.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दन|स्पंदन|स्पंदनं|स्पन्दनं
स्पन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Beating, throbbing, pulsation, quivering.<BR>2 Quickening of the child in the womb.<BR>3 Going.<BR>E.<BR>स्पदि to throb, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दमान
स्पन्दमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Throbbing, beating.<BR>2 Going.<BR>E.<BR>स्पदि to beat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दित|स्पंदित
स्पन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Throbbing, beating.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pulsation.<BR>E.<BR>स्पदि to throb, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परितृ
स्परितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>The agent or active cause of pain or distress, as an enemy, an oppressor, a disease, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृ to breathe, aff. तृच्, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=955" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्ध
स्पर्द्ध<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्पर्द्धते)<BR>To vie, to envy, to desire another's reduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्ध
स्पर्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>Envious, emulous.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्द्ध envy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धता
स्पर्द्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Enviousness, emulation.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्द्ध, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धा
स्पर्द्धा<BR>f. (-र्द्धा)<BR>1 Envy, emulation, rivalry.<BR>2 Equality, sameness.<BR>3 Successive elevation.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्द्धा to envy or vie with, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धित
स्पर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Vied or contended with, defied.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्द्ध to vie with, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धिन्
स्पर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिणी-र्द्धि)<BR>1 Emulous, envious.<BR>2 Superb, gorgeous.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्द्धा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्पर्शयति)<BR>1 To take.<BR>2 To unite, to join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Touch, contact.<BR>2 The thing touching or feeling.<BR>3 Gift, donation.<BR>4 Sickness, disease.<BR>5 Morbid heat.<BR>6 A consonant of either of the five first classes of the alphabet.<BR>7 An enemy, a disease, &c., the agent or instrument of pain, trouble, or distress.<BR>8 Air, wind.<BR>f. (-र्शा)<BR>A wanton, an unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शक|स्पर्शकः
स्पर्शक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Touching, toucher, that which touches or is in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शन|स्पर्शनं|स्पर्शनः
स्पर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Touch, contact.<BR>2 Gift, donation.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनीय
स्पर्शनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>What is to be or may be touched, sensible, tangible.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणि|स्पर्शमणिः
स्पर्शमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A stone, the philosopher's stone, converting every thing it touches to gold.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्श touch, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणिप्रभव|स्पर्शमणिप्रभवं
स्पर्शमणिप्रभव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्शमणि a stone, and प्रभव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शलज्जा
स्पर्शलज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जाः)<BR>A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्श the touch, and लज्जा ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शशुद्धा
स्पर्शशुद्धा<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्श touch, and शुद्धा pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शस्पन्द|स्पर्शस्पंद|स्पर्शस्पन्दः
स्पर्शस्पन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्श the touch, and स्पन्द who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शानन्दा
स्पर्शानन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>One of the Apsarasas.<BR>E.<BR>स्पर्श touch, आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टृ
स्पर्ष्टृ<BR>m. (-र्ष्टा)<BR>1 Morbid heat.<BR>2 The agent or instrument of bodily pain.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश|स्पशः
स्पश<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्पशति-ते)<BR>1 To obstruct, to oppose.<BR>2 To string together.<BR>3 To touch.<BR>4 To make evident or clear.<BR>5 To inform.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्पाशयते)<BR>1 To take.<BR>2 To unite, to connect, or join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश|स्पशः
स्पश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 Fighting with a dangerous animal, as a tiger, a buffalo, &c. for reward.<BR>E.<BR>स्पश to inform, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Evident, manifest, apparent.<BR>2 Clear, easy, intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>स्पश to make clear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टार्थ
स्पष्टार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Clear, perspicuous, intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>स्पष्ट, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टीकरण
स्पष्टीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making clear or intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>स्पष्ट, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टीकृत|स्पष्टीकृतं
स्पष्टीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Explained, expounded, elucidated, made clear, and intelligible.<BR>2 Made manifest, revealed, exposed.<BR>E.<BR>स्पष्ट easy, clear, च्चि augment, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पाशित
स्पाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused to be stopped, hindered, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्पश to stop, causal v., क्त aff. form, irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृ
स्पृ<BR>r. 5th. cl. (स्पृणोति)<BR>1 To please, to gratify.<BR>2 To cherish, to protect.<BR>3 To breathe, to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृक्का
स्पृक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, कक् aff., form. irr.; also पृक्का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश|स्पृशः
स्पृश<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्पृशति)<BR>To touch, to take with the hand.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To tread upon.<BR>2 To bathe, to sip water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Who or what touches.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशत्
स्पृशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शती-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Touching.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशा
स्पृशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A plant, commonly Kaṅkālī.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशी
स्पृशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A prickly nightshade, (Solanum Jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, क and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्य
स्पृश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>What may be or is to be felt or touched.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट|स्पृष्टः
स्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Touched, felt.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टव्य
स्पृष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What is to be or may be touched, felt, &c., स्पृश to touch, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टि|स्पृष्टिः
स्पृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Touch, feeling, contact.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट्वा
स्पृष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having felt or touched.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह
स्पृह<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्पृहयति)<BR>To wish, to desire, to long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयमाण
स्पृहयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Desiring, wishing.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृह to desire, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहा
स्पृहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृह to wish, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहनीय
स्पृहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Desirable, to be wished.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृह to wish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयालु|स्पृहयालुः
स्पृहयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Wishing, desiring, cupidinous.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृह to wish, आलुच् aff., and युक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्य|स्पृह्यः
स्पृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be wished, desirable.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A large kind of lime.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृह to wish, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what touches, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 Morbid heat.<BR>2 The agent or instrumental cause of pain or distress, as an enemy, a disease, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, तृच् aff., and the first ऋ converted to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट|स्फटः
स्फट<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्फटति)<BR>1 To open, to unfold, to burst.<BR>2 To break or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट|स्फटः
स्फट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>A snake's expanded neck or hood.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Alum.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to swell, aff. क, and the vowel changed to अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिक|स्फटिकः
स्फटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to expand, क्वुन् aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकप्रभ
स्फटिकप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Crystalline, transparent.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिक, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकमय
स्फटिकमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of crystal.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिक, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाचल|स्फटिकाचलः
स्फटिकाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mount Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिक crystal, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाद्रिभिद|स्फटिकाद्रिभिदः
स्फटिकाद्रिभिद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिकाद्रि Kailāsa, and भिद what breaks, what shames, being whiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाश्मन्
स्फटिकाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिक the same, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फड
स्फड<BR>(इ) स्फडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (स्फण्डति-स्फण्डयति)<BR>To jest or joke with, to smile or laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फर|स्फरः
स्फर<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्फरति)<BR>1 To throb, to beat, to tremble.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To be manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=956" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फरण|स्फरणं
स्फरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throbbing, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>स्फर to throb, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फल
स्फल<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्फलति)<BR>1 To throb, to beat, to tremble.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To be manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटक|स्फाटकं|स्फाटकः
स्फाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>स्फट to break, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिक|स्फाटिकं
स्फाटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Crystalline, made &c. of crystal.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>स्फटिक the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिकोपल|स्फाटिकोपलः
स्फाटिकोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाटिक the same, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटीक|स्फाटीकं
स्फाटीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Crystal:<BR>E.<BR>see स्फटिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फात|स्फातः
स्फात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Swollen, enlarged.<BR>E.<BR>स्फायी to increase, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाति|स्फातिः
स्फाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Increase, growth.<BR>2 Swelling, intumescence.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाय to increase, क्तिन् aff., and the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाय
स्फाय<BR>(ई) स्फायी r. 1st cl. (स्फायते)<BR>To grow, to increase, to become large or bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
स्फार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Loud.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Throbbing, quivering.<BR>2 A bubble or flaw in gold, &c.<BR>3 Twanging as of a bow-string.<BR>E.<BR>स्फर to throb, aff. घञ्, or स्फाय to swell, रक् Uṇādi aff., and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारण|स्फारणं
स्फारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throbbing, shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>स्फर to throb, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाल|स्फालः
स्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Throbbing, quivering, trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>स्फल to shake, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालन|स्फालनं
स्फालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Shaking, quivering.<BR>2 Rubbing, friction.<BR>3 Rubbing or patting a horse.<BR>E.<BR>स्फल to shake, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फावयत्
स्फावयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Increasing, augmenting.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाय to increase, शतृ aff., वङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिक्घातनक|स्फिक्घातनकः
स्फिक्घातनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिच्
स्फिच्<BR>f. du. (-चौ)<BR>The buttocks.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाय to swell, डिच् aff. or स्फिट to hurt, aff. क्विप्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट
स्फिट<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्फेटयति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, or kill.<BR>2 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्ट
स्फिट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्फिट्टयति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>2 To dwell.<BR>3 To give.<BR>4 To be strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाय to swell, किरच् aff. deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीत|स्फीतः
स्फीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Much, many.<BR>2 Swollen, enlarged.<BR>3 Successful, prosperous, risen in rank or fortune.<BR>4 Affected by hereditary disease.<BR>E.<BR>स्फायी to swell, aff. क्त; also स्फात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीति|स्फीतिः
स्फीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Increase, enlargement.<BR>2 Prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>स्फाय to swell, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्फेटते) r. 6th cl. (स्फुटति)<BR>To blow, to blossom, to open as a bud or flower.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्फोटयति or with आङ् prefixed आस्फोटयति) also (इर) स्फुटिर r. 1st cl. (स्फोटति) and (इ) स्फुटि r. 1st cl. (स्फुण्टति)<BR>1 To divide, to break, to tear, to pierce.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR>स्फुटि r. 10th cl. (स्फुण्टयति)<BR>To laugh at or with, to jest, to joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Blown, opened, expanded, (as a flower.)<BR>2 Apparent, manifest, evident.<BR>3 Known, understood.<BR>4 Plain, distinct.<BR>5 Spread, diffused.<BR>6 White.<BR>7 Burst, broken.<BR>8 Rent, torn.<BR>9 (In astronomy,) True or apparent, as स्फुटसूर्य्यगतिः true or apparent motion of the sun.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>The expanded hood of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to blow, as a flower, &c. aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटत्
स्फुटत्<BR>mfn. (-टन्-टन्ती-टती-टत्)<BR>1 Bursting, blowing.<BR>2 Becoming manifest or clear.<BR>3 Evolving.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटता
स्फुटता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Manifestation, evidence.<BR>2 Blossoming.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटन|स्फुटनं
स्फुटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tearing, rending.<BR>2 Opening, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to blow, ल्युट् aff., and the vowel unchanged; also स्फोटन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटफल
स्फुटफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>(In geometry,) Distinct or precise area.<BR>E.<BR>ष्फुट, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटवल्कली
स्फुटवल्कली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Heart-pea.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट burst, and वल्कल bark or rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटार्थ
स्फुटार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Intelligible, obvious, significant.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटि|स्फुटिः
स्फुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>1 Kibe, swelling of the feet.<BR>2 A sort of melon, (Cucumis momordica, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to open or break, and कि aff., with ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटित|स्फुटितः
स्फुटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Budded, blown.<BR>2 Broken, burst.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to blow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्ट
स्फुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्फुट्टयति)<BR>To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुड
स्फुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्फुडति)<BR>To clothe, to cover.<BR>(इ) स्फुडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (स्फुण्डति-स्फुण्डयति)<BR>To laugh at, to jest, to joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्कार|स्फुत्कारः
स्फुत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Crackling, burning.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुत् imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर|स्फुरः
स्फुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्फुरति)<BR>1 To throb, to beat.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To swell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर|स्फुरः
स्फुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A shield.<BR>2 Throbbing, trembling.<BR>3 Swelling.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to shake, &c., aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरण|स्फुरणं
स्फुरण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Trembling, throbbing, pulsation.<BR>2 Quivering of the lips, throbbing of the eyes, &c.<BR>3 Expansion of mind.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to shake, aff. ल्युट् or युच्, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरत्
स्फुरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Quivering, trembling, shaking, throbbing.<BR>2 Expanding, swelling.<BR>3 Going, moving.<BR>4 Going tremulously.<BR>5 Darting, starting.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to swell, &c., aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरित|स्फुरितं
स्फुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, agitated.<BR>2 Trembling, heaving, throbbing, palpitating.<BR>3 Swelled, swollen.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Trembling or throbbing of the eye-lids.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to move or swell, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्च्छ
स्फुर्च्छ<BR>(आ) स्फुर्च्छा r. 1st cl. (स्फुर्च्छति)<BR>1 To spread, to expand.<BR>2 To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्ज|स्फुर्ज
स्फुर्ज्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्फुर्ज्जति)<BR>To thunder: more properly स्फूर्ज्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्जक|स्फुर्जक|स्फुर्ज्जकः
स्फुर्ज्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर्ज्ज to make a noise like thunder, (on being burnt,) aff. वुन्; also स्फूर्ज्जक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्जथु|स्फुर्जथु|स्फुर्जथुः
स्फुर्ज्जथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>A clap of thunder.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर्ज्ज to sound as thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल|स्फुलं
स्फुल<BR>r. 6th cl. (स्फुलति)<BR>1 To throb.<BR>2 To heap or crowd.<BR>3 To be manifest or apparent.<BR>4 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल|स्फुलं
स्फुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुल to expand, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलण
स्फुलण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throbbing, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to shake, aff. ल्युट्, and ल substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिङ्ग<BR>mfn. subst. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>A spark of fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्फु for स्फुत् imitative sound, लिगि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्गिनी|स्फुलिंगिनी
स्फुलिङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>One, of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुलिङ्ग a spark, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्ज|स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्जः
स्फूर्ज्ज<BR>(ओ आ) ओस्फूर्ज्जा r. 1st cl. (स्फूर्ज्जति)<BR>To thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=957" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्ज|स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्जः
स्फूर्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>1 The sound of thunder.<BR>2 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज to sound, as thunder, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जक|स्फूर्जक|स्फूर्जकः
स्फूर्ज्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज to sound like thunder, (in the fire, from its abounding with resin,) वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जथु|स्फूर्जथु|स्फूर्जथुः
स्फूर्ज्जथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>A clap of thunder, the sound of falling thunder, or that immediately following a stroke of lightning.<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज to sound as thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जन|स्फूर्जन|स्फूर्जनं
स्फूर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Thundering.<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जावत्|स्फूर्जावत्|स्फूर्जावन्त्
स्फूर्ज्जावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Thundering.<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Throbbing, palpitating, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to shake, aff. क्तिन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्त्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमन्त्
स्फूर्त्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Kind-hearted.<BR>2 Tremulous, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>स्फूर्त्ति agitation, मतुप् aff., and the म retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very much or many.<BR>E.<BR>स्फिर many, ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेष्ठ|स्फेष्ठः
स्फेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very much or many.<BR>E.<BR>स्फिर much, इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोट|स्फोटः
स्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A boil, a tumor.<BR>2 Breaking, bursting.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>The hood of the snake.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to break or open, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटक|स्फोटकः
स्फोटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A boil, a tumor.<BR>f. (-टिका)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to burst, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tearing, rending.<BR>2 Fidgetting with the hand, cracking the finger-joints, snapping the fingers, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A gimblet, an auger.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to open, (as a flower, &c.) causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटायन|स्फोटायनः
स्फोटायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Muni so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटित
स्फोटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Torn, rent.<BR>2 Made to open or burst.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to break, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्य|स्फ्यं
स्फ्य<BR>m. (-स्फ्यः)<BR>An implement used in sacrifices, a piece of wood shaped like a sword, for stirring the boiled rice, or according to some for trimming the mound used as an altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बृ
स्बृ<BR>r. 9th cl. (स्बृणाति-स्बृणीते)<BR>To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म<BR>ind.<BR>1 An expletive.<BR>2 A particle which added to verbs in the present tense gives them a past sense, as हन्तिस्मरावणंरामः RĀMA killed (instead of kills) RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>षो to end or destroy, ङ्म aff., or ष्मिङ to smile, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मय|स्मयः
स्मय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Surprise, astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>स्मि to smile, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर|स्मरः
स्मर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA, the deity of love.<BR>2 Recollection.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकर्म्मन्|स्मरकर्मन्
स्मरकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Lasciviousness, wanton pleasures.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकूपक|स्मरकूपकः
स्मरकूपक<BR>mf. (-पकः-पिका)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर KĀMA, कूप a well, and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगुरु|स्मरगुरुः
स्मरगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, गुरु the spiritual or natural father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगृह|स्मरगृहं
स्मरगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर KĀMA, and गृह mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरच्छत्र|स्मरच्छत्रं
स्मरच्छत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The clitoris.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, च्छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरण|स्मरणं
स्मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Recollecting, remembering, memory, recollection<BR>2 Regretting, remembering with regret.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणापत्यतर्पक|स्मरणापत्यतर्पकः
स्मरणापत्यतर्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>स्मरण memory, अपत्य offspring, and तर्पक who pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणीय
स्मरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be remembered.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरत्
स्मरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Remembering, recollecting, considering.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वज|स्मरध्वजं|स्मरध्वजः
स्मरध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Any musical instrument.<BR>2 The penis.<BR>3 A sort of fabulous fish or marine monster, the emblem of KĀMADEVA.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The vulva.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A bright moonlight night.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर KĀMA, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरप्रिया
स्मरप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>RATI, the wife of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर the deity of love, and प्रिया wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमन्दिर|स्मरमन्दिरं
स्मरमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमोह|स्मरमोहः
स्मरमोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Passion, love.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and मोह fascination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमोहित
स्मरमोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Overcome by love or passion.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and मोहित bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरलेखनी
स्मरलेखनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Sārika, (Turdus salica,) or Maina, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, लेखनी a pen, a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवल्लभ|स्मरवल्लभः
स्मरवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर KĀMA, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवीथिका
स्मरवीथिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A harlot.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, वीथि a shop, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरसख|स्मरसखः
स्मरसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर CUPID, and सख a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्तम्भ|स्मरस्तम्भः
स्मरस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर CUPID, and स्तम्भ post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्मर्य्य|स्मरस्मर्य|स्मरस्मर्यः|स्मरस्मर्य्यः
स्मरस्मर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर KĀMA, and स्मर्य्य to be remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरहर|स्मरहरः
स्मरहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर the deity of love, and हर destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराकुल
स्मराकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>In love.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and आकुल overcome; also स्मराकुलित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरागार|स्मरागारं
स्मरागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, आगार abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराङ्कुश|स्मरांकुश|स्मराङ्कुशः
स्मराङ्कुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A finger nail.<BR>2 A lover, a lecher.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरातुर
स्मरातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Overcome with love or passion.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and आतुर perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरान्ध|स्मरांध
स्मरान्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Infatuated with love.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरार्त्त|स्मरार्त
स्मरार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Overcome or agitated by love.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरासव|स्मरासवः
स्मरासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Saliva.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर love, आसव wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोत्सुक
स्मरोत्सुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Devoted to love.<BR>E.<BR>स्मर, and उत्सुक fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्त्तव्य|स्मर्तव्य
स्मर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be remembered.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्य्यमाण|स्मर्यमाण
स्मर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being remembered.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारण|स्मारणं
स्मारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Calling to mind, reminding, causing to remember.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारित
स्मारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Called to memory, caused to remember.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Legal, canonical, according to the doctrines of the Smṛtis or inspired codes of law.<BR>2 Following or professing the doctrine of the law books.<BR>3 Memorial, relating to memory.<BR>4 Within memory, what may be remembered.<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A Brahman following the revealed law.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति law collectively, and अण् aff. of reference, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=958" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त्तकाल|स्मार्तकाल|स्मार्तकालः
स्मार्त्तकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Time to which memory may extend; according to the jurists, as far as a century.<BR>E.<BR>स्मार्त्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्माययते)<BR>To slight.<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्मयते)<BR>To smile. Also ष्मिङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट
स्मिट<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्मेटयति)<BR>To slight, to disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित|स्मितं
स्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Smiling.<BR>2 Blown, (as a flower.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A smile, a gentle laugh.<BR>E.<BR>ष्मि to smile, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितदृश्
स्मितदृश्<BR>f. (-दृक्)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्मित, and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितशालिन्
स्मितशालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Smiling, laughing.<BR>E.<BR>स्मित, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील
स्मील<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्मीलति)<BR>To wink, to twinkle, to close or contract like the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्मरति)<BR>1 To remember, to recollect, to call to mind.<BR>2 To remember with regret, to miss.<BR>r. 5th cl. (स्मृणोति)<BR>1 To please or delight.<BR>2 To guard, to protect, to cherish.<BR>3 To breathe or live.<BR>With वि prefixed,<BR>To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत|स्मृतः
स्मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Recollected, remembered, called to mind.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृति|स्मृतिः
स्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Recollection, remembrance, memory.<BR>2 Law, the body of law, as delivered originally by MANU, YĀJÑAVALKYA, and other inspired legislators, to their respective pupils, and committed by them from recollection to writing.<BR>3 A law book, a code of laws.<BR>4 Wish, desire.<BR>5 Understanding.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिमत्|स्मृतिमन्त्
स्मृतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Remembering, recollecting, having a good memory.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति memory, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरुद्ध|स्मृतिविरुद्धः
स्मृतिविरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Illegal, unjust, contrary to law.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति jurisprudence, and विरुद्ध opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरोध|स्मृतिविरोधः
स्मृतिविरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Opposition to law, illegality, impropriety.<BR>2 Disagreement between two or more codes of law.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति, and विरोध opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशास्त्र|स्मृतिशास्त्रं
स्मृतिशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A work on law, a code, a digest, &c. as the Menu Saṃhitā, the Mitākṣarā, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति law, and शास्त्र an inspired treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिहेतु|स्मृतिहेतुः
स्मृतिहेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The proximate cause of recollection, the act of the mind by which any thing is called to memory, association, recollection.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति memory, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्यपेत|स्मृत्यपेतः
स्मृत्यपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Illegal, unjust.<BR>2 Forgotten.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति law, or memory, अप implying reverse, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्युक्त
स्मृत्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Enjoined, prescribed, laid down in codes of law.<BR>E.<BR>स्मृति, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Smiling, laughing.<BR>2 Blown, opened, expanded, (as a flower.)<BR>3 Evident, apparent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Manifestation, appearance.<BR>E.<BR>ष्मि to smile, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरमुख
स्मेरमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Having a smiling look.<BR>E.<BR>स्मेर, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरविष्किर|स्मेरविष्किरः
स्मेरविष्किर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>स्मेर smiling, and विष्किर a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद|स्यदः
स्यद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Speed, velocity.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to go, घञ् aff., and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन
स्यन<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्यनयते)<BR>To think, to consider, to reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यंदः|स्यन्दः
स्यन्द<BR>(ऊ) स्यन्दू r. 1st cl. (स्यन्दते)<BR>1 To sprinkle, to drop, to ooze or distil.<BR>2 To go.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>अनुष्यन्दते or अनुस्यन्दते<BR>to drop, &c.; the sibilant being optionally changed after this and other prepositions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यंदः|स्यन्दः
स्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Oozing, trickling.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>3 A car, a chariot.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यन्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A warchariot.<BR>2 A tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.)<BR>3 A Jina of the past era.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Dropping, oozing, trickling.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Going swiftly.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Saliva.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to go, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनद्रुम|स्यन्दनद्रुमः
स्यन्दनद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A timber tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.)<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्दन a car, and द्रुम a tree; the wood being used to make wheels, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनारूढ
स्यन्दनारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mounted on or riding in a car.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्दन, and आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनारोह|स्यंदनारोह|स्यन्दनारोहः
स्यन्दनारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A warrior who fights in a car.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्दन a war-chariot, and आरोह who ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनि|स्यन्दनिः
स्यन्दनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.)<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्दन a car, ञि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिन्|स्यंदिन्
स्यन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>1 Oozing, trickling, dropping.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>f. (-न्दिनी)<BR>1 Saliva.<BR>2 A cow bearing twins.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to drop or flow, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्न|स्यन्नः
स्यन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Flowing, dropping, or trickling.<BR>E.<BR>स्यन्द to drop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम
स्यम<BR>(उ) स्यमु r. 6th cl. (स्यमति)<BR>To sound.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्यमयति-ते)<BR>To consider, to think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The gem worn by KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीक|स्यमीकः
स्यमीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An ant-hill.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 Time.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Indigo.<BR>E.<BR>स्यम to sound, कन् Uṇādi aff. with ईट् augment; also with इट्, स्यमिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यात्
स्यात्<BR>ind.<BR>It may be: implying doubt, as स्यादस्ति, स्यान्नास्ति it may be, it may not be.<BR>E.<BR>the verbal conditional form used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याल|स्यालः
स्याल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wife's brother.<BR>E.<BR>स्यम to consider, aff. अच्, and म changed to ल; also स्याल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्युम्न
स्युम्न<BR>n. (-म्नं)<BR>Happiness, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sewn, stitched.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sack.<BR>E.<BR>(-षिव) to sew, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूति|स्यूतिः
स्यूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Sewing, stitching, working with needle and thread.<BR>2 Offspring, lineage.<BR>3 A sack.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यून|स्यूनः
स्यून<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A sack.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, Uṇādi aff. न, and यूच् substituted for the last two radical letters; also with the vowel of the augment changed स्योन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूम|स्यूमं|स्यूमः
स्यूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, मन् Uṇādi aff., and यूच् substituted for the radical finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योत|स्योतः
स्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sack, a coarse canvas bag.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, क्त aff., यूच् substituted for the finals, and the vowel changed; also स्यूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>3 A coarse canvas bag or sack.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Happiness, pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>षिव to sew, Uṇādi aff. न, and यूच् substituted for the radical finals, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस|स्रंसः
स्रंस<BR>(उ) स्रंसु r. 1st cl. (स्रंसते)<BR>To fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसमान
स्रंसमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Falling, dropping, slipping off or down.<BR>2 Fainting.<BR>E.<BR>स्रंस to fall, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=959" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Falling or hanging down, pendulous, depending.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A tree, commonly Pilu, and applied to several sorts, (as to Careya arborea, and Salvadora Persica, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रंस to fall down, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिनीफल|स्रंसिनीफलः
स्रंसिनीफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa Sirisha.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रंसिनी pendulous, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रक
स्रक<BR>(इ) स्रकि r. 1st cl. (स्रंकते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्धर
स्रग्धर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wearing a garland.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A species of the Prakṛti metre, a stanza of four lines of 21 syllables, and each line divided into three portions of seven syllables each.<BR>E.<BR>स्रज्, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्विन्
स्रग्विन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Bearing a chaplet, &c.<BR>f. (-विनी)<BR>A species of Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>स्रज् a garland, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज्<BR>f. (स्रक् or स्रग्)<BR>1 A chaplet, a wreath of flowers worn over the forehead.<BR>2 Any garland or string of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to quit, क्तिन् aff., and the vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजिष्ठ|स्रजिष्ठः
स्रजिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Covered with garlands, profusely decorated with chaplets, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्रग्विन् having a garland, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative and the possessive termination dropped; also with ईयसुन् aff. of the same, स्रजीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रद्धू
स्रद्धू<BR>f. (-द्धूः)<BR>A fart.<BR>E.<BR>शृध to fart, ऊ aff.; more properly श्रद्धू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रम्भ
स्रम्भ<BR>(उ) स्रम्भु r. 1st cl. (स्रम्भते)<BR>To trust, to have faith or confidence in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रव|स्रवः
स्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Oozing, dropping, trickling, flowing, the gradual issue or progress of any fluid.<BR>2 A fountain.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to flow or drop, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवण|स्रवणं
स्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>2 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>3 Piss, urine.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to ooze, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्
स्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>1 Oozing, flowing.<BR>2 Dropping, distilling.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 The situation of the spleen, the left hypochondriac region.<BR>3 A drug.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to drop, participial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्स्वेदजल
स्रवत्स्वेदजल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Perspiring much, covered with perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्रवत्, स्वेदजल perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्गर्ब्भा
स्रवद्गर्ब्भा<BR>f. (-र्ब्भा)<BR>A woman or cow miscarrying by accident.<BR>E.<BR>स्रवत् falling, गर्ब्भ the foetus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्रङ्ग|स्रवद्रङ्गः
स्रवद्रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A fair, a market.<BR>E.<BR>स्रव moving, and द्रङ्ग a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 A creator, a maker.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, तृच् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त|स्रस्तं
स्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Fallen down, off, or from.<BR>2 Separated, disjoined.<BR>3 Loosened, relaxed, given way.<BR>E.<BR>स्रंस to fall, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तहस्त
स्रस्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Letting go, relaxing one's hold.<BR>E.<BR>स्रस्त, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्ताङ्ग|स्रस्तांग
स्रस्ताङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Having the limbs relaxed, swooning, fainting, falling.<BR>E.<BR>स्रस्त, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक्<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly, instantly.<BR>E.<BR>स्रै to cook or ripen, क्विप् aff., स्रा maturity, अक् to obtain, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राव|स्रावः
स्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Oozing, flowing, dripping.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to go or flow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावक|स्रावकं
स्रावक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Black-pepper.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to ooze, causal form, खुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ
स्रिभ<BR>(उ) स्रिभु r. 1st cl. (स्रेभति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिम्भ
स्रिम्भ<BR>(उ) स्रिम्भु r. 1st cl. (स्रिम्भति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव
स्रिव<BR>(उ) स्रिवु r. 4th cl. (स्रिव्यति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्रवति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To flow.<BR>3 To drop, to distil, to ooze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुग्दारु
स्रुग्दारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रुच् a sacrificial ladle, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुग्ध्नी
स्रुग्ध्नी<BR>f. (-ध्नी)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच्<BR>f. (स्रुक् or स्रुग्)<BR>A sort of ladle or long spoon, generally made of wood, and used to pour Ghee or clarified butter upon the sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to drop, (Ghee,) क्विप् aff., and चिट् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Flowing, dropping, falling, as a fluid.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to flow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुव|स्रुवः
स्रुव<BR>mf. (-वः-वा)<BR>A ladle with a double extremity, or two oval collateral excavations, made of wood, and used to pour Ghee upon the sacrificial fire.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A shrub, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>2 A tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to drop or ooze, (from or by it,) aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवावृक्ष|स्रुवावृक्षः
स्रुवावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>स्रुवा a sacrificial ladle, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू<BR>f. (स्रूः)<BR>A sacrificial ladle: see स्रुव.<BR>2 A cascade.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to drop, (Ghee from it,) Uṇādi aff. क्किप्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक
स्रेक<BR>(ऋ) स्रेकृ r. 1st cl. (स्रेकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्रायति)<BR>1 To boil or melt; also श्रै and श्रा.<BR>2 To cook or ripen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत|स्रोतं|स्रोतः
स्रोत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A natural or rapid stream: see स्रोतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतईश|स्रोतईशः
स्रोतईश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a stream, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस्<BR>n. (-तः)<BR>1 A current, a natural or rapid stream.<BR>2 A river in general.<BR>3 The flow or course of water.<BR>4 Water.<BR>5 A spring.<BR>6 An organ of sense.<BR>E.<BR>स्रु to flow, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, and तुट् augment; also with a final vowel स्रोत, and palatial sibilant श्रोतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्य|स्रोतस्यः
स्रोतस्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a stream, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a current, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्विनी
स्रोतस्विनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a current, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोञ्जन|स्रोतोञ्जनं
स्रोतोञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Antimony.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a stream, and अञ्जन collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोवह
स्रोतोवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Flowing like a stream or river.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्रोतस् a stream, and वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व<BR>Pron. mfn. (स्वः स्वा स्वं)<BR>Own.<BR>Subst. m. (स्वः)<BR>1 A kinsman.<BR>2 The soul.<BR>3 Self-identity, individuality.<BR>n. (स्वं)<BR>1 Wealth, property.<BR>2 (In algebra,) Plus, or affirmative quantity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, aff. ड, or षू to send or order, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Own, proper, peculiar.<BR>E.<BR>स्व as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकम्पन|स्वकंपन|स्वकम्पनः
स्वकम्पन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, कम्पन agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मकृत्|स्वकर्मकृत्
स्वकर्म्मकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>An independant workman, one doing business on his own account.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, कर्म्म business, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मन्|स्वकर्मन्
स्वकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मा)<BR>Own act, business, duty, conduct, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मवश|स्वकर्मवश
स्वकर्म्मवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Suffering the consequences of one's own acts.<BR>E.<BR>स्वकर्म्म, and वश subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मस्थ|स्वकर्मस्थ
स्वकर्म्मस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Who or what adheres to its own business or duty.<BR>E.<BR>स्वकर्म्म, and स्थ staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=960" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकार्य्य|स्वकार्य
स्वकार्य्य<BR>n. (-य्य)<BR>Own business or duty.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Of one's own family.<BR>2 Own in general, as property, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, छ aff., and कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुटुम्ब
स्वकुटुम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>Own family.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कुटुम्ब family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुल
स्वकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Own family or race.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुलक्षय|स्वकुलक्षयः
स्वकुलक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, कुल race, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकृत
स्वकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done or made by one's self, self-performed.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक्ष
स्वक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा or क्षी-क्षं)<BR>1 Handsome-eyed.<BR>2 Acute, sensitive, having keen organs.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, अक्षि the eye, or अक्ष an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वग
स्वग<BR>(इ) स्वगि r. 1st cl. (स्वंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगत|स्वगतं
स्वगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kept to one's self, apart, aside.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Aside (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, गत gone, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगृह|स्वगृहः
स्वगृह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A small bird, (Loxia Philippensis.)<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Own house.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगुप्त
स्वगुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Self-defended or preserved.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>Cowach, (Carpogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, गुप्त preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्ग|स्वंग|स्वंगः|स्वङ्गः
स्वङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Handsome and well-shaped.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>1 Healthy, sound, convalescent.<BR>2 White.<BR>3 Pure, free from stain or soil.<BR>4 Transparent, pellucid.<BR>E.<BR>सु exceedingly, and अच्छ clean, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छता
स्वच्छता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Purity, transparency, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, स्वच्छत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्वच्छन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>1 Unrestrained, uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>2 Spontaneous.<BR>3 Uncultivated.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, and छन्द inclination; also स्वच्छन्दक mfn. (-कः-का-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छपत्र|स्वच्छपत्रं
स्वच्छपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Talc.<BR>E.<BR>स्वच्छ transparent, and पत्र a leaf, a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्वज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Self-born, produced in or by one's self.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Blood.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, self, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजन|स्वजनः
स्वजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A distant kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, जन man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजाति|स्वजातिः
स्वजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Own caste, tribe, or species.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजातीय
स्वजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of one's own tribe, caste, species, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and जातीय of a caste, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज्ञाति|स्वज्ञातिः
स्वज्ञाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Kindred, kin.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and ज्ञाति kin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ
स्वठ<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्वठयति)<BR>1 To finish.<BR>2 To leave unfinished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्र|स्वतंत्र|स्वतन्त्रः
स्वतन्त्र<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>1 Unrestrained, uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>2 Independant, free.<BR>3 Full grown, of age, no longer subject to the authority of parents, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, तन्त्र inclination, will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रता
स्वतन्त्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Independence, wilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतस्
स्वतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Of itself, by one's self.<BR>2 Own, peculiar.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्र|स्वत्रः
स्वत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Self-preserving.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A blind man.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, and त्र who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्व|स्वत्वं
स्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Self-existence, independant being or condition.<BR>2 Own right or property, ownership, proprietary right.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, and त्व aff. of the abstract; also स्वत्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वनिवृत्ति|स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः
स्वत्वनिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Cessation or loss of proprietary right.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वबोधन
स्वत्वबोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Indication or proof of ownership.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and बोधन making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वव्यभिचारित्व
स्वत्वव्यभिचारित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Doubt or uncertainty of ownership.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and व्यभिचारित्व want of steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहानि|स्वत्वहानिः
स्वत्वहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Loss or forfeiture of proprietary title or right.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and हानि loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहेतु|स्वत्वहेतुः
स्वत्वहेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Ground or cause of proprietary right.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वाभाव
स्वत्वाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Non-existence of proprietary right.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वावगम
स्वत्वावगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Determination or ascertainment of ownership.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and अवगम certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वास्पद
स्वत्वास्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The subject or thing in which proprietary right is vested.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and आस्पद site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वोत्पत्ति
स्वत्वोत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Origin or production of proprietary right.<BR>E.<BR>स्वत्व, and उत्पत्ति production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद
स्वद<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वदते)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To be sweet or agreeable; also ष्वद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदन|स्वदनं
स्वदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>स्वद to taste, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदारनिरत
स्वदारनिरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uxorious, devoted to a wife.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, दार wife, निरत attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten, well eaten.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The term used after presenting food to the manes, asking if they are satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>स्वद to taste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेश|स्वदेशः
स्वदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Native country, home.<BR>2 Own or proper place.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेशपरिधि
स्वदेशपरिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Circumference of a circle of longitude in any place that has latitude.<BR>E.<BR>स्वदेश, and परिधि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेशमध्यपरिधि
स्वदेशमध्यपरिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Circumference of the terrestrial equator.<BR>E.<BR>स्वदेश, मध्य centre, and परिधि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्म|स्वधर्म|स्वधर्मः|स्वधर्म्मः
स्वधर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Peculiar duty or occupation, as praying of a Brahman, fighting of a soldier, &c.<BR>2 Property, peculiarity.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मच्युत|स्वधर्मच्युत
स्वधर्म्मच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Neglecting one's duty.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधर्म्म, and च्युत fallen from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मत्याग|स्वधर्मत्याग
स्वधर्म्मत्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Neglect of duty.<BR>2 Apostacy.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधर्म्म, and त्याग abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मस्थ|स्वधर्मस्थ
स्वधर्म्मस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Attached to or performing one's peculiar duty.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधर्म्म, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मस्खलन|स्वधर्मस्खलन
स्वधर्म्मस्खलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Neglecting or disregarding duty.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधर्म्म, and स्खलन slipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्वधा<BR>ind.<BR>1 An exclamation used on presenting an oblation to the manes. (aptote noun).<BR>2 The food of deceased ancestors.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A personification of Māyā or worldly illusion, the self-contained associate of the Creator.<BR>2 A nymph, the food of the manes personified, and sometimes represented as the wife of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वद to taste, आ aff., and द changed to ध; or स्व self, धा to hold, aff. अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाकार|स्वधाकारः
स्वधाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Pronouncing the exclamation Svadhā.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधा, and कार making; also स्वधाकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाप्रिय|स्वधाप्रियः
स्वधाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Black sesamum.<BR>2 AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधा the exclamation used in making oblations to the manes, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=961" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाभुज्
स्वधाभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>1 A divine or deified ancestor.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधा the food of the manes, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिति|स्वधितिः
स्वधिति<BR>mf. (-तिः-ती)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, धा to hold, क्तिन् aff.; also श्वधिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितिहेतिक|स्वधितिहेतिकः
स्वधितिहेतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A soldier armed with an axe.<BR>E.<BR>स्वधिति an axe, and हेतिक armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधीत
स्वधीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well read, versed in.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and अधीत read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन<BR>r. 1st. cl. (स्वनति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>(स्वनयति)<BR>To dress, to adorn.<BR>With वि or अव prefixed, in a limited sense, the initial is changed,<BR>(अवष्वणति or विष्वणति)<BR>To make a noise whilst eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनगर
स्वनगर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Own or native town.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and नगर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनत्
स्वनत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनवत्|स्वनवन्त्
स्वनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sounding, thundering.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन sound, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनाश
स्वनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Self-destruction.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and नाश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनि|स्वनिः
स्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The noise of thunder.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, aff. क्त, or स्वन sound, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनुष्ठित
स्वनुष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well or duly observed, practised, performed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, अनुष्ठित followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपत्
स्वपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>Sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपन|स्वपनं
स्वपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न|स्वप्नः
स्वप्न<BR>m. (-प्नः)<BR>1 Sleep.<BR>2 Dreaming, a dream.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, न Uṇādi aff., तन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नकृत्
स्वप्नकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Narcotic, producing sleep.<BR>n. (-कृत्)<BR>A potherb, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न sleep, and कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नगृह
स्वप्नगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A bed-chamber.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज्<BR>mfn. (-प्नक्)<BR>Sleeping, asleep.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, नजिङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदोष|स्वप्नदोषः
स्वप्नदोष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Pollutio nocturna.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न sleep, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्ननिकेतन
स्वप्ननिकेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bed chamber.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न, and निकेतन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचार|स्वप्नविचारः
स्वप्नविचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Interpretation of dreams.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न, and विचार investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचारिन्
स्वप्नविचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An interpreter of dreams.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न a dream, and विचारिन् who investigates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नशील
स्वप्नशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Sleepy.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न, and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नावस्था
स्वप्नावस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>State of dreaming, applied especially to life or ignorance of worldly illusion.<BR>E.<BR>स्वप्न, and अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाजन|स्वभाजनं
स्वभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Civility, courtesy, welcome or adieu.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, भज to serve, causal form, aff. ल्युट्; also सभाजन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाव|स्वभावः
स्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Nature, natural state, property or disposition.<BR>2 Purpose, intention.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावज
स्वभावज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Innate, natural, produced from, or by the natural disposition.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावतस्
स्वभावतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From or according to natural property or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावदौर्जन्य
स्वभावदौर्जन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Natural or innate wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and दौर्जन्य badness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावद्वेष
स्वभावद्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Natural or inherent enmity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and द्वेष hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावोक्त
स्वभावोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Uttered or declared naturally or spontaneously.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावोक्ति
स्वभावोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Spontaneous declaration.<BR>2 Description of living objects by circumstances or acts suited to their character.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभू
स्वभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभूमि
स्वभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 Own land or estate.<BR>2 Native country.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवर|स्वयंवरः
स्वयंवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The public choice of a husband by a princess, from a number of suitors assembled for the purpose.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A girl choosing her husband.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् of herself, वर selecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंशीर्ण
स्वयंशीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Fallen or dropped spontaneously.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम्, and शीर्ण decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्कृत|स्वयंकृत|स्वयङ्कृतः|स्वयंकृतः
स्वयङ्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Self-formed, natural, spontaneous.<BR>2 Done to one's self.<BR>3 Done by or for one's self.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्गुप्ता|स्वयंगुप्ता
स्वयङ्गुप्ता<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, and गुप्त preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयन्दत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Self-given.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A child who has given himself to adoptive parents.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम्<BR>ind.<BR>Self, spontaneously, of one's own self or own accord.<BR>E.<BR>सु auspiciously, अय to go, अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुक्ति|स्वयमुक्तिः
स्वयमुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Voluntary declaration.<BR>2 (In law,) Information, deposition.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम्, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्प्रभ|स्वयंप्रभ|स्वयंप्रभः
स्वयम्प्रभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A Jaina of the future era.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, and प्रभ illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भु|स्वयंभु|स्वयम्भुः
स्वयम्भु<BR>m. (-म्भुः)<BR>BRAHMĀ: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भुव|स्वयंभुव|स्वयम्भुवः
स्वयम्भुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The first MANU.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, भू to be or exist, aff. क, or स्वयम्भू BRAHMĀ, and अण् pleonasm or patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भू|स्वयंभू
स्वयम्भू<BR>m. (-म्भूः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A Jina or Jaina deified sage.<BR>3 An emperor of the world according to the Jainas.<BR>4 Time.<BR>5 Love.<BR>6 VIṢṆU.<BR>7 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम् self, भू to exist, क्विप् aff., the self-existent; also read with a short final, or स्वयम्भु m. (-भुः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्वयोनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Of kin, related by the mother's side.<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A sister or near female relative.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्वरयति)<BR>1 To blame, to censure, to reprove.<BR>2 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर्<BR>ind. (aptote noun.)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise, the residence of INDRA and the celestials.<BR>2 Sky, ether.<BR>3 Splendour, beauty.<BR>4 One of the divisions of the universe, the space between the sun and polar star and region of the planets and constellations; in this sense, this word is one of the three mystical words, to be repeated daily at the morning ceremonies, &c., with the holy Gāyatrī.<BR>E.<BR>स्वृ to sound, to be in pain, विच् aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An accent.<BR>2 A vowel.<BR>3 A note in music.<BR>4 Air, breathed through the nostrils, snoring.<BR>5 Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरपत्तन|स्वरपत्तनं
स्वरपत्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर an accent, and पत्तन a city: this Veda is chaunted according to a peculiar rhythm, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">Page963</a>] and the efficacy of its prayers depends chiefly on their accurate accentuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=962" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्ग|स्वरभंग|स्वरभङ्गः
स्वरभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Fluttering of the voice, &c. as indicative of agitation or feeling.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a sound or note, and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्गिन्
स्वरभङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note, and भङ्गिन् who breaks or divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमण्डलिका|स्वरमंडलिका
स्वरमण्डलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of stringed musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note of the gamut, मण्डल a region, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरलासिका
स्वरलासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flute, a pipe.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note, लस to be skilled, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशून्य
स्वरशून्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Unmelodious, unmusical.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर, and शून्य devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरस|स्वरसः
स्वरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Expressed or extracted juice.<BR>2 Sediment of oil, &c. ground on a stone.<BR>3 Proper or peculiar flavour.<BR>4 Proper or peculiar taste or sentiment in composition.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, रस flavour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरांश|स्वरांशः
स्वरांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A half or quarter tone in music.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note, अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्
स्वराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ or supreme spirit.<BR>2 A form of metre used in the Vedas, a verse of three lines, two containing eight syllables each, and one ten.<BR>3 A variety of the same containing four lines.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, राज to shine, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरापगा
स्वरापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर heaven, आपगा river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरारूढ
स्वरारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Ascended to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्, and आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराष्ट्र
स्वराष्ट्र<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Own country or principality.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and राष्ट्र country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Accented.<BR>2 Articulated.<BR>3 Sounded as a note, pitched.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The third or circumflex accent.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर a note or accent, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरु|स्वरुः
स्वरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A sacrifice.<BR>4 Shavings of the wood of which a sacrificial post is made.<BR>5 Sunshine.<BR>6 A kind of scorpion.<BR>E.<BR>स्वृ to sound, Uṇādi aff. उ; also with उसि, aff. स्वरुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुचि|स्वरुचिः
स्वरुचि<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Wilful, self-willed, uncontrolled.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, रुचि inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुस्
स्वरुस्<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt, &c.: see स्वरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्वरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा or पी-पं)<BR>1 Wise, learned.<BR>2 Pleasing, handsome.<BR>3 Similar, like.<BR>4 Of like purport or character.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Natural state or condition, nature.<BR>2 Natural and obvious purpose or conclusion.<BR>3 Kind, sort.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपगत
स्वरूपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having a like object or character.<BR>E.<BR>स्वरूप, and गत obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपता
स्वरूपता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Natural state.<BR>2 Handsomeness.<BR>3 Identity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, स्वरूपत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरेणु|स्वरेणुः
स्वरेणु<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>One of the wives of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग|स्वर्गः
स्वर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Heaven, INDRA'S paradise, and the residence of deified mortals and the inferior gods.<BR>E.<BR>सु happiness, ऋज to go, or obtain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गत
स्वर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगमन
स्वर्गगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगामिन्
स्वर्गगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Who or what goes to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गङ्गा|स्वर्गंगा
स्वर्गङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, गङ्गा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गजित्
स्वर्गजित्<BR>mfn. (-जित्)<BR>Obtaining or ensuring paradise.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग heaven, and जित् what conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गत
स्वर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone to heaven.<BR>2 Dead.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गति|स्वर्गतिः
स्वर्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Going to heaven, future felicity.<BR>2 Death.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्, and गति going; also स्वर्गमन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गपति|स्वर्गपतिः
स्वर्गपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग paradise, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गपर
स्वर्गपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Desirous of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गभर्त्तृ|स्वर्गभर्तृ
स्वर्गभर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्तां)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and भर्त्तृ sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गलोक|स्वर्गलोकः
स्वर्गलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Paradise.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गलोकेश|स्वर्गलोकेशः
स्वर्गलोकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्गलोक, and ईश lord; the paradise of INDRA, being appropriated to corporeal felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गवधू
स्वर्गवधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>An Apsaras, a nymph or courtesan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग paradise, and वधू woman or wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गापगा
स्वर्गापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग heaven, and आपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गारोहण
स्वर्गारोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ascending to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and आरोहण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गारूढ
स्वर्गारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Gone to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिगिरि|स्वर्गिगिरिः
स्वर्गिगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Mount Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्गि a god, and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिन्
स्वर्गिन्<BR>m. (-र्गो)<BR>1 A god, a celestial.<BR>2 (In law,) Dead.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग heaven, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिरि|स्वर्गिरिः
स्वर्गिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Mount Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिवधू
स्वर्गिवधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>A nymph of paradise.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्गि a celestial, and वधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीय
स्वर्गीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Heavenly, divine, relating to Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गौकस्
स्वर्गौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>A god, a deity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग paradise, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग्य|स्वर्ग्यः
स्वर्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>Heavenly, paradisiacal.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ग heaven, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ण|स्वर्णं
स्वर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>सु excellent, ऋण to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक
स्वर्णक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Golden, of gold.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्णं, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकाय|स्वर्णकायः|स्वर्ण्णकाय
स्वर्णकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकार|स्वर्णकारः
स्वर्णकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and कार maker, worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकृत्
स्वर्णकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक्षीरी
स्वर्णक्षीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A medicinal kind of moon-plant, said to be brought from the Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, (like or yellow,) क्षीर milk, or milky sap, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णगैरिक|स्वर्णगैरिकं
स्वर्णगैरिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of ochre, golden ochre.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and गैरिक red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णचूड|स्वर्णचूडः
स्वर्णचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 The blue jay.<BR>2 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, चूडा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णज|स्वर्णजं
स्वर्णज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदी
स्वर्णदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर heaven, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदीधिति|स्वर्णदीधितिः
स्वर्णदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, दीधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=963" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णद्रु|स्वर्णद्रुः
स्वर्णद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree with yellow blossoms.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपक्ष|स्वर्णपक्षः
स्वर्णपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and पक्ष a wing or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपद्मा
स्वर्णपद्मा<BR>f. (-द्मा)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, पद्म a lotus; bearing golden lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपुष्प|स्वर्णपुष्पः
स्वर्णपुष्प<BR>mf. (-ष्पः-ष्पी)<BR>The Cassia fistula.<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>The gum Arabic tree, (Mimosa Arabica).<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णयूथी
स्वर्णयूथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णरेखा
स्वर्णरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A streak of gold.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण, and रेखा a line; also स्वर्णलेखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णवर्णा
स्वर्णवर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णां)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णवल्कल|स्वर्णवल्कलः
स्वर्णवल्कल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णविन्दु
स्वर्णविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A spot of yellow or gold.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and विन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णसेफालिका
स्वर्णसेफालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and सेफालिका Nyctanthes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णारि|स्वर्णारिः
स्वर्णारि<BR>n. (-रिः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर्ण gold, and अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्त्त|स्वर्त
स्वर्त्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्वर्त्तयति)<BR>To be miserable or distrest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्द्द|स्वर्द
स्वर्द्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वर्द्दते)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To be pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्नदी
स्वर्नदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and नदी a river, and the न unchanged; also स्वर्णदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानु|स्वर्भानुः
स्वर्भानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, भानु shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यात|स्वर्यातः
स्वर्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्लोक|स्वर्लोकः
स्वर्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वधू
स्वर्वधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>An Apsaras.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and वधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वापी|स्वर्व्वापी
स्वर्वापी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, वापी a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वेश्या|स्वर्व्वेश्या
स्वर्वेश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>A nymph of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and वेश्या a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वैद्य|स्वर्वैद्यः
स्वर्वैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>Either of the twin sons of the sun by the nymph Aśvini, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, and वैद्य a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्प|स्वल्पः
स्वल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>1 Very small.<BR>2 Very few.<BR>E.<BR>सु very, अल्प little or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पक
स्वल्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Little.<BR>2 Few.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पकेशिन्
स्वल्पकेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>Root of sweet flag.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प little, few, केश a filament, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पपत्रक|स्वल्पपत्रकः
स्वल्पपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of Mahwa tree, (Bassia,) with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प small, पत्र a leaf, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पवल
स्वल्पवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Weak, feeble.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प, and वल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पविषय|स्वल्पविषयः
स्वल्पविषय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A small matter or object.<BR>2 A small part.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प, and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्यय|स्वल्पव्ययः
स्वल्पव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Niggardliness, little expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प, and व्यय expence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्रीड
स्वल्पव्रीड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Shameless, impudent.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प, and व्रीडा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वव
स्वव<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्ववति)<BR>To revile, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववश
स्ववश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Self-subdued, self-controlled.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववहित
स्ववहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Alert, active.<BR>2 Automatous.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and वहित impelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववासिनी
स्ववासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman, whether married or unmarried, dwelling in her father's house.<BR>E.<BR>स्व her own, (family,) वासिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववीज
स्ववीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The soul.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववृत्ति
स्ववृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Own, or peculiar duty or occupation.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशरीर
स्वशरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Own body.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशरीरवत्
स्वशरीरवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like or as one's self.<BR>E.<BR>स्वशरीर, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंवृत
स्वसंवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Self-defended, on one's guard.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and संवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृ
स्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A sister.<BR>E.<BR>सु before अस to be or live, Uṇādi aff. ऋत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्क
स्वस्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वस्कते)<BR>To go, more generally read ष्वष्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्ति
स्वस्ति<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of benediction.<BR>2 An auspicious particle.<BR>3 A term of sanction or approbation, (so be it, amen.)<BR>E.<BR>सु well, अस to be, aff. क्तिच् or ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिक|स्वस्तिकः
स्वस्तिक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A temple of a particular form, with a portico in front.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Any lucky or auspicious object.<BR>2 The meeting of four roads.<BR>3 A building or palace of a peculiar shape, described as surrounded by a terrace or portion, on the north, west, and south sides, and having the door or entrance on the east.<BR>4 A kind of mystical figure, the inscription of which on any person or thing is generally considered to be lucky; it consists of 卐 and amongst the Jainas is the emblem of the seventh deified teacher of the present era.<BR>5 The crossing of the arms, as resembling the preceding.<BR>6 A kind of cake.<BR>7 A libertine.<BR>8 Garlic.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमत्|स्वस्तिमन्त्
स्वस्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Happy, auspicious.<BR>E.<BR>स्वस्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमुख|स्वस्तिमुखः
स्वस्तिमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A letter, a note.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>3 A panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>स्वस्ति, and मुख beginning or the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचन|स्वस्तिवाचनं
स्वस्तिवाचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A religious rite, preparatory to any important observance, in which the Brahmans strew boiled rice on the ground, and invoke the blessings of the gods on the ceremony about to commence.<BR>E.<BR>स्वस्ति inceptive and benedictory particle, वाचन uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्त्ययन
स्वस्त्ययन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Auspicious, propitious.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The aversion of evil by the recitation of Mantras.<BR>2 The benediction of a Brahman after presentation of offerings.<BR>E.<BR>स्वस्ति good, and अयन coming or bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थ|स्वस्थः
स्वस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Confident, resolute, firm, relying upon one's self.<BR>2 Well, at ease, in health.<BR>3 Self-sufficient.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, and स्थ staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीय|स्वस्रीयः
स्वस्रीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sister's son.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A sister's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>स्वसृ a sister, and छ aff.; also with घ aff. स्वस्रिय, mf. (-यः-या) or with ढक् aff. स्वस्रेय, mf. (-यः-यी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहित
स्वहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Good for one's self.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and हित good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहितैषिन्
स्वहितैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Seeking one's own welfare.<BR>E.<BR>स्वहित, and एषिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाकार
स्वाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having one's own form.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and आकार form; also स्वाकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=964" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वागत|स्वागतं
स्वागत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Welcome, salutation.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाच्छन्द्य|स्वाच्छंद्य|स्वाच्छंद्यं|स्वाच्छन्द्यं|स्वाछन्द्य
स्वाच्छन्द्य<BR>n. (-न्द्यं)<BR>Wilfulness, independence.<BR>E.<BR>स्वच्छन्द selfwilled, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वातन्त्र्य|स्वातंत्र्य|स्वातंत्र्यं|स्वातन्त्र्यं
स्वातन्त्र्य<BR>n. (-न्त्र्यं)<BR>Wilfulness, independence.<BR>E.<BR>स्वतन्त्र self-willed, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाति|स्वातिः
स्वाति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 One of the wives of the sun.<BR>2 The star Arcturus, or fifteenth lunar asterism, consisting of but one star.<BR>3 A sword.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, auspiciously, अत to go or be, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद|स्वादः
स्वाद<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वादते)<BR>To taste.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (स्वादति स्वादयति)<BR>To be agreeable or pleasing.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्वादयति)<BR>To cover; also ष्वद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद|स्वादः
स्वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Taste, flavour.<BR>2 Tasting, either food or drink, eating, drinking.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाद to taste, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादन|स्वादनं
स्वादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tasting, either as food or drink, eating, drinking.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाद to taste, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादित|स्वादितः
स्वादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tasted, touched with the lips.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाद to taste, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादु|स्वादुः
स्वादु<BR>mfn. (-दुः-दु or -द्वी-दु)<BR>1 Sweet.<BR>2 Agreeable, desired.<BR>3 Handsome.<BR>4 Grateful to the palate, dainty, delicate.<BR>m. (-दुः)<BR>1 The sweet taste or flavour, sweetness.<BR>2 Treacle, molasses.<BR>3 A medicinal root, commonly Jivaka.<BR>f. (-द्वी or -दुः)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वद to taste or be pleasing, उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुकण्टक|स्वादुकण्टकः
स्वादुकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR>2 A sort of creeper, (Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुकार
स्वादुकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Delicate in taste, dainty.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाटु, and कार who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुखण्ड|स्वादुखंड|स्वादुखण्डः
स्वादुखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Molasses, raw sugar.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, and खण्ड a fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुगन्धा
स्वादुगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A creeper, (Convolvulus paniculatus,) the dark sort.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाटु sugar, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुधन्वन्
स्वादुधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, (flowers,) धन्वन् a bowyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुफल|स्वादुफलं
स्वादुफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fruit of the jujube.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाटु sweet, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुमज्जन्
स्वादुमज्जन्<BR>m. (-ज्जा)<BR>A sort of tree, a Pilu growing in the hills.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, मज्जन् sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुमूल|स्वादुमूलं
स्वादुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A carrot.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुरसा
स्वादुरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>2 The hog plum, (the fruit.)<BR>3 Vinous liquor.<BR>4 A grape.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, or sugar, &c., and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुशीत
स्वादुशीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sweet and cool.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु, and शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुशुद्ध|स्वादुशुद्धं
स्वादुशुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Rock or river salt.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, and शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वन्न
स्वाद्वन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Dainties, delicacies, choice food.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वम्ल|स्वाद्वम्लः
स्वाद्वम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>The pomegranate tree.<BR>E.<BR>स्वादु sweet, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिकार|स्वाधिकारः
स्वाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Own or peculiar office or station.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and अधिकार duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिपत्य
स्वाधिपत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Supreme sway, royalty, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and अधिपत्य supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीन|स्वाधीनः
स्वाधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Independant, uncontrolled.<BR>2 One's own dependant.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनता
स्वाधीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Independence.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, स्वाधीनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनपतिका
स्वाधीनपतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman independant of her husband or lover.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाधीन independant, पति husband, कन् fem. form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनभर्त्तृका|स्वाधीनभर्तृका
स्वाधीनभर्त्तृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman who is independant of her lover or husband.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, अधीन subservient, and भर्त्तृ a husband, कन् added; keeping her husband in subjection or dependance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्याय|स्वाध्यायः
स्वाध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Inaudible reading or muttering of prayers.<BR>2 The Vedas or scripture.<BR>3 Perusal or study of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>स्व one's self, अध्याय reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायवत्|स्वाध्यायवन्त्
स्वाध्यायवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A student of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाध्याय perusing the Vedas, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायिन्
स्वाध्यायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A tradesman, a citizen and dealer.<BR>2 A student of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाध्याय muttering, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान|स्वानः
स्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुरूप
स्वानुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Natural, inherent, innate.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and अनुरूप conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान्त|स्वांत|स्वान्तं
स्वान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Sounded, making a noise.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 The mind, the faculty of thought and feeling.<BR>2 A cave, a cavern.<BR>E.<BR>स्वन to sound, क्त aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाप|स्वापः
स्वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Sleep, sleeping.<BR>2 Sleepiness, sloth.<BR>3 Paralysis, palsy, loss of sensation.<BR>4 Ignorance.<BR>5 Dreaming, a dream.<BR>6 Temporary and partial palsy from pressure on a nerve, numbness, the sleep of a limb, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्वप to sleep, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापतेय|स्वापतेयं
स्वापतेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Wealth, property.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, पति master, ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापद|स्वापदः
स्वापद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A wild beast.<BR>E.<BR>स substituted for शः see श्वापद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविक|स्वाभाविकः
स्वाभाविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Natural, peculiar, inherent.<BR>E.<BR>स्वभाव natural property or nature, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभिजङ्घिन्
स्वाभिजङ्घिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्घी)<BR>PARAŚURĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामित्व|स्वामित्वं
स्वामित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Ownership, mastership.<BR>2 Sovereignty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to स्वामिन्; also with तल्, स्वामिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Owner, proprietor, master or mistress, &c.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 A master, a lord.<BR>2 A sovereign, a prince, a monarch.<BR>3 A husband, a lover.<BR>4 A spiritual preceptor.<BR>5 A learned Brahman or Paṇḍita.<BR>6 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>7 VIṢṆU.<BR>8 ŚIVA.<BR>9 The Muni VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>10 A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, आमिनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिकार्य्य|स्वामिकार्य
स्वामिकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>The business of a prince or master.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामिन्, and कार्य्य affair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिमूल
स्वामिमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Depending upon, or originating from the master, husband, or lord.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामिन्, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसद्भाव|स्वामिसद्भावः
स्वामिसद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Existence of a master or owner.<BR>2 Amiability of a master or lord.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामि, and सत् being, or good, भाव existence or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसेवा
स्वामिसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Attention to a master, husband, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामिन्, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्य|स्वाम्यं
स्वाम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Mastership, ownership.<BR>2 Right or title to property.<BR>3 Rule, supremacy.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामिन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्युपकारक|स्वाम्युपकारकः
स्वाम्युपकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>स्वामि a master, उपकार assistance, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुव|स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायम्भुव<BR>m. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Relating to Svayambhū.<BR>2 Derived from the self-born.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The son of Svayambhū.<BR>E.<BR>स्वयम्भू, and अण् aff.; also स्वायम्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=965" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्
स्वाराज्<BR>m. (-णाट्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वर् heaven, राज ruler; the first र rejected, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्य|स्वाराज्यं|स्वाराज्यः
स्वाराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>1 Final felicity, union with BRAHMA.<BR>2 INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>स्वराज्, and ष्यञ् aff., or स्वाराज् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिष|स्वारोचिषः
स्वारोचिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The second MANU.<BR>E.<BR>स्वरोचिस्, and अञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थ|स्वार्थः
स्वार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थ)<BR>1 Pleonastic.<BR>2 Having a plain or literal meaning, or similar force or sense.<BR>3 Having one's own object.<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>1 Property, substance.<BR>2 Same effect or meaning, a pleonasm.<BR>3 Own object or desire.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, and अर्थ wealth or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थपरायण
स्वार्थपरायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Selfish.<BR>E.<BR>स्वार्थ, and परायण diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थलिप्सु
स्वार्थलिप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desirous of having one's own way, self-seeking.<BR>E.<BR>स्वार्थ, and लिप्सु desirous of getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थसिद्धि
स्वार्थसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Accomplishment of one's object, attainment of the thing desired.<BR>E.<BR>स्वार्थ, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थिक
स्वार्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Expressing its own or literal meaning.<BR>2 Having one's own object.<BR>3 Done with one's own wealth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्वार्थ, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पी-ल्पं)<BR>1 Small.<BR>2 Few.<BR>n. (-ल्पं)<BR>1 Littleness.<BR>2 Paucity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वल्प, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाशित
स्वाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well fed.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and आशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्तीर्ण
स्वास्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Well spread.<BR>E.<BR>सु, and आस्तीर्ण spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्य|स्वास्थ्यं
स्वास्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>1 Health.<BR>2 Content, happiness, complacency^1, satisfaction.<BR>3 Fortitude, firmness, self-dependance.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, स्थ who is, or stays, ष्यञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation used in making an oblation to the gods.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A personification of the preceding, as the wife of fire, and goddess presiding over burnt offerings.<BR>2 A female divinity, peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, auspiciously, आङ् before ह्वेञ् to call, to invoke, (the gods,) and डा aff., or स्वाद to taste, aff. आ, and द changed to ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाकार|स्वाहाकारः
स्वाहाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Utterance of the term Svāhā.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाहा, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहापति|स्वाहापतिः
स्वाहापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाहा the goddess, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाप्रिय|स्वाहाप्रियः
स्वाहाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाहा the goddess, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाभुज्
स्वाहाभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्त्)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाहा the exclamation, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वित्
स्वित्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of questioning, (hey, what?)<BR>2 An exclamation of doubt or surprise.<BR>3 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>सु well, इण् to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विदित|स्विदितः
स्विदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sweated, melted.<BR>2 Sweating, perspiring.<BR>E.<BR>स्वाद to be unctuous, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विन्न|स्विन्नः
स्विन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Sweating, perspiring.<BR>E.<BR>ष्विद to perspire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरण|स्वीकरणं
स्वीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Assenting, agreeing.<BR>2 Promising.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरणीय
स्वीकरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be promised.<BR>2 To be admitted, consented, or agreed to.<BR>E.<BR>स्व before कृ to make, अनीयर् aff., च्चि augment; also स्वीकर्त्तव्य and स्वीकृत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार|स्वीकारः
स्वीकार<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 Promise.<BR>2 Assent, agreement.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, कार making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकाररहित
स्वीकाररहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not agreed or assented to.<BR>E.<BR>स्वीकार, and रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकारान्त
स्वीकारान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Agreed to, consequent upon a promise or assent.<BR>E.<BR>स्वीकार, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत
स्वीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Agreed, assented to.<BR>2 Promised.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत्य
स्वीकृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having agreed or promised.<BR>E.<BR>स्व, and कृत्य having made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Own, relating or belonging to one.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A virtuous woman, one attached solely to her husband.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वरति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To be diseased.<BR>3 To pain or torture.<BR>With सम् prefixed, in an intransitive sense, the verb becomes deponent,<BR>(संस्वरते)<BR>It sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वॄ
स्वॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (स्वृणाति-स्वृणीते)<BR>To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छा
स्वेच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>Wilfulness, following one's own purpose or inclination.<BR>E.<BR>स्व own, इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छामृत्यु|स्वेच्छामृत्युः
स्वेच्छामृत्यु<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेच्छा wish, and मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छाहार
स्वेच्छाहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Omnivorous, eating anything at pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेच्छा, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेद|स्वेदः
स्वेद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Warm, perspiring.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Warmth, heat.<BR>2 Perspiration, sweat.<BR>3 Warm vapour, steam.<BR>E.<BR>ष्विद to perspire, &c, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदचूषक|स्वेदचूषकः
स्वेदचूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pleasant and cooling breeze.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद perspiration, चूष to suck or imbibe, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदछिद्|स्वेदच्छिद्
स्वेदछिद्<BR>mfn. (-छित्)<BR>Cooling, allaying perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद, and छिद् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदज|स्वेदजः
स्वेदज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Engendered by heat and damp, as insects and worms.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद sweat or warm vapour, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदजल
स्वेदजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदन|स्वेदनं
स्वेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Perspiration, sweat.<BR>2 Sweeting, causing to perspire.<BR>3 A diaphoretic, a sudorific.<BR>E.<BR>ष्विद to be unctuous or sweaty, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनिका
स्वेदनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An iron plate or pan used as a cooking utensil.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेदन sweat, ङीष् aff., and कन् fem. form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनी
स्वेदनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An iron plate or pan used as a frying pan, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ष्विद to perspire, ल्युट् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदमलोञ्झितदेह
स्वेदमलोञ्झितदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A holy or sainted teacher of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद perspiration, मल excrement, उञ्झित abandoned, and देह body: whose body is no longer subject to its original impurities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदविन्दु
स्वेदविन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>A drop of perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदविप्रुष्
स्वेदविप्रुष्<BR>f. (-प्रुट्)<BR>A drop of perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद sweat, and विप्रुष् a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदित
स्वेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sweated, heated.<BR>E.<BR>स्विद to sweat, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोदक
स्वेदोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>स्वेद, and उदक water; also स्वेदोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR>2 Slow, lazy.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Following one's own inclination.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, ईर to go or be, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरवृत्त
स्वैरवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Acting or living as one likes.<BR>E.<BR>स्वैर, and वृत्त practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=966" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wilfulness, independence.<BR>E.<BR>स्वैर self-willed, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिता
स्वैरिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>स्वैरिन् self-willed, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Uncontrouled, self-willed.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 An unchaste wife, an adulteress^1.<BR>2 A wanton woman.<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, ईर to go, णिनि aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोपार्जित|स्वोपार्ज्जितः
स्वोपार्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Self-got, self-acquired, (as wealth, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>स्व self, उपार्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोरस|स्वोरसः
स्वोरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Sediment of oil, &c. ground with a stone and muller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह<BR>The thirty-third and last consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet; the letter H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह<BR>Subst. mfn. (हः-हा-हं)<BR>Laughter.<BR>Adj.<BR>Mad, drunk.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A cypher.<BR>4 Meditation.<BR>5 Auspiciousness.<BR>6 Sky, heaven.<BR>7 Paradise.<BR>8 Blood.<BR>9 Dying.<BR>10 Fear.<BR>11 Knowledge.<BR>12 The moon.<BR>13 VIṢṆU.<BR>14 War, battle.<BR>15 Horripilation.<BR>16 A horse.<BR>17 Pride.<BR>18 A physician.<BR>19 Cause, motive.<BR>f. (हा)<BR>1 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>2 Coition.<BR>3 A lute.<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>GOD, the supreme soul.<BR>2 Pleasure, delight.<BR>3 Calling, calling to.<BR>4 A weapon.<BR>5 The sparkling of a gem.<BR>6 The sound of a lute.<BR>ind.<BR>1 An expletive.<BR>2 A vocative particle (ho! holla!)<BR>2 A term of rejection or disdain.<BR>4 A particle of abuse or reproach: see हा, ही, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, or हन to strike, &c., aff. क or ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंस|हंसः
हंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A goose, a gander, a swan.<BR>2 BRAHMA, the supreme soul.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>5 A liberal or moderate prince, one not covetous nor ambitious.<BR>6 A sort of ascetic or devotee.<BR>7 A particular Mantra, or mystical or magical prayer.<BR>8 A horse.<BR>9 One of the vital airs.<BR>10 Envy, malice.<BR>11 ŚIVA.<BR>12 (In composition,) Best, excellent.<BR>13 Preceding, before, in front.<BR>14 A spiritual preceptor.<BR>15 A mountain.<BR>16 A buffalo.<BR>17 KĀMA.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to hurt or kill, Uṇādi aff. स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसक|हंसकः
हंसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An ornament for the feet, described as being made like a goose's foot.<BR>2 The flamingo.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकूट|हंसकूटः
हंसकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The hump on the shoulder of the Indian ox.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगद्गदा
हंसगद्गदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A woman speaking sweetly or pleasantly.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, गद to sound, reiterated, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगामिनी
हंसगामिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A graceful woman.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, (or swan,) and गामिनी who goes, (like.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसदाहन|हंसदाहनं
हंसदाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and दाहन burning, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनाद|हंसनादः
हंसनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Cackling, the cry or noise of a goose.<BR>E.<BR>हंस, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनादिन्
हंसनादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Cackling, making a noise like a goose.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An elegant woman, one of slender waist and large posteriors, with the gait of an elephant and voice of a Koïl.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, नाद cry, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपदी
हंसपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>1 A scandent shrub, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>2 Another plant, perhaps Clitoria ternata.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and पद foot; from a fancied resemblance between it and the flower; also हंसपादी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपाद|हंसपादं
हंसपाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A shrub, (Clitoria ternata ?)<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, पाद a foot, (to which they are compared in colour, form, &c.): see the last; also in the fem. form, कन् added, हंसपादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसमाला
हंसमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A duck.<BR>2 A flight or flock of wild geese.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, माला a garland or wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसरथ|हंसरथः
हंसरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and रथ vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोमश|हंसलोमशं
हंसलोमश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Sulphate of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवती
हंसवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, (its foot,) and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवाहन|हंसवाहनः
हंसवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and वाहन A vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाङ्घ्रि|हंसाङ्घ्रिः
हंसाङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, and अङ्घ्रि the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाभिख्य|हंसाभिख्यं
हंसाभिख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>हंस a goose, अभिख्या beauty; being of similar colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>हंसी the same, and कन् added, or हन to kill, सिकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of calling, (ho, holla!).<BR>2 A particle of haughtiness or arrogance.<BR>3 An arrogantly interrogative particle.<BR>E.<BR>हं and हो, both vocative particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्क|हक्कः
हक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>The call of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>हक् imitative sound, कै to utter, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्कार|हक्कारः
हक्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Calling, calling to.<BR>E.<BR>हक् sound of calling, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जा|हंजा
हञ्जा<BR>ind.<BR>(In theatrical language.) A vocative particle used in calling to a female attendant.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to treat with disrespect or contempt, aff. आ, and the deriv. irr.; also with ए, aff. हञ्जे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जि|हञ्जिः
हञ्जि<BR>m. (-ञ्जिः)<BR>Sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जे|हंजे
हञ्जे<BR>ind.<BR>(In theatrical language,) a vocative particle to be used in addressing a female attendant.<BR>E.<BR>see हञ्जा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट
हट<BR>r. 1st cl. (हटति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्ट|हट्टः
हट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A market, a moveable market, a fair.<BR>f. (-ट्टी)<BR>A petty market or fair.<BR>E.<BR>हट to shine, ट aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टचौरक|हट्टचौरकः
हट्टचौरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thief, one stealing at fairs and markets.<BR>E.<BR>हट्ट a market, and चौर a thief, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टविलासिनी
हट्टविलासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A sort of drug and perfume.<BR>2 A whore.<BR>E.<BR>हट्ट a market, विलस to wanton or delight, णिनि and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (हठति)<BR>1 To leap or jump.<BR>2 To be wicked.<BR>3 To treat with violence, to oppress.<BR>4 To bind to a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 Violence.<BR>2 Oppression.<BR>3 Rapine.<BR>mf. (-ठः-ठी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>हठ to treat with violence, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठपर्णी
हठपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>हठ Pistia, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठालु|हठालुः
हठालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>हठ the same, and आलु a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडि|हडिः
हडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>A sort of stocks or wooden fetters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिक|हडिकः
हडिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sweeper, a servant of the lowest caste and meanest function.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्ड|हड्डं
हड्ड<BR>n. (-ड्डं)<BR>A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डक|हड्डकः
हड्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sweeper, a Mehter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=967" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डज|हड्डजं
हड्डज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The marrow of the bones.<BR>E.<BR>हड्ड a bone, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डा|हंडा
हण्डा<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of calling to a low female: see हण्डे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डिका|हंडिका
हण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An earthen pot or boiler; also हण्डी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डिकासुत|हण्डिकासुतः
हण्डिकासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small earthen pot.<BR>E.<BR>हण्डिका an earthen pot, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डे|हंडे
हण्डे<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle to be addressed in theatrical language to a female of inferior rank.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to treat with contempt or disrespect, aff. ए, and the form irr.; also with आ, aff. हण्डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत|हतः
हत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Struck, hurt, killed.<BR>2 Destroyed.<BR>3 Departed, lost.<BR>4 Ended.<BR>5 Deprived of, devoid of.<BR>6 Disappointed.<BR>7 Multiplied, (in arithmetic.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Multiplication.<BR>2 Hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to strike or hurt, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतक|हतकः
हतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A coward, a poltroon.<BR>E.<BR>हत slain, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतचित
हतचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bewildered, astounded, bereft of sense.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and चित mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतजीवित
हतजीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Deprived of life or hope, overcome with despair.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Despair.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and जीवित living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतताप
हतताप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Cool after great heat.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतसम्पद
हतसम्पद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Reduced to poverty.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and सम्पद property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतसाध्वस
हतसाध्वस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Fearless, free from fear.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताधिमन्थ
हताधिमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>Loss of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश|हताशः
हताश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Cruel, merciless.<BR>2 Desponding, despairing.<BR>3 Vile, wicked.<BR>4 Barren.<BR>5 Weak, powerless.<BR>E.<BR>हत destroyed, and आशा hope, (in or by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश्व
हताश्व<BR>mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं)<BR>Having the horses killed.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतौजस्
हतौजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Debilitated, weak.<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A kind of fever, fever with debility.<BR>E.<BR>हत, and ओजस् vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्नु|हत्नुः
हत्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to kill or hurt, कत्नुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्या
हत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Killing, slaying, (used chiefly in composition, as ब्रह्महत्या the murder of a Brahman, रिपुहत्या killing an enemy.)<BR>E.<BR>हन् to kill, क्यप् aff., and न changed to त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्वा
हत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having struck or killed.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt, &c., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हथ|हथः
हथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A man dejected or in low spirits.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to hurt, क्थन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद
हद<BR>r. 1st cl. (हदते)<BR>To evacuate as fæces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन|हनः
हन<BR>r. 2nd cl. (हन्ति pl. घ्नन्ति)<BR>1 To hurt, to strike, to injure, to do any act which tends to the destruction of life, to kill.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR>3 To put an end to in any manner.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To sound a musical instrument.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To smite.<BR>With नि or परि,<BR>To destroy, entirely.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To strike.<BR>2 To place upon.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To refute or destroy, an opposite argument.<BR>With वि and आङ्,<BR>To obstruct, to prevent, to hinder.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To slaughter:<BR>(घन् or ध्न is substituted for the radical letters of this verb in many of its inflections and derivatives; the root also takes most of the prefixes with little or no variation of the sense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन|हनः
हन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A killer, a slayer.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, अच् aff.; also with क्विप्, aff. हन् m. (-हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनन|हननं|हननः
हनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, destroying.<BR>2 Injuring, hurting, striking.<BR>3 (In arithmetic,) Multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to hurt or kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हननीय
हननीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>What may be or ought to be struck, beaten, killed.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनु|हनुः
हनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः or नूः)<BR>The jaw.<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>1 A drug and perfume: see हट्टविलासिनी.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>3 Sickness.<BR>4 Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to hurt or kill, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुग्रह|हनुग्रहः
हनुग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Locked jaw.<BR>E.<BR>हनु, and ग्रह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमत्|हनुमन्त्
हनुमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>1 The monkey chief HANUMĀN, the son of AÑJANĪ, by PAVANA, or the wind, the friend, ally and spy of RĀMACANDRA, in his invasion of Laṅkā.<BR>2 A particular sort of monkey, (Simia sinica.)<BR>E.<BR>हनु the jaw, and मतुप् aff.; also with हनू the same, हनूमत् m. (-मान्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुस्तम्भ|हनुस्तम्भः
हनुस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Locked jaw.<BR>E.<BR>हनु, and स्तम्भ stiffness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूष|हनूषः
हनूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A goblin, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, ऊषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त|हंत
हन्त<BR>ind.<BR>1 An inceptive particle.<BR>2 An exclamation of grief, (ah, alas!)<BR>3 Of pity.<BR>4 Of pleasure.<BR>5 Of hurry or haste.<BR>E.<BR>हन् to kill, त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तव्य
हन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What may be, or ought to be struck, killed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हन, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्ताकार
हन्ताकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rice to be given to a guest.<BR>E.<BR>हन्ता a measure of food, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तु|हंतुः|हन्तुः
हन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, तु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तृ|हंतृ
हन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A murderer, a slayer.<BR>2 A measure of food, four times four double handfuls.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, तृच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तोक्ति|हंतोक्ति|हन्तोक्तिः
हन्तोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Tenderness, compassion.<BR>E.<BR>हन्त alas! and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्न|हन्नं|हन्नः
हन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Passed as ordure.<BR>E.<BR>हद to void fæces, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्यमान|हन्यमानः
हन्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being killed or struck.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt or kill, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
हम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of wrath.<BR>2 An expression of courtesy or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भा|हंभा
हम्भा<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>The lowing of kine.<BR>E.<BR>हम् imitative sound, भा to shine, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भारवविराविन्
हम्भारवविराविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि)<BR>Lowing, bellowing.<BR>E.<BR>हम्भा, रव sound, विराविन् uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्म
हम्म<BR>r. 1st cl. (हम्मति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय<BR>r. 1st cl. (हयति)<BR>1 To move.<BR>2 To worship.<BR>3 To sound.<BR>4 To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A man of a particular class.<BR>3 The number seven.<BR>4 INDRA.<BR>5 The Yak.<BR>6 (In prosody,) A foot of four short syllables, a proceleusmaticus.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>हय to go, or हि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयगन्धा
हयगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयग्रीव|हयग्रीवः
हयग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A prince of the Daityas, who during BRAHMĀ'S sleep at the end of a Kalpa stole the Vedas; in the recovery of them, he was slain by VIṢṆU, after his descent as the Matsya or fish Avatāra.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and ग्रीबा neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=968" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयग्रीवहन्
हयग्रीवहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हयग्रीव the Daitya, and हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयङ्कष|हयंकष|हयंकषः|हयङ्कषः
हयङ्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A driver, a charioteer.<BR>2 INDRA'S charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and कष to hurt, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयज्ञ|हयज्ञः
हयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A horse-dealer, a groom, one who is a judge of the qualities of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>हय, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयज्ञता
हयज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Horsemanship, knowledge of horses and their management.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयद्विषत्|हयद्विषन्त्
हयद्विषत्<BR>m. (-न्)<BR>The buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>हय, and द्विषत् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयन|हयनं|हयनः
हयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A covered carriage.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>हय to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयपुच्छ
हयपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A horse's tail.<BR>f. (-च्छी)<BR>A leguminous plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and पुच्छ the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयप्रिय|हयप्रियः
हयप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमारक|हयमारकः
हयमारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shrub, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and मारक killer; also with मार the same, हयमार m. (-रः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमारण|हयमारणः
हयमारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and मारण killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमेध|हयमेधः
हयमेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The sacrifice of a horse: see अश्वमेघ.<BR>E.<BR>हय, and मेध sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयवाहन|हयवाहनः
हयवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The son of SŪRYA or the sun.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयवाहनसङ्कर|हयवाहनसंकर
हयवाहनसङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Mountain ebony, the red sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयानन्द|हयानन्दः
हयानन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारि|हयारिः
हयारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A shrub, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and अरि inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारूढ|हयारूढः
हयारूढ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A horseman, a rider.<BR>E.<BR>हय, and आरूढ mounted on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारोह|हयारोहः
हयारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Riding, horsemanship.<BR>E.<BR>हय, and आरीह mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयाशना
हयाशना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The gum Olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयोत्तम|हयोत्तमः
हयोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An excellent horse.<BR>E.<BR>हय a horse, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री or रा-रं)<BR>Who or what takes or seizes, carries or conveys, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 AGNI.<BR>3 An ass.<BR>4 (In arithmetic,) A divisor; also the denominator of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. अप् or टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरक|हरकः
हरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>2 A person of reflection.<BR>3 A taker, a conveyer, a seizer.<BR>4 (In arithmetic,) A divisor; also division.<BR>5 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरचूडामणि|हरचूडामणिः
हरचूडामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>हर ŚIVA, चूडा the crest, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरण|हरणं
हरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking, (either in a good or bad sense,) accepting, receiving, seizing, carrying off or away.<BR>2 A special gift, as a nuptial present, alms to a student at his initiation, &c.<BR>3 The arm.<BR>4 Semen virile.<BR>5 Gold.<BR>6 A Kowri.<BR>7 Boiling water.<BR>8 (In arithmetic,) Dividing, division.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The hand.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरणीय
हरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taken, seized, accepted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरत्
हरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत)<BR>Taking, seizing.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवीज
हरवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>हर ŚIVA, and वीज semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरशेखरा
हरशेखरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>हर ŚIVA, and शेखरा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरहूरा
हरहूरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A grape; also हारहूरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हराद्रि|हराद्रिः
हराद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>Mount Kailāsa, the favourite resort of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हर ŚIVA, and अद्रि mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>1 Green.<BR>2 Tawny.<BR>3 Yellow.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU, or as considered to be the same deity, KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 YAMA.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>4 INDRA.<BR>5 The moon.<BR>6 The sun.<BR>7 A lion.<BR>8 A ray of light.<BR>9 A horse.<BR>10 A parrot.<BR>11 An ape.<BR>12 A snake.<BR>13 A frog.<BR>14 ŚIVA.<BR>15 One of the nine Varṣas into which the known continent is divided.<BR>16 BRAHMĀ.<BR>17 Fire.<BR>18 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>19 A goose.<BR>20 A peacock.<BR>21 Green, (the colour.)<BR>22 Tawny, the colour.<BR>23 A golden colour, or yellow.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, to seize, (the world or men's hearts, &c.,) Uṇādi aff. इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिक|हरिकः
हरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A horse of a yellowish blue tint.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>3 A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेलीय|हरिकेलीयः
हरिकेलीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, केलि sport, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेश|हरिकेशः
हरिकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, क BRAHMĀ, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगृह|हरिगृहं
हरिगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A city and district, also Sambhalpur.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and गृह abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचन्दन|हरिचंदन|हरिचन्दनं|हरिचन्दनः
हरिचन्दन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 A yellow and fragrant sort of Sandal wood.<BR>2 One of the trees of paradise.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Saffron.<BR>2 Moon-light.<BR>3 The farina of the lotus.<BR>4 The person of a lover or mistress.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, or yellow, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Yellowish white.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A deer.<BR>2 Yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>3 White.<BR>4 VIṢṆU.<BR>5 ŚIVA.<BR>6 The sun.<BR>7 A goose.<BR>8 A minor division of the world.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A doe.<BR>2 A golden image.<BR>3 A woman, one of the four kinds, the same as the Citriṇī, or female of the man termed Mṛga.<BR>4 A form of metre, a variety of the class termed Atyaṣṭi or verse of four lines of 17 syllables each.<BR>5 Green: see हरित.<BR>6 Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, Uṇādi aff. इनच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकलङ्क|हरिणकलंक|हरिणकलङ्कः
हरिणकलङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, कलङ्क a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनयन
हरिणनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Deer-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण, and नयन the eye; also हरिण, लोचन, हरिणाक्षि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनर्त्तक|हरिणनर्तक|हरिणनर्तकः|हरिणनर्त्तकः
हरिणनर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chorister of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, and नर्त्तक a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणप्लुता
हरिणप्लुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A stanza having eleven syllables in every first and third Pāda, and twelve in every second and fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणहृदय|हरिणहृदयः
हरिणहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearful, timid.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, and हृदय heart; deer-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्षी
हरिणाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>1 A perfume, commonly Hāttavilāsinī.<BR>2 A woman with handsome eyes.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, and अक्षि the eye, fem. aff. ङीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाङ्क|हरिणांक|हरिणाङ्कः
हरिणाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, and अङ्क mark or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित्<BR>mfn. (-रित्)<BR>Green, of a green colour.<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>1 Green, (the colour.)<BR>2 A swift horse or a horse of the sun.<BR>3 Kidneybean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>4 A lion.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>6 VIṢṆU.<BR>mn. (-रित्)<BR>Grass.<BR>f. (-रित्).<BR>1 A quarter or region, a point of the compass.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, Uṇādi aff. इति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or रिणी-तं)<BR>1 Green, of a green colour. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">Page970</a>]<BR>2 Grassy, verdant.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Green, (the colour.)<BR>2 A lion.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Bent grass.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>3 A brown or tawny grape.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, इतन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=969" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितक|हरितकं
हरितक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A potherb.<BR>E.<BR>हरित green, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितछद|हरितच्छद
हरितछद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Green-leaved.<BR>E.<BR>हरित, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितायत्
हरितायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Becoming green.<BR>E.<BR>हरित used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>2 A streak or line in the sky, (the milky way?)<BR>3 A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>हरित green, अल to possess or adorn, aff. अण्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालक|हरितालकं|हरितालकः
हरितालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The green pigeon.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Theatrical decoration, painting the person, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हरिताल orpiment, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालिका
हरितालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of grass, (Panicum dactylon, Rox.)<BR>2 The fourth lunar day of the month Bhadra.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to हरिताल, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताश्मन्
हरिताश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>1 Blue vitriol.<BR>2 A turquoise.<BR>3 An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>हरित green, अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितीकृत
हरितीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made verdant or green, coloured green, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हरित, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्पर्ण|हरित्पर्णं
हरित्पर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A radish.<BR>E.<BR>हरित् green, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदश्व|हरिदश्वः
हरिदश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>हरित् green, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदेव|हरिदेवः
हरिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The asterism Srāvaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and देव presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रव|हरिद्रवः
हरिद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A powder of the blossoms of the Mesua ferrea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Turmeric, (either the plant or the powdered root.)<BR>E.<BR>हरित् green, द्रु to flow or ooze, aff. ड, or हरि VIṢṆU, &c., दृ to be regarded, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राक्त
हरिद्राक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Smeared or stained with turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>हरिद्रा, and अक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राङ्ग|हरिद्राङ्गः
हरिद्राङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A yellow bird.<BR>E.<BR>हरिद्रा turmeric, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राभ|हरिद्राभः
हरिद्राभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Of a yellow colour.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>2 Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>3 Yellow, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>हरिद्रा turmeric, आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राराग|हरिद्रारागः
हरिद्राराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Fickle, capricious, unsteady, in affection or attachment.<BR>E.<BR>हरिद्रा turmeric, and राग colour, in opposition to the नीलराग or true blue; also with कन् added. हरिद्रारागक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रु|हरिद्रुः
हरिद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>हरि a monkey, द्रु to go, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्वार|हरिद्वारं
हरिद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The town of Haridvār, where the Ganges descends into the level land of Hindustan.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and द्वार gate; being the road to Vaikuṇṭha or VIṢṆU'S heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनामन्
हरिनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>हरि the same, and नामन् appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनेत्र|हरिनेत्रं|हरिनेत्रः
हरिनेत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An owl.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, &c., and नेत्र an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिन्मणि|हरिन्मणिः
हरिन्मणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>हरित् green, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिपर्ण|हरिपर्णं
हरिपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A radish.<BR>E.<BR>हरि green, and पर्ण a leaf; also हरित्पर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रिय|हरिप्रियं|हरिप्रियः
हरिप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Liked or loved by VIṢṆU, &c.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A tree, (Nauclea Cadamba.)<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>4 Armour, mail.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A dark sort of Sandal wood.<BR>2 The fragrant root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 Tulasi or basil.<BR>3 The twelfth day of the lunar fortnight.<BR>4 The earth.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिबालुक|हरिबालुकं
हरिबालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A perfume and drug, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>हरि tawny, बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभद्र|हरिभद्रं
हरिभद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Elavāluka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभुज्
हरिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>हरि a frog, and भुज् what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
हरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Time.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, इमनिच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थ|हरिमन्थः
हरिमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 A tree, (Premna longifolia.)<BR>2 Chick pea.<BR>E.<BR>हरि fire or a horse, &c., and मन्थ agitating or churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थक|हरिमन्थकः
हरिमन्थक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Chick pea, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थज|हरिमन्थजः
हरिमन्थज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Chick pea.<BR>2 A sort of kidney-bean.<BR>E.<BR>हरि a horse, &c., मन्थ churning, chewing, जन to produce, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिय|हरियः
हरिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A horse of a yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिले
हरिले<BR>ind.<BR>A term of calling in theatrical language, addressed to a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिलोचन|हरिलोचनः
हरिलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A crab.<BR>2 An owl.<BR>E.<BR>हरि green, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवत्|हरिवन्त्
हरिवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि a horse, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवर्ष|हरिवर्षं|हरिवर्षः
हरिवर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>A division of the old or known continent; the country between the Niṣadha and Hemakūṭa mountains.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and वर्ष a division of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवाहन|हरिवाहनः
हरिवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवीज|हरिवीजं
हरिवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and वीज semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवृष|हरिवृषं
हरिवृष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A division of the continent: see हरिवर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिशर|हरिशरः
हरिशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and शर an arrow; VIṢṆU having served him as the shaft which set the cities of TRIPURA on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्र|हरिश्चंद्रः|हरिश्चन्द्रः
हरिश्चन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A sovereign, the twenty-eighth of the solar dynasty in the second age, celebrated for his piety and liberality, and who on those accounts was elevated, together with his subjects, to heaven: having been insidiously induced by NĀRADA, to relate his actions with unbecoming pride, he descended from Svarga, a stage at each sentence, till stopping in time, and doing homage to the gods, he was fixed with his capital in mid-air.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and चन्द्र the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्रपुर|हरिश्चन्द्रपुरं
हरिश्चन्द्रपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>हरिश्चन्द्र a name, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिषेण|हरिषेणः
हरिषेण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The tenth of the twelve universal emperors enumerated by the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, &c., and सेना a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसुत|हरिसुतः
हरिसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the emperors of the Jainas; also named HARIṢEṆA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहय|हरिहयः
हरिहय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 SKANDA.<BR>4 GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि green, and हय a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहरात्मक|हरिहरात्मकः
हरिहरात्मक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 GARUḌA.<BR>2 DAKṢA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि VIṢṆU, and हर ŚIVA, आत्मन् self, same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतकी
हरीतकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Yellow or Chebulic myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula); seven varieties of this are distinguished.<BR>E.<BR>हरि green, (colour,) इत gone, got, कन् added, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=970" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणु|हरेणुः
हरेणु<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>1 A drug and perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>2 A reputable woman.<BR>3 Pulse, peas.<BR>4 A deer of a copper colour.<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 Laṅkā.<BR>2 A creeper, marking the boundary of a village.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, एणु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्त्तव्य|हर्तव्य
हर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be seized, taken, accepted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, तव्यर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्त्तृ|हर्तृ
हर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Taking, seizing, conveying, who takes or receives.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take or convey, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्मन्|हर्मन्
हर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Gaping, yawning.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्मित|हर्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्म्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thrown, cast, sent.<BR>2 Burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्मुट|हर्मुट|हर्मुटः|हर्म्मुटः
हर्म्मुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्म्य
हर्म्म्य<BR>n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>A palace, a mansion, the habitation of a man of wealth or rank.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, (the mind,) यत् aff., and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्य|हर्य
हर्य्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (हर्य्यति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To desire.<BR>3 To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यक्ष|हर्यक्ष|हर्यक्षः|हर्य्यक्षः
हर्य्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>हरि tawny or green, and अक्षि the eye, षच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यत|हर्यत|हर्यतः|हर्य्यतः
हर्य्यत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A steed fit for an Aśvamedha.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, अतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यश्व|हर्यश्व|हर्यश्वः|हर्य्यश्वः
हर्य्यश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Joy, pleasure, delight, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Delighting, pleasing, delightful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to please, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षकर
हर्षकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Causing delight, gratifying, delighting.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं)<BR>Causing delight, delighting, delightful, pleasurable, pleasant, &c.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A cause of pleasure, any thing which confers pleasure.<BR>2 The fourteenth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>3 A morbid affection of the eyes.<BR>4 A deity presiding over Śrāddhas.<BR>5 A kind of Śrāddha.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Pleasing, making happy.<BR>2 Rejoicing, being happy.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षमाण|हर्षमाणः
हर्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Joyful, cheerful, happy.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु<BR>mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु)<BR>Causing delight, delighting.<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>A son, a child.<BR>n. (-त्नु)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, Uṇādi aff. इत्नुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षविह्वल
हर्षविह्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Overjoyed.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and विह्वल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षसमन्वित
हर्षसमन्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Joyful.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and समन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षस्वन|हर्षस्वनः
हर्षस्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cry or sound expressing joy or pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष gladness, and स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षित|हर्षितः
हर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Happy, delighted, gladdened, made glad or happy.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and इतच् aff., or हृष to be pleased, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुल|हर्षुलः
हर्षुल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>1 A deer.<BR>2 A lover.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, उलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोत्कर्ष|हर्षोत्कर्षः
हर्षोत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Great happiness.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and उत्कर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोदय|हर्षोदयः
हर्षोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Appearance or occurrence of happiness.<BR>E.<BR>हर्ष, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल<BR>r. 1st cl. (हलति)<BR>To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A plough.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Vinous liquor.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>हल to plough, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलधर|हलधरः
हलधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Holding or having a plough.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न, and धर who holds or has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृत्
हलभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Having a plough.<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>हल a plough, and भृत् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृति|हलभृतिः
हलभृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Agriculture.<BR>2 A saint so named.<BR>E.<BR>हल a plough, and भृति having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहति
हलहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Ploughing, furrowing.<BR>E.<BR>हल, and हति striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहलाशब्द
हलहलाशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>Noise, tumult.<BR>E.<BR>हलहला imitative sound, शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हला
हला<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle, addressed in theatrical language to a female friend.<BR>E.<BR>हल to plough, आ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलायुध|हलायुधः
हलायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>हल a plough, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाह|हलाहः
हलाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of mixed colour; also read हालाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाहल|हलाहलं|हलाहलः
हलाहल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>2 A Jaina or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>3 A sort of lizard or newt.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न to plough, अच् aff., अ negative, and हल the same; also हलहस्न, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलि|हलिः
हलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 A furrow.<BR>2 Agriculture.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न to plough, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिन्
हलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 BALADEVA.<BR>2 A ploughman, a cultivator.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, commonly Lāṅgalīya.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न a plough, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिप्रिय|हलिप्रियः
हलिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Kadamba, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>हस्नि BALARĀMA, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीन|हलीनः
हलीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The teak tree.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न a plough, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीमक|हलीमकः
हलीमक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्य|हल्यं
हल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Ploughed, tilled.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A multitude of ploughs.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>Ploughing.<BR>E.<BR>हस्न a plough, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लक|हल्लकं
हल्लक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लाद to delight, ण्वुल् aff.; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लन|हल्लनं
हल्लन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rolling or tossing as in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीष|हल्लीषं
हल्लीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 A minor dramatic entertainment, chiefly of singing and dancing by one male and eight or ten female performers, a ballet.<BR>2 A dance performed by women in a circle.<BR>E.<BR>हेला wanton sport, लष् or स्नस to be skilful, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.; also हल्लीस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीषक|हल्लीषकं
हल्लीषक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>Dancing in a ring as performed by women.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to हल्लीस or हल्लीष, whence it is also read हल्लीसक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीस
हल्लीस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>A dramatic entertainment, &c.: see हल्लीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 Call, calling.<BR>3 Order, command.<BR>4 Challenging, defying.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, or ह्वे to call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवङ्ग
हवङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Eating rice and curds from a cup of bell-metal.<BR>E.<BR>हव sacrifice, गम to go, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवन|हवनं|हवनः
हवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sacrifice, offering, oblation.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A hole in the ground for receiving a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, ल्युट्. or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनायुस्
हवनायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हवन burnt-offering, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनीय|हवनीयं
हवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be offered with fire, fit for an oblation, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवा
हवा or हवाव<BR>ind.<BR>A term implying undoubtedly, certainly: see हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=971" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविःशेष
हविःशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The residue of an oblation of Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>हविस्, and शेष rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवित्री
हवित्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A hole in the ground for containing a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविरशन|हविरशनः
हविरशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हविस् Ghee, अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्गेह|हविर्गेहं
हविर्गेह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A room in which a burnt-offering is made, a place of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>हविस् Ghee, and गेह a house or apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्भुज्
हविर्भुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हविस्, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्याजिन्
हविर्याजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A priest.<BR>E.<BR>हविस्, and याजिन् who offers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्य|हविष्यं
हविष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 Clarified butter.<BR>2 Rice mixed with Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>हविस् an oblation, यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यभुज्
हविष्यभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हविष्य, and भुज् who eats; also हविष्याशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविस्
हविस्<BR>n. (-विः)<BR>1 Clarified butter.<BR>2 An intended oblation, the article to be so offered, usually clarified butter.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>हु to offer in oblation, असि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्य|हव्यं
हव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be offered in oblation.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 An offering to the gods.<BR>2 Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यपाक|हव्यपाकः
हव्यपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An oblation dressed for the deities.<BR>2 The vessel in which it is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>हव्य an offering to the gods, and पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यवाह|हव्यवाहः
हव्यवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हव्य an oblation, and वाह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यवाहन|हव्यवाहनः
हव्यवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हव्य an oblation, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्याश|हव्याशः
हव्याश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हव्य an oblation, and अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्याशन|हव्याशनः
हव्याशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>हव्य a burnt offering, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस<BR>(ए) हसे r. 1st cl. (हसति)<BR>1 To laugh.<BR>2 To laugh at, to ridicule: (this root does not take the middle voice when it implies reciprocal action, as व्यतिहसन्ति they laugh at each other.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Laughter, laughing, laugh.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसत्
हसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Laughing, smiling.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A portable fire-pan, a small furnace.<BR>2 Arabian jasmine.<BR>3 A Śākinī or female spirit attendant on DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन|हसनं
हसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Laughter, laughing.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A portable fire-place or pan.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनीमणि|हसनीमणिः
हसनीमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>हसनी a fire-place, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन्तिका|हसंतिका
हसन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A portable furnace or fire-pan.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to हसन्ती; see हसत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसिका
हसिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Laughter.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित|हसितं|हसितः
हसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blown, budded, (as a flower.)<BR>2 Smiling.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Laughter.<BR>2 Smiling.<BR>3 The bow of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त|हस्तं|हस्तः
हस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>1 The hand.<BR>2 An elephant's trunk.<BR>3 The thirteenth lunar asterism, designated by a hand, and containing five stars, one of which is γ or δ Corvi.<BR>4 A head of hair, or abundance of hair.<BR>5 A cubit measured by the hand and arm, or from the elbow to the tip of the middle finger.<BR>6 (In prosody,) An anapæst.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>A bellows.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, Uṇādi aff. तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तछेदन|हस्तच्छेदन
हस्तछेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cutting off the hand.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त, and छेदन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ततल
हस्ततल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The palm of the hand.<BR>2 The hand.<BR>3 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त, and तल surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तधारण|हस्तधारणं
हस्तधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Warding off a blow, stopping, resisting, (in a conflict.)<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, and धारण restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तपुच्छ|हस्तपुच्छं
हस्तपुच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>The hand below the wrist.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, and पुच्छ tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवर्त्तिन्|हस्तवर्तिन्
हस्तवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>In hand, seized, held, caught hold of.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त, and वर्त्तिन what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवारण|हस्तवारणं
हस्तवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Resisting an assault, warding off a blow.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, and वारण prohibiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तविम्ब
हस्तविम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>Perfuming the person.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, and विम्ब a red fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तसूत्र
हस्तसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A bracelet, one worn at the wrist.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, and सूत्र a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तस्थ
हस्तस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>In hand, held, grasped.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त, and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तस्थित
हस्तस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Held, in hand.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त, and स्थित staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकक्ष्य|हस्तिकक्ष्यः
हस्तिकक्ष्य<BR>m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, कश to hurt, स aff., and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्ण|हस्तिकर्णः
हस्तिकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The castor oil tree.<BR>2 The Butea frondosa.<BR>3 A demi-god of a particular class.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिन् an elephant, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्णक|हस्तिकर्णकः
हस्तिकर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्णदल|हस्तिकर्णदलः
हस्तिकर्णदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, कर्ण the ear, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकन्द|हस्तिकन्दः
हस्तिकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकोलि|हस्तिकोलिः
हस्तिकोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of jujube.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and कोलि jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिगिरि|हस्तिगिरिः
हस्तिगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The city Kāñci, a place of pilgrimage in the peninsula.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिघोषा
हस्तिघोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A kind of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and घोषा the generic name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिघ्न|हस्तिघ्नः
हस्तिघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिचारिन्
हस्तिचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An elephant-driver.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति, and चारिन् who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिदन्त|हस्तिदंत|हस्तिदन्तं|हस्तिदन्तः
हस्तिदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The radish.<BR>2 A pin or bracket projecting from a wall to hang any thing upon.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Ivory.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and दन्त a tooth; also with कन् added, हस्तिदन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिद्वयस|हस्तिद्वयसः
हस्तिद्वयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>As big as an elephant, gigantic, elephantine.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, द्वयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिन्
हस्तिन्<BR>m. (-स्ती)<BR>An elephant.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>2 A female; one of the four kinds into which they are classed, and described as of low stature, corpulent habits, curly hair, dark complexion, libidinous appetite, and furious passions.<BR>3 A drug and perfume; also हट्टविस्नासिनी.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त a trunk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनख|हस्तिनखः
हस्तिनख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>A sort of covered way, a raised place of earth or masonry, covering the access to the gate of a city or fort.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and नख nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुर|हस्तिनापुरं
हस्तिनापुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Ancient Dehli, the capital of YUDHIṢṬHIRA and his brethren, the remains of which still exist, about 57 [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">Page973</a>] miles north-east of the modern city, on the banks of the old channel of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिन् the name of a king, its founder, or an elephant, &c., and पुर city; also हस्तिनीपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=972" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिप|हस्तिपः
हस्तिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An elephant rider or driver.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिन् an elephant, पाल to cherish or rear, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिपक|हस्तिपकः
हस्तिपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An elephant-driver or keeper.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिप the same, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिपर्णी
हस्तिपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Moraṭā.<BR>2 A sort of gourd, (Momordica mixta.)<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमद|हस्तिमदः
हस्तिमद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples when in rut.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and मद the frontal juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमल्ल|हस्तिमल्लः
हस्तिमल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 ŚAṄKHA, the eighth of the chief Nāgas or serpents of the infernal regions.<BR>3 The elephant of INDRA.<BR>4 A heap of ashes.<BR>5 A shower of dust.<BR>6 Frost, cold.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and मल्ल a wrestler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिवाह|हस्तिवाहः
हस्तिवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A goad.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and वाह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिशाला
हस्तिशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An elephant stall or stable.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and शाला hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिशुण्डा
हस्तिशुण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा or ण्डी)<BR>1 An elephant's trunk.<BR>2 A flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, शुण्डा the trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तेकरण|हस्तेकरणं
हस्तेकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand in the seventh case, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>1 Given with the hand.<BR>2 Done with the hand, manual.<BR>E.<BR>हस्त the hand, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्यारोह|हस्त्यारोहः
हस्त्यारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An elephant rider or driver.<BR>E.<BR>हस्ति an elephant, and आरोह who mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>Stupid, ignorant, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh at or deride, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहल|हहलं
हहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A Gandharba or chorister of heaven; also हाहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा<BR>r. 3rd cl. (ओ क,) ओहाक् (जहाति)<BR>1 To quit, to leave, to abandon.<BR>2 To wander or deviate:<BR>(ओ ड,) ओहाङ् (जिहते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of weariness.<BR>2 Of sorrow, pain.<BR>3 An exclamation of pleasure.<BR>4 A term of reproach.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, aff. क्विप्; the word corresponds to ah, alas, oh, ha, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाङ्गर|हांगर|हांगरः|हाङ्गरः
हाङ्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Golden, of gold, (as a weight or coin.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>हट to shine, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकमय|हाटकमयं
हाटकमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of gold, golden.<BR>E.<BR>हाटक gold, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हातव्य|हातव्यं
हातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be abandoned, to be left.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, तव्यर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्र|हात्रं|हात्रः
हात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Wages, hire.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abandoning, relinquishing.<BR>2 Prowess, valour.<BR>E.<BR>हा to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानि|हानिः
हानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Loss, privation, abandonment, relinquishment.<BR>E.<BR>हा to leave, Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानुक|हानुकः
हानुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mischievous, hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt or kill, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्द्र|हान्द्रं
हान्द्र<BR>n. (-न्द्रं)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुचिका
हापुचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird, (a wagtail.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्री
हापुत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाफिका
हाफिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायन|हायनं|हायनः
हायन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>A year.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A flame, a ray.<BR>2 A sort of rice.<BR>E.<BR>हा to go or leave, ल्युट् aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
हार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what takes, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A porter, a carrier.<BR>2 Taking, conveying.<BR>3 A string or garland of pearls, &c.<BR>4 War, battle.<BR>5 (In prosody,) A long syllable.<BR>6 (In arithmetic,) A divisor, also the denominator of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to seize, (the mind, &c.) and घञ् aff., or causal form, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारक|हारकः
हारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 A cheat, a rogue.<BR>3 Prose.<BR>4 Science.<BR>5 A gambler.<BR>6 A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>7 A plunderer, a ravisher, one who carries off any thing.<BR>8 (In arithmetic,) A divisor.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयष्टि|हारयष्टिः
हारयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A necklace.<BR>E.<BR>हार, and यष्टि a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूर|हारहूरः
हारहूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Wine, vinous liquor.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः or -री-रि)<BR>Handsome, charming.<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 Defeat, discomfiture, either in war or gambling, &c.<BR>2 A traveller's progeny or family.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take or steal, aff. इञ्, optionally in the fem. form ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिकण्ठ|हारिकंठ|हारिकण्ठः
हारिकण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठी-ण्ठं)<BR>Wearing or having a necklace.<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>हारि for हार a necklace, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Relating to deer, (deer-flesh, skin, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>हरिण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिक|हारिणिकः
हारिणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A species of the Atyaṣṭi metre.<BR>E.<BR>हरिण a deer, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lost, relinquished, made away with.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The green or wood pigeon.<BR>2 Green, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, causal v., क्त aff., or हरित् green, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितक|हारितकं|हारितकः
हारितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A potherb.<BR>E.<BR>हरित the same, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्र|हारिद्रः
हारिद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>1 Stained, dyed, or coloured with turmeric.<BR>2 Yellow.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Cadamba.)<BR>2 Yellow, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>हरिद्रा turmeric, and अण् or अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
हारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Taking, getting, who takes or gets.<BR>2 Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीत|हारीतः
हारीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The green or wood pigeon, (Columba hariala, BUC.)<BR>2 A Muni, and legislator.<BR>3 Roguery, cheating, fraud.<BR>E.<BR>हार a necklace, or हारि defeat, and इत gone, got; or हरित green, अण् aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्द्द|हार्द|हार्दं|हार्द्दं
हार्द्द<BR>n. (-र्द्दं)<BR>Affection, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>हृद the heart, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्य्य|हार्य|हार्यः|हार्य्यः
हार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be taken, to be taken away.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाल|हालः
हाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 BALARĀMA.<BR>2 A name of ŚĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>3 A plough.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Wine, vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>(-ली)<BR>A wife's younger sister.<BR>E.<BR>हाल a plough, aff. अण्, or हल to plough, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालक|हालकः
हालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse of a yellowish red, or tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहल|हालहलं
हालहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहाल|हालहालं
हालहाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison; also variously read हलाहलं, हस्नहलं, हास्नाहलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाह|हालाहः
हालाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A piebald horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=973" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहल|हालाहलं|हालाहलः
हालाहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison: see हास्नहाल.<BR>f. (-स्ना)<BR>A small mouse.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Wine, spirituous liquor.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of worm or insect, a kind of newt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलधर|हालाहलधरः
हालाहलधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small black and venomous snake.<BR>E.<BR>हालाहल poison, and धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिक|हालिकः
हालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a plough, as a ploughman, cattle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हल a plough, ठञ् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालु|हालुः
हालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>हल to plough, उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाव|हावः
हाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Any feminine act of amorous pastime, or tending to excite amorous sensations, coquetry, blandishment, dalliance.<BR>2 Calling.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, (to incite passion,) घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास|हासः
हास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Laughing, laughter.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासक|हासकः
हासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A buffoon.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, causal v., वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासकर
हासकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Laughing, laughing at.<BR>2 Causing laughter, merry, ridiculous.<BR>E.<BR>हास, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासस्
हासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>The moon, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, असुन् aff., and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिका
हासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Laughter, mirth.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिन्
हासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Laughing, smiling.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिक|हास्तिकं|हास्तिकः
हास्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A herd of elephants.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A rider on an elephant, an elephant-driver, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिन् an elephant, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिन|हास्तिनं
हास्तिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Elephantine, large, as big as an elephant, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hastināpura, ancient Dehli.<BR>E.<BR>हस्तिन् a sovereign, founder of the city, or an elephant, and अण् aff. of derivation, or abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिनपुर|हास्तिनपुरं
हास्तिनपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Hastināpura.<BR>E.<BR>हास्तिन the same, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Laughable, ridiculous.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Laughter. laughing, mirth.<BR>E.<BR>हस to laugh, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहल|हाहलं
हाहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison: see हलाहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस्<BR>m. (-हाः)<BR>A Gandharba, a celestial being of an inferior order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
हाहा<BR>m. (-हाः)<BR>A Gandharba, a demi-god of an inferior order, attendant on KUVERA and the other gods, and especially the chanter of their praises.<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of surprise, or grief, or pain.<BR>E.<BR>हा alas, interjection of sorrow, हा to abandon, क्विप् aff., or with असि, aff. हाहस्, or हा interjection repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाकार|हाहाकारः
हाहाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The noise or uproar of battle.<BR>2 Lamentation, sound of grief or pity.<BR>E.<BR>हाहा interjection of pain, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाल|हाहालं
हाहाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of poison: see हलाहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि<BR>r. 5th cl. (हिनोति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To send.<BR>3 To grow or increase.<BR>4 To be in pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि<BR>ind.<BR>1 Because, for, on account of.<BR>2 Assembly, certainly, (assertion.)<BR>3 Indeed, surely, (interrogation.)<BR>4 A particle, implying difference or distinction.<BR>5 An expletive.<BR>6 Ah, alas.<BR>7 An interjection of envy or contempt.<BR>8 An interjection of hurry.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Mischievous, malignant, ferocious, savage.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A beast of prey.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>3 A Brahman, who has studied the Atharvan Veda.<BR>E.<BR>हिसि to injure, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसन|हिंसनं
हिंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Injuring, hurting.<BR>E.<BR>हिसि to hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Injury, mischief, &c.; it is usually distinguished as of three sorts, mental, (as malice,) verbal, (abuse,) personal, (striking, wounding, beating, &c.)<BR>2 Slaughter, killing, slaying.<BR>E.<BR>हिंसि to hurt or kill, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाकर्म्मन्|हिंसाकर्मन्
हिंसाकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Incantation to destroy, or the practice of magic, or employment of mystical texts for malevolent and injurious purposes.<BR>2 Any mischievous or malevolent act.<BR>E.<BR>हिंसा injury, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसात्मक
हिंसात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Injurious.<BR>E.<BR>हिंसा, and आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारु|हिंसारुः
हिंसारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>हिंसा injury, ऋ to go or affect, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>E.<BR>हिंसा injury, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालुक|हिंसालुकः
हिंसालुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mischievous or savage dog.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीर|हिंसीरः
हिंसीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 A wretch, a villain.<BR>E.<BR>हिसि to hurt or kill, Uṇādi aff. ईरन् or ईरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>1 Mischievous, hurtful, injurious.<BR>2 Murderous.<BR>3 Formidable, terrible.<BR>4 Fierce, savage.<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>1 BHĪMA.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 A beast of prey.<BR>f. (-स्रा)<BR>1 Spikenard (Valeriana Jaṭāmāṃsī.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Abrus precatorious.)<BR>3 A sort of grain, (Coix barbata.)<BR>4 A vein, a nerve.<BR>E.<BR>हिसि to hurt, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रक|हिंस्रकः
हिंस्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A beast of prey.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रपशु|हिंस्रपशुः
हिंस्रपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A beast of prey.<BR>E.<BR>हिंस्र mischievous, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्क
हिक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (हिक्कति-ते)<BR>1 To sound inarticulately.<BR>2 To hiccough.<BR>r. 10th cl. (हिक्कयते)<BR>To hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्का
हिक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>Hiccough.<BR>E.<BR>हिक्क to hiccough, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्कार|हिंकार|हिंकारः|हिङ्कारः
हिङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>हिं imitative sound, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गु|हिंगु
हिङ्गु<BR>mn. (-ङ्गुः-ङ्गु)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, deriv. irr., or हिम frost, गम to go, डु aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुनिर्य्यास|हिङ्गुनिर्यास|हिंगुनिर्यास|हिङ्गुनिर्यासः
हिङ्गुनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The Nimb tree.<BR>2 Asafoetida, (the gum.)<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafoetida, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुपची
हिङ्गुपची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A leaf, and drug, perhaps the leaf of the asafoetida plant.<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafoetida, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुपर्णी
हिङ्गुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, commonly Banspatri.<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafoetida, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुल|हिंगुल|हिंगुलं|हिंगुलः|हिङ्गुलः
हिङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena).<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafoetida, स्ना to take or give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलि|हिंगुलि|हिंगुलिः|हिङ्गुलिः
हिङ्गुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafœtida, स्ना to take or give, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलिका|हिंगुलिका
हिङ्गुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A prickly night-shade, (Solanum Jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गुली the egg-plant, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलु|हिंगुलु|हिङ्गुलुः
हिङ्गुलु<BR>mn. (-लुः-लु)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafœtida, स्ना to give or take, aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुशिराटिका
हिङ्गुशिराटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Banspatri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गूल|हिङ्गूलं
हिङ्गूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्ज|हिज्जः
हिज्ज<BR>m. (-ज्जः)<BR>A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्जस्न
हिज्जस्न<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, commonly Hijjal, (Barringtonia acutangula).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिञ्जीर|हिंजीर|हिंजीरः|हिञ्जीरः
हिञ्जीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rope or chain for an elephant's feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=974" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिड|हिडं
हिड<BR>(इ) हिडि r. 1st cl. (हिण्डते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To disregard or disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्ब|हिडिंब|हिडिंबः|हिडिम्बः
हिडिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A prince of the Rākṣasas slain by BHĪMA.<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>The sister of Hiḍimbā carried off by BHĪMA: these names are also read हिडम्ब, हिडम्बा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बजित्|हिडिंबजित्
हिडिम्बजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>BHĪMA, the second of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>हिडिम्ब a Rākṣasa, and जित् conqueror; also similar compounds, as हिडिम्बनिसूदनः, हिडिम्बभिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बभिद्|हिडिंबभिद्
हिडिम्बभिद्<BR>m. (-भित् or भिद्)<BR>BHĪMA; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बापति|हिडिम्बापतिः
हिडिम्बापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 HANUMĀN.<BR>2 BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>हिडिम्बा a female Rākṣasa, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बारमण|हिडिम्बारमणः
हिडिम्बारमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 HANUMĀN, the monkey friend and ally of RĀMA.<BR>2 BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>हिडिम्बा a female Rākṣasa, and रमण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डन|हिंडन|हिंडनं|हिण्डनं
हिण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wandering, roaming.<BR>2 Copulation.<BR>3 Writing.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डिक|हिंडिकः|हिण्डिकः
हिण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to go, aff. अच्, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डिर|हिंडिर|हिंडिरः|हिण्डिरः
हिण्डिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to go, or despise, aff. इरन्; also हिण्डीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डी|हिंडी
हिण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to go, or despise, (the Asuras,) अच् aff., and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीप्रियतम|हिण्डीप्रियतमः
हिण्डीप्रियतम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हिण्डी DURGĀ, and प्रियतम dearest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीर|हिंडीर|हिंडीरः|हिण्डीरः
हिण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Cuttle fish bone, considered to be the indurated foam of the sea.<BR>2 A man, a male.<BR>3 The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>4 A tonic or stomachic.<BR>E.<BR>हिडि to go, or despise, aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR>1 Suitable, proper, fit, worthy, right.<BR>2 Gone, proceeded.<BR>3 Held, taken, seized, placed.<BR>4 (In medicine,) Proper, as diet or menstrua, suitable to the case or the medicines taken.<BR>5 Friendly, affectionate, kind.<BR>6 Useful.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A good, a benefit.<BR>(-ता)<BR>A causeway, a dike.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have or hold, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकर|हितकरः
हितकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Friendly, kind, favourable.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A benefactor.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम
हितकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Wishing well to, kind or friendly to.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम्या
हितकाम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>Concern for another's welfare.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and काम्या desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रणी
हितप्रणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary.<BR>E.<BR>हित proper, and प्रणी who instructs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रेप्सु
हितप्रेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Benevolent, benign.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and प्रेप्सु wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितबुद्धि
हितबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Well-disposed to, wishing well to.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवत्|हितवन्त्
हितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Friendly, favourable, doing good to.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवादिन्
हितवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Giving good counsel, directing or advising what is right.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A director, an adviser.<BR>E.<BR>हित proper, and वादिन् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितानुकारिन्
हितानुकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Kind.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and अनुकारिन् who acts conformably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितान्वेषिन्
हितान्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Seeking another's welfare.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and अन्वेषिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिताहित
हिताहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Good and evil, beneficial and disadvantageous.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and अहित bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितैषिन्
हितैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Wishing well to.<BR>E.<BR>हित, and एषिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोक्ति|हितोक्तिः
हितोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Compassion, clemency, tenderness.<BR>2 Good advice.<BR>E.<BR>हित kind, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोपदेश|हितोपदेशः
हितोपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Friendly or proper advice.<BR>E.<BR>हित proper, and उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वा
हित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having left or abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>हा to leave, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्ताल|हिंताल|हिंतालः|हिन्तालः
हिन्ताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The marshy date tree, (Phoenix or Elate paludosa.)<BR>E.<BR>हीन defective, i. e. small, ताल the palm, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोल|हिंदोल|हिंदोलः|हिन्दोलः
हिन्दोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A swing.<BR>2 One of the Rāgas or personified musical modes.<BR>E.<BR>हि particle, दुल to shake, घञ् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलक|हिंदोलक|हिंदोलकः|हिन्दोलकः
हिन्दोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A swing.<BR>E.<BR>हि particle, दुल to shake, aff. घञ्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम|हिमं|हिमः
हिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Cold, frigid.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Frost, snow.<BR>2 Cold.<BR>3 Sandal.<BR>4 Fresh butter.<BR>5 Tin.<BR>6 A pearl.<BR>7 A lotus.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The Sandal tree.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 The Himālaya mountain.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Small cardamoms.<BR>2 Reṇukā, a perfume.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt, मक् Uṇādi aff., and हि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमऋतु
हिमऋतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The cold season.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and ऋतु season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमकर|हिमकरः
हिमकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Frigorific, cold.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and कर who makes, or a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमकूट|हिमकूटः
हिमकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Winter.<BR>E.<BR>हिम frost or cold, and कूट a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमज|हिमजः
हिमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by cold, in the Himālaya, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The mountain Maināka.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 Zedoary.<BR>E.<BR>हिम the Himāla personified, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमज्झटि|हिमज्झटिः
हिमज्झटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>Mist, dew, fog.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, ज्झट to be entangled, इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमदुर्द्दिन|हिमदुर्दिन|हिमदुर्दिनं
हिमदुर्द्दिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Winter, wintry weather, frost and snow.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and दुर्द्दिन bad weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमद्युति|हिमद्युतिः
हिमद्युति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, cooling, and द्युति radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमप्रस्थ|हिमप्रस्थः
हिमप्रस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>The Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and प्रस्थ abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमबालुका
हिमबालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्|हिमवन्त्
हिमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Cold, freezing, chilly, frosty.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The Himālaya range.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्सुत|हिमवत्सुतः
हिमवत्सुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The mountain Maināka.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>हिमवत् the Himālaya, and सुत son, or सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशीतल
हिमशीतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very cold, frosty, freezing.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and शीतल cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशैलजा
हिमशैलजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ or PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>हिमशैल the snowy mountains, and जा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमश्रथ|हिमश्रथः
हिमश्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and श्रथि to shed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमसंहति|हिमसंहतिः
हिमसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Ice and snow.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमहानकृत्
हिमहानकृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, हान loss, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमहासक|हिमहासकः
हिमहासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The marshy date tree.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold or winter, and हासक smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=975" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांशु|हिमांशुः
हिमांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांश्वभिख्य|हिमांश्वभिख्यं
हिमांश्वभिख्य<BR>n. (-ख्या)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>हिमांशु the moon, अभिख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमागम|हिमागमः
हिमागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The cold season, winter.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold or frost, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाद्रि|हिमाद्रिः
हिमाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The snowy range of mountains, skirting the north of India, the Imaus or Emodus.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानी
हिमानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Ice and snow.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, ङीष् aff., and आनुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानिल|हिमानिलः
हिमानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A frosty or cold wind.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाभ
हिमाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Like frost and snow.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाराति|हिमारातिः
हिमाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, अराति the enemy; also similar compounds, as, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमार्त्त|हिमार्त
हिमार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Chilly, cold, suffering from cold.<BR>E.<BR>हिम, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमालय|हिमालयः
हिमालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Himāla or Himālaya range of mountains, which bounds India on the north, and separates it from Tartary; the Imaus and Emodus of the ancients, giving rise to the Ganges, and Indus, and many other considerable rivers, and containing the highest elevations in the world: in mythology, the mountain is personified as the husband of MENAKĀ, and the father of GAṄGĀ or the Ganges, and DURGĀ or UMĀ in her descent as PĀRVATĪ, the mountain nymph, to captivate ŚIVA, and withdraw him from a course of ascetic austerity practised in those regions.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, or frost and snow, and आस्नय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमावती
हिमावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A sort of moon-plant; also स्वर्णक्षीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाह्व|हिमाह्वः
हिमाह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>हिम snow, आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाह्वय|हिमाह्वयः
हिमाह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमिका
हिमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hoar frost.<BR>E.<BR>हिम frost, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमेलु|हिमेलुः
हिमेलु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Suffering from cold, chilly, frozen.<BR>E.<BR>हिम cold, एलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम्य|हिम्यः
हिम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Frozen, snowy, cold, frigid.<BR>E.<BR>हिम frost and snow, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरङ्गु|हिरंगुः|हिरङ्गुः
हिरङ्गु<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>The personified ascending node^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण|हिरणं
हिरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Semen.<BR>3 A cowry.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, ल्युट् aff., and इ substituted for the antepen. vowel: see हिरण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्मय|हिरण्मयं|हिरण्मयः
हिरण्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of gold, golden.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>One of the Varṣas or divisions of the continent; the part between the mountainous ranges Śveta and Śṛṅgavān.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण् for हिरण gold, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्य|हिरण्यं
हिरण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Either of the precious metals, crude bullion, unwrought gold or silver.<BR>3 Silver, crude or wrought.<BR>4 A measure.<BR>5 A cowry.<BR>6 Semen virile.<BR>7 Imperishable matter, that which is eternal.<BR>8 Thing, substance.<BR>9 Wealth, property.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, Uṇādi aff. कन्यन्, and किरच् substituted for the radical letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपु|हिरण्यकशिपुः
हिरण्यकशिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A Daitya, the father of PRAHLĀDA, for whose destruction, VIṢṆU descended in the fourth or NARASIṂHA Avatāra.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, and कशिपु clothing, or food and clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपुहन्
हिरण्यकशिपुहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्यकशिपु a Daitya, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यगर्भ|हिरण्यगर्भः
हिरण्यगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, गर्भं embryo; or the mundane egg floating on the water at creation, of that metal, or of similar colour, from which the deity issued, according to some legends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यद|हिरण्यदः
हिरण्यद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, and द what gives or yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यनाभ|हिरण्यनाभः
हिरण्यनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The mountain Maināka.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, नाम navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यबाहु|हिरण्यबाहुः
हिरण्यबाहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>1 The river Śoṇa.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य golden, बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यरेतस्
हिरण्यरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, and रेतस् semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यव|हिरण्यवः
हिरण्यव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A divine treasure.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, व possessive aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवर्णा
हिरण्यवर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवाह|हिरण्यवाहः
हिरण्यवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The river Śoṇa.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, वह to bear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्याक्ष|हिरण्याक्षः
हिरण्याक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The name of a demon, killed by VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हिरण्य, and अक्ष for अक्षि eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरुक्
हिरुक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Without, except.<BR>2 In the midst of, amongst.<BR>3 Near.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, रुकक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल
हिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (हिलति)<BR>To express amorous inclination, to dally, to wanton, to sport amorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिलमोचि|हिलमोचिः
हिलमोचि<BR>f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>हिल sporting, मुच्च to loosen, इन् aff., ङीष् optionally added; also with कन् added, fem. form, हिलभोचिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्ल|हिल्लः
हिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लिः)<BR>A bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिव
हिव<BR>(इ) हिवि r. 1st cl. (हिव्वति)<BR>1 To be satisfied.<BR>2 To satisfy or please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिस
हिस<BR>(इ) हिसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (हिंसति हिंसयति) and 7th cl. (हिनस्ति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to do any thing tending to the prejudice of another in word, thought, or deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिहि
हिहि<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of surprise or merriment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ही
ही<BR>ind.<BR>1 An exclamation or interjection of surprise;<BR>2 Of fatigue or despondence;<BR>3 Of sorrow;<BR>4 A particle implying cause, (therefore, so.)<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt, डी aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Deficient, defective.<BR>2 Blamable, vile, bad.<BR>3 Left, abandoned, quitted.<BR>4 Wasted, worn, decayed.<BR>5 Void of, free from.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An insufficient or objectionable witness.<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनकर्म्मन्|हीनकर्मन्
हीनकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Neglecting, or not performing the customary rites, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हीन, and कर्म्मन् act; also हीनक्रिय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनजाति|हीनजातिः
हीनजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Outcaste, vile, degraded.<BR>E.<BR>हीन abandoned, and जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवर्ण|हीनवर्णः
हीनवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Of a low caste, outcaste, vile.<BR>E.<BR>हीन, and वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवाद|हीनवादः
हीनवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Prevarication, contradictory evidence.<BR>E.<BR>हीन, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=976" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवादिन्
हीनवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Dumb, speechless.<BR>2 Inadmissible, (as a witness.)<BR>3 Contradictory, prevaricating.<BR>E.<BR>हीन left, or defective, वाद speech, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसख्य|हीनसख्यं
हीनसख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Keeping low company, associating with persons of degraded castes and occupations.<BR>E.<BR>हीन an outcaste, and सख्य friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसन्धि|हीनसंधि|हीनसन्धिः
हीनसन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>Destitute of peace or reconciliation.<BR>E.<BR>हीन, and सन्धि alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसेवा
हीनसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Serving or attending on low persons, associating with them.<BR>E.<BR>हीन, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनाङ्ग|हीनांग|हीनाङ्गः
हीनाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Crippled, maimed, defective.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>An ant.<BR>E.<BR>हीन deficient, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन्ताल|हींताल|हींतालः|हीन्तालः
हीन्ताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The marshy date tree: see हिन्ताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीर|हीरं|हीरः
हीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>4 A necklace.<BR>5 A lion.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A diamond.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A cockroach.<BR>3 An ant.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, क aff., and ईरु substituted for the radical finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरक|हीरकः
हीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The diamond.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीराङ्ग|हीरांग|हीराङ्गः
हीराङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>हीर the diamond, and अङ्ग substance; being supposed to be the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हील|हीलं
हील<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुक|हीलुकं
हीलुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rum, spirits distilled from molasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of surprise, (ah, ha!)<BR>2 An interjection of laughter, (hee, hee!)<BR>E.<BR>ही repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु<BR>r. 3rd cl. (जुहोति)<BR>1 To sacrifice, to offer in oblation.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>3 To take.<BR>4 To please or satisfy.<BR>5 To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कार|हुंकार|हुङ्कारः
हुङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Uttering a menacing sound, roaring, bellowing.<BR>E.<BR>हुम्, and कार making; also similar compounds, as हुङ्कृति, हुङ्कृत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कृत|हुंकृत|हुंकृतं
हुङ्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uttered or pronounced as an incantation.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 An incantation.<BR>2 The roar or grunt of the wild boar.<BR>3 Any roar.<BR>E.<BR>हुम् a mystical monosyllable, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड|हुडः
हुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (हुडति)<BR>To heap together, to collect or accumulate.<BR>(ऋ) हुडृ r. 1st cl. (होडति)<BR>To go or move.<BR>(इ) हुडि r. 1st cl. (हुण्डते)<BR>1 To heap, &c.<BR>2 To accept, to agree to, or assent.<BR>3 To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडु|हुडुः
हुडु<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>हुड to assemble, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्क|हुडुक्कः
हुडुक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>1 A gallinule.<BR>2 A drunken man.<BR>3 A small hourglass-shaped drum.<BR>4 A stick or staff, one bound with iron.<BR>5 The bar of a door.<BR>E.<BR>हुडुक् imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड|हुंड|हुंडः|हुण्डः
हुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 A village hog.<BR>3 A blockhead.<BR>4 An imp, a goblin.<BR>5 A ram.<BR>E.<BR>हुडि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्च्छ
हुर्च्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (हुर्च्छति)<BR>To be crooked, (literally or figuratively,) to be fraudulent.<BR>2 To retreat, to hide or abscond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
हुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Offered with fire, burnt as an oblation.<BR>2 Called, invoked.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, or ह्वे to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुक्प्रिया
हुतभुक्प्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The wife of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>हुतभुज् AGNI, and प्रिया the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुज्
हुतभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>हुत an oblation, भुज to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतवह|हुतवहः
हुतवह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>हुत an oblation, and वह who carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतहोम|हुतहोमः
हुतहोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Brahman who has offered an oblation.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>An oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हुत, and होम sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताग्नि
हुताग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Fire with which oblation is made.<BR>E.<BR>हुत, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताश|हुताशः
हुताश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Fire or its deity AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>हुत an oblation, and अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशन|हुताशनः
हुताशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Fire or its deity.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हुत burnt-offering, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुति|हुतिः
हुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Binding, capture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत्वा
हुत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having offered in oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हु to offer, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of remembering, (ha, ah!)<BR>2 Of repulse or reproach, (away!)<BR>3 Interrogation, (hey?)<BR>4 Assent, (yes.)<BR>5 Doubt.<BR>6 A mystical syllable of frequent occurrence in incantations.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, डुम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुयमान
हुयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being offered in oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हु to offer, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल|हुलः
हुल<BR>r. 1st cl. (होस्नति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To kill.<BR>3 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुस्नहुली
हुस्नहुली<BR>f. (-स्नी)<BR>Inarticulate sounds made by women, especially a sort of Ululatus, though apparently employed upon pleasurable and not sorrowful occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>A Gandharba.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, डु aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहू
हुहू<BR>m. (-हूः)<BR>A Gandharba or chorister of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, डु aff., form irr.; it is also read हुहु, हूहु, and हूहू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of calling, of contempt, of pride, and of grief or weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूङ्कार|हूंकार|हूङ्कारः
हूङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Uttering the sound Hum.<BR>2 Roaring.<BR>E.<BR>हूम्, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड
हूड<BR>(ऋ) हूडृ r. 1st cl. (हूडति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूण|हूणः
हूण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A barbarian, a Hun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत<BR>m. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Called, summoned, invited.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वे to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूति|हूतिः
हूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Calling.<BR>2 Calling to in defiance, challenging.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle or doubt or consideration (humph, ha.)<BR>2 An interrogatory particle, (hey, indeed.)<BR>3 A particle of assent, (yes, well, so be it, amen.)<BR>4 An interjection, of anger.<BR>5 Of fear.<BR>6 Of reproach, contempt, (equivalent to be silent, tush, pish.)<BR>7 Of aversion, repulse, or dislike, &c.<BR>8 A magical or mystical monosyllable.<BR>9 An imitative sound.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, aff. डूम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूयमान
हूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being offered in oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हु to offer pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरव|हूरवः
हूरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>हू a cry of fear or wrath, and रव, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्च्छन
हूर्च्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Crookedness, (literal or figurative,) craft, cunning.<BR>E.<BR>हुर्च्छ to be crooked, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहु|हूहुः
हूहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>A Gandharba: see हुहू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहू
हूहू<BR>m. (-हूः)<BR>A Gandharba: see हुहू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ञ्) हृञ् r. 1st cl. (हरति-ते)<BR>1 To convey.<BR>2 To take or accept.<BR>3 To steal.<BR>4 To destroy or annul.<BR>r. 3rd cl. (हजर्त्ति)<BR>To take by violence.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To imitate.<BR>With अप,<BR>1 To remove, to take away or apart.<BR>2 To leave behind. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">Page978</a>]<BR>3 To steal.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To assault.<BR>With अभि and आङ्,<BR>To reason.<BR>With अभि and उत्,<BR>To deliver.<BR>With अभि, वि, and आङ्,<BR>To utter, to pronounce.<BR>With अव,<BR>1 To regain.<BR>2 To punish or fine.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To raise, to lift or take up.<BR>2 To expel.<BR>With उद् and आङ्,<BR>1 To say or tell.<BR>2 To illustrate, to exemplify.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To bring near to.<BR>2 To give.<BR>With उप and सम्,<BR>To withhold.<BR>With नि changed to नी,<BR>To freeze.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To shew disrespect.<BR>With निर् and आङ्,<BR>To fast.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To reproach, to abuse or censure.<BR>2 To leave, to shun, to abandon.<BR>3 To resist.<BR>4 To extract.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To strike.<BR>With प्रति changed to प्रती,<BR>To keep watch.<BR>With प्रति and आङ्,<BR>To think abstractedly by restraining the organs of sense.<BR>With प्रति and सम्,<BR>To disregard, to abandon.<BR>With वि,<BR>To sport, to ramble for pleasure.<BR>With वि, or वि and आङ्,<BR>To say, to utter, to speak.<BR>With वि and अव,<BR>1 To transact business.<BR>2 To litigate.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To kill.<BR>With सम्, or सम् and आङ्,<BR>To collect, to assemble.<BR>With सम्, अभि, वि and आङ्,<BR>To speak in concert.<BR>With सम्, उत् and आङ्,<BR>To relate.<BR>With सम् and उप,<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To assemble, to collect.<BR>With सम् and प्र,<BR>To fight.<BR>With वि and अति prefixed and implying reciprocity<BR>(व्यतिहरते)<BR>To steal or plunder mutually. In the first sense (to convey), this verb governs two accusatives, as भारं हरति ग्रामं he takes the load (to) the village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=977" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृच्छय|हृच्छयः
हृच्छय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>हृत् the heart, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणिया
हृणिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Shame, modesty.<BR>2 Censure, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>हृणीङ् Kaṇḍvādi root, to be ashamed, यक् aff., and the vowel made short; otherwise हृणीया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीया
हृणीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Censure, reproach.<BR>2 Shame, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत|हृतं
हृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken, taken away, seized.<BR>2 Accepted.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतसर्व्वस्व|हृतसर्वस्व
हृतसर्व्वस्व<BR>mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>Robbed or stripped of all, entirely ruined.<BR>E.<BR>हृत, and सर्व्वस्व all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृताधिकार
हृताधिकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Neglecting one's duty.<BR>2 Deprived of an office, turned out.<BR>3 Barred or deprived of one's right.<BR>E.<BR>हृत, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतोत्तर
हृतोत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Left without a reply.<BR>E.<BR>हृत, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्पिण्ड|हृत्पिंड|हृत्पिण्डः
हृत्पिण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>The heart.<BR>E.<BR>हृत्, and पिण्ड lump of flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्वा
हृत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken, seized, accepted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्स्थ
हृत्स्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्स्थः-त्स्था-त्स्थं)<BR>Seated in the heart.<BR>E.<BR>हृत्, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्
हृद्<BR>n. (हृत् or हृद्)<BR>1 The heart.<BR>2 The mind, the faculty or seat of thought and feeling.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added; or हृद् substituted for the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदय|हृदयं
हृदय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 The mind, the seat or faculty of thought and feeling.<BR>2 The heart.<BR>3 Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, कयन् Uṇādi aff., and दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयग्राहिन्
हृदयग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Captivating, engaging the affections.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय, and ग्राहिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयङ्गम|हृदयंगम|हृदयङ्गमं
हृदयङ्गम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Apposite and proper, (as speech.)<BR>2 Affecting, touching.<BR>3 Dear, beloved.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, गम to go, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयवत्|हृदयवन्त्
हृदयवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Good-hearted, kind, humane.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयस्थान|हृदयस्थानं
हृदयस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The breast, the chest.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयात्मन्
हृदयात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयालु|हृदयालुः
हृदयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Good-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयाविध्
हृदयाविध्<BR>mfn. (-त् or द्)<BR>Heart-piercing.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय, and आविध् what pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिक|हृदयिकः
हृदयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Good-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिन्
हृदयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Good-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयेश|हृदयेशः
हृदयेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय the heart, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयोदङ्क|हृदयोदङ्कः
हृदयोदङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Heart-heaving, distressing.<BR>E.<BR>हृदय, उत् up, अंक what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदावर्त्त|हृदावर्त|हृदावर्तः|हृदावर्त्तः
हृदावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A curl or lock of hair on a horse's neck, or breast.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, and आवर्त्त a twist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिस्पृश्
हृदिस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक)<BR>Dear, beloved, cherished.<BR>E.<BR>हृदि in the heart, and स्पृश् what effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गत
हृद्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conceived, come to mind, designed.<BR>E.<BR>हृद्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गोल|हृद्गोलः
हृद्गोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a mountainous district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गोलीय|हृद्गोलीयः
हृद्गोलीय<BR>m. pl. (-याः)<BR>The military inhabitants of the Hṛdgola mountains.<BR>E.<BR>हृद्गोल as above, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्देश|हृद्देशः
हृद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The heart or the region of it.<BR>E.<BR>हृद्, देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्य|हृद्यं|हृद्यः
हृद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Dear, beloved, cherished, desired.<BR>2 Grateful, pleasant, agreeable.<BR>3 Produced in or from the heart.<BR>4 Affectionate, kind.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A Mantra of the Vedas for effecting any one's subjection or fascination.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Vṛddhi, a medicinal root, so named.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Cassia bark.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्यगन्ध|हृद्यगन्धं|हृद्यगन्धः
हृद्यगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The Bel tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>1 Small cardamoms.<BR>2 Sochal salt.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Great-flowered jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>हृद्य agreeable, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्यता
हृद्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Agreeableness, delightfulness.<BR>E.<BR>हृद्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, हृद्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्रोग|हृद्रोगः
हृद्रोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Heart-burn.<BR>2 Any disease of the heart.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, and रोग disease; also हृदयरोग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्रोगवैरिन्
हृद्रोगवैरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>हृद्रोग the heart-burn, and वैरिन् hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्वण्टक|हृद्वंटक|हृद्वण्टकः
हृद्वण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The stomach.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, and वण्टक a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लास|हृल्लासः
हृल्लास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Hiccough.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, लस् to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लेख|हृल्लेखः
हृल्लेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Regret, sorrow for any object absent or missing.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>हृद् the heart, लिख to write, aff. घञ्; also हृदयलेख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष
हृष<BR>(इर उ) इरहृषु r. 4th cl. (हृष्यति)<BR>To rejoice, to exult, to be pleased or delighted.<BR>(उ) हृषु r. 1st cl. (हर्षति)<BR>To lie, to affirm falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषित|हृषितं
हृषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Astonished, surprised.<BR>2 Pleased, delighted.<BR>3 Exquisitely delighted, having the hair of the body [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">Page979</a>] erect with pleasure.<BR>4 Disappointed, baulked, deceived.<BR>5 Bent, bowed.<BR>6 Armed, accountred.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, aff. क्त, with the augment इट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=978" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीक|हृषीकं
हृषीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Any organ of sense.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to affirm falsely, ईकन् Uṇādi aff., and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीकेश|हृषीकेशः
हृषीकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हृषीक an organ of sense, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट|हृष्टः
हृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>2 Laughing, smiling.<BR>3 Having the hair of the body erect with pleasure.<BR>4 Astonished, surprised.<BR>5 Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, or to affirm falsely, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टपुष्ट
हृष्टपुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Well-conditioned, well fed and happy.<BR>E.<BR>हृष्ट, and पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टमानस|हृष्टमानसः
हृष्टमानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Happy, glad.<BR>E.<BR>हृष्ट pleased, मानस the mind, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टरोमन्
हृष्टरोमन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Having the hair of the body on end.<BR>E.<BR>हृष्ट delighted, रोमन् the down of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टहृदय
हृष्टहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Happy, light-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>हृष्ट, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टि|हृष्टिः
हृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Delight, pleasure, happiness.<BR>2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>हृष to be pleased, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे<BR>ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle.<BR>2 A particle of calling out to, or challenging.<BR>3 An interjection, expressing envy or malice.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, aff. डे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>Hiccough.<BR>E.<BR>हिक्क to hiccough, aff. अच्, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेट
हेट<BR>r. 1st cl. (हेटते)<BR>To resist, to oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ|हेठः
हेठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (हेठते) (ऋ) हेठृ (हेठति)<BR>1 To resist, to oppose, to contend with, to vex or harass.<BR>2 To be wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ|हेठः
हेठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 Obstruction, opposition, hindering, preventing.<BR>2 Injury, hurting.<BR>E.<BR>हेठ to annoy or oppose, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड|हेडः
हेड<BR>r. 1st cl. (हेडति)<BR>To surround, to encompass.<BR>(ऋ) हेडृ (हेडते)<BR>To disregard, to contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडज|हेडजः
हेडज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Passion, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडावुक्क|हेडावुक्कः
हेडावुक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेढ
हेढ<BR>r. 9th cl. (हेढणाति)<BR>1 To be past birth.<BR>2 To produce young.<BR>3 To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेति|हेतिः
हेति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>2 A ray of the sun.<BR>3 Flame.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, or हन to kill, aff. क्तिन्; the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतु|हेतुः
हेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Cause, origin, motive.<BR>2 The reason or argument for an inference or deduction.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, Uṇādi aff. तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Causal, instrumental.<BR>2 Relating or belonging to the cause or motive.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An active cause. an instrument or agent.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु cause, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुता
हेतुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Causation, cause, causativeness, the abstract existence of cause or motive.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु cause, तल aff.; also हेतुत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुमत्|हेतुमन्त्
हेतुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Having a cause, proceding from one, acknowledging one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवाद|हेतुवादः
हेतुवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Disputation.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु, and वाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतौ
हेतौ<BR>ind.<BR>By reason or cause of.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु in the seventh case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वाभास|हेत्वाभासः
हेत्वाभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>(In logic,) Fallacious semblance of reason or argument, assignment of proof or cause which can be shewn to be incorrect; various kinds are specified.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु, and आभास semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम|हेमं|हेमः
हेम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A horse of a dark colour.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Gold.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 An Apsaras or courtesan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>2 A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, मक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकन्दस्न
हेमकन्दस्न<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and कन्दस्न a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकार|हेमकारः
हेमकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन् gold, and कार who makes or works; also हेमकर्त्तृ (-र्त्ता,) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकूट|हेमकूटः
हेमकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>One of the ranges of mountains dividing the known continent into nine Varṣas; this range is the second south of Ilāvṛta, or the central division, and is immediately to the north of the Himālaya, forming with it the boundaries of the Kinnara Varṣam.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold or golden, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकेलि|हेमकेलिः
हेमकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and केलि who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकेश|हेमकेशः
हेमकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and केश् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमक्षीरी
हेमक्षीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and क्षीरी a name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमगन्धिनी|हेमगंधिनी
हेमगन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Reṇuka, a perfume.<BR>E.<BR>हेम golden, and गन्धिनी a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमज्वास्न
हेमज्वास्न<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमतरु|हेमतरुः
हेमतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>Datura or thorn-apple.<BR>E.<BR>हेम, and तरु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमतार|हेमतारं
हेमतार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, तृ to pass, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमदुग्ध|हेमदुग्धः
हेमदुग्ध<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>The glomerous fig tree.<BR>f. (-ग्धी)<BR>A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, टुग्ध milk; also with कन् added, हेमटुग्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमदुग्धक|हेमदुग्धकः
हेमदुग्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata): see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Gold.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 The planet MERCURY.<BR>2 Winter.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमन्त<BR>mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>The cold season, winter, the two months, Agrahāyaṇa and Pauṣa, or about November-December.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt, भच् Uṇādi aff., हि substituted for the root, and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्तनाथ|हेमन्तनाथः
हेमन्तनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Elephant or wood-apple.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन्त winter, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपर्व्वत|हेमपर्वत|हेमपर्वतः|हेमपर्व्वतः
हेमपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The mountain Meru.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and पर्व्वत mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपुष्प|हेमपुष्पं|हेमपुष्पः
हेमपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 The Aśoka tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>2 The China rose, the flower.<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 The Champaka, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2 The Lodh tree.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>Bengal madder.<BR>E.<BR>हेम golden, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपुष्पक|हेमपुष्पकः
हेमपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Champaka.<BR>f. (-ष्पिका)<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममाला
हेममाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The wife of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमरत्नमय
हेमरत्नमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Full of gold and gems.<BR>E.<BR>हेम, and रत्न a gem, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमरागिणी
हेमरागिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, राग colour, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमल|हेमलः
हेमल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A goldsmith.<BR>2 A chameleon, a lizard.<BR>3 A touchstone.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, ला to have or take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, वल surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशङ्ख|हेमशंख|हेमशङ्खः
हेमशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=979" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशिखा
हेमशिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and शिखा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमसूत्रक|हेमसूत्रकं
हेमसूत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A necklace.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, सूत्र a string, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्ग|हेमांग|हेमाङ्गः
हेमाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 GARUḌA.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 The mountain Sumeru.<BR>4 BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 The Champaka, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाद्रि|हेमाद्रिः
हेमाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The mountain Meru.<BR>E.<BR>हेम gold, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
हेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be left, abandoned, avoided, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेर|हेरं
हेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A sort of crown or tiara.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>3 The illusion of a demon.<BR>E.<BR>हि to go, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्ब|हेरंब|हेरंबः|हेरम्बः
हेरम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A buffalo.<BR>3 A hero inflated with his own valour and prowess.<BR>4 A Buddha or Bauddha deity.<BR>E.<BR>हे calling or defying, रवि to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्बजननी|हेरंबजननी
हेरम्बजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>हेरम्ब GAṆEŚA, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्बहट्ट|हेरम्बहट्टः
हेरम्बहट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A country included in the enumeration of the provinces of the Dekhin.<BR>E.<BR>हेरम्ब GAṆEŚA, and हट्ट fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरिक|हेरिकः
हेरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरुक|हेरुकः
हेरुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An attendant on Mahākāla, or ŚIVA in that form.<BR>2 An inferior divinity of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलञ्ची
हेलञ्ची<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलन|हेलनं
हेलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Disrespect, disregard, contempt.<BR>2 Wantoning, dalliance.<BR>E.<BR>हिस्न to disregard, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेला
हेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Wanton dalliance, lascivious endearment.<BR>2 Disrespect, contempt.<BR>3 Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>हिल to dally, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलावुक्क|हेलावुक्कः
हेलावुक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलि|हेलिः
हेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Dalliance, wanton sport.<BR>E.<BR>हिस्न to dally, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष|हेषः
हेष<BR>(ऋ) हेषृ r. 1st cl. (हेषते)<BR>To neigh as a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषा
हेषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Neighing, (as a horse, or braying, as an ass.)<BR>E.<BR>हेष to sound, to neigh, aff. अच् and ठाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषिन्
हेषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>हेषा neighing, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेहे
हेहे<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of addressing, a vocative particle.<BR>2 An interjection of calling aloud.<BR>E.<BR>हे the same, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

है
है<BR>ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle.<BR>2 An interjection of calling.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वे to call, डै aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक|हैतुकः
हैतुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Causal, causative.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A follower of the Mīmāṃsā doctrines.<BR>2 A sceptic, a causalist.<BR>E.<BR>हेतु cause, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Golden.<BR>2 Frigid, freezing, cold.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Hoar-frost.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन् gold, or हिम frost, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
हैमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Cold, wintry.<BR>2 Growing in winter.<BR>2 Suitable to winter.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The month Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The winter season.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन्त winter, अण् aff., and the final optionally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्त|हैमन्तं
हैमन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>1 Wintry, cold.<BR>2 Growing in winter, &c.<BR>3 Suitable to the winter, (as abode or clothing, &c.)<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The winter season.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन्त winter, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्तिक|हैमंतिक|हैमन्तिकं
हैमन्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Wintry, freezing, frigid.<BR>E.<BR>हेमन्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमल|हैमलः
हैमल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>Winter.<BR>E.<BR>हिमल cold, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवत|हैमवतं|हैमवतः
हैमवत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Bharata Varṣa or India.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 Chebulic myrobalan.<BR>3 A medicinal kind of moon-plant.<BR>4 A white kind of Orris root.<BR>5 The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>हिसवत् the snowy mountains skirting India, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैयङ्गवीन|हैयंगवीन|हैयंगवीनं|हैयङ्गवीनं
हैयङ्गवीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Clarified butter prepared a day before it is used.<BR>2 Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>ह्य yesterday, गोदोह milk, हियङ्ग substituted for them, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरिक|हैरिकः
हैरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहय|हैहयः
हैहय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀRTAVĪRYA, a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहेय|हैहेयः
हैहेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A prince; also KĀRTAVĪRYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हो
हो<BR>ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle.<BR>2 An interjection of calling out to, or challenging.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, डो aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड|होडः
होड<BR>(ऋ) होडृ r. 1st cl. (होडति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>(होडते)<BR>To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड|होडः
होड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A raft, a float, a boat.<BR>E.<BR>हाड to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडृ
होडृ<BR>m. (-डा)<BR>A robber, a footpad or highway robber.<BR>E.<BR>हुड to collect, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढ|होढं
होढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Stolen.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>Stolen goods.<BR>E.<BR>हुड to steal, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृ
होतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A priest, who at a sacrifice recites the prayers of the Rig Veda; one conversant with that Veda.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, Uṇādi aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्र|होत्रं
होत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 An article intended or fit for offering with fire, generally clarified butter.<BR>2 Burnt-offering, oblation with fire.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रीय|होत्रीयं|होत्रीयः
होत्रीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A place where oblations are offered.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A priest offering an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>होत्र an offering, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम|होमः
होम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Burnt-offering, the casting of clarified butter, &c. into the sacred fire, as an offering to the gods, accompanied with prayers or invocations, according to the object of the sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमकुण्ड|होमकुंड|होमकुण्डं
होमकुण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A hole in the ground or an altar, for receiving the fire for an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>होम burnt-offering, and कुण्ड a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमधूम|होमधूमः
होमधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The smoke of burnt-offering.<BR>E.<BR>होम as above, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमभस्मन्
होमभस्मन्<BR>n. (-स्म)<BR>The ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR>E.<BR>होम as above, भस्मन् ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमवत्|होमवन्त्
होमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having performed sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>होम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमाग्नि|होमाग्निः
होमाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>होम an oblation, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमि|होमिः
होमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 Clarified butter.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, मिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिन्
होमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>The offerer of an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, मिनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरा
होरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The rising of a sign of the zodiac.<BR>2 Part of the duration of a sign, the twenty-fourth part of a day, an hour.<BR>3 A mark, a line.<BR>4 A science or work in science, probably on astrology.<BR>E.<BR>होड to go, to proceed, affs. अच and टाप, and ड changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=980" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलाका
होलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The ceremony of throwing a red powder called Holi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होहौ
होहौ<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of calling.<BR>2 An exclamation of challenging or defiance.<BR>E.<BR>हो, and हौ both the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौ
हौ<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of defiance or challenge.<BR>2 A vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>ह्वेञ् to call, डौ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or appertaining to the Hotṛ or priest so named.<BR>E.<BR>हौतृ a priest, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्य|हौम्यं
हौम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>होम burnt-offering, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्यधान्य|हौम्यधान्यं
हौम्यधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>हौम्य relating to burnt-offering, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नु
ह्नु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ह्नुते)<BR>To take away, to withhold or secrete.<BR>With अप or नि prefixed,<BR>To conceal, to hide, to deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्मल
ह्मल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्मलति)<BR>To move, to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्
ह्यस्<BR>ind.<BR>Yesterday.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्तन|ह्यस्तनं
ह्यस्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Of yesterday, produced or occurred yesterday.<BR>E.<BR>ह्यस् yesterday, द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्त्य|ह्यस्त्यः
ह्यस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>Of yesterday: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>ह्यस् yesterday, and त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रग
ह्रग<BR>(ए) ह्रगे r. 1st cl. (ह्रगति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रणिया
ह्रणिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Censure, reproach.<BR>2 Shame.<BR>E.<BR>हृणीङ् Kaṇḍvādi root, to feel shame, यक् aff., form irr.: see ह्रिणीया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद|ह्रदः
ह्रद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A deep lake, a large or deep piece of water.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>ह्राद to sound, aff. अच्, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदग्रह|ह्रदग्रहः
ह्रदग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An alligator, a crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रद a lake, and ग्रह abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदिनी
ह्रदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रद deep water, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रप
ह्रप<BR>r. 10th cl. (ह्रापयति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस
ह्रस<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्रसति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To be small or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसित
ह्रसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made little, diminished.<BR>2 Sounded.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिष्ठ|ह्रसिष्ठः
ह्रसिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very short or small.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, aff. of the irr. superlative इष्ठन्, form irr.; also with इयसुन् aff. ह्रसीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिमन्
ह्रसिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Smallness, shortness.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, small, इमनिच् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्व|ह्रस्वं|ह्रस्वः
ह्रस्व<BR>mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>1 Short, low in stature.<BR>2 Short, as a vowel.<BR>m. (-स्वः)<BR>A dwarf.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस to be small, and व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वगवेधुका
ह्रस्वगवेधुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, गवेधुका coix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वदर्भ|ह्रस्वदर्भः
ह्रस्वदर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A short kind of Kuśa grass.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, दर्भ the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वपत्रक|ह्रस्वपत्रकः
ह्रस्वपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of Bassia.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, पत्र a leaf, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वाग्नि|ह्रस्वाग्निः
ह्रस्वाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The gigantic Asclepias, (A. gigantea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वाङ्ग|ह्रस्वांग|ह्रस्वाङ्गः
ह्रस्वाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A medicinal root, commonly Jīvaka.<BR>2 A dwarf.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस्व short, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद|ह्रादः
ह्राद<BR>r. 1st cl. (-ह्रादते)<BR>To sound, inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद|ह्रादः
ह्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Noise, sound.<BR>E.<BR>ह्राद to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिन्
ह्रादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Sounding, making a sound or noise.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>3 A river in general.<BR>4 The Olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>ह्राद to sound, affs. इनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रास|ह्रासः
ह्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रस to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणीया
ह्रिणीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Censure, abuse.<BR>2 Shame.<BR>E.<BR>हृणीङ्^1 to be ashamed, aff. यक्, and the vowel changed to रि; also हृणीया, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रित|ह्रितः
ह्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ashamed, modest, bashful.<BR>2 Divided, portioned.<BR>3 Taken, conveyed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A portion, a share.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, क्त aff., and the vowel made short; or हृ to take, aff. क्त, and रि substituted for ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिति|ह्रितिः
ह्रिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Taking, conveying.<BR>E.<BR>रि substituted for ऋ: see हृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रियमाण
ह्रियमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Being taken or seized.<BR>2 Being captivated, attracted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिवेर|ह्रिवेरं
ह्रिवेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A perfume.<BR>E.<BR>see ह्रीवेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री<BR>r. 3rd cl. (जिह्रेति)<BR>To be modest or ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री<BR>f. (-ह्रीः)<BR>Shame, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीका
ह्रीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Modesty, shame.<BR>2 Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, Uṇādi aff. कन्; also र changed to ल, ह्लीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीकु|ह्रीकुः
ह्रीकु<BR>mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>Ashamed, modest.<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 Lac.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, Uṇādi aff. कुक्; also ह्लीकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीच्छ
ह्रीच्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्रीच्छति)<BR>To be modest or ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीजित|ह्रीजितः
ह्रीजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री shame, and जित overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीण|ह्रीणः
ह्रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्तु, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीत|ह्रीतः
ह्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ashamed, bashful, modest.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्त, form reg.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीनिरास|ह्रीनिरासः
ह्रीनिरास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Shamelessness.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री, and निरास throwing aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीमत्|ह्रीमन्त्
ह्रीमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेर|ह्रीवेरं
ह्रीवेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A drug and perfume, commonly Bāla.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री shame, and वेर saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेल|ह्रीवेलं
ह्रीवेल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A perfume: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रीवेर as before, र changed to ल; also with कन् added, ह्रीवेलकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपण|ह्रेपणं
ह्रेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Putting to shame, excelling, surpassing.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपयत्
ह्रेपयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Putting to shame, outvieing, surpassing.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपित
ह्रेपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made ashamed, put to shame.<BR>2 Excelled, surpassed.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुड
ह्रुड<BR>(ऋ) ह्रुडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रुडति)<BR>To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रूड
ह्रूड<BR>(ऋ) ह्रूडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रूडति)<BR>1 To collect.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेष
ह्रेष<BR>(ऋ) ह्रेषृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रेषते)<BR>1 To sound inarticulaly, to neigh as a horse.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषा
ह्रेषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Neighing as a horse.<BR>E.<BR>ह्रेष to neigh, affs. अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रोड
ह्रोड<BR>(ऋ) ह्रोडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रोडति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लग
ह्लग<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्लगति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लप
ह्लप<BR>r. 10th cl. (ह्लापयति)<BR>To speak, to speak articulately: also ह्रप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लस
ह्लस<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्लसति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद|ह्लादः
ह्लाद<BR>(ई) ह्लादी r. 1st cl. (ह्लादते)<BR>1 To gladden, to delight.<BR>2 To be glad or delighted.<BR>3 To sound, especially as a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद|ह्लादः
ह्लाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Pleasure, joy.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लाद to be glad, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=981" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादन|ह्लादनं
ह्लादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Joy, delight.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लाद to be glad, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादित
ह्लादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delighted, happy.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लाद to be happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिन्
ह्लादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Happy, glad.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लाद pleasure, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीका
ह्लीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Shame, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>ह्नी to be ashamed, कन् Uṇādi aff., and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीकु|ह्लीकुः
ह्लीकु<BR>mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>Ashamed, modest.<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 Lac.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, aff. कुक्, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लेषा
ह्लेषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Neighing, as a horse or ass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ह्लेष for ह्रेष to neigh, aff. अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वल
ह्वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्वलति)<BR>To move, to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृ
ह्वृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्वरति)<BR>To bend, to curve, to make crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वे
ह्वे<BR>r. 1st cl. (ह्वयति)<BR>1 To emulate, to vie with, to wish to overcome or surpass.<BR>2 To struggle or contend with.<BR>3 To call.<BR>4 To challenge.<BR>With उप, नि, वि or सम् the verb is deponent<BR>(उपह्नयते);<BR>also with आङ् if rivalry be signified,<BR>(आह्वयते)<BR>he challenges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=982" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

